t\n][59]\nSectors\n[ Defense ][60] [ Civilian ][61] [ Healthcare ][62] [ Tribal ][63]\nState, Local, and Education (SLED)\n][64]\nSectors\n[ Energy ][65] [ Water/Wastewater ][66] [ Transportation ][67] [ Public Safety ][68]\n* [Customers][69]\nFor Customers\nClaroty Customer Experience\nAccelerating your CPS cybersecurity journey.\n][70] [\nCustomer Case Studies\nHow customers secure their critical operations with Claroty.\n][71] [\nClaroty xCel Academy\nEnablement and training for customers.\n][72]\nFeatured Case Studies\n[ [Featured image for our Case Study: Claroty xDome Drives Business Value and Enhanced Exposure\nManagement at Ohio State University Wexner Medical Center]\n\n#### Claroty xDome Drives Business Value and Enhanced Exposure Management at Ohio State University\n#### Wexner Medical Center\n\n][73] [ [By partnering with Claroty and implementing its purpose-built healthcare solution,\nClaroty xDome for Healthcare, PHSA and FHA were able to quickly fill the immediate gaps in device\ndiscovery, tracking, and risk management.]\n\n#### Provincial Health Services Authority and Fraser Health Authority Boost Cybersecurity\n#### Processes and Compliance with Claroty xDome\n\n][74] [ [In partnership with Claroty, Phlow implemented a tailored CPS security infrastructure.\nPhlow now has a robust security layout, providing rigorous network visibility, real-time\nmonitoring, and instantaneous threat detection.]\n\n#### Phlow Leverages Claroty Technologies for Unparalleled Cyber-Physical System Protection\n\n][75]\n* [Partners][76]\nTechnology Alliance Partners\n][77] [\nChannel Partners\n][78] [\nPartner Login\n][79]\n* [Threat Research][80]\nTeam82 Home\n][81] [\nThreat Intelligence\n][82] [\nVulnerability Disclosure Dashboard\n][83] [\nResearch\n][84] [\nTalks\n][85] [\nPGP Key\n][86]\n* [Resources][87]\nResources\nResource Library\n][88]\n[ Blog ][89] [ Reports ][90] [ White Papers ][91] [ Datasheets & Solution Overviews ][92] [\nIntegration Briefs ][93] [ Case Studies ][94] [ On-Demand Webinars ][95] [ Videos ][96] [ Glossary\n][97]\nPodcasts, Articles, & Videos\n[ [Nexus Connect X logo]\nVisit our Nexus Website\n][98]\nFeatured Content\n\n#### Life, uninterrupted.\n\n][99] [\n\n#### Claroty Named a Leader in 2026 Gartner\u00ae Magic Quadrant\u2122 for CPS Protection Platforms\n\n][100] [ [Featured image for our Guide: The Guide to Building Operational Resilience in Healthcare\nEnvironments]\n\n#### The Guide to Building Operational Resilience in Healthcare Environments\n\n][101] [ [Featured image for our report: Resolving the CPS Identity Crisis]\n\n#### Resolving the CPS Identity Crisis\n\n][102]\n* [Company][103]\nAbout Us\n][104] [\nCareers\n][105] [\nLeadership\n][106] [\nNewsroom\n][107] [\nxCel Enablement & Training\n][108] [\nTrust Center\n][109] [\nEvents\n][110] [\nEnvironmental, Social, and Governance Policies\n][111] [\nContact Us\n][112]\n[ Toggle Search ][113] Menu\n\n# Our Leadership Team\n\n[Executive Team][114] [Board of Directors][115] [Advisory Board][116]\n\n## Executive Team\n\n[Image of Yaniv Vardi for the Claroty leadership page]\n\n#### Yaniv Vardi\n\nChief Executive Officer\n\n[Image of Grant Geyer for the Claroty leadership page]\n\n#### Grant Geyer\n\nChief Strategy Officer\n\n[Image of Gil Gur Arie for the Claroty leadership page]\n\n#### Gil Gur Arie\n\nChief Product Officer\n\n[Image of Udi Bar Sela for the Claroty leadership page]\n\n#### Udi Bar Sela\n\nChief Financial Officer and Chief Operating Officer\n\n[Image of Upa Campbell for the Claroty leadership page]\n\n#### Upa Campbell\n\nChief Marketing Officer\n\n[Image of James Love for the Claroty leadership page]\n\n#### James Love\n\nChief Revenue Officer\n\n[Image of Shira Bar Yosef for the Claroty leadership page]\n\n#### Shira Bar Yosef\n\nChief Customer Officer\n\n[Image of Rotem Sher for the Claroty leadership page]\n\n#### Rotem Sher\n\nChief of Staff\n\n[Image of Yuval Fessler for the Claroty leadership page]\n\n#### Yuval Fessler\n\nChief Legal Officer\n\n[Image of Amir Preminger for the Claroty leadership page]\n\n#### Amir Preminger\n\nChief Technology Officer\n\n[Image of Yuval Zilberman for the Claroty leadership page]\n\n#### Yuval Zilberman\n\nChief Information Officer\n\n[Image of Natalie Katester Boimer for the Claroty leadership page]\n\n#### Natalie Katester Boimer\n\nChief Human Resources Officer\n\n## Board of Directors\n\n#### Dave DeWalt\n\nBoard Chairman, Founder & CEO of NightDragon\n\n[Image of Yaniv Vardi for the Claroty leadership page]\n\n#### Yaniv Vardi\n\nChief Executive Officer\n\n#### Amir Zilberstein\n\nDirector & Co-founder\n\n#### Galina Antova\n\nDirector & Co-founder\n\n#### Yuval Shachar\n\nDirector, Team8\n\n#### David Cowan\n\nDirector, Bessemer Venture Partners\n\n#### Amit Lubovsky\n\nDirector, SoftBank Vision Fund\n\n#### Meir Ukeles\n\nDirector, MoreVC\n\n#### Rossa Shanks\n\nDirector, Istari\n\n#### Peter Marturano\n\nDirector, Standard Investments\n\n#### John Miller\n\nDirector, Rockwell Automation\n\n#### Amit Chaturvedy\n\nManaging Partner, SE Ventures\n\n[Image of Robert Tuchscherer for the Claroty leadership page]\n\n#### Robert Tuchscherer\n\nDirector, Golub Growth\n\n## Advisory Board\n\n[In this episode of Claroty's Nexus podcast, retired Adm. Mike Rogers, former director of the\nNational Security Agency and commander of U.S. Cyber Command joins to talk about ransomware and its\nimpact on ICS and OT, defensive strategies, and whether to pay ransom demands in order to promptly\nresume production.]\n\n#### Admiral (Ret.) Michael S. Rogers\n\nChairman - Board of Advisors\n\n#### Chris Inglis\n\nFormer U.S. National Cyber Director\n\n#### Jim LaBonty\n\nFormer Head of Global Automation Engineering, Pfizer\n\n#### Jesse Whaley\n\nFormer Chief Information Security Officer, Amtrak\n\n#### Charles Carmakal\n\nChief Technology Officer, Mandiant Consulting\n\n## Claroty Demo\n\nReady to Secure Your CPS Environment?\n\n[ Request a Demo ][117]\nSolutions\n* [Claroty xDome Platform][118]\n* [Industrial Cybersecurity][119]\n* [Healthcare Cybersecurity][120]\n* [Commercial Cybersecurity][121]\n* [Public Sector Cybersecurity][122]\nThreat Research\n* [Team82 Home][123]\n* [Vulnerability Disclosure Dashboard][124]\n* [Research][125]\n* [PGP Key][126]\nPartners\n* [Partners][127]\n* [Technology Alliance Partners][128]\n* [Channel Partners][129]\n* [Become a Partner][130]\n* [Partner Login][131]\nResources\n* [Resource Library][132]\n* [Blog][133]\n* [White Papers][134]\n* [Reports][135]\n* [Case Studies][136]\n* [Datasheets][137]\n* [Integration Briefs][138]\n* [Videos][139]\n* [Claroty Nexus][140]\nCompany\n* [About Us][141]\n* [Careers][142]\n* [Leadership][143]\n* [Newsroom][144]\n* [xCel Enablement & Training][145]\n* [Trust Center][146]\n* [Customer Experience][147]\n* [Events][148]\n* [Environmental, Social, and Governance Policies][149]\n* [Contact Us][150]\n[ [Claroty] ][151]\n\n\u00a9 2026 Claroty. All rights reserved.\n\n[ LinkedIn ][152] [ Twitter ][153] [ YouTube ][154] [ Facebook ][155]\n[Terms & Conditions][156] / [Privacy Policy][157]\nClose Modal\n[Image of Yaniv Vardi for the Claroty leadership page]\n[ LinkedIn ][158]\n\n## Yaniv Vardi\n\nChief Executive Officer\n\nYaniv Vardi is a dynamic and highly accomplished entrepreneur with more than two decades of global\nexecutive leadership experience. He has established a long-standing and impressive track record of\ndeveloping and executing global business strategies and directing worldwide growth. As Claroty\u2019s\nChief Executive Officer, Vardi is leading the company through its next stage of growth and\nsolidifying its position as the leader in cyber-physical systems security. Prior to joining Claroty,\nhe recently served as the Global Managing Director of Centrica Business Solutions, International,\nmanaging 8 countries and expanding the company\u2019s proposition mainly in Europe, South America, and\nAsia Pacific into a significant business. Prior to joining Centrica, Vardi was the CEO of Panoramic\nPower, a global pioneer in energy management solutions for global C&I customers, which was acquired\nby Centrica. Prior to joining Panoramic Power, Vardi was Co-founder and Managing Director of Sparta\nSystems EMEA, successfully driving its operations to be the leading provider of QMS in the Life\nScience industry, and leading the company to a successful acquisition. Based on his wealth of\nexperience, Vardi brings vital knowledge of operational direction and strategies as a board director\nand chairman in different companies in Israel, Europe, and the United States. Vardi graduated Magna\nCum Laude from the New Jersey Institute of Technology majoring in Industrial and Management\nEngineering and Management of Information Systems and served in the Israeli Air Force for five\nyears.\n\nClose Modal\n[Image of Grant Geyer for the Claroty leadership page]\n[ LinkedIn ][159]\n\n## Grant Geyer\n\nChief Strategy Officer\n\nGrant Geyer is Chief Strategy Officer at Claroty, responsible for leading the company\u2019s strategy\nprocess, determining possible market opportunities, category adjacencies, and investment theses for\nvalue creation. He works with stakeholders in the executive leadership team to determine the best\nways to accelerate the execution of the corporate vision. He has had a successful career as an\noperator in the cybersecurity industry for over 20 years at companies of different stages of growth.\nHe previously served as Claroty\u2019s Chief Product Officer, overseeing the product management,\nengineering, and research organizations, and was responsible for the company\u2019s product strategy and\ndevelopment. Prior to joining Claroty, he worked as an Executive-in-Residence at Scale Venture\nPartners, where he assisted the firm in analyzing cybersecurity markets and ventures. Previously,\nGeyer held the role of Senior Vice President of Products for RSA, responsible for both traditional\nand SaaS product offerings. Prior to RSA, Geyer served as Vice President at Symantec, which he\njoined through its acquisition of Riptech. Earlier in his career, Geyer served as a Military\nIntelligence officer for the U.S. Army. He holds a B.S. in Computer Science from the U.S. Military\nAcademy at West Point and a M.S. in Engineering Management from the University of Maryland,\nBaltimore.\n\nClose Modal\n[Image of Gil Gur Arie for the Claroty leadership page]\n[ LinkedIn ][160]\n\n## Gil Gur Arie\n\nChief Product Officer\n\nGil Gur Arie is Chief Product Officer of Claroty, where he is responsibl"
