        "crawl_text": "International Business Machines Corporation Publicly traded company North America Asia Pacific Europe Cloud Computing Quantum Computing Hybrid Cloud Strong brand recognition Extensive research and development Global presence Diverse product portfolio ISO 27001 GDPR HIPAA 1 New Orchard Road, Armonk, New York 10504-1722, United States Australia Bangladesh Bhutan Singapore Malaysia New Zealand Hong Kong India Japan Vietnam Korea Republic Macao United States Australia Bangladesh Bhutan Singapore Malaysia New Zealand Hong Kong India Japan Vietnam Korea Republic Macao Global IBM has over 300,000 employees across 170+ countries. IBM offers over 660 products tailored to meet various business needs. Hybrid cloud and AI integration Sustainability and ethical AI Quantum computing advancements Intense competition in the technology sector Rapid technological changes Regulatory compliance challenges Growing demand for cloud computing solutions Increased adoption of AI technologies Expansion into emerging markets IBM is a leading global technology and consulting company, recognized for its innovation and extensive portfolio of products and services. Investment in research and development Strategic partnerships Focus on customer-centric solutions 1. [ Home ][1]\n2. About\n\n# About IBM\n\nClients, partners and creators putting technology to work in the real world\n\n[ Get the latest IBM news ][2]\n[Front view of the IBM office building at Madison One avenue in NYC]\n\n## What IBM does\n\nIBM brings together software, consulting and infrastructure to help clients solve the business\nchallenges that matter most. Our platforms embed AI into core systems and workflows, improve the\neconomics of real work and scale securely across hybrid cloud environments. We deploy solutions\ninside IBM before we bring them to clients, so what we deliver is not just designed, but proven.\n\n[ See IBM leadership ][3] [ Explore financial information ][4]\n\n## Fast facts\n\n300,000+\n\nemployees across 170+ countries\n\n2,500+\n\nbusinesses in our Partner Plus program\n\n660+\n\nproducts tailored to meet your every need\n\n80+\n\nyears of delivering breakthrough research\n\nTechnology and services\n\n### Software\n\nTurn complexity into advantage with software that is hybrid, open and responsible by design\u2014built to\nmake your systems work together, not just side by side.\n\n[ Learn more ][5]\n[Two people looking at an application screen at Think]\n\n### Infrastructure\n\nModernize applications, servers and storage in place, at your own pace, to integrate with hybrid\ncloud and AI.\n\n[ Learn more ][6]\n[Close-up of lab worker inspecting a unit taken out of a FlashSystem 5600.]\n\n### Consulting\n\nWork with IBM experts to drive high-impact outcomes using advanced AI and a science-based approach\nto tackle your most critical challenges.\n\n[ Learn more ][7]\n[Two professionals discussing within a modern office setting]\n\n### Strategic Partnerships\n\nDiscover the power of IBM partnerships that combine expertise, resources and technologies to help\nyou accelerate growth.\n\n[ Learn more ][8]\n[Two colleagues collaborating in a modern office setting, with a whiteboard on the background]\n\n### Red Hat\n\nSimplify complexity, reduce costs and unleash innovation with Red Hat on IBM Cloud.\n\n[ Learn more ][9]\n[Person in an office building interacting with stacked lego-shaped boxes]\n\n## Origin story\n\nFor over a century, IBM has been at the forefront of technological innovation. Beginning in the\nearliest days of computing, IBM has blended intelligence, innovation and science to improve\nbusiness, society and the human experience.\n\n[Learn more about our rich history ][10]\n1. 1880-1929\n2. 1930-1949\n3. 1950-1979\n4. 1980-1999\n5. 2000-2023\n6. 2024-present\n\n### Industrial Revolution to early 20th century\n\nIBM\u2019s roots trace back to Herman Hollerith\u2019s 1896 invention of the tabulating machine,\nrevolutionizing data processing for the 1890 US Census. In 1911, IBM was founded as the\nComputing-Tabulating-Recording Company, later renamed IBM in 1924. Key innovations followed, such as\nthe 1928 introduction of the 80-column punched card, which became a global data standard.\n\n[A woman at work on a punched card tabulator in 1900. ]\n\n### Rise of computing and world conflict\n\nIBM introduced the electric accounting machine in 1929. By 1935, it supported Social Security with\nrecord-keeping systems. During World War II, IBM aided military operations with punch card\ntechnology and in 1945, it founded the Watson Scientific Computing Lab, marking a significant step\ntoward modern computing.\n\n[A woman monitoring punched card processing at an IBM 77 Collator in 1936.]\n\n### Space Age and Mainframe Revolution\n\nLaunched in 1964, IBM\u2019s System/360 was a pivotal mainframe computer for businesses and governments.\nIn 1969, IBM systems helped NASA achieve the Apollo moon landing. In 1973, the introduction of the\nUPC barcode revolutionized retail industries by streamlining inventory management.\n\n[Three men and a woman with the System/360 Model 91 at NASA's Goddard Space Center in Greenbelt,\nMaryland. ]\n\n### PC Revolution and digital transformation\n\nIn 1981, IBM released the IBM PC, revolutionizing personal computing. In 1997, Deep Blue made\nhistory by defeating a world chess champion, Garry Kasparov. By the late 1990s, IBM had also\ndeveloped the world's fastest supercomputer, showcasing its leadership in AI and high-performance\ncomputing.\n\n[The IBM 5150, IBM's first personal computer, introduced in August of 1981]\n\n### Global connectivity and AI\n\nIBM shifted toward cloud computing and AI with Watson's 2011 Jeopardy! win, reshaping business\noptimization and AI-driven solutions. In 2018, IBM and Airbus launched CIMON, the first AI assistant\nfor the International Space Station, expanding its reach into space technology. IBM remains focused\non ethical AI systems today.\n\n[View through a spacecraft window showing Earth below, sunlight, and a circular hatch with a white\nface illustration.]\n\n### Future of technology and sustainability\n\nIBM continues to push the boundaries of AI, quantum computing and sustainability. As a leader in\nethical AI, IBM shapes transparent systems to address global challenges, from healthcare to\nenvironmental sustainability. The company also aims to drive innovation through partnerships in\nspace technology, cloud computing and data-driven industries.\n\n[Technician working on a high-tech industrial equipment plant]\n\n## Global impact\n\n[Laboratory technician handling bioreactor vessels with tubing and control instruments on a lab\nbench]\nStories of impact\nIBM creates lasting impact in communities worldwide\n[Technician showing weather tracking technology]\nIBM Impact Accelerator\nIBM provides technology expertise to nonprofits and governments worldwide\n[Student and instructor working on project]\nIBM SkillsBuild\nIBM aims to provide 30 million people with skills needed for future jobs by the year 2030\n[IBM volunteer working with community]\nGiving and volunteerism\nIBMers are empowered to dedicate their skills and time to make a positive difference\n\n## The future of smarter business\n1. Hybrid cloud + AI\n2. Enterprise AI in action\n3. Client Zero advantage\n4. Quantum and what\u2019s next\n\nSmarter businesses will be defined by intelligence embedded where work happens. IBM is advancing AI\nacross hybrid cloud environments to bring intelligence directly into core systems and\nprocesses\u2014turning enterprise complexity into clarity, adaptability and smarter decisions at scale.\n\n[Engineers installing equipment into server]\n\nAs AI matures, value\u2014not experimentation\u2014matters most. IBM delivers enterprise AI that produces real\neconomic impact by embedding intelligence into workflows and operations. Building on proven results,\nwe help organizations boost productivity, efficiency and competitive advantage at scale.\n\n[Two technicians working in a factory setting]\n\nSmarter business is something we practice first. Through our Client Zero approach, IBM applies AI,\nautomation and hybrid cloud across our own operations before scaling them to clients\u2014ensuring our\nplatforms evolve through real\u2011world use and proven performance.\n\n[Group meeting at a modern office]\n\nThe future of smarter business depends on platforms built to endure. Alongside hybrid cloud and AI,\nIBM is engineering quantum computing from foundational science into enterprise reality\u2014laying the\ngroundwork for breakthroughs that integrate seamlessly with today\u2019s systems.\n\n[IBM Quantum System room]\n\n## Stay connected\n\n[Illustration of an eye with connecting lines to data]\n\n## What's New at IBM newsletter subscription\n\n[1]: /\n[2]: https://newsroom.ibm.com/\n[3]: https://newsroom.ibm.com/executive-bios\n[4]: https://www.ibm.com/investor\n[5]: https://www.ibm.com/software\n[6]: https://www.ibm.com/solutions/infrastructure-modernization\n[7]: https://www.ibm.com/consulting\n[8]: https://www.ibm.com/strategic-partnerships\n[9]: https://www.ibm.com/products/cloud/redhat\n[10]: https://www.ibm.com/history # Contact IBM\n\nGet answers to questions about products, sales, support and everything else IBM.\n\n[Woman smiling while working on a laptop computer]\nSupport [ IBM Support\nReceive help from our tech experts and check the status of a support case.\n][1] [ IBM Documentation\nSearch IBM product documentation.\n][2] [ Product fixes\nFix Central provides fixes and updates for your software, hardware, and operating system.\n][3] [ Developer resources\nOpen source projects, knowledge resources, and developer advocates are ready to help. What will you\ncreate?\n][4] [ IBM Community\nConnect with other developers via forums, blogs, files and face-to-face networking.\n][5] [ IBM Partner Support Desk\nGet personalized, proactive support to navigate Partner Plus Programs.\n][6] [ Customer support\nFind support for contracts, orders, and invoices in your country or region.\n][7] [ Technical Support Contacts\nFind contacts for software and hardware support in your country or region.\n][8] [ IBM Careers\nGet support for technical issues related to the application process and explore FAQs about working\nat IBM.\n][9]\nSales [ Contact IBM sales\nQuestions about our products? Ready to purchase? Reach out to our sales team for assistance.\n][10]\nLearn [ Learn\nIBM Training and certifications offer you the ability to earn credentials to demonstrate your\nexpertise.\n][11]\nBusiness partners [ IBM Partner Plus\nExplore how partners are transforming the way business is done by leveraging IBM solutions to grow\ntheir business and solve client problems.\n][12]\nAdditional resources [ Investor relations\nLearn how IBM is positioned to lead as we enter the era of hybrid cloud.\n][13] [ MyIBM ID\nLog in to access your account, services, and support options.\n][14] [ Media relations\nView announcements, media contacts and press tools.\n][15] [ Privacy\nContact the IBM Chief Privacy Office for questions regarding privacy.\n][16] [ Corporate responsibility\nSee how IBM and IBMers are making a difference in communities around the world.\n][17] [ Popular trials\nLooking to try out a product, like SPSS? Explore our trials page.\n][18] [ Employment verification process\nEmployment verification for active and former IBMers.\n][19]\nContact information\nCorporate address\n\n**1 New Orchard Road\nArmonk, New York 10504-1722\nUnited States\n\n[ Contact HR ][20]\nPhone numbers\n\n**General:**\n**Toll Free**: 1-800-426-4968\n\n**Shopping assistance:**\n**Toll Free**: 1-888-746-7426\n\n**Directory assistance:**\n914-499-1900\n\n**Software**:\n**Toll Free**: 1-800-426\u20137378\n**Tel**: +1-303-939-1414\n\n**Hardware**:\n**Toll Free**: 1-800-426\u20137378\n**Tel**: +1-303-939-1414\n\nFollow IBM\n\n[LinkedIn][21]\n\n[X][22]\n\n[Instagram][23]\n\nSearch for geography-specific contact information.\n\nAccessibility:\n\nIBM is committed to equal access for people of all abilities.\n\n[IBM Accessibility][24]\n\n## Asia Pacific\n\n**Australia**\n[ Contact IBM ][25]\n**Bangladesh**\n[ Contact IBM ][26]\n**Bhutan**\n\n**General inquiries**\n\n**Tel**: 1800-418-1000 1\n+65-6418-1000 2\n**Fax**: +65-6418-2000\n\n**Address\nIBM Singapore Pte. Ltd.**\n7 Changi Business P"
