        "crawl_text": "Nozomi Networks Inc. Compliant with various cybersecurity regulations. North America Europe Middle East Asia-Pacific Latin America APAC Leader in 2026 Gartner Magic Quadrant for CPS Protection Platforms Leader in IoT Security Solutions by Forrester Leader in 2023 Frost Radar 2026 Fortress Cybersecurity Award in Operational Technology Category 2025 IoT Excellence Award from IoT Evolution World 2026 Gartner\u00ae Magic Quadrant\u2122 for CPS Protection Platforms AI-driven insights Real-time monitoring Integration with existing IT systems Deep Packet Inspection Behavioral analysis Automated incident response 100% customer retention 12,000+ installations worldwide 115M+ devices monitored Industry-specific expertise Comprehensive asset visibility Real-time threat detection Deep expertise in OT and IoT security Global partner ecosystem DoW ZT for OT ISA/IEC 62443 Standards NERC CIP NIS2 Directive SEC Cybersecurity Rules TSA Security Directives Mendrisio, Switzerland 330 5th Avenue SW, Suite 1800, Calgary, AB T2P 0L4, Canada Via Maria Ghioldi-Schweizer 2, 6850 Mendrisio, Switzerland Strandvejen 60, 2900 Hellerup, Denmark Viale Certosa, 218, 20156 Milan, Italy Novotel Business Park, Tower 2, 1st Floor, Unit No. 43, Dammam, 6140-32232, Saudi Arabia Level 19 & 20, Tower 2, One Raffles Place, Singapore 048616 World Trade Center 30F, Trade Tower, 511 Young Dong St, Gangnam-gu, Seoul 06164, Republic of Korea DIC Building 9, 3rd floor, Office 301, Dubai, United Arab Emirates United States Canada Switzerland Denmark Italy Saudi Arabia Singapore South Korea United Arab Emirates Global Middle East Latin America North America APAC Nozomi Networks is recognized as a leader in OT and IoT cybersecurity, with a strong focus on critical infrastructure. The company has a global presence with significant installations across various industries. Continuous innovation and customer-centric solutions are key to their market leadership. Nozomi Networks specializes in cybersecurity for operational technology and IoT environments. The company has a strong focus on compliance with industry regulations for critical infrastructure. Nozomi Networks monitors over 115 million OT, IoT, and IT devices globally. The company has over 12,000 installations worldwide. Nozomi Networks has achieved 100% customer retention. Nozomi Networks has expanded its product offerings to include advanced endpoint security solutions. The company has been recognized in multiple industry reports for its innovative approach to cybersecurity. Nozomi Networks expands presence in Latin American markets. Nozomi Networks platform now available on Google Cloud Marketplace. Nozomi Networks wins multiple cybersecurity awards. Enhancing cybersecurity for critical infrastructure sectors. Expanding global partnerships to improve service delivery. Expanding global presence in cybersecurity for industrial sectors. Enhancing AI capabilities for better threat detection. Enhancing cybersecurity for critical infrastructure. Expanding global partnerships and market presence. Innovating in AI-driven cybersecurity solutions. The rapidly evolving cybersecurity landscape poses ongoing challenges for maintaining security effectiveness. Competition from other cybersecurity firms in the OT and IoT space. Increasing sophistication of cyber threats targeting industrial environments. Regulatory compliance challenges across different regions. Increasing cyber threats targeting critical infrastructure. Regulatory compliance in various regions. Competition in the cybersecurity market. Growing demand for cybersecurity solutions in critical infrastructure sectors. Potential for expansion into emerging markets. Expansion into emerging markets. Growing demand for OT and IoT security solutions. Partnerships with leading technology providers. Leader in OT and IoT cybersecurity solutions for critical infrastructure. Increasing cyber threats targeting critical infrastructure. Regulatory requirements driving demand for enhanced security solutions. Increased investment in cybersecurity due to rising threats. Expansion of IoT devices in industrial applications. Rising cyber threats in industrial sectors. Increased investment in cybersecurity by enterprises. Expansion of IoT devices in critical infrastructure. A Note to our Customers and Partners in the Middle East\n[More Information][1]\nAcademy\n][2][\nLabs\n][3][\nCareers\n][4][\nPartner Login\n][5][\nSupport\n][6]\n[[Nozomi logo]][7]\nPlatform\n\n### Platform Overview\n\nOur industrial cybersecurity solutions deliver unmatched asset intelligence, threat detection and\nAI-driven insights.\n\nLearn more\n][8]\nMANAGERS\nVantage\nCloud\n][9][\nCentral Management Console\nOn-prem\n][10]\nSENSORS\nGuardian\nNetwork\n][11][\nGuardian Air\nWireless\n][12][\nArc\nEndpoint\n][13][\nArc Embedded\nEndpoint\n][14]\nENHANCEMENTS\nVantage IQ\n][15][\nAsset Intelligence\n][16][\nThreat Intelligence\n][17][\nSmart Polling\n][18][\nTI Expansion Pack\nPowered by Mandiant\n][19][\nIntegrations\n][20]\n\n### Professional Services\n\nOT and IoT security expertise that speeds solution deployment and maximizes value\n\nLearn more\n][21]\nSolutions\nBUSINESS NEED\nAsset Inventory Management\n][22][\nThreat Detection & Response\n][23][\nContinuous Network Monitoring\n][24][\nVulnerability Management\n][25][\nRisk Management\n][26][\nIoT Security\n][27][\nData Center Cybersecurity\n][28][\nBuilding Automation System\nCybersecurity\n][29]\nINDUSTRY\nAirports\n][30][\nElectric Utilities\n][31][\nHealthcare\n][32][\nManufacturing\n][33][\nMaritime\n][34][\nMining\n][35][\nOil & Gas\n][36]\nPharmaceutical\n][37][\nRail\n][38][\nRetail\n][39][\nSmart Cities\n][40][\nStadiums & Arenas\n][41][\nWater &\nWastewater\n][42]\n[Icon of a government building with three columns, a triangular roof, and a blue flag on top.]\nPUBLIC SECTOR\nFederal Government\n][43]\nState & Local\n][44]\nCOMPLIANCE\nDoW ZT for OT\n][45][\nISA/IEC 62443 Standards\n][46][\nNERC CIP\n][47][\nNERC CIP-015\n][48][\nNIS2 Directive\n][49][\nSEC Cybersecurity Rules\n][50][\nTSA Security Directives\n][51]\nPartners\n\n### Why Partner with Us\n\nOur global partner network deploys OT & IoT cybersecurity solutions for customers around the world.\n\nLearn more\n][52]\n\n### Our Partners\n\nExplore all Nozomi Networks partners\n\nLearn more\n][53]\n\n### Find a Partner\n\nFind a certified Nozomi Networks partner in your country.\n\nLearn more\n][54]\n\n### Partner Portal\n\nLog into the Nozomi Networks partner portal.\n\nLog In\n][55]\nResources\n\n### Resource Library\n\nBrowse OT & IoT security research, guides, videos and more from the Nozomi Networks team.\n\nView Resources\n][56]\nRESOURCES\nCase Studies\n][57][\nContent Packs\n][58][\nData Sheets\n][59][\nOT Cyber FAQs\n][60][\nGuides\n][61][\nResearch Reports\n][62]\nSolution Briefs\n][63][\nVideos\n][64][\nWebinars\n][65][\nWhite Papers\n][66][\nTrust Center\n][67]\n\n### Customer Hub\n\nExplore our latest customer resources, including webinars, how-to videos, content packs and more.\n\nView Hub\n][68]\nBlog\n][69]\nCompany\n\n### About Nozomi Networks\n\nWe keep critical infrastructure and operational technology cyber resilient.\n\nLearn more\n][70]\nLeadership Team\n][71][\nEvents\n][72][\nNewsroom\n][73]\nCareers\n][74][\nCustomer Stories\n][75][\nContact Us\n][76]\n[Request Demo][77]\n\n# OT & IoT Security Analyst Recognition and Industry Awards\n\nRead what the top OT & IoT security analysts say about us.\n\n## Nozomi Networks Named a Leader Again in 2026 Gartner**^{\u00ae}** Magic Quadrant^{\u2122 }for\n## CPS Protection Platforms\n\nFor a second consecutive year, Gartner has named Nozomi Networks a Leader in its Magic Quadrant\u2122 for\nCPS Protection Platforms. Gartner evaluated Nozomi Networks alongside 12 other vendors and evaluated\nthem on the basis of Completeness of Vision and Ability to Execute.\n\n[Access the Report][78]\n[Gartner Magic Quadrant for CPS Protection Platforms as of March 2026, showing Leaders including\nNozomi Networks, Claroty, Armis, Dragos; Challengers like Forescout Technologies, Tenable, Fortinet;\nNiche Players including Microsoft, Cisco, Palo Alto Networks, Honeywell, TXOne Networks; and\nVisionary Darktrace.]\n\n## Nozomi Networks Named a Leader in IoT Security Solutions by Forrester\n\nHighest score in Current Offering category in the Forrester Wave\u2122: IoT Security Solutions, Q3 2025.\n\n[Access the Report][79]\n[The Forrester Wave chart for IoT Security Solutions Q3 2025 shows nine vendors positioned by\nstrength of offering and strength of strategy, categorized into Contenders, Strong Performers, and\nLeaders, with Armis, Claroty, and Nozomi Networks as Leaders, some marked as Customer Favorites.]\n\n## Nozomi Networks Named the Leader in 2023 Frost Radar\n\n[Read Report][80]\n[Frost Radar]\n\n\u201cLeading all vendors on the Frost Radar, Nozomi Networks achieves a perfect score (5 out of 5) in\nboth Innovation and Growth because of its impressive year-over-year revenue growth, strong brand\npresence through partnerships and thought leadership, and a regular cadence of updates and\ncapability enhancements to its Vantage, Arc, and Guardian solutions.\u201d\n\n\u2014 Danielle VanZandt, Frost & Sullivan\n[Logo for 451 Research S&P Global Market Intelligence.]\n\n\u201cWith the release of Arc Embedded, Nozomi now covers the entire OT technology stack from Level 0 to\nLevel 3 in the Purdue model.\u201d\n\n\u2014 Johan Vermij, 451 Research\n[Learn More][81]\n[Logo for 451 Research S&P Global Market Intelligence.]\n\n\u201cBy moving down to Level 1 devices and adding wireless security with Guardian Air, Nozomi aims to\nprovide one of the most comprehensive OT security suites available in the market.\u201d\n\n\u2014 **Johan Vermij, 451 Research**\n[Learn More][82]\n[VDC Research logo]\n\n\u201cNozomi Networks was the overall share leader for industrial cybersecurity software revenue in 2022.\nNozomi Networks\u2019 ability to continually introduce new and innovative solutions such as Vantage,\nOnePass, and Arc has been a critical differentiator.\u201d\n\n\u2014 Jared Weiner, VDC Research\n[Learn More][83]\n[Omdia logo]\n\n\u201cUnlike some other vendors in the industrial cybersecurity space, Nozomi Networks has been focusing\non OT security since its inception a decade ago \u2013 meaning it is well versed in navigating the\nrequirements of OT cybersecurity as opposed to IT.\u201d\n\n\u2014 Hollie Hennessy, Omdia\n[Learn More][84]\n[ARC Advisory logo]\n\n\u201cNozomi Networks executives share ARC\u2019s view of the challenges critical infrastructure companies are\nfacing and the need for better visibility of cyber risks. It demonstrates their commitment to\nhelping companies address these issues. Nozomi Networks is a leading provider of critical\ninfrastructure visibility products that are used by companies around the world to minimize cyber\nrisks and maximize operational resilience. Their Guardian and Vantage solutions provide real-time\nasset visibility, threat detection and actionable intelligence for critical infrastructure.\u201d\n\n\u2014 Sid Snitkin, ARC Advisory Group\n[Learn More][85]\n[Frost & Sullivan logo]\n\n\u201cThe company\u2019s flexible, scalable, and comprehensive Vantage and Guardian solutions provide complete\nIT, IoT, and OT visibility, providing actionable insights that enable clients to secure their\nenvironment and improve their security posture over time.\u201d\n\n\u2014 Tara Semon, Best Practices Research Team Leader, Frost\n& Sullivan\n[Learn More][86]\nAwards and Recognition\n[Fast Company Most Innovative Companies 2025 badge with lightbulb icon, No. 03 Security awarded to\nNozomi Networks.]\n[IoT Evolution IoT Excellence 2024 award badge with gold ribbon and red background.]\n[Plant Engineering 2024 Product of the Year Gold Award emblem.]\n[Shield-shaped badge with text '2024 Fortress Cyber Security Award' and a lock icon at the bottom.]\n[CRN Women of the Channel 2024 logo with red and black text on white and black background.]\n[Global Infosec Awards Winner 2024 badge from Cyber Defense Magazine.]\n[CRN IoT Internet of Things 50 2024 award badge with The Channel Co. logo.]\n[Globee Awards Gold Winner emblem with a globe centered and laurel branches surrounding it on a gold\nbackground.]\n[Logo for The Channel Co.'s CRN Channel Chiefs 2024 recognition.]\n[IoT Evolution IoT Excellence 2023 award badge with a gold ribbon and three sta"
