            "url": "https://www.nozominetworks.com/solutions/building-automation-system-cybersecurity",
            "text": "A Note to our Customers and Partners in the Middle East\n[More Information][1]\nAcademy\n][2][\nLabs\n][3][\nCareers\n][4][\nPartner Login\n][5][\nSupport\n][6]\n[[Nozomi logo]][7]\nPlatform\n\n### Platform Overview\n\nOur industrial cybersecurity solutions deliver unmatched asset intelligence, threat detection and\nAI-driven insights.\n\nLearn more\n][8]\nMANAGERS\nVantage\nCloud\n][9][\nCentral Management Console\nOn-prem\n][10]\nSENSORS\nGuardian\nNetwork\n][11][\nGuardian Air\nWireless\n][12][\nArc\nEndpoint\n][13][\nArc Embedded\nEndpoint\n][14]\nENHANCEMENTS\nVantage IQ\n][15][\nAsset Intelligence\n][16][\nThreat Intelligence\n][17][\nSmart Polling\n][18][\nTI Expansion Pack\nPowered by Mandiant\n][19][\nIntegrations\n][20]\n\n### Professional Services\n\nOT and IoT security expertise that speeds solution deployment and maximizes value\n\nLearn more\n][21]\nSolutions\nBUSINESS NEED\nAsset Inventory Management\n][22][\nThreat Detection & Response\n][23][\nContinuous Network Monitoring\n][24][\nVulnerability Management\n][25][\nRisk Management\n][26][\nIoT Security\n][27][\nData Center Cybersecurity\n][28][\nBuilding Automation System\nCybersecurity\n][29]\nINDUSTRY\nAirports\n][30][\nElectric Utilities\n][31][\nHealthcare\n][32][\nManufacturing\n][33][\nMaritime\n][34][\nMining\n][35][\nOil & Gas\n][36]\nPharmaceutical\n][37][\nRail\n][38][\nRetail\n][39][\nSmart Cities\n][40][\nStadiums & Arenas\n][41][\nWater &\nWastewater\n][42]\n[Icon of a government building with three columns, a triangular roof, and a blue flag on top.]\nPUBLIC SECTOR\nFederal Government\n][43]\nState & Local\n][44]\nCOMPLIANCE\nDoW ZT for OT\n][45][\nISA/IEC 62443 Standards\n][46][\nNERC CIP\n][47][\nNERC CIP-015\n][48][\nNIS2 Directive\n][49][\nSEC Cybersecurity Rules\n][50][\nTSA Security Directives\n][51]\nPartners\n\n### Why Partner with Us\n\nOur global partner network deploys OT & IoT cybersecurity solutions for customers around the world.\n\nLearn more\n][52]\n\n### Our Partners\n\nExplore all Nozomi Networks partners\n\nLearn more\n][53]\n\n### Find a Partner\n\nFind a certified Nozomi Networks partner in your country.\n\nLearn more\n][54]\n\n### Partner Portal\n\nLog into the Nozomi Networks partner portal.\n\nLog In\n][55]\nResources\n\n### Resource Library\n\nBrowse OT & IoT security research, guides, videos and more from the Nozomi Networks team.\n\nView Resources\n][56]\nRESOURCES\nCase Studies\n][57][\nContent Packs\n][58][\nData Sheets\n][59][\nOT Cyber FAQs\n][60][\nGuides\n][61][\nResearch Reports\n][62]\nSolution Briefs\n][63][\nVideos\n][64][\nWebinars\n][65][\nWhite Papers\n][66][\nTrust Center\n][67]\n\n### Customer Hub\n\nExplore our latest customer resources, including webinars, how-to videos, content packs and more.\n\nView Hub\n][68]\nBlog\n][69]\nCompany\n\n### About Nozomi Networks\n\nWe keep critical infrastructure and operational technology cyber resilient.\n\nLearn more\n][70]\nLeadership Team\n][71][\nEvents\n][72][\nNewsroom\n][73]\nCareers\n][74][\nCustomer Stories\n][75][\nContact Us\n][76]\n[Request Demo][77]\n\n#### INDUSTRY\n\n# OT & IoT Cybersecurity for Building Management Systems\n\nToday, almost every new building larger than 100,000 sq/ft (or 10,000 sq/m) is engineered to be a\nsmart building. That is, they rely on building automation systems (BAS) comprising thousands of IoT\nand OT devices, sensors and networks to keep occupants comfortable and safe. These assets also\nintroduce cyber risk, especially if unprotected and exposed to the internet. To maintain operational\nresilience, facility managers and their cybersecurity counterparts must be able to identify and\nmonitor all connected devices and prioritize remediation based on risk.\n\n[Request a Demo][78][See the Platform][79]\n\nThe Nozomi Networks platform is purpose-built to protect OT and IoT networks in commercial,\nresidential and industrial environments from cyber and operational risk.\n\nIt provides the teams responsible for BAS with real-time visibility, asset inventory, AI-powered\ncontinuous monitoring and threat intelligence, so they can detect anomalies, failing OT and IoT\ndevices, and network stability issues before they cause disruption.\n\n## The Connected Smart Building\n\nFrom elevators and HVACS to surveillance cameras and card key access, OT and IoT play a crucial role\nin ensuring the safety, efficiency and comfort of smart buildings. That includes residential and\ncommercial buildings, REITS, hospital systems, large retailers and universities.\n\n[Building automation IoT]\n\n## Building Management Systems Face Four Major Challenges\n\n**Unclear System Ownership**\n\nDuring construction, BAS installation often goes to the lowest-bidding system integrator. Commercial\nowners then hire a facility management company. Physical assets are out of scope for corporate IT\nteams, so BAS cybersecurity falls between the cracks.\n\n**\u201cSet It and Forget It\u201d\n\nSmart building devices must be powerful enough to perform complex automation tasks but simple to\nmaintain. When devices are connected over an open network, this combination creates a large and\nvulnerable attack surface.\n\n**Remote Access Free-for-All**\n\nHighly customized for each building, BAS depend wholly on local service contractors for maintenance.\nThere\u2019s a steady stream of vendors logging into the network, with scant endpoint security.\n\n**Flat Architecture WANs**\n\nMost large companies operate wide area networks (WANs) with flat architectures lacking firewalls and\nsegmentation. Without cyber defenses in place, large OT/IoT networks are attractive targets for\nlaunching enterprise-side exploitations.\n\nNozomi Networks OT-IoT monitoring system is a top-tier solution for protecting OT-IoT environments.\nIts advanced security features, seamless integration, and impressive scalability make it an\nessential tool for organizations looking to safeguard their IoT devices from cyber threats.\n\nDirector of Infrastructure\nReal Estate\n$1B - 10B USD\n[Read Gartner Peer Reviews][80]\n\n## Benefits of Our Cybersecurity Solutions for Smart Buildings\n\n**Automate asset inventory** to identify and manage heterogeneous IoT devices and BAS that run\nautonomously.\n\n[Learn More][81]\n\n**Detect any cyber or operational threat** so you can pinpoint the risks that matter most before\nincidents impact occupants and visitors.\n\n[Learn More][82]\n\n**Prioritize and accelerate remediation** with actionable intelligence and playbooks to address the\nmost critical vulnerabilities and risks.\n\n[Learn More][83]\n\n**Scale continuous OT & IoT monitoring** within large locations and across geographically dispersed\nportfolios.\n\n[Learn More][84]\n[View Platform][85]\n\n## Cybersecurity Regulatory Compliance for Smart Buildings\n\nThe **U.S. **[**National Cybersecurity Strategy**][86]** **includes Commercial Facilities as one of\n16 [critical infrastructure sectors][87] whose assets, systems and networks must be secure and\nresilient. Includes sites such stadiums, retail centers, office and apartment buildings, lodging and\ncasinos.\n\nThe **EU\u2019s **[**NIS2 Directive**][88]** **(effective October 2024) requires operators of medium to\nlarge enterprises to implement security measure to provide resilience against attacks. This includes\nsectors such as health, food, digital infrastructures, research, transport and public\nadministration.\n\n## Building Management Cybersecurity Case Studies\n\nCustomer profile\n\n### Top 5 Global Mall\n\nGOALS\nVisibility into environment with high number of IoT and OT devices\nTighter oversight of systems managed by third-party vendors\nRESULTS\nFull visibility into core BMS, including ones controlled by vendors\nAutomated asset inventory and consolidated monitoring\nCustomer profile\n\n### **Top 5 Hotel Chain**\n\nGOALS\nMinimize cyber risk\nProtect brand from negative consequences of a cyberattack\nRESULTS\nClear visibility into any IoT, OT or IT devices exposed to cyber threats\nActionable insights to implement mitigation and accelerate response\n[Read All Case Studies][89]\n\n## **Sample Deployment Architecture for Smart Buildings **\n\n[Smart Building Deployment Architecture]\n\n## Related Resources\n\nResource\n\n### Solving Cybersecurity for Building Automation Systems\n\n][90]\nBLOG\n\n### Securing Building Management Systems from Cybersecurity Threats\n\n][91]\nResource\n\n### Securing IoT in an OT World: How to Evaluate and Implement the Right IoT Security Solution for\n### Your Industrial Enterprise\n\n][92]\nBLOG\n\n### Why Gaining Complete Asset Visibility Across OT/IoT Environments Is So Crucial for Cybersecurity\n\n][93]\n\n## Take the next step.\n\nDiscover how easy it is to identify and respond to cyber threats by automating your OT and IoT asset\ndiscovery, inventory, and management.\n\n[Request a Demo][94][Watch Demo][95]\n[View our Privacy Policy][96]\n\n## Subscribe\n\n][97][\n\n## LinkedIn\n\n][98][\n\n## Demo\n\n][99]\n\n### PLATFORM\n\n[Platform Overview][100][Vantage][101][Central Management Console][102][Guardian][103][Guardian\nAir][104][Arc][105][Asset Intelligence][106][Threat Intelligence][107][Smart\nPolling][108][Integrations][109][PSIRT][110]\n\n### Professional Services\n\n[Professional Services][111][Designated Engineer][112][Fast Track Services][113][Health Check\nService][114][Optimization Service][115]\n\n### Solutions: Business needs\n\n[Threat Detection & Response][116][Continuous Network Monitoring][117][Asset Inventory\nManagement][118][Risk & Vulnerability Management][119][IoT Security][120][Data Center\nCybersecurity][121]\n\n### Solutions: Compliance\n\n[DoW ZT for OT][122][ISA/IEC 62443 Standards ][123][NERC CIP][124][NIS2 Directive][125][SEC\nCybersecurity Rules][126][TSA Security Directives][127]\n\n### Solutions: Industry\n\n[Airports][128][Electric Utilities][129][Healthcare][130][Federal\nGovernment][131][Manufacturing][132][Maritime][133][Mining][134][Oil &\nGas][135][Pharmaceutical][136][Rail][137][Retail][138][Smart Cities][139][Water & Wastewater][140]\n\n### Learn\n\n[Academy][141][Careers][142][Company][143][Customer Stories][144][Contact\nUs][145][Partners][146][Resources][147][Labs][148][Legal][149][Trust Center][150]\n[[LinkedIn logo]][151]\n\u00a9 2026 Nozomi Networks Inc. All Rights Reserved. [Privacy Notice][152] and Certifications. [System\nStatus][153].\n\n[1]: https://www.nozominetworks.com/blog/a-note-to-our-customers-and-partners-in-the-middle-east\n[2]: /academy\n[3]: /labs\n[4]: /company/careers\n[5]: https://partners.nozominetworks.com/English/\n[6]: /support\n[7]: /\n[8]: /platform\n[9]: /platform/vantage\n[10]: /platform/central-management-console\n[11]: /platform/guardian\n[12]: /platform/guardian-air\n[13]: /platform/arc\n[14]: /platform/arc-embedded\n[15]: /platform/vantage-iq\n[16]: /platform/asset-intelligence\n[17]: /platform/threat-intelligence\n[18]: /platform/smart-polling\n[19]: /platform/ti-expansion-pack-powered-by-mandiant\n[20]: /technology-alliance-ecosystem\n[21]: /professional-services\n[22]: /solutions/iot-ot-asset-inventory-management\n[23]: /solutions/threat-detection-and-response\n[24]: /solutions/iot-ot-network-monitoring\n[25]: /solutions/iot-ot-vulnerability-management\n[26]: /solutions/ot-risk-management\n[27]: /solutions/iot-security\n[28]: /solutions/data-center-cybersecurity\n[29]: /solutions/building-automation-system-cybersecurity\n[30]: /industries/airport-cybersecurity\n[31]: /industries/electric-utilities-cybersecurity\n[32]: /industries/healthcare-cybersecurity\n[33]: /industries/manufacturing-cybersecurity\n[34]: /industries/maritime-cybersecurity\n[35]: /industries/mining-cybersecurity\n[36]: /industries/oil-gas-cybersecurity\n[37]: /industries/pharmaceutical-cybersecurity\n[38]: /industries/rail-cybersecurity\n[39]: /industries/retail-cybersecurity\n[40]: /industries/smart-cities-cybersecurity\n[41]: /industries/stadiums-arenas\n[42]: /industries/water-wastewater-cybersecurity\n[43]: /industries/federal-government\n[44]: /industries/state-local-government\n[45]: /compliance/dow-zt-for-ot\n[46]: /compliance/isa-iec-62443-standards\n[47]: /compliance/nerc-cip\n[48]: /compliance/nerc-cip-015\n[49]: /compliance/nis2-directive-compliance\n[50]: /compliance/sec-cybersecurity-rules\n[51]: /compliance/tsa-security-directives\n[52]: /partners\n[53]: /partners#our-partners\n[54]: /partners/find-a-partner\n[55]: https://partners.nozominetworks.com/English/\n[56]: /resources\n[57]: /customer-"
