            "text": "A Note to our Customers and Partners in the Middle East\n[More Information][1]\nAcademy\n][2][\nLabs\n][3][\nCareers\n][4][\nPartner Login\n][5][\nSupport\n][6]\n[[Nozomi logo]][7]\nPlatform\n\n### Platform Overview\n\nOur industrial cybersecurity solutions deliver unmatched asset intelligence, threat detection and\nAI-driven insights.\n\nLearn more\n][8]\nMANAGERS\nVantage\nCloud\n][9][\nCentral Management Console\nOn-prem\n][10]\nSENSORS\nGuardian\nNetwork\n][11][\nGuardian Air\nWireless\n][12][\nArc\nEndpoint\n][13][\nArc Embedded\nEndpoint\n][14]\nENHANCEMENTS\nVantage IQ\n][15][\nAsset Intelligence\n][16][\nThreat Intelligence\n][17][\nSmart Polling\n][18][\nTI Expansion Pack\nPowered by Mandiant\n][19][\nIntegrations\n][20]\n\n### Professional Services\n\nOT and IoT security expertise that speeds solution deployment and maximizes value\n\nLearn more\n][21]\nSolutions\nBUSINESS NEED\nAsset Inventory Management\n][22][\nThreat Detection & Response\n][23][\nContinuous Network Monitoring\n][24][\nVulnerability Management\n][25][\nRisk Management\n][26][\nIoT Security\n][27][\nData Center Cybersecurity\n][28][\nBuilding Automation System\nCybersecurity\n][29]\nINDUSTRY\nAirports\n][30][\nElectric Utilities\n][31][\nHealthcare\n][32][\nManufacturing\n][33][\nMaritime\n][34][\nMining\n][35][\nOil & Gas\n][36]\nPharmaceutical\n][37][\nRail\n][38][\nRetail\n][39][\nSmart Cities\n][40][\nStadiums & Arenas\n][41][\nWater &\nWastewater\n][42]\n[Icon of a government building with three columns, a triangular roof, and a blue flag on top.]\nPUBLIC SECTOR\nFederal Government\n][43]\nState & Local\n][44]\nCOMPLIANCE\nDoW ZT for OT\n][45][\nISA/IEC 62443 Standards\n][46][\nNERC CIP\n][47][\nNERC CIP-015\n][48][\nNIS2 Directive\n][49][\nSEC Cybersecurity Rules\n][50][\nTSA Security Directives\n][51]\nPartners\n\n### Why Partner with Us\n\nOur global partner network deploys OT & IoT cybersecurity solutions for customers around the world.\n\nLearn more\n][52]\n\n### Our Partners\n\nExplore all Nozomi Networks partners\n\nLearn more\n][53]\n\n### Find a Partner\n\nFind a certified Nozomi Networks partner in your country.\n\nLearn more\n][54]\n\n### Partner Portal\n\nLog into the Nozomi Networks partner portal.\n\nLog In\n][55]\nResources\n\n### Resource Library\n\nBrowse OT & IoT security research, guides, videos and more from the Nozomi Networks team.\n\nView Resources\n][56]\nRESOURCES\nCase Studies\n][57][\nContent Packs\n][58][\nData Sheets\n][59][\nOT Cyber FAQs\n][60][\nGuides\n][61][\nResearch Reports\n][62]\nSolution Briefs\n][63][\nVideos\n][64][\nWebinars\n][65][\nWhite Papers\n][66][\nTrust Center\n][67]\n\n### Customer Hub\n\nExplore our latest customer resources, including webinars, how-to videos, content packs and more.\n\nView Hub\n][68]\nBlog\n][69]\nCompany\n\n### About Nozomi Networks\n\nWe keep critical infrastructure and operational technology cyber resilient.\n\nLearn more\n][70]\nLeadership Team\n][71][\nEvents\n][72][\nNewsroom\n][73]\nCareers\n][74][\nCustomer Stories\n][75][\nContact Us\n][76]\n[Request Demo][77]\n\n#### SOLUTION\n\n# **Unparalleled OT/ICS Asset Inventory & Visibility**\n\nYou need more than a database or list of IP addresses. You need a complete asset inventory with deep\ninsights into asset behavior and communications \u2014 the starting point for effective anomaly\ndetection, vulnerability management, threat management and ultimately **risk management**.\n\n## **Get Complete Asset Data & Context **\n\nSee how the Nozomi Networks platform automates asset inventory with passive and active monitoring,\nDPI and AI-enhanced detection. (2 min)\n\n[Diagram illustrating asset inventory flow from Data and Context section on the left, linked to Our\nAI Engine section on the right.]\n\nUsing a combination of endpoint-to-air sensors, passive and active data collection, OT/IoT protocol\nsupport and third-party IT asset data, the Nozomi Networks platform provides a complete asset\ninventory \u2014 turbocharged with actionable, AI-powered asset intelligence.\n\n## The Five Pillars of Complete Asset Visibility\n\n**Endpoint-to-Air Sensors**\n\nAll the sensor types you need to efficiently monitor your extended environment\n\n**Data Collection **\n\nActive and passive discovery techniques combined with third-party data ingestion for full coverage\n\n**Actionable Context**\n\nDeep packet inspection (DPI) and comprehensive OT, IoT and IT protocol fluency to understand asset\nbehavior\n\n**Behavioral Baselining**\n\nAI-powered anomaly detection that monitors behavior for deviations from baselines and thresholds\n\n**Asset Intelligence**\n\nAn AI engine that learns from millions of global assets, raising inventory accuracy across our\ncustomer base\n\n## Unmatched Sensor Variety for Complete Asset and Network Visibility\n\n[Network sensors][78] and remote collectors that passively collect, analyze and visualize network\ndata for continuous monitoring and threat and anomaly detection\n[Wireless sensors][79] to detect not just Wi-Fi and Bluetooth but Zigbee, LoRaWAN, Drone RF and\nother wireless protocols frequently used in OT/IoT environments\n[Endpoint sensors][80] for Windows, Linux and MacOS endpoints that are lightweight, non-disruptive\nand understand OT/IoT protocols\n[Endpoint embedded sensors][81] that provide unprecedented visibility into the PLCs and the field\nassets they control, all the way down to Purdue Level 0\n\n## **Industry-Leading Collection Methodologies**\n\nRelying on [passive discovery techniques alone][82] isn\u2019t enough to keep up with the increasing\nsophistication and frequency of industrial threats. Nozomi Networks combines passive and active\ndiscovery techniques with a growing library of third-party connectors to cover your OT, IoT and IT\ndevices.\n\nPassive discovery through our workhorse [**network sensors**][83]**,** long the standard for OT/ICS\nasset discovery where active scanning and probing techniques may be inappropriate\n\nPassive discovery through low-resource [**remote collectors**][84], designed to cover hard-to-reach\nand unmanned locations where a network sensor isn\u2019t cost efficient of practical\n\n**Active querying** via [Smart Polling][85] to non-invasively gather detailed information not\navailable from passive sensors, such as for embedded and non-communicating devices\n\n**Third-party connectors** that ingest asset data stored in Microsoft Active Directory, Microsoft\nDefender, Cisco routers and switches, CrowdStrike, ServiceNow and other leading IT security\nsolutions\n\n## The Asset Details and Context SOC Teams Need to Act\n\nA combination of DPI, comprehensive protocol coverage and behavior analysis ensures we don\u2019t just\ndiscover assets \u2014 we *understand* them.\n\n**Deep Packet Inspection**\nOur passive sensors use DPI to automatically discover network components, connections and topology.\nGreater visibility into process variables and flows is essential for early anomaly detection.\n\n**Protocol\nCoverage\n\u200d**Our platform understands [hundreds of OT, IoT and IT protocols][86], from common to obscure. Using\nour protocol software development kit (SDK), we can quickly create new protocol support on demand.\n\n**Asset\nBehavior\n\u200d**Even enriched device profiles are incomplete without analyzing network traffic and asset-to-asset\ncommunications, key indicators for flagging potential issues in your environment.\n\n## AI-Powered Behavior Baselining for Anomaly Detection\n\nAI and machine learning are essential for baselining asset behavior \u2014 a key part of asset profiles \u2014\nand detecting anomalies.\n\n### **Learning Mode**\n\nUpon deployment, the platform begins monitoring device communications in \u201clearning\u201d mode, down to\nprocess-level variables.\n\n### **Behavior Baselining**\n\nUsing AI, it creates detailed profiles of expected behavior for every device at each stage in a\nprocess to establish a baseline of \u201cnormal\u201d behavior.\n\n### **Protection Mode**\n\nWhen switched to \u201cprotection\u201d mode, the platform uses behavior analytics to monitor and alert on\nsuspicious events that deviate from baselines.\n\n### **Alert Filtering**\n\nBenign anomalous activity below established thresholds is filtered out to reduce false positives.\n\n## **AI Enrichment from Asset Intelligence**\n\nThe Nozomi Networks AI engine learns from millions of assets that we monitor in customer\nenvironments across industries around the globe. This data trove is used to fill in gaps about\nidentical devices across environments.\n\nAI-powered [asset intelligence][87] provides the context and insights needed at the asset, zone and\nsite level to reduce alerts, prioritize actions and track risk reduction over time.\n\n[[Details of Axis P3245-LVE-3 License Plate Verifier camera showing image of white fixed dome\ncamera, specifications including HDTV 1080p, Axis OS, IP and MAC addresses, firmware version\n10.12.130, lifecycle marked end of sale with end date 2023-02-28, and support until\n2029-02-28.]][88]\n\n*Information outlined in red is populated from Asset Intelligence matching.*\n\n## Take the next step.\n\nDiscover how easy it is to identify and respond to cyber threats by automating your OT and IoT asset\ndiscovery, inventory, and management.\n\n[Request a Demo][89][Watch Demo][90]\n[View our Privacy Policy][91]\n\n## Subscribe\n\n][92][\n\n## LinkedIn\n\n][93][\n\n## Demo\n\n][94]\n\n### PLATFORM\n\n[Platform Overview][95][Vantage][96][Central Management Console][97][Guardian][98][Guardian\nAir][99][Arc][100][Asset Intelligence][101][Threat Intelligence][102][Smart\nPolling][103][Integrations][104][PSIRT][105]\n\n### Professional Services\n\n[Professional Services][106][Designated Engineer][107][Fast Track Services][108][Health Check\nService][109][Optimization Service][110]\n\n### Solutions: Business needs\n\n[Threat Detection & Response][111][Continuous Network Monitoring][112][Asset Inventory\nManagement][113][Risk & Vulnerability Management][114][IoT Security][115][Data Center\nCybersecurity][116]\n\n### Solutions: Compliance\n\n[DoW ZT for OT][117][ISA/IEC 62443 Standards ][118][NERC CIP][119][NIS2 Directive][120][SEC\nCybersecurity Rules][121][TSA Security Directives][122]\n\n### Solutions: Industry\n\n[Airports][123][Electric Utilities][124][Healthcare][125][Federal\nGovernment][126][Manufacturing][127][Maritime][128][Mining][129][Oil &\nGas][130][Pharmaceutical][131][Rail][132][Retail][133][Smart Cities][134][Water & Wastewater][135]\n\n### Learn\n\n[Academy][136][Careers][137][Company][138][Customer Stories][139][Contact\nUs][140][Partners][141][Resources][142][Labs][143][Legal][144][Trust Center][145]\n[[LinkedIn logo]][146]\n\u00a9 2026 Nozomi Networks Inc. All Rights Reserved. [Privacy Notice][147] and Certifications. [System\nStatus][148].\n\n[1]: https://www.nozominetworks.com/blog/a-note-to-our-customers-and-partners-in-the-middle-east\n[2]: /academy\n[3]: /labs\n[4]: /company/careers\n[5]: https://partners.nozominetworks.com/English/\n[6]: /support\n[7]: /\n[8]: /platform\n[9]: /platform/vantage\n[10]: /platform/central-management-console\n[11]: /platform/guardian\n[12]: /platform/guardian-air\n[13]: /platform/arc\n[14]: /platform/arc-embedded\n[15]: /platform/vantage-iq\n[16]: /platform/asset-intelligence\n[17]: /platform/threat-intelligence\n[18]: /platform/smart-polling\n[19]: /platform/ti-expansion-pack-powered-by-mandiant\n[20]: /technology-alliance-ecosystem\n[21]: /professional-services\n[22]: /solutions/iot-ot-asset-inventory-management\n[23]: /solutions/threat-detection-and-response\n[24]: /solutions/iot-ot-network-monitoring\n[25]: /solutions/iot-ot-vulnerability-management\n[26]: /solutions/ot-risk-management\n[27]: /solutions/iot-security\n[28]: /solutions/data-center-cybersecurity\n[29]: /solutions/building-automation-system-cybersecurity\n[30]: /industries/airport-cybersecurity\n[31]: /industries/electric-utilities-cybersecurity\n[32]: /industries/healthcare-cybersecurity\n[33]: /industries/manufacturing-cybersecurity\n[34]: /industries/maritime-cybersecurity\n[35]: /industries/mining-cybersecurity\n[36]: /industries/oil-gas-cybersecurity\n[37]: /industries/pharmaceutical-cybersecurity\n[38]: /industries/rail-cybersecurity\n[39]: /industries/retail-cybersecurity\n[40]: /industries/smart-cities-cybersecurity\n[41]: /industries/stadiums-arenas\n[42]: /industries/water-wastewater-cybersecurity\n[43]: /industries/federal-government\n[44]: /industries/state-local-government\n[45]: "
