        "crawl_text": "[Skip to main content][1]\n[U.S. flag]\n\nAn official website of the United States government\n\nHere\u2019s how you know\n\nHere\u2019s how you know\n[Dot gov]\n\n**Official websites use .gov**\nA **.gov** website belongs to an official government organization in the United States.\n\n[HTTPS]\n\n**Secure .gov websites use HTTPS**\nA **lock** ([Lock]) or **https://** means you\u2019ve safely connected to the .gov website. Share\nsensitive information only on official, secure websites.\n\n[\n[Freedom 250 icon]\n\nCountdown to America's 250th Anniversary!\n\n2026-07-04\n** 0 ** Days\n** 0 ** Hours\n** 0 ** Minutes\n][2]\n\n[Staying Secure at Events][3][no-cost Cyber Services][4][Secure by design\u00a0][5][Secure Your\nBusiness][6][Report A Cyber Issue][7]\u00a0\n\n[[Cybersecurity & Infrastructure Security Agency logo America\u2019s Cyber Security Defense Agency\nNational Coordinator For Critical Infrastructure Security and Resilience][Cybersecurity &\nInfrastructure Security Agency logo America\u2019s Cyber Security Defense Agency National Coordinator For\nCritical Infrastructure Security and Resilience]][8]\n[[CISA Logo]][9]\n\nSearch\n\nMenu\n[America's Cyber Defense Agency]\nClose\n\u00a0\n* Topics\n  [Topics][10]\n  [ Cybersecurity Best Practices ][11]\n  [ Cyber Threats and Response ][12]\n  [ Critical Infrastructure Security and Resilience ][13]\n  [ Election Security ][14]\n  [ Emergency Communications ][15]\n  [ Industrial Control Systems ][16]\n  [ Information and Communications Technology Supply Chain Security ][17]\n  [ Partnerships and Collaboration ][18]\n  [ Physical Security ][19]\n  [ Risk Management ][20]\n  [ How can we help? ][21]\n  [Government][22][Educational Institutions][23][Industry][24][State, Local, Tribal, and\n  Territorial][25][Individuals and Families][26][Small and Medium Businesses][27][Find Help\n  Locally][28][Faith-Based Community][29][Executives][30][High-Risk Communities][31]\n* [ Spotlight ][32]\n* Resources & Tools\n  [Resources & Tools][33]\n  [ All Resources & Tools ][34]\n  [ Services ][35]\n  [ Programs ][36]\n  [ Resources ][37]\n  [ Training ][38]\n  [ Groups ][39]\n* News & Events\n  [News & Events][40]\n  [ Directives ][41]\n  [ News ][42]\n  [ Events ][43]\n  [ Cybersecurity Alerts & Advisories ][44]\n  [ Request a CISA Speaker ][45]\n  [ Congressional Testimony ][46]\n  [ CISA Conferences ][47]\n  [ CISA Live! ][48]\n* Careers\n  [Careers][49]\n  [ Benefits & Perks ][50]\n  [ Hiring and Recruitment ][51]\n  [ New Employee Orientation & Onboarding ][52]\n  [ Students & Recent Graduates ][53]\n  [ Veteran and Military Spouses ][54]\n* About\n  [About][55]\n  [ Divisions & Offices ][56]\n  [ Regions ][57]\n  [ Leadership ][58]\n  [ Doing Business with CISA ][59]\n  [ Site Links ][60]\n  [ CISA GitHub ][61]\n  [ CISA Central ][62]\n  [ Contact Us ][63]\n  [ Subscribe ][64]\n  [ Transparency and Accountability ][65]\n  [ Policies & Plans ][66]\n\n[Staying Secure at Events][67][no-cost Cyber Services][68][Secure by design\u00a0][69][Secure Your\nBusiness][70][Report A Cyber Issue][71]\u00a0\n\nBreadcrumb\n1. Home\nShare:\n[Public Service Announcement: Russian Intelligence Services Continue to Target Commercial Messaging\nApplications]\n\n### Russian Intelligence Services Continue to Target Commercial Messaging Applications\n\nCISA and the FBI issue updated public service announcement on phishing campaigns targeting\ncommercial messaging apps.\n\n[Learn More][72]\n[Using SASE in a Modern TIC 3.0 Solution]\n\n### Using Secure Access Service Edge in a Modern TIC 3.0 Solution\n\nThis guidance reinforces the flexibilities available to agencies to meet zero trust objectives and\nadopt modern architectures supported under the Trusted Internet Connections (TIC) 3.0 initiative.\n\n[Read Guidance][73]\n[Now Hiring. Apply Now!]\n\n### We're Hiring\n\nWe have new positions open to help secure our nation's critical infrastructure.\n\n[View Open Positions][74]\n[BOD 26-04: Carousel]\n\n### CISA Issues Binding Operational Directive 26-04: Prioritizing Security Updates Based on Risk\n\nCISA\u2019s new Directive requires federal agencies to rapidly remediate high-risk vulnerabilities,\nprovides flexibility for lower-risk issues, and is supported by comprehensive implementation\nguidance.\n\n[Read the Directive][75]\n[Fact Sheet: CISA and Partners Urge Hardening Automatic Tank Gauge Systems]\n\n### CISA and Partners Release Fact Sheet on Securing Automatic Tank Gauge Systems\n\nCyber threat actors are\u00a0compromising\u00a0internet-exposed\u00a0automatic\u00a0tank gauge systems in\u00a0U.S.\u00a0critical\ninfrastructure\u00a0and\u00a0modifying\u00a0them through command execution.\u00a0This fact sheet\u00a0outlines\u00a0TTPs,\nhighlights risks, and\u00a0provides immediate mitigations.\n\n[Learn More][76]\n[Alert]\n\n### CISA Issues Alert on Software Supply Chain Intrusions Targeting Developer Ecosystems\n\nSupply chain compromises are targeting developer environments, including GitHub and Nx Console.\nThreat actors are abusing enterprise, cloud, and DevOps tools to gain unauthorized access and\nexfiltrate sensitive data.\n\n[Read the Alert][77]\nPreviousNext\n\n## News Updates\n\nJun 24, 2026\nPress Release\n\n### [New CISA Guide Assists Federal Agencies with Tra [Skip to main content][1]\n[U.S. flag]\n\nAn official website of the United States government\n\nHere\u2019s how you know\n\nHere\u2019s how you know\n[Dot gov]\n\n**Official websites use .gov**\nA **.gov** website belongs to an official government organization in the United States.\n\n[HTTPS]\n\n**Secure .gov websites use HTTPS**\nA **lock** ([Lock]) or **https://** means you\u2019ve safely connected to the .gov website. Share\nsensitive information only on official, secure websites.\n\n[\n[Freedom 250 icon]\n\nCountdown to America's 250th Anniversary!\n\n2026-07-04\n** 0 ** Days\n** 0 ** Hours\n** 0 ** Minutes\n][2]\n\n[Staying Secure at Events][3][no-cost Cyber Services][4][Secure by design\u00a0][5][Secure Your\nBusiness][6][Report A Cyber Issue][7]\u00a0\n\n[[Cybersecurity & Infrastructure Security Agency logo America\u2019s Cyber Security Defense Agency\nNational Coordinator For Critical Infrastructure Security and Resilience][Cybersecurity &\nInfrastructure Security Agency logo America\u2019s Cyber Security Defense Agency National Coordinator For\nCritical Infrastructure Security and Resilience]][8]\n[[CISA Logo]][9]\n\nSearch\n\nMenu\n[America's Cyber Defense Agency]\nClose\n\u00a0\n* Topics\n  [Topics][10]\n  [ Cybersecurity Best Practices ][11]\n  [ Cyber Threats and Response ][12]\n  [ Critical Infrastructure Security and Resilience ][13]\n  [ Election Security ][14]\n  [ Emergency Communications ][15]\n  [ Industrial Control Systems ][16]\n  [ Information and Communications Technology Supply Chain Security ][17]\n  [ Partnerships and Collaboration ][18]\n  [ Physical Security ][19]\n  [ Risk Management ][20]\n  [ How can we help? ][21]\n  [Government][22][Educational Institutions][23][Industry][24][State, Local, Tribal, and\n  Territorial][25][Individuals and Families][26][Small and Medium Businesses][27][Find Help\n  Locally][28][Faith-Based Community][29][Executives][30][High-Risk Communities][31]\n* [ Spotlight ][32]\n* Resources & Tools\n  [Resources & Tools][33]\n  [ All Resources & Tools ][34]\n  [ Services ][35]\n  [ Programs ][36]\n  [ Resources ][37]\n  [ Training ][38]\n  [ Groups ][39]\n* News & Events\n  [News & Events][40]\n  [ Directives ][41]\n  [ News ][42]\n  [ Events ][43]\n  [ Cybersecurity Alerts & Advisories ][44]\n  [ Request a CISA Speaker ][45]\n  [ Congressional Testimony ][46]\n  [ CISA Conferences ][47]\n  [ CISA Live! ][48]\n* Careers\n  [Careers][49]\n  [ Benefits & Perks ][50]\n  [ Hiring and Recruitment ][51]\n  [ New Employee Orientation & Onboarding ][52]\n  [ Students & Recent Graduates ][53]\n  [ Veteran and Military Spouses ][54]\n* About\n  [About][55]\n  [ Divisions & Offices ][56]\n  [ Regions