            "text": "[Skip to content][1]\n\n[Careers][2] [Contact][3]\n\n[Careers][4] [Contact][5]\n\n[Carri\u00e8res][6] [Contact][7]\n\n[Karriere][8] [Kontakte][9]\n\n[Careers][10] [Contact][11]\n\n[Urat][12] [Yhteystiedot][13]\n\n[Carri\u00e8res][14] [Contact][15]\n\n[Karriere][16] [Kontakt][17]\n\n[Careers][18] [Contact][19]\n\n[Careers][20] [Contact][21]\n\n[Karriere][22] [Kontakt][23]\n\n[Kariera][24] [Kontakt][25]\n\n[Cariere][26] [Contact][27]\n\n[Carreras][28] [Contacto][29]\n\n[Karri\u00e4rer][30] [Kontakta][31]\n\n[Karriere][32] [Kontakt][33]\n\n[Careers][34] [Contact][35]\n\n[Carreras][36] [Contacto][37]\n\n[Carreiras][38] [Contato][39]\n\n[Carreras][40] [Contacto][41]\n\n[Carreras][42] [Contacto][43]\n\n[Carreras][44] [Contacto][45]\n\n[Carreras][46] [Contacto][47]\n\n[Carreras][48] [Contacto][49]\n\n[Carreras][50] [Contacto][51]\n\n[Careers][52] [Contact][53]\n\n[\u0627\u0644\u0648\u0638\u0627\u0626\u0641][54] [\u0627\u062a\u0635\u0627\u0644][55]\n\n[Careers][56] [Contact][57]\n\n[Careers][58] [Contact][59]\n\n[Careers][60] [Contact][61]\n\n[\u0e2d\u0e32\u0e0a\u0e35\u0e1e][62] [\u0e15\u0e34\u0e14\u0e15\u0e48\u0e2d][63]\n\n[\u8077\u6daf\u767c\u5c55][64] [\u63a5\u89f8][65]\n\n[Careers][66] [Contact][67]\n\n[Careers][68] [Contact][69]\n\n[S\u1ef1 nghi\u1ec7p][70] [Li\u00ean h\u1ec7][71]\n\n[Karier][72] [Kontak][73]\n\n[Kerjaya][74] [Kenalan][75]\n\n[Mga Karera][76] [Makipag-ugnayan][77]\n\n[\u30ad\u30e3\u30ea\u30a2][78] [\u63a5\u89e6][79]\n\n[\uacbd\ub825][80] [\uc5f0\ub77d\ud558\ub2e4][81]\n\n[Careers][82] [Contact][83]\n\n[ Home[convergint logo]][84]\n][85]\n* [Who we are][86]\n* [History][87]\n* Leadership\n* [Executive Leadership][88]\n* [Board of Managers][89]\n* [Culture Committee][90]\n* [Company news][91]\n* [Why we do it][92]\n* [Social responsibility][93]\n* [Step Up for Schools][94]\n* [Sustainability][95]\n* [Acquisitions][96]\n* [What we do][97]\n* [Systems][98]\n* [Access Control][99]\n* [Video Surveillance][100]\n* [Intrusion Detection Systems][101]\n* [Fire & Life Safety Systems][102]\n* [Communications][103]\n* [Advanced Threat Detection][104]\n* [Security Operations Centers][105]\n* [Physical Security][106]\n* [Services][107]\n* [Consulting & Advisory][108]\n* [Assessments & Site Surveys][109]\n* [Engineering & Estimating][110]\n* [Installation & Integration][111]\n* [Project & Program Management][112]\n* [Professional Services][113]\n* [Remote Services][114]\n* [Maintenance][115]\n* [Who we serve][116]\n* [Industries][117]\n* [Aviation / Transportation][118]\n* [Data Centers][119]\n* [Government / Public Sector][120]\n* [Critical Infrastructure][121]\n* [Utilities][122]\n* [Medical / Hospital / Healthcare][123]\n* [Biopharmaceutical / Laboratory / Research][124]\n* [Education][125]\n* [Financial Institutions][126]\n* [Corporate Enterprise][127]\n* [Real Estate][128]\n* [Hospitality / Entertainment][129]\n* [Manufacturing][130]\n* [Retail][131]\n* [Customer stories][132]\n* [How we do it][133]\n* [Our approach][134]\n* [Technology partners][135]\n* [Our perspective][136]\n* [Where we operate][137]\n* [U.S. Locations][138]\n* [North America][139]\n* [Latin America][140]\n* [Europe][141]\n* [Middle East / Africa][142]\n* [Asia Pacific][143]\n\n# Executive Leadership.\n\nAt Convergint, our leaders share a common purpose: to be our customers\u2019 best service provider.\nGrounded in our Values & Beliefs and driven by a strong, service-oriented culture, this team of\nexecutives brings decades of experience and a shared commitment to guiding colleagues and customers\nwith integrity, care, and vision.\n\n[Ann Fandozzi]\n\n## Ann Fandozzi\n\nChief Executive Officer\n\nAnn Fandozzi joined Convergint as Chief Executive Officer in February 2024. This is her fourth CEO\nrole, having previously served as CEO for RB Global, Abra Auto Body & Glass, and vRide\u2014leading these\ncompanies through unprecedented transformation and growth. Prior to these roles, Ann held senior\nleadership positions at Whirlpool, DaimlerChrysler, Ford Motor Company, and Lockheed Martin. She\nholds a B.S. degree in Computer Engineering from Stevens Institute of Technology, an M.S. degree in\nSystems Engineering from the University of Pennsylvania, and an MBA from The Wharton School of the\nUniversity of Pennsylvania.\n\n[ ][144]\n\n[Sean Flint]\n\n## Sean Flint\n\nPresident\n\nSean Flint has over 30 years of leadership and industry experience. He joined Convergint as Senior\nVice President, Eastern Region in May of 2016. Sean served in leadership roles with Tyco/Simplex\nGrinnell from 1993 to 2010, where he rose to become Vice President of Western Operations. From 2010\nto 2012, Sean served as the President of UTC Fire & Security, a $550 million fire safety and\nsecurity integration business. His ability to lead teams and grow customer relationships is key to\nthe continual growth of Convergint\u2019s national and global customer relationships.\n\n[ ][145]\n\n[Kevin Geisner]\n\n## Kevin Geisner\n\nChief Strategy Officer\n\nKevin Geisner joined Convergint in 2024 as Chief Strategy Officer. He brings 25 years of corporate\nstrategy and business growth experience, including CSO roles at RB Global and ABRA, as well as roles\nwith Amazon, Microsoft, and McKinsey & Co. For the first decade of his career, Kevin was an engineer\nwith General Electric and Lockheed Martin, working on radar and missile defense systems. Kevin has\nhis Professional Engineer\u2019s license, and holds M.S. degrees in Electrophysics and Engineering\nManagement from Drexel University and an M.B.A. from Harvard Business School.\n\n[ ][146]\n\n[Eric Jacobs]\n\n## Eric Jacobs\n\nChief Financial Officer\n\nEric Jacobs joined Convergint in 2024 as its Chief Financial Officer. He formerly served as the CFO\nof RB Global and Wheels Up Experience Inc., where he played pivotal roles in strategic growth\ninitiatives. Prior to his CFO roles, Jacobs held various senior positions at Cox Automotive, Inc.\nand Dealertrack Technologies, Inc. Before transitioning to business leadership roles, he practiced\ncorporate law at O\u2019Melveny & Myers LLP and worked as an audit manager at KPMG LLP. Eric holds a J.D.\nfrom Rutgers School of Law-Newark and a Bachelor of Science in Business Administration from Rider\nUniversity.\n\n[ ][147]\n\n[David Liebman headshot]\n\n## David Liebman\n\nChief Legal and Human Resources Officer\n\nDavid Liebman serves as Convergint\u2019s Chief Legal and Human Resources Officer. He is a seasoned\nleader with extensive experience in human resources, corporate law, government investigations,\nemployment law, mergers and acquisitions, and global operations. David previously served as Chief\nLegal Officer and Global Head of Administration at Frank Recruitment Group, where he led legal and\nadministrative functions across international markets. He also served as General Counsel at vRide,\noverseeing legal and compliance through its acquisition by Enterprise Rent-A-Car. Earlier in his\ncareer, David held roles as Assistant General Counsel at Bimbo Bakeries and as a Senior Associate in\nthe M&A group at Cozen O\u2019Connor. He graduated cum laude from Temple University\u2019s James Beasley\nSchool of Law and Fox School of Business.\n\n[ ][148]\n\n[Mike Mathes headshot]\n\n## Mike Mathes\n\nExecutive Vice President, Western Operations\n\nMike Mathes is currently Executive Vice President, Western Operations for Convergint. One of\nConvergint\u2019s founding members, he opened the Los Angeles and San Francisco locations for Convergint\nin 2002 and 2003. In his current role, he is responsible for the support and development of the\nWestern United States. Prior to Convergint, Mike held several positions at Johnson Controls over a\n15-year career. He holds a B.Sc.E.E. from the University of Manitoba in Canada.\n\n[ ][149]\n\n[Chris McCurdy headshot]\n\n## Chris McCurdy\n\nChief Commercial Officer\n\nChris McCurdy has more than 28 years in the IT consulting industry, specializing in information\nsecurity and advisory Services. Prior to joining Convergint, he held leadership roles at several\nconsulting firms\u2014including IBM, Andersen, International Network Services, and Lucent\nTechnologies\u2014and he has extensive experience working with large global enterprises, as well as\ngovernment clients around the world. Chris also served as a CIO at a retail automotive group, where\nhe led an expansion of business operations via the use of technology and acquisition. He is\ncurrently the Senior Vice President of Global Accounts at Convergint.\n\n[ ][150]\n\n[Julie Roehm headshot]\n\n## Julie Roehm\n\nChief Marketing Officer\n\nJulie Roehm, who serves as Convergint\u2019s Chief Marketing Officer, is an innovative customer-centric\nexperience, marketing, and B2B/B2C digital and operations transformation executive for public and\nprivate companies. She strategizes profitable corporate turnarounds with fast revenue growth by\nengaging potential/existing customers with stories supported by technology that positively reinvents\nthe customer journey. Julie is known for her hyper-focus on the customer. She was recently named a\n\u201c2023 Top 50 Marketer\u201d award winner by ONCON ICON, for her global digital marketing achievements.\nHer BS in Environmental Engineering from Purdue University combined with an MBA in Marketing from\nThe University of Chicago Booth fuels her metrics-driven, performance oriented business approach.\n\n[ ][151]\n\n[Kevin Sheridan]\n\n## Kevin Sheridan\n\nSVP, Vertical Markets & Central Operations\n\nKevin Sheridan is Senior Vice President, Vertical Markets & Central Region at Convergint, where he\nleads strategic growth and industry-focused solutions across key sectors of the business. Since\njoining Convergint in 2017, Kevin has played a pivotal role in strengthening the organization\u2019s\nleadership position across vertical markets, with particular depth in financial services. He has\nbeen instrumental in integrating acquisitions, scaling high-performing teams, and aligning\noperational execution with industry-specific customer needs. His leadership has helped elevate\nperformance, consistency, and growth across Convergint\u2019s vertical market strategy. Known for his\ninnovative thinking and growth mindset, Kevin brings a strong focus on operational excellence,\ncollaboration, and customer outcomes. He works closely with enterprise leadership and serves as a\nmember of Convergint\u2019s Central Division Leadership Team, helping guide strategy across some of the\ncompany\u2019s most established and high-performing regions.\n\n[ ][152]\n\n[Eric Yunag headshot]\n\n## Eric Yunag\n\nExecutive Vice President, Products and Services\n\nEric Yunag serves as EVP of Product and Services at Convergint, bringing more than 25 years of\ndedicated leadership experience in the security integration industry. He joined Convergint in 2016\nthrough the acquisition of his company, where he served as CEO. Since that time, Eric has held\nleadership roles across key strategic areas including Mergers & Acquisitions, Marketing, Innovation,\nand Technology. In his current role, he is responsible for evaluating the impact of industry trends\non customer requirements and developing strategic technology partnerships and comprehensive solution\nofferings. Throughout his career, Eric has demonstrated a proven ability to lead diverse functions\nwithin the industry, including operations, business development, and technology, contributing to\nboth organizational growth and industry advancement.\n\n[ ][153]\n\n### Other leadership.\n\n#### Board of Managers.\n\nOur Board of Managers plays a vital role in shaping a customer focused, people-first strategy. Their\nleadership reinforces our culture of service, ensuring that every decision supports stronger\npartnerships, long-term stakeholder value, and meaningful outcomes for those we serve.\n\n[Learn more][154]\n\n#### Culture Committee.\n\nThe committee has a single, clear charter: to ensure that the values and beliefs that have defined\nus over the past decades, and that we hold so close to our hearts, continue to guide us well into\nthe future. This is about honoring our legacy while building something enduring.\n\n[Learn more][155]\n\n[[Convergint Logo]][156]\n\n**Explore**\n\n[Who we are][157]\n[What we do][158]\n[Who we serve][159]\n[How we do it][160]\n[Where we operate][161]\n\n[ ][162] [ ][163] [ ][164] [ ][165] [ ][166]\n\n[Careers][167]\n[Contact][168]\n[Locations][169]\n\n[News & Insights][170]\n[Our Values & Beliefs][171]\n\n[iCare Standard Customer Portal][172]\n[iCare Federal Customer Portal][173]\n[Pay Your Invoice][174]\n\n[Terms of Use][175]\n[Privacy][176]\n[C"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://www.convergint.com/who-we-are/acquisitions/",
            "text": "[Skip to content][1]\n\n[Careers][2] [Contact][3]\n\n[Careers][4] [Contact][5]\n\n[Carri\u00e8res][6] [Contact][7]\n\n[Karriere][8] [Kontakte][9]\n\n[Careers][10] [Contact][11]\n\n[Urat][12] [Yhteystiedot][13]\n\n[Carri\u00e8res][14] [Contact][15]\n\n[Karriere][16] [Kontakt][17]\n\n[Careers][18] [Contact][19]\n\n[Careers][20] [Contact][21]\n\n[Karriere][22] [Kontakt][23]\n\n[Kariera][24] [Kontakt][25]\n\n[Cariere][26] [Contact][27]\n\n[Carreras][28] [Contacto][29]\n\n[Karri\u00e4rer][30] [Kontakta][31]\n\n[Karriere][32] [Kontakt][33]\n\n[Careers][34] [Contact][35]\n\n[Carreras][36] [Contacto][37]\n\n[Carreiras][38] [Contato][39]\n\n[Carreras][40] [Contacto][41]\n\n[Carreras][42] [Contacto][43]\n\n[Carreras][44] [Contacto][45]\n\n[Carreras][46] [Contacto][47]\n\n[Carreras][48] [Contacto][49]\n\n[Carreras][50] [Contacto][51]\n\n[Careers][52] [Contact][53]\n\n[\u0627\u0644\u0648\u0638\u0627\u0626\u0641][54] [\u0627\u062a\u0635\u0627\u0644][55]\n\n[Careers][56] [Contact][57]\n\n[Careers][58] [Contact][59]\n\n[Careers][60] [Contact][61]\n\n[\u0e2d\u0e32\u0e0a\u0e35\u0e1e][62] [\u0e15\u0e34\u0e14\u0e15\u0e48\u0e2d][63]\n\n[\u8077\u6daf\u767c\u5c55][64] [\u63a5\u89f8][65]\n\n[Careers][66] [Contact][67]\n\n[Careers][68] [Contact][69]\n\n[S\u1ef1 nghi\u1ec7p][70] [Li\u00ean h\u1ec7][71]\n\n[Karier][72] [Kontak][73]\n\n[Kerjaya][74] [Kenalan][75]\n\n[Mga Karera][76] [Makipag-ugnayan][77]\n\n[\u30ad\u30e3\u30ea\u30a2][78] [\u63a5\u89e6][79]\n\n[\uacbd\ub825][80] [\uc5f0\ub77d\ud558\ub2e4][81]\n\n[Careers][82] [Contact][83]\n\n[ Home[convergint logo]][84]\n][85]\n* [Who we are][86]\n* [History][87]\n* Leadership\n* [Executive Leadership][88]\n* [Board of Managers][89]\n* [Culture Committee][90]\n* [Company news][91]\n* [Why we do it][92]\n* [Social responsibility][93]\n* [Step Up for Schools][94]\n* [Sustainability][95]\n* [Acquisitions][96]\n* [What we do][97]\n* [Systems][98]\n* [Access Control][99]\n* [Video Surveillance][100]\n* [Intrusion Detection Systems][101]\n* [Fire & Life Safety Systems][102]\n* [Communications][103]\n* [Advanced Threat Detection][104]\n* [Security Operations Centers][105]\n* [Physical Security][106]\n* [Services][107]\n* [Consulting & Advisory][108]\n* [Assessments & Site Surveys][109]\n* [Engineering & Estimating][110]\n* [Installation & Integration][111]\n* [Project & Program Management][112]\n* [Professional Services][113]\n* [Remote Services][114]\n* [Maintenance][115]\n* [Who we serve][116]\n* [Industries][117]\n* [Aviation / Transportation][118]\n* [Data Centers][119]\n* [Government / Public Sector][120]\n* [Critical Infrastructure][121]\n* [Utilities][122]\n* [Medical / Hospital / Healthcare][123]\n* [Biopharmaceutical / Laboratory / Research][124]\n* [Education][125]\n* [Financial Institutions][126]\n* [Corporate Enterprise][127]\n* [Real Estate][128]\n* [Hospitality / Entertainment][129]\n* [Manufacturing][130]\n* [Retail][131]\n* [Customer stories][132]\n* [How we do it][133]\n* [Our approach][134]\n* [Technology partners][135]\n* [Our perspective][136]\n* [Where we operate][137]\n* [U.S. Locations][138]\n* [North America][139]\n* [Latin America][140]\n* [Europe][141]\n* [Middle East / Africa][142]\n* [Asia Pacific][143]\n\n# Build what\u2019s next, together.\n\n##### We don\u2019t just acquire companies, we build enduring partnerships.\n\nAcquisition is the start of a long-term relationship. Most of the leaders and colleagues from the\ncompanies we\u2019ve acquired still grow with Convergint today. We show respect, transparency, and\nfairness at every stage.\n\n[Let\u2019s start the conversation][144]\n\n### Why companies choose Convergint.\n\n## Growth isn\u2019t about scale alone, it\u2019s about elevating service, culture, and impact together.\n\nAt Convergint, our acquisitions aim to:\n* Deepen local proximity to customers\n* Expand technical and vertical expertise\n* Enrich our team by attracting and retaining top talent\n\nConvergint\u2019s rapid growth has been fueled by an extensive acquisition strategy and a long history of\nsuccessful integrations across North America and around the world.\n\n### A track record that speaks for itself.\n\n## Cultural compatibility is our most important acquisition criterion.\n\nWe prioritize safety, keep promises to customers and colleagues, and live our Values & Beliefs\ndaily. That\u2019s why so many former owners are still here leading, mentoring, and growing.\n\n### \u201cConvergint has been an amazing platform to accelerate growth\u2026 culture and service as a\n### competitive advantage.\u201d\n\nEric Yunag\nFormer owner, now VP\n\n### \u201cConvergint\u2019s commitment to living its Values & Beliefs every day\u2026 I couldn\u2019t be more excited\n### and proud.\u201d\n\nDan Chastanet\nFormer President/CEO, recently retired\n\n### \u201cJoining Convergint lifted the ceiling\u2026 global market leader\u2026 camaraderie second-to-none.\u201d\n\nDean Monaghan\nFormer owner, now Managing Director\n\n### \u201cDeep technical resources and positive service culture\u2026 accelerators for growth.\u201d\n\nKevin Sheridan\nFormer owner, now SVP, Vertical Markets & Central Operations\n\n### \u201cSelling or merging a company you\u2019ve invested your life in is always a major decision. . .they\n### did everything they said they would, and, more importantly, nothing they said they wouldn\u2019t...\n### Convergint did a terrific job taking care of my team.\u201d\n\nThomas C. Ballou\nFormer owner of Ballou Fire Systems, current Sales Leader\n\n### \u201cThe integration was made possible thanks to a shared set of core values and a professional\n### culture built with patience and passion. I feel fulfilled that together we succeeded in becoming\n### part of the Convergint family while fully preserving our customer portfolio. A dream come true!\u201d\n\nMarius Retegan\nFormer owner of Helinick, recently retired\n\n### \u201cTheir integrity and transparency throughout the process gave me complete confidence. Everything\n### they said they would do; they did. Three years later and I'm still here... not a single\n### colleague left because of the acquisition... Convergint guided us through every step of the\n### transition with a proven playbook that works.\u201d\n\nKeith Simpson\nFormer owner of Simpson Security Systems, current Business Development Manager\n\n### \u201cConvergint allowed us to stay true to what made our company special. . .strengthened what we\n### already did best while honoring the culture, commitment, and people that got us here.\u201d\n\nScott Bartmess\nFormer co-owner of Esscoe, current General Manager\n\n### \u201cJoining Convergint in 2022, as a first acquisition in the Middle East region, has been an\n### absolute game changer. Convergint has been our force multiplier, enabling our accelerated\n### growth, geographic expansion, and graduating colleagues into global roles. The promises made,\n### were promises kept since and throughout.\u201d\n\nSaid Kiwan\nFormer owner of MVP Tech, current Managing Director\n\n### \u201cWhat impressed me most was how open and attentive Convergint\u2019s leadership was to our ideas. . .\n### .the collaboration and access to Convergint\u2019s national clients significantly accelerated our\n### growth.\u201d\n\nMaxime Boivin\nFormer owner of Panavideo, recently retired\n\n### What you can expect.\n\n## We strive to make every stage clear, collaborative, and human-centered.\n\n#### Introduction & mutual exploration.\n\nWe start with conversation, no rigid commitments, just curiosity. If the fit feels right, we proceed\nunder a mutual non-disclosure agreement.\n\n#### Preliminary assessment & shared vision.\n\nWe dive into culture, capabilities, structure, and customer fit to shape a shared vision and\nhigh-level structure.\n\n#### Formal proposal & letter of intent.\n\nWithin approximately three weeks after receiving materials, we aim to align on terms and issue a\nletter of intent.\n\n#### Due diligence & agreement finalization.\n\nOver the next 60\u201390 days, we jointly validate assumptions, refine integration plans, and finalize\nall transaction documents.\n\n#### Closing & integration.\n\nWe close the deal and begin structured integration designed to protect customers, colleagues, and\nlegacy strengths throughout the transition.\n\n### Recent acquisitions.\n\n## We\u2019re proud to welcome new partners who share our commitment to service, culture, and community,\n## each strengthening Convergint\u2019s local expertise and global reach.\n\n[JSC Systems logo]\n\n### JSC Systems\n\nExpanding fire and life safety capabilities throughout the Southeast U.S.\n\n[NUSOURCE LOGO]\n\n### Nusource Financial\n\nExpanding financial services security solutions expertise.\n\n[A+ Technology & Security Logo]\n\n### A+ Technology & Security Solutions\n\nExpanding integrated security expertise across the Northeast.\n\n[Digital Visions Logo]\n\n### Digital Visions\n\nStrengthening service coverage and collaboration in the Midwest.\n\n[Fiber Solutions Logo]\n\n### Fiber Solutions\n\nEnhancing security and AV capabilities throughout the Southeast U.S.\n\n[Delco Security Logo]\n\n### Delco Security\n\nExtending systems integration services across Canada.\n\n[esscoe logo]\n\n### Esscoe\n\nBroadening compliance and enterprise solutions in the Midwest.\n\n[Helinick Logo]\n\n### Helinick\n\nGrowing Convergint\u2019s presence and capabilities across Eastern Europe.\n\n### Let\u2019s talk.\n\n## Considering the next chapter for your business? Convergint partners with organizations that share\n## our service-first values and growth mindset. Connect with our acquisitions team to start a\n## confidential conversation.\n\n[Schedule a conversation][145]\n\n[[Convergint Logo]][146]\n\n**Explore**\n\n[Who we are][147]\n[What we do][148]\n[Who we serve][149]\n[How we do it][150]\n[Where we operate][151]\n\n[ ][152] [ ][153] [ ][154] [ ][155] [ ][156]\n\n[Careers][157]\n[Contact][158]\n[Locations][159]\n\n[News & Insights][160]\n[Our Values & Beliefs][161]\n\n[iCare Standard Customer Portal][162]\n[iCare Federal Customer Portal][163]\n[Pay Your Invoice][164]\n\n[Terms of Use][165]\n[Privacy][166]\n[Cookie Policy][167]\n[Online Reporting][168]\n[Compliance][169]\n[Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information][170]\n\n\u00a9 2026 Convergint Technologies LLC, All Rights Reserved. Convergint\u00ae and the stylized \u2018i\u2019 are\nregistered trademarks of Convergint in the U.S. and abroad.\nOklahoma Alarm Locksmith License #AC1750\n\n[[Convergint Logo]][171]\n\n**Explore**\n\n[Who we are][172]\n[What we do][173]\n[Who we serve][174]\n[How we do it][175]\n[Where we operate][176]\n\n[ ][177] [ ][178] [ ][179] [ ][180] [ ][181]\n\n[Careers][182]\n[Contact][183]\n[Locations][184]\n\n[News & Insights][185]\n[Our Values & Beliefs][186]\n\n[iCare Standard Customer Portal][187]\n[Pay Your Invoice][188]\n\n[Terms of Use][189]\n[Privacy][190]\n[Cookie Policy][191]\n[Online Reporting][192]\n[Compliance][193]\n[Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information][194]\n\n\u00a9 2026 Convergint Technologies LLC, All Rights Reserved. Convergint\u00ae and the stylized \u2018i\u2019 are\nregistered trademarks of Convergint in the U.S. and abroad.\n\n[[Convergint Logo]][195]\n\n**Ontdekken**\n\n[Wie wij zijn][196]\n[Wat wij doen][197]\n[Wie wij bedienen][198]\n[Hoe we het doen][199]\n[Waar wij actief zijn][200]\n\n[ ][201] [ ][202] [ ][203] [ ][204] [ ][205]\n\n[Carri\u00e8res][206]\n[Contact][207]\n[Locaties][208]\n\n[Nieuws en inzichten][209]\n\n[iCare klantenportaal][210]\n[Betaal uw factuur][211]\n\n[Gebruiksvoorwaarden][212]\n[Privacy][213]\n[Cookiebeleid][214]\n[Online rapportage][215]\n[Naleving][216]\n[Verkoop of deel mijn persoonlijke gegevens niet][217]\n\n\u00a9 2026 Convergint Technologies LLC, alle rechten voorbehouden. Convergint\u00ae en de gestileerde 'i'\nzijn geregistreerde handelsmerken van Convergint in de VS en daarbuiten.\n\n[[Convergint Logo]][218]\n\n**Udforske**\n\n[Hve