            "text": "* [Skip to Main Navigation][1]\n* [Skip to Main Content][2]\n* [Skip to Footer][3]\n[ Tenable ][4] [\nPlatform ][5]\nSolutions\nWhy Tenable\nResources\nCompany [\nPricing ][6]\n[ contact_icon ][7]\n[ English ][8] [ Deutsch ][9] [ Fran\u00e7ais (France) ][10] [ Espa\u00f1ol (Am\u00e9rica Latina) ][11] [ Portugu\u00eas\n(Brasil) ][12] [ Italiano ][13]\n[ \u7b80\u4f53\u4e2d\u6587 ][14] [ \u7e41\u9ad4\u4e2d\u6587 ][15] [ \u65e5\u672c\u8a9e ][16] [ \ud55c\uad6d\uc5b4 ][17] [ \u0627\u0644\u0639\u0631\u0628\u064a\u0629 ][18]\n[ Tenable Product Login\n][19] [ Community & Support\n][20]\n[ Buy ][21] [ Try ][22]\n\n#### Exposure Management\n\n][23]\nManage cyber risk with one platform to find, prioritize and eliminate exposures across your attack\nsurface.\n[ Find out more\n][24]\nAI Security ][25] [\nCloud Security ][26] [\nOT Security ][27] [\nVulnerability Management ][28] [\nHexa AI ][29]\nIdentity Security ][30] [\nPatch Management ][31] [\nAttack Surface Management ][32] [\nWeb App Scanning ][33] [\nSecurity Tool Connectors ][34] [ View all products\n][35]\n\n#### Explore By Use Case\n\nSecure AI\n][36] [\nSecure OT/IoT\n][37] [\nExposure Management\n][38] [\nCloud Security\n][39] [\nCompliance\n][40] [\nVulnerability Management\n][41] [\nAsset Inventory\n][42] [\nHighly Secure Environments\n][43] [\nSecure Data Centers\n][44] [\nZero-Trust\n][45]\n\n#### Explore By Industry\n\n[ Financial Services\n][46] [ Energy\n][47] [ Healthcare\n][48] [ Technology\n][49] [ Education\n][50] [ Government Defense\n][51] [ Retail\n][52]\n[ Why choose Tenable\n][53] [ Industry recognition\n][54] [ Customer stories\n][55] [ Tenable vs competitors\n][56]\nReport\n\n###### Tenable is the one clear leader in Exposure Management\n\n[ See why\n][57]\n[ Resource library\n][58] [ Exposure management resources\n][59] [ Blog\n][60] [ Research center\n][61]\n[ Training and certification\n][62] [ Cybersecurity guide\n][63] [ Customer stories\n][64] [ Find a partner\n][65]\nResources\n\n#### Exposure management\n#### resource center\n\n###### Accelerate your exposure management strategy with practical resources and tools.\n\n[ Explore\n][66]\n[ About Tenable\n][67] [ Leadership\n][68] [ Investor relations\n][69] [ Tenable ventures\n][70] [ Awards and recognition\n][71]\n[ Media room\n][72] [ Careers\n][73] [ Engagement and inclusion\n][74] [ Exposure Management Leadership Council\n][75]\nPlatform\nSolutions\nWhy Tenable\nResources\nCompany [\nPricing ][76]\n[ contact_icon ][77]\n[ English ][78] [ Deutsch ][79] [ Fran\u00e7ais (France) ][80] [ Espa\u00f1ol (Am\u00e9rica Latina) ][81] [\nPortugu\u00eas (Brasil) ][82] [ Italiano ][83]\n[ \u7b80\u4f53\u4e2d\u6587 ][84] [ \u7e41\u9ad4\u4e2d\u6587 ][85] [ \u65e5\u672c\u8a9e ][86] [ \ud55c\uad6d\uc5b4 ][87] [ \u0627\u0644\u0639\u0631\u0628\u064a\u0629 ][88]\n[ Tenable Product Login\n][89] [ Community & Support\n][90]\n[ Buy ][91] [ Try ][92]\nPlatform\nExposure Management ][93] [\nAI Security ][94] [\nCloud Security ][95] [\nOT Security ][96] [\nVulnerability Management ][97] [\nHexa AI ][98] [\nIdentity Security ][99] [\nPatch Management ][100] [\nAttack Surface Management ][101] [\nWeb App Scanning ][102] [\nSecurity Tool Connectors ][103] [ View all products\n][104]\nSolutions\n\n#### Explore By Use Case\n\n[ Secure AI\n][105] [ Secure OT/IoT\n][106] [ Exposure Management\n][107] [ Cloud Security\n][108] [ Compliance\n][109] [ Vulnerability Management\n][110] [ Asset Inventory\n][111] [ Highly Secure Environments\n][112] [ Secure Data Centers\n][113] [ Zero-Trust\n][114]\n\n#### Explore By Industry\n\n[ Financial Services\n][115] [ Energy\n][116] [ Healthcare\n][117] [ Technology\n][118] [ Education\n][119] [ Government Defense\n][120] [ Retail\n][121]\nWhy Tenable\n[ Why choose Tenable\n][122] [ Industry recognition\n][123] [ Customer stories\n][124] [ Tenable vs competitors\n][125]\nReport\n\n###### Tenable is the one clear leader in Exposure Management\n\n[ See why\n][126]\nResources\n[ Resource library\n][127] [ Exposure management resources\n][128] [ Blog\n][129] [ Research center\n][130] [ Training and certification\n][131] [ Cybersecurity guide\n][132] [ Customer stories\n][133] [ Find a partner\n][134]\nResources\n\n#### Exposure management\n#### resource center\n\n###### Accelerate your exposure management strategy with practical resources and tools.\n\n[ Explore\n][135]\nCompany\n[ About Tenable\n][136] [ Leadership\n][137] [ Investor relations\n][138] [ Tenable ventures\n][139] [ Awards and recognition\n][140] [ Media room\n][141] [ Careers\n][142] [ Engagement and inclusion\n][143] [ Exposure Management Leadership Council\n][144]\n[ ][145]\n\n# Tenable leadership\n\n### Executive team\n\n[Steve Vintz]\n\n#### Steve Vintz\n\n###### Co-chief executive officer\n\nSteve Vintz is an accomplished executive with more than 25 years of financial, operational and\nstrategic planning experience working with growth companies in the technology industry. As Tenable\u2019s\nco-chief executive officer (CEO) he oversees product, cybersecurity, corporate development and all\ngeneral and administrative functions. In 2015, Steve led Tenable through its Series B funding round\nwhich was, at the time, the largest capital raise for a private cybersecurity company. He then led\nthe company\u2019s initial public offering in 2018, which was one of the largest raises for a U.S.-listed\nsecurity company. Previously, from 2001 until its sale in June 2014, Steve served as executive vice\npresident and CFO of Vocus. During his tenure, he positioned the company for 40 consecutive quarters\nof revenue growth and rapid expansion, including an IPO, a follow-on offering and several\nacquisitions. Prior to Vocus, Steve was Snyder Communications\u2019 vice president of strategic planning\nand analysis, where he played a lead role in more than 45 acquisitions and oversaw its growth from\n$86 million to nearly $1 billion in revenue. He also worked for Ernst & Young\u2019s entrepreneurial\nservices/middle market group in Washington, D.C. and Baltimore.\n\nSteve has received numerous awards and distinctions during his career, including Northern Virginia\nTechnology Council's Public Company CFO of the Year. He is a certified public accountant and has a\nBachelor of Business Administration degree from Loyola University, Sellinger School of Business.\n\n[Mark Thurmond]\n\n#### Mark Thurmond\n\n###### Co-chief executive officer\n\nMark Thurmond is an accomplished technology industry veteran with deep go-to-market experience\nleading global sales and operations for prominent IT and cloud technology companies. He serves as\nTenable\u2019s co-chief executive officer (CEO), overseeing the company\u2019s go-to-market (GTM) functions,\nincluding sales, professional services, technical support, marketing and customer success. In 2020,\nThurmond joined Tenable as chief operating officer (COO), responsible for global field operations,\nincluding sales, professional services, technical support and demand generation. Previously, he\nserved as COO of Turbonomic, where he was responsible for aligning the company\u2019s global operations\nto help customers on their journey to hybrid cloud. Prior to this role, he was executive vice\npresident at Qlik Technologies, where he led worldwide sales and services. Mark also served in\nmultiple global sales and operations leadership positions for divisions of Dell EMC, including\nsenior vice president of worldwide sales at VCE and RSA.\n\n[Matt Brown]\n\n#### Matt Brown\n\n###### Chief financial officer\n\nMatt Brown, Tenable\u2019s chief financial officer, is responsible for leading the company's global\nfinance organization. He oversees Tenable\u2019s financial strategy, planning, accounting, and reporting.\nWith more than two decades of experience, Matt has a proven track record of leading finance teams at\npremier technology and cybersecurity companies. Prior to Tenable, he served as CFO at Altair\nEngineering, overseeing a period of significant growth in revenue and profitability. Prior to Altair\nEngineering, he served as interim CFO at NortonLifeLock and chief accounting officer at Symantec. He\nhas also held key finance leadership roles at Blue Coat Systems, NETGEAR, and Brocade\nCommunications, after beginning his career at KPMG.\n\nMatt is a certified public accountant and holds a bachelor's degree in business administration from\nthe Walter A. Haas School of Business at the University of California, Berkeley.\n\n[Dino DiMarino]\n\n#### Dino DiMarino\n\n###### Chief revenue officer\n\nDino DiMarino, Tenable\u2019s chief revenue officer, leads the global sales organization, partner\necosystems, government affairs and revenue operations. Dino is responsible for driving Tenable\u2019s\nnext phase of hyper-growth as the company scales to meet surging enterprise demand for exposure\nmanagement and AI security. A veteran of the cybersecurity industry, Dino brings over 20 years of\nleadership experience in scaling global technology organizations and navigating emerging market\nopportunities. Prior to joining Tenable, he served as CEO of AppViewX, a leader in automated\ncertificate lifecycle management. He has also served as CRO at Snyk, where he drove triple-digit\ngrowth, and held the same role at Qualys, delivering consistent double-digit expansion. His track\nrecord of value creation also includes serving as CRO at Mimecast, and in senior leadership\npositions at RSA Security and Dell EMC. Dino earned a business administration degree from Wilfrid\nLaurier University.\n\n[Eric Doerr]\n\n#### Eric Doerr\n\n###### Chief product officer\n\nEric Doerr, Tenable\u2019s chief product officer, leads the company\u2019s global product organization,\noverseeing strategy, innovation and execution across a growing cybersecurity portfolio. He brings\nnearly 30 years of experience building and scaling security products at some of the world\u2019s most\nrespected technology companies. Prior to Tenable, Eric most recently served as vice president of\nsecurity products at Google Cloud, where he led Google SecOps (formerly Chronicle) and Google Threat\nIntelligence, as well as the Mandiant integration. He previously spent more than 20 years at\nMicrosoft in senior leadership roles across the security and identity space, including general\nmanager of Microsoft Account and corporate vice president of Cloud Security and the Microsoft\nSecurity Response Center (MSRC). Eric also served as chief product officer at Porch, a home services\nstartup.\n\n[Meg O\u2019Leary]\n\n#### Meg O\u2019Leary\n\n###### Chief marketing officer\n\nMeg O\u2019Leary has more than two decades of marketing and communications experience. She has built\npowerhouse brands for some of the most respected companies in cybersecurity. Meg\u2019s expertise spans\nproduct marketing, messaging and positioning, data-driven demand generation and go-to-market\nstrategies. Most recently, she served as chief marketing officer at Cybereason, where she helped to\nposition the company as an endpoint security leader. Prior to joining Cybereason, she was chief\nmarketing officer at Capsule8, a pioneer in cloud workload protection, which was acquired by Sophos.\nOutside of her CMO tenures, Meg co-founded InkHouse Marketing+Media, a bi-coastal public relations\nagency (now part of Berlin-Rosen), where she spearheaded hundreds of company and product launches,\ninitial public offerings (IPOs), and exits. Meg also held senior-level marketing positions at\nCharles River Ventures, where she consulted to the firm\u2019s portfolio companies on go-to-marketing\nstrategies; Novera Software (now IBM), where she was vice president of marketing; and RSA Security,\nwhere she held various marketing and product management roles.\n\n[Robert Huber]\n\n#### Robert Huber\n\n###### Chief security officer\n\nRobert Huber, Tenable\u2019s chief security officer, head of research and president of Tenable Public\nSector, LLC, oversees the company's global security and research teams, working cross-functionally\nto reduce risk to the organization, its customers and the broader industry. He has more than 25\nyears of cyber security experience across the financial, defense, critical infrastructure and\ntechnology sectors. Prior to joining Tenable, Robert was a chief security and strategy officer at\nEastwind Networks. He was previously co-founder and president of Critical Intelligence, an OT threat\nintelligence and solutions provider, which cyber threat intelligence leader iSIGHT Partners acquired\nin 2015. He also served as a member of the Lockheed Martin CIRT, an OT security researcher at Idaho\nNational Laboratory and was a chie"
          }
