            "text": "][1]\n* [Platform][2]\n* * * [Overview][3]\n* [Risk Mitigation][4]\n* [Segmentation Orchestration][5]\n* [Inventory and Visibility][6]\n* [Vulnerability Prioritization][7]\n* [Threat and Response][8]\n* [Governance, Risk, and Compliance][9]\n* * * [Configuration Control][10]\n* [IoT Patching][11]\n* [Operational Efficiency][12]\n* [Risk Modeling][13]\n* [Integrations][14]\n* [Industries][15]\n* * * [Energy and Utilities][16]\n* [Financial Services][17]\n* [Government][18]\n* [Healthcare][19]\n* [Higher Education][20]\n* [Hospitality][21]\n* [Life Sciences][22]\n* [Manufacturing][23]\n* [Retail][24]\n* [Transportation and Logistics][25]\n* [Solutions][26]\n* * * #### Connected Device Visibility\n* [Automated IoT Visibility And Deep Categorization][27]\n* [IoT Device Detail Enrichment][28]\n* * #### Vulnerability Detection And Mitigation\n* [Continuous IoT Vulnerability Detection][29]\n* [Risk-based IoT Vulnerability Prioritization][30]\n* [Device Prioritization by Risk][31]\n* [Efficient Mitigation Workflows][32]\n* [Network Segmentation and Microsegmentation][33]\n* * #### IoMT\n* [FDA Recalls and Security Advisories][34]\n* [Medical Device Utilization][35]\n* [IoMT Pre-Purchase Risk Avoidance][36]\n* [Risk Reduction Services][37]\n* * #### IT, IoT and OT\n* [OT Security][38]\n* [IoT Risk Simulator][39]\n* [Incident Response Readiness with Packet Capture][40]\n* [Asimily for IT][41]\n* * #### Compliance and Regulation\n* [CMMC][42]\n* [Cyberscope][43]\n* [DORA][44]\n* [FDA][45]\n* [HIPAA][46]\n* [MITRE ATT&CK][47]\n* [NERC CIP][48]\n* [NIS2][49]\n* [NIST CSF 2.0][50]\n* [PCI-DSS][51]\n* [Zero Trust][52]\n* [Resources][53]\n* * * [All Resources][54]\n* [Blog][55]\n* [FAQ][56]\n* [Press][57]\n* [Glossary][58]\n* [About Us][59]\n* * * [About Asimily][60]\n* [Careers][61]\n* [Partners][62]\n* [Leadership][63]\n* [Contact Us][64]\n* [Request Demo][65]\n* [EN][66]\n* [DE][67]\n[ Request Demo ][68]\n* [Product][69]\n* Segmentation Orchestration\n\n# Streamlined, Scalable Network Segmentation Orchestration\n\nLabor-intensive segmentation enforcement becomes efficient, automated, and accurate with a\ncontinuous process.\n\n[ Request a Demo ][70]\n[Stock photo of iot devices featuring icons]\n\nSegment More Efficiently\n\n[Control Panel for Physical process]\n\n#### Segmentation Simplified, Automated, Made Scalable\n\nTransform segmentation efforts with contextual intelligence and actionable insights about every\nconnected asset.\n\n[ Get in Touch ][71]\n\nSmart Segmentation\n\n## Risk-Aware Insights Powering Dynamic Policies\n\n### Identify and Classify All Devices on the Network\n\nIP and MAC addresses aren\u2019t enough. Asimily provides proper device context and real-time network\ninsights to create segmentation policies that scale seamlessly with every IoMT, OT, IoT, and IT\nasset added to your network.\n\n### Map and Track Device Communication Patterns\n\nBefore you can segment safely, you need to understand how every device communicates \u2013 what it\nconnects to, on which ports, using which protocols and services, and whether those connections are\nexpected. Asimily maps these communication patterns in full detail to generate policies you can\nenforce with confidence that nothing breaks.\n\n### Prioritize the Most Critical Assets\n\nAsimily\u2019s risk-based prioritization takes the guesswork out of reducing the attack surface. By\ntargeting the riskiest assets first, organizations can reduce exposure quickly and efficiently.\n\n[Asimily Prioritization]\n\n### Create Safe and Enforceable Policies That Scale\n\nThe distinct operational nuances of medical, IoT, and OT devices must be carefully accounted for.\nAsimily determines what traffic to permit or restrict with a thorough understanding of what each\ndevice can and cannot support, and creates automated recommendations and segmentation groups\naccordingly.\n\n### Continuously Verify and Validate Policies\n\nSegmentation is not a one-and-done process. Asimily continuously monitors policies to ensure\neffectiveness and can simulate segmentation scenarios to understand the impact of the policies being\napplied.\n\n### Secure Every IoT Device.\n### Automatically.\n\nCyber threats move fast \u2014 so should you. Asimily gives instant inventory and smart, prioritized risk\nmitigation insights for every IoT, OT, and IoMT device \u2014 so you can take action before threats\nstrike.\n\n[ Schedule a Demo ][72]\n\n#### Our Gartner Peer Insights Reviews\n\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Peer Insights Review 4976678] ][73]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Peer Insights Review 511214] ][74]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Review 4925308] ][75]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Review 4959932] ][76]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Review 4959378] ][77]\n[Previous slide]\n[Next slide]\n\n## Protecting Your Industry\u2019s Unique Devices\n\n### Healthcare\n\nAsimily provides the necessary tools to identify and address IoT vulnerabilities in healthcare,\nensuring the protection of patient data without interrupting the delivery of critical care.\n\n[ Discover More ][78]\n\n### Manufacturing\n\nIn an industry that relies heavily on IoT devices to drive automation, efficiency, and connectivity,\nAsimly can help. By ensuring the security of IoT devices, manufacturers can safeguard their\nintellectual property, prevent production disruptions, and maintain the trust of their customers and\npartners.\n\n[ Discover More ][79]\n\n### Higher Education\n\nEducational institutions depend on interconnected devices to facilitate learning, research, and\ncampus operations. Protect sensitive student and faculty data, maintain operational integrity, and\nfoster a secure, productive academic environment with Asimily.\n\n[ Discover More ][80]\n\n### Government\n\nAsimily equips government entities worldwide with the necessary tools to secure their IoT devices,\nprotect critical infrastructure, and ensure data privacy. Defend against cyber threats and uphold\npublic trust by proactively mitigating vulnerabilities.\n\n[ Discover More ][81]\n\n### Life Sciences\n\nWhere delicate research, development, and data exchange are ongoing, securing your IoT devices is a\ntop priority. Proactively manage and mitigate vulnerabilities, reducing the risk of theft or loss of\ncritical research and development efforts.\n\n[ Discover More ][82]\n\n### Frequently Asked Questions\n\nWhy is network segmentation so difficult for organizations to implement?\n\nTraditional network segmentation relies on IP addresses and VLANs, but IoT, OT, and IoMT devices\nhave unique operational requirements that generic IT approaches can\u2019t account for. Many connected\ndevices use unexpected ports, proprietary protocols, or communicate with services that aren\u2019t\nwell-documented \u2013 so applying a blanket segmentation policy risks breaking critical workflows like\npatient monitoring or industrial control systems. Asimily solves this by deeply classifying every\nconnected asset and mapping its full communication behavior \u2013 what it talks to, on which ports,\nusing which protocols \u2013 so segmentation policies are built on actual device context, not guesswork.\n\nHow does Asimily automate network segmentation policy creation?\n\nAsimily continuously discovers and classifies every IoT, OT, IoMT, and IT device on your network,\nthen maps each device\u2019s real communication patterns in detail. From that intelligence, the platform\nautomatically generates segmentation policy recommendations \u2013 specifying what traffic to permit or\nrestrict \u2013 tailored to what each device can and cannot support operationally. This replaces the\nmanual, spreadsheet-driven process most organizations struggle with and produces enforceable\npolicies that scale as new devices join the network.\n\nWhat happens if a network segmentation policy breaks a connected device?\n\nThis is one of the biggest risks organizations face when attempting segmentation, especially in\nhealthcare and manufacturing where device downtime can have serious consequences. Asimily addresses\nthis by letting you simulate segmentation scenarios before enforcement, so you can see the impact a\nproposed policy will have on device communication and operations before anything changes in\nproduction. Combined with continuous monitoring after deployment, this ensures policies remain\neffective without disrupting critical services.\n\nIs network segmentation a one-time project or an ongoing process?\n\nNetwork segmentation must be treated as a continuous process, not a one-time project. Devices are\nconstantly being added, retired, updated, or reconfigured \u2013 and each change can invalidate existing\npolicies. Asimily continuously monitors and validates segmentation policies post-deployment,\nflagging drift or gaps as your environment evolves. This ongoing verification ensures your\nsegmentation posture stays aligned with your actual network, not a snapshot of what it looked like\nmonths ago.\n\nHow does Asimily prioritize which devices to segment first?\n\nNot all devices carry equal risk, and trying to segment an entire network at once is a recipe for\nstalled projects. Asimily uses risk-based prioritization to identify the most vulnerable and\nexploitable assets on your network, so your security team can focus segmentation efforts where\nthey\u2019ll reduce the most attack surface the fastest. By targeting the highest-risk devices first,\norganizations see measurable security improvement early \u2013 building momentum instead of getting\nburied in a years-long segmentation initiative.\n* Platform\n* [Overview][83]\n* [Risk Mitigation][84]\n* [Inventory and Visibility][85]\n* [Vulnerability Prioritization][86]\n* [Threat and Response][87]\n* [Segmentation Orchestration][88]\n* [IoT Patching][89]\n* [Configuration Control][90]\n* [Risk Modeling][91]\n* [Governance, Risk, and Compliance][92]\n* [Operational Efficiency][93]\n* [Integrations][94]\n* Industries\n* [Energy and Utilities][95]\n* [Financial Services][96]\n* [Government][97]\n* [Healthcare][98]\n* [Higher Education][99]\n* [Hospitality][100]\n* [Life Sciences][101]\n* [Manufacturing][102]\n* [Retail][103]\n* [Transportation and Logistics][104]\n* Solutions\n* column1\n* [Automated IoT Visibility And Deep Categorization][105]\n* [IoT Device Detail Enrichment][106]\n* [Continuous IoT Vulnerability Detection][107]\n* [Risk-based IoT Vulnerability Prioritization][108]\n* [Device Prioritization by Risk][109]\n* [Efficient Mitigation Workflows][110]\n* [Network Segmentation and Microsegmentation][111]\n* column2\n* [FDA Recalls and Security Advisories][112]\n* [Medical Device Utilization][113]\n* [IoMT Pre-Purchase Risk Avoidance][114]\n* [Risk Reduction Services][115]\n* [IoT Risk Simulator][116]\n* [Incident Response Readiness with Packet Capture][117]\n* [Asimily for IT][118]\n* [IoT Security][119]\n* [OT Security][120]\n* [Medical Devices][121]\n* column3\n* [CMMC][122]\n* [Cyberscope][123]\n* [DORA][124]\n* [FDA][125]\n* [HIPAA][126]\n* [MITRE ATT&CK][127]\n* [NERC CIP][128]\n* [NIS2][129]\n* [PCI-DSS][130]\n* [Zero Trust][131]\n* two columns\n* Resources\n* [All Resources][132]\n* [Blog][133]\n* [FAQ][134]\n* [Glossary][135]\n* About Us\n* [About Asimily][136]\n* [Careers][137]\n* [Leadership][138]\n* [Partners][139]\n* [Contact Us][140]\n\n\u00a9 2026 Asimily All Rights Reserved.\n\n[ Privacy Policy ][141]\n[ Product Security ][142]\n\n[1]: https://asimily.com\n[2]: #\n[3]: https://asimily.com/product/overview/\n[4]: https://asimily.com/product/risk-mitigation/\n[5]: https://asimily.com/product/segmentation-orchestration/\n[6]: https://asimily.com/product/inventory-visibility/\n[7]: https://asimily.com/product/vulnerability-prioritization/\n[8]: https://asimily.com/product/threat-response/\n[9]: https://asimily.com/product/governance-risk-compliance/\n[10]: https://asimily.com/product/configuration-control/\n[11]: https://asimily.com/product/iot-patching/\n[12]: https://asimily.com/product/operational-efficiency/\n[13]: https://asimily.com/product/risk-modeling/\n[14]: https://asimily.com/product/integrations/\n[15]: #\n[16]: https://asimily.com/industries/energy-utilities/\n[17]: https://asimily.com/industries/financial-services/\n[18]: https://asimily.com/industries/government/\n[19]: https://asimily.com/industries/healthcare/\n[20]: https://asimily.com/industries/higher-education/\n[21]: https://asimily.co"
