            "url": "https://asimily.com/product/configuration-control/",
            "text": "][1]\n* [Platform][2]\n* * * [Overview][3]\n* [Risk Mitigation][4]\n* [Segmentation Orchestration][5]\n* [Inventory and Visibility][6]\n* [Vulnerability Prioritization][7]\n* [Threat and Response][8]\n* [Governance, Risk, and Compliance][9]\n* * * [Configuration Control][10]\n* [IoT Patching][11]\n* [Operational Efficiency][12]\n* [Risk Modeling][13]\n* [Integrations][14]\n* [Industries][15]\n* * * [Energy and Utilities][16]\n* [Financial Services][17]\n* [Government][18]\n* [Healthcare][19]\n* [Higher Education][20]\n* [Hospitality][21]\n* [Life Sciences][22]\n* [Manufacturing][23]\n* [Retail][24]\n* [Transportation and Logistics][25]\n* [Solutions][26]\n* * * #### Connected Device Visibility\n* [Automated IoT Visibility And Deep Categorization][27]\n* [IoT Device Detail Enrichment][28]\n* * #### Vulnerability Detection And Mitigation\n* [Continuous IoT Vulnerability Detection][29]\n* [Risk-based IoT Vulnerability Prioritization][30]\n* [Device Prioritization by Risk][31]\n* [Efficient Mitigation Workflows][32]\n* [Network Segmentation and Microsegmentation][33]\n* * #### IoMT\n* [FDA Recalls and Security Advisories][34]\n* [Medical Device Utilization][35]\n* [IoMT Pre-Purchase Risk Avoidance][36]\n* [Risk Reduction Services][37]\n* * #### IT, IoT and OT\n* [OT Security][38]\n* [IoT Risk Simulator][39]\n* [Incident Response Readiness with Packet Capture][40]\n* [Asimily for IT][41]\n* * #### Compliance and Regulation\n* [CMMC][42]\n* [Cyberscope][43]\n* [DORA][44]\n* [FDA][45]\n* [HIPAA][46]\n* [MITRE ATT&CK][47]\n* [NERC CIP][48]\n* [NIS2][49]\n* [NIST CSF 2.0][50]\n* [PCI-DSS][51]\n* [Zero Trust][52]\n* [Resources][53]\n* * * [All Resources][54]\n* [Blog][55]\n* [FAQ][56]\n* [Press][57]\n* [Glossary][58]\n* [About Us][59]\n* * * [About Asimily][60]\n* [Careers][61]\n* [Partners][62]\n* [Leadership][63]\n* [Contact Us][64]\n* [Request Demo][65]\n* [EN][66]\n* [DE][67]\n[ Request Demo ][68]\n* [Product][69]\n* Configuration Control\n\n# Prevent Attacks Against Misconfigured Devices\n\nAsimily captures known good states for any IoT, OT, and IoMT if it ever drifts from a secure state.\nGet notifications, alerts, comparisons, and reports.\n\n[Configurations being snapshotted and restored by Asimily, to add to Configuration Control.]\n[Medical monitor in a hospital]\n\nReduce Device Cyber Risk\n\n[Control Panel for Physical process]\n\n#### Set It and Never Forget It\n\nEvery IoT, OT, and IoMT has an intended, correct configuration. Store it, get alerts on important\ndeviations, and avoid risky configuration drift.\n\n[ Get in Touch ][70]\n\nReceive Only Important Drift Alerts\n\n## Only Get Alerts on Important Changes\n\n### Reduce Risk from Misconfigurations\n\nWhen IoT, OT, and IoMT are misconfigured, attackers can notice and take advantage. Reduce your\nexposure time by detecting and quickly restoring devices to the state you want them in.\n\n[Person at keyboard evaluating risk, and how to reduce it.]\n\n### Spot Deviations\n\nWhen a device drifts from your snapshotted, preferred configuration\u2026 you\u2019ll know. And you\u2019ll know\njust what it should be, keeping your defenses from regressing.\n\n[Spotting deviations on a computer screen with colored boxes on it.]\n\n### Prioritize Snapshot Factors\n\nNot one size fits all so Asimily lets you assign High / Medium / Low (or None) to IoT, OT, and IoMT\nconfiguration categories to prevent Alert storms. For example, IP address changes may be Low\npriority but firmware version changes would be High.\n\n[3 snapshots of IoT, OT, and IoMT in Polaroid-style frames.]\n\n### Secure Every IoT Device.\n### Automatically.\n\nCyber threats move fast \u2014 so should you. Asimily gives instant inventory and smart, prioritized risk\nmitigation insights for every IoT, OT, and IoMT device \u2014 so you can take action before threats\nstrike.\n\n[ Schedule a Demo ][71]\n\n#### Our Gartner Peer Insights Reviews\n\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Peer Insights Review 4976678] ][72]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Peer Insights Review 511214] ][73]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Review 4925308] ][74]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Review 4959932] ][75]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Review 4959378] ][76]\n[Previous slide]\n[Next slide]\n\n## Protecting Your Industry\u2019s Unique Devices\n\n### Healthcare\n\nAsimily provides the necessary tools to identify and address IoT vulnerabilities in healthcare,\nensuring the protection of patient data without interrupting the delivery of critical care.\n\n[ Discover More ][77]\n\n### Manufacturing\n\nIn an industry that relies heavily on IoT devices to drive automation, efficiency, and connectivity,\nAsimly can help. By ensuring the security of IoT devices, manufacturers can safeguard their\nintellectual property, prevent production disruptions, and maintain the trust of their customers and\npartners.\n\n[ Discover More ][78]\n\n### Higher Education\n\nEducational institutions depend on interconnected devices to facilitate learning, research, and\ncampus operations. Protect sensitive student and faculty data, maintain operational integrity, and\nfoster a secure, productive academic environment with Asimily.\n\n[ Discover More ][79]\n\n### Government\n\nAsimily equips government entities worldwide with the necessary tools to secure their IoT devices,\nprotect critical infrastructure, and ensure data privacy. Defend against cyber threats and uphold\npublic trust by proactively mitigating vulnerabilities.\n\n[ Discover More ][80]\n\n### Life Sciences\n\nWhere delicate research, development, and data exchange are ongoing, securing your IoT devices is a\ntop priority. Proactively manage and mitigate vulnerabilities, reducing the risk of theft or loss of\ncritical research and development efforts.\n\n[ Discover More ][81]\n\n### Frequently asked questions\n\nWhy do configurations for IoT, OT, and IoMT drift unsafely?\n\nEven well-intentioned users with access to configurations can make changes that reduce\ncybersecurity. These can be accidental, due to lack of context, or intentional by criminals.\n\nWho makes these unintended changes?\n\nMost configuration changes are by authorized users, such as operational staff or device\nmanufacturers. Some of these can be remote, but manual changes requiring physical access are also\npossible\n\nHow do configuration drift changes get detected?\n\nOften, they are not detected. Most monitoring software is too dangerous for many IoT, OT, and IoMT\ndue to the fragility of many devices. It requires a purpose-built approach that stores\nconfigurations and can check current configurations against them.\n\nWhy is it hard to manage IoT/ OT/ IoMT configurations for restoration?\n\nWhile every network device, server, VM, or container is pretty similar to others, every IoT, OT, and\nIoMT device is different. It has different metadata, configurations and expected behavior. It has\nbeen difficult to keep track of that variation in a single place, across multiple vendors\u2019 products,\nimpeding good recordkeeping.\n\nHow often should configuration snapshots be taken?\n\nEvery time a configuration is in a known secure state, a new snapshot should be taken. That could be\nfrequent or infrequent, depending on manufacturer updates, new security vulnerabilities discovered,\nor even regulatory and compliance changes.\n* Platform\n* [Overview][82]\n* [Risk Mitigation][83]\n* [Inventory and Visibility][84]\n* [Vulnerability Prioritization][85]\n* [Threat and Response][86]\n* [Segmentation Orchestration][87]\n* [IoT Patching][88]\n* [Configuration Control][89]\n* [Risk Modeling][90]\n* [Governance, Risk, and Compliance][91]\n* [Operational Efficiency][92]\n* [Integrations][93]\n* Industries\n* [Energy and Utilities][94]\n* [Financial Services][95]\n* [Government][96]\n* [Healthcare][97]\n* [Higher Education][98]\n* [Hospitality][99]\n* [Life Sciences][100]\n* [Manufacturing][101]\n* [Retail][102]\n* [Transportation and Logistics][103]\n* Solutions\n* column1\n* [Automated IoT Visibility And Deep Categorization][104]\n* [IoT Device Detail Enrichment][105]\n* [Continuous IoT Vulnerability Detection][106]\n* [Risk-based IoT Vulnerability Prioritization][107]\n* [Device Prioritization by Risk][108]\n* [Efficient Mitigation Workflows][109]\n* [Network Segmentation and Microsegmentation][110]\n* column2\n* [FDA Recalls and Security Advisories][111]\n* [Medical Device Utilization][112]\n* [IoMT Pre-Purchase Risk Avoidance][113]\n* [Risk Reduction Services][114]\n* [IoT Risk Simulator][115]\n* [Incident Response Readiness with Packet Capture][116]\n* [Asimily for IT][117]\n* [IoT Security][118]\n* [OT Security][119]\n* [Medical Devices][120]\n* column3\n* [CMMC][121]\n* [Cyberscope][122]\n* [DORA][123]\n* [FDA][124]\n* [HIPAA][125]\n* [MITRE ATT&CK][126]\n* [NERC CIP][127]\n* [NIS2][128]\n* [PCI-DSS][129]\n* [Zero Trust][130]\n* two columns\n* Resources\n* [All Resources][131]\n* [Blog][132]\n* [FAQ][133]\n* [Glossary][134]\n* About Us\n* [About Asimily][135]\n* [Careers][136]\n* [Leadership][137]\n* [Partners][138]\n* [Contact Us][139]\n\n\u00a9 2026 Asimily All Rights Reserved.\n\n[ Privacy Policy ][140]\n[ Product Security ][141]\n\n[1]: https://asimily.com\n[2]: #\n[3]: https://asimily.com/product/overview/\n[4]: https://asimily.com/product/risk-mitigation/\n[5]: https://asimily.com/product/segmentation-orchestration/\n[6]: https://asimily.com/product/inventory-visibility/\n[7]: https://asimily.com/product/vulnerability-prioritization/\n[8]: https://asimily.com/product/threat-response/\n[9]: https://asimily.com/product/governance-risk-compliance/\n[10]: https://asimily.com/product/configuration-control/\n[11]: https://asimily.com/product/iot-patching/\n[12]: https://asimily.com/product/operational-efficiency/\n[13]: https://asimily.com/product/risk-modeling/\n[14]: https://asimily.com/product/integrations/\n[15]: #\n[16]: https://asimily.com/industries/energy-utilities/\n[17]: https://asimily.com/industries/financial-services/\n[18]: https://asimily.com/industries/government/\n[19]: https://asimily.com/industries/healthcare/\n[20]: https://asimily.com/industries/higher-education/\n[21]: https://asimily.com/industries/hospitality-iot-security/\n[22]: https://asimily.com/industries/life-sciences/\n[23]: https://asimily.com/industries/manufacturing/\n[24]: https://asimily.com/industries/retail/\n[25]: https://asimily.com/industries/transportation/\n[26]: #\n[27]: https://asimily.com/solutions/automated-iot-visibility-deep-categorization/\n[28]: https://asimily.com/solutions/iot-device-detail-enrichment/\n[29]: https://asimily.com/solutions/continuous-iot-vulnerability-detection/\n[30]: https://asimily.com/solutions/risk-based-iot-vulnerability-prioritization/\n[31]: https://asimily.com/solutions/iot-device-prioritization-by-risk/\n[32]: https://asimily.com/solutions/efficient-security-risk-mitigation-workflows/\n[33]: https://asimily.com/solutions/network-segmentation-and-microsegmentation/\n[34]: https://asimily.com/solutions/fda-recalls-and-security-advisories/\n[35]: https://asimily.com/solutions/medical-device-utilization/\n[36]: https://asimily.com/solutions/pre-purchase-security-risk-avoidance/\n[37]: https://asimily.com/solutions/risk-reduction-services/\n[38]: https://asimily.com/solutions/ot-security/\n[39]: https://asimily.com/solutions/iot-risk-simulator/\n[40]: https://asimily.com/solutions/incident-response-readiness-with-packet-capture/\n[41]: https://asimily.com/solutions/it-capabilities/\n[42]: https://asimily.com/compliance-cmmc/\n[43]: https://asimily.com/compliance-cyberscope/\n[44]: https://asimily.com/compliance-dora/\n[45]: https://asimily.com/compliance-fda/\n[46]: https://asimily.com/compliance-hipaa/\n[47]: https://asimily.com/compliance-mitre-attack-framework/\n[48]: https://asimily.com/compliance-nerc-cip/\n[49]: https://asimily.com/compliance-nis2-directive/\n[50]: https://asimily.com/compliance-nist-csf/\n[51]: https://asimily.com/compliance-pci-dss/\n[52]: https://asimily.com/compliance-zero-trust-security-framework/\n[53]: #\n[54]: https://asimily.com/resources/\n[55]: https://asimily.com/blog/\n[56]: https://asimily.com/resources/faq/\n[57]: https://asimily.com/press/\n[58]: https://asimily.com/resources/glossary/\n[59]: #\n[60]: https://asimily.com/about-us/\n[61]: https://asimily.com/about-us/careers/\n[62]: https://asimily.com/about-us/partners/\n[63]: http"
