          {
            "url": "https://asimily.com/solutions/continuous-iot-vulnerability-detection/",
            "text": "][1]\n* [Platform][2]\n* * * [Overview][3]\n* [Risk Mitigation][4]\n* [Segmentation Orchestration][5]\n* [Inventory and Visibility][6]\n* [Vulnerability Prioritization][7]\n* [Threat and Response][8]\n* [Governance, Risk, and Compliance][9]\n* * * [Configuration Control][10]\n* [IoT Patching][11]\n* [Operational Efficiency][12]\n* [Risk Modeling][13]\n* [Integrations][14]\n* [Industries][15]\n* * * [Energy and Utilities][16]\n* [Financial Services][17]\n* [Government][18]\n* [Healthcare][19]\n* [Higher Education][20]\n* [Hospitality][21]\n* [Life Sciences][22]\n* [Manufacturing][23]\n* [Retail][24]\n* [Transportation and Logistics][25]\n* [Solutions][26]\n* * * #### Connected Device Visibility\n* [Automated IoT Visibility And Deep Categorization][27]\n* [IoT Device Detail Enrichment][28]\n* * #### Vulnerability Detection And Mitigation\n* [Continuous IoT Vulnerability Detection][29]\n* [Risk-based IoT Vulnerability Prioritization][30]\n* [Device Prioritization by Risk][31]\n* [Efficient Mitigation Workflows][32]\n* [Network Segmentation and Microsegmentation][33]\n* * #### IoMT\n* [FDA Recalls and Security Advisories][34]\n* [Medical Device Utilization][35]\n* [IoMT Pre-Purchase Risk Avoidance][36]\n* [Risk Reduction Services][37]\n* * #### IT, IoT and OT\n* [OT Security][38]\n* [IoT Risk Simulator][39]\n* [Incident Response Readiness with Packet Capture][40]\n* [Asimily for IT][41]\n* * #### Compliance and Regulation\n* [CMMC][42]\n* [Cyberscope][43]\n* [DORA][44]\n* [FDA][45]\n* [HIPAA][46]\n* [MITRE ATT&CK][47]\n* [NERC CIP][48]\n* [NIS2][49]\n* [NIST CSF 2.0][50]\n* [PCI-DSS][51]\n* [Zero Trust][52]\n* [Resources][53]\n* * * [All Resources][54]\n* [Blog][55]\n* [FAQ][56]\n* [Press][57]\n* [Glossary][58]\n* [About Us][59]\n* * * [About Asimily][60]\n* [Careers][61]\n* [Partners][62]\n* [Leadership][63]\n* [Contact Us][64]\n* [Request Demo][65]\n* [EN][66]\n* [DE][67]\n[ Request Demo ][68]\n\nShorten the Time New Vulnerabilities are Exploitable\n\n# Rapid Awareness Keeps Attackers Out\n\n###### Rapid Attacks\n\nOne out of four High Risk CVEs are exploited on publication date. Defenders have to be faster than\never to stay ahead.\n\n###### Organized Adversaries\n\nOrganized criminal groups weaponize new vulnerabilities in hours. The fantasy that \u201cThey\u2019re not\ninterested in me\u201d is harder to justify each year.\n\n###### Threat Intel Sprawl\n\nWarnings about new threats can come from any direction. Keeping track of them can be a full-time\njob. Get time back.\n\n### How to Choose the Right\n### IoT Security Solution in 2026\n\nProtecting the growing IoT architecture\nin a complicated security environment\n\n[ Get The Whitepaper ][69]\n\nRanked, Continuous, Personalized\n\n## How Asimily Approaches Continuous Vulnerability Detection\n\nAutomating learning from the CVE feed is just the beginning. The difficult part is determining the\nrisk. That includes Asimily\u2019s vulnerability analysis (MITRE ATT&CK based), and using unique customer\nenvironment as an input for prioritization.\n\n### Ranked\n\nAsimily\u2019s Device Ranker combined Asimily analysis of potential attacks that use a vulnerability to\ngive a stack ranked list of what devices (and vulnerabilities) should be addressed to reduce risk\nnow.\n\n### Continuous\n\nVulnerability Detection should work around the clock and use multiple techniques. Attackers who can\nhide from one threat detection method will find it harder to hide from many. Both humans and AI can\nbe involved, but automation is important too.\n\n### Personalized\n\nInformation about vulnerabilities alone isn\u2019t enough. A vulnerability can be risky or not, depending\non context, neighbors, and IoT device importance. Asimily takes that into account for targeted\nguidance and prioritization that delivers maximum risk reduction.\n\n### The Necessity of Continuous Vulnerability Detection\n\nWith continuous vulnerability detection, organizations gain a more accurate picture of what possible\nweaknesses there are in their IoT devices on a more consistent basis.\n\n[ See Why ][70]\n[The Necessity of Continuous Vulnerability Detection]\n\n### Shadow IoT Put Companies at Risk\n\nShadow IT is one of the most persistent cybersecurity challenges today. Already, researchers\nestimate that 53% of departments refuse to use IT-approved tools and 80% of workers admit to using\nSaaS applications at work without getting approval from the IT department. Then there\u2019s the issue of\nshadow Internet of Things (IoT) usage complicating matters even more.\n\n[ Learn Why ][71]\n[Shadow IoT How Unmanaged Devices Put Companies at Risk]\n\n#### Our Gartner Peer Insights Reviews\n\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Peer Insights Review 4976678] ][72]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Peer Insights Review 511214] ][73]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Review 4925308] ][74]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Review 4959932] ][75]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Review 4959378] ][76]\n[Previous slide]\n[Next slide]\n* Platform\n* [Overview][77]\n* [Risk Mitigation][78]\n* [Inventory and Visibility][79]\n* [Vulnerability Prioritization][80]\n* [Threat and Response][81]\n* [Segmentation Orchestration][82]\n* [IoT Patching][83]\n* [Configuration Control][84]\n* [Risk Modeling][85]\n* [Governance, Risk, and Compliance][86]\n* [Operational Efficiency][87]\n* [Integrations][88]\n* Industries\n* [Energy and Utilities][89]\n* [Financial Services][90]\n* [Government][91]\n* [Healthcare][92]\n* [Higher Education][93]\n* [Hospitality][94]\n* [Life Sciences][95]\n* [Manufacturing][96]\n* [Retail][97]\n* [Transportation and Logistics][98]\n* Solutions\n* column1\n* [Automated IoT Visibility And Deep Categorization][99]\n* [IoT Device Detail Enrichment][100]\n* [Continuous IoT Vulnerability Detection][101]\n* [Risk-based IoT Vulnerability Prioritization][102]\n* [Device Prioritization by Risk][103]\n* [Efficient Mitigation Workflows][104]\n* [Network Segmentation and Microsegmentation][105]\n* column2\n* [FDA Recalls and Security Advisories][106]\n* [Medical Device Utilization][107]\n* [IoMT Pre-Purchase Risk Avoidance][108]\n* [Risk Reduction Services][109]\n* [IoT Risk Simulator][110]\n* [Incident Response Readiness with Packet Capture][111]\n* [Asimily for IT][112]\n* [IoT Security][113]\n* [OT Security][114]\n* [Medical Devices][115]\n* column3\n* [CMMC][116]\n* [Cyberscope][117]\n* [DORA][118]\n* [FDA][119]\n* [HIPAA][120]\n* [MITRE ATT&CK][121]\n* [NERC CIP][122]\n* [NIS2][123]\n* [PCI-DSS][124]\n* [Zero Trust][125]\n* two columns\n* Resources\n* [All Resources][126]\n* [Blog][127]\n* [FAQ][128]\n* [Glossary][129]\n* About Us\n* [About Asimily][130]\n* [Careers][131]\n* [Leadership][132]\n* [Partners][133]\n* [Contact Us][134]\n\n\u00a9 2026 Asimily All Rights Reserved.\n\n[ Privacy Policy ][135]\n[ Product Security ][136]\n\n[1]: https://asimily.com\n[2]: #\n[3]: https://asimily.com/product/overview/\n[4]: https://asimily.com/product/risk-mitigation/\n[5]: https://asimily.com/product/segmentation-orchestration/\n[6]: https://asimily.com/product/inventory-visibility/\n[7]: https://asimily.com/product/vulnerability-prioritization/\n[8]: https://asimily.com/product/threat-response/\n[9]: https://asimily.com/product/governance-risk-compliance/\n[10]: https://asimily.com/product/configuration-control/\n[11]: https://asimily.com/product/iot-patching/\n[12]: https://asimily.com/product/operational-efficiency/\n[13]: https://asimily.com/product/risk-modeling/\n[14]: https://asimily.com/product/integrations/\n[15]: #\n[16]: https://asimily.com/industries/energy-utilities/\n[17]: https://asimily.com/industries/financial-services/\n[18]: https://asimily.com/industries/government/\n[19]: https://asimily.com/industries/healthcare/\n[20]: https://asimily.com/industries/higher-education/\n[21]: https://asimily.com/industries/hospitality-iot-security/\n[22]: https://asimily.com/industries/life-sciences/\n[23]: https://asimily.com/industries/manufacturing/\n[24]: https://asi