            "url": "https://asimily.com/solutions/iot-device-prioritization-by-risk/",
            "text": "][1]\n* [Platform][2]\n* * * [Overview][3]\n* [Risk Mitigation][4]\n* [Segmentation Orchestration][5]\n* [Inventory and Visibility][6]\n* [Vulnerability Prioritization][7]\n* [Threat and Response][8]\n* [Governance, Risk, and Compliance][9]\n* * * [Configuration Control][10]\n* [IoT Patching][11]\n* [Operational Efficiency][12]\n* [Risk Modeling][13]\n* [Integrations][14]\n* [Industries][15]\n* * * [Energy and Utilities][16]\n* [Financial Services][17]\n* [Government][18]\n* [Healthcare][19]\n* [Higher Education][20]\n* [Hospitality][21]\n* [Life Sciences][22]\n* [Manufacturing][23]\n* [Retail][24]\n* [Transportation and Logistics][25]\n* [Solutions][26]\n* * * #### Connected Device Visibility\n* [Automated IoT Visibility And Deep Categorization][27]\n* [IoT Device Detail Enrichment][28]\n* * #### Vulnerability Detection And Mitigation\n* [Continuous IoT Vulnerability Detection][29]\n* [Risk-based IoT Vulnerability Prioritization][30]\n* [Device Prioritization by Risk][31]\n* [Efficient Mitigation Workflows][32]\n* [Network Segmentation and Microsegmentation][33]\n* * #### IoMT\n* [FDA Recalls and Security Advisories][34]\n* [Medical Device Utilization][35]\n* [IoMT Pre-Purchase Risk Avoidance][36]\n* [Risk Reduction Services][37]\n* * #### IT, IoT and OT\n* [OT Security][38]\n* [IoT Risk Simulator][39]\n* [Incident Response Readiness with Packet Capture][40]\n* [Asimily for IT][41]\n* * #### Compliance and Regulation\n* [CMMC][42]\n* [Cyberscope][43]\n* [DORA][44]\n* [FDA][45]\n* [HIPAA][46]\n* [MITRE ATT&CK][47]\n* [NERC CIP][48]\n* [NIS2][49]\n* [NIST CSF 2.0][50]\n* [PCI-DSS][51]\n* [Zero Trust][52]\n* [Resources][53]\n* * * [All Resources][54]\n* [Blog][55]\n* [FAQ][56]\n* [Press][57]\n* [Glossary][58]\n* [About Us][59]\n* * * [About Asimily][60]\n* [Careers][61]\n* [Partners][62]\n* [Leadership][63]\n* [Contact Us][64]\n* [Request Demo][65]\n* [EN][66]\n* [DE][67]\n[ Request Demo ][68]\n\nConcentrated IoT Weaknesses are Risky\n\n# Without Device-level Analysis, Defense is Harder\n\n###### Mitigation Work Needs to Be Efficient\n\nIoT Devices can have some, many or no vulnerabilities. Since they are often distributed\ngeographically, it can help to understand issues on each IoT. This way, teams can fix multiple\nissues at one time, increasing efficiency.\n\n###### Device Protection Should Be Rapid\n\nInefficient security teams struggle to stay ahead of attackers. Vulnerabilities can stay around\nlonger than needed, and attackers can concentrate their attention on the slowest and most\nexploitable targets.\n\n###### Devices Should Not Be Unprotected for Long\n\nWhen exposure windows are long, dwell time for intrusions can increase too. This gives attackers\nmore time to exfiltrate, establish persistence and every other bad outcome CISOs strive to avoid.\n\n### How to Choose the Right\n### IoT Security Solution in 2026\n\nProtecting the growing IoT architecture\nin a complicated security environment\n\n[ Get The Whitepaper ][69]\n\nAggregated, Dynamic, Rich\n\n## How Asimily Prioritizes Devices\n\nAsimily customers get a stack ranked list of what devices to work on next. It\u2019s based on the\ndevice\u2019s importance to its owner, the vulnerabilities present, and known exploitability. This\nprecise approach is intended to reduce the workload for security teams without sacrificing the\namount of risk reduced.\n\n### Aggregated\n\nA security expert would look at all the information available about a risky IoT / IoMT / OT device\nbefore doing any work on it to improve security. Asimily makes that process simple and scalable by\naggregating all the information about the device, vulnerability and exploitability. It reduces an\nendless list of security to-do\u2019s to one that reduces true risk.\n\n### Dynamic\n\nAround 30,000 security vulnerabilities are cataloged every year. Even more are found and don\u2019t get a\nCommon Vulnerability Enumeration (CVE) number, and stay in attackers\u2019 secret inventories. Asimily\nuses its sources and technology to alert customers about risky devices as soon as that risk is\nknown.\n\n### Rich\n\nTo be efficient, the device inventory must have all the information needed for teams to deploy\nmitigation. That includes tags for handing off work, understanding the organizational owner and\nclassifying devices accurately so security teams can move quickly to fend off attackers. Rich data \u2013\nsuch as manufacturer, serial #, model and device family \u2013 help route work better.\n\n### Not All Vulnerabilities Are Created Equal\n\nAfter detecting vulnerabilities, you need a solution that has a deep contextual engine to prioritize\nthem according to their exploitability in both senses. Risk is contextual; the public rating of a\nvulnerability\u2019s severity is not. Similarly, a vulnerability that has seen a spike in usage in the\nwild is more exploitable than it was.\n\n[ Explore Now ][70]\n\n### Why It\u2019s Critical to Mitigate the Risk of IoT Device Sprawl\n\nThis number of IoT devices in use creates a new problem: device sprawl. Companies are implementing\nmore connected equipment in their infrastructure, such as printers, environment sensors, and smart\nTVs. As more devices are added to corporate networks to solve a particular problem, cybersecurity\nteams are faced with the challenge of mitigating the risk that this connected equipment presents.\n\n[ Learn Why ][71]\n[Why It\u2019s Critical to Mitigate the Risk of IoT Device Sprawl | Asimily]\n\n#### Our Gartner Peer Insights Reviews\n\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Peer Insights Review 4976678] ][72]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Peer Insights Review 511214] ][73]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Review 4925308] ][74]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Review 4959932] ][75]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Review 4959378] ][76]\n[Previous slide]\n[Next slide]\n* Platform\n* [Overview][77]\n* [Risk Mitigation][78]\n* [Inventory and Visibility][79]\n* [Vulnerability Prioritization][80]\n* [Threat and Response][81]\n* [Segmentation Orchestration][82]\n* [IoT Patching][83]\n* [Configuration Control][84]\n* [Risk Modeling][85]\n* [Governance, Risk, and Compliance][86]\n* [Operational Efficiency][87]\n* [Integrations][88]\n* Industries\n* [Energy and Utilities][89]\n* [Financial Services][90]\n* [Government][91]\n* [Healthcare][92]\n* [Higher Education][93]\n* [Hospitality][94]\n* [Life Sciences][95]\n* [Manufacturing][96]\n* [Retail][97]\n* [Transportation and Logistics][98]\n* Solutions\n* column1\n* [Automated IoT Visibility And Deep Categorization][99]\n* [IoT Device Detail Enrichment][100]\n* [Continuous IoT Vulnerability Detection][101]\n* [Risk-based IoT Vulnerability Prioritization][102]\n* [Device Prioritization by Risk][103]\n* [Efficient Mitigation Workflows][104]\n* [Network Segmentation and Microsegmentation][105]\n* column2\n* [FDA Recalls and Security Advisories][106]\n* [Medical Device Utilization][107]\n* [IoMT Pre-Purchase Risk Avoidance][108]\n* [Risk Reduction Services][109]\n* [IoT Risk Simulator][110]\n* [Incident Response Readiness with Packet Capture][111]\n* [Asimily for IT][112]\n* [IoT Security][113]\n* [OT Security][114]\n* [Medical Devices][115]\n* column3\n* [CMMC][116]\n* [Cyberscope][117]\n* [DORA][118]\n* [FDA][119]\n* [HIPAA][120]\n* [MITRE ATT&CK][121]\n* [NERC CIP][122]\n* [NIS2][123]\n* [PCI-DSS][124]\n* [Zero Trust][125]\n* two columns\n* Resources\n* [All Resources][126]\n* [Blog][127]\n* [FAQ][128]\n* [Glossary][129]\n* About Us\n* [About Asimily][130]\n* [Careers][131]\n* [Leadership][132]\n* [Partners][133]\n* [Contact Us][134]\n\n\u00a9 2026 Asimily All Rights Reserved.\n\n[ Privacy Policy ][135]\n[ Product Security ][136]\n\n[1]: https://asimily.com\n[2]: #\n[3]: https://asimily.com/product/overview/\n[4]: https://asimily.com/product/risk-mitigation/\n[5]: https://asimily.com/product/segmentation-orchestration/\n[6]: https://asimily.com/product/inventory-visibility/\n[7]: https://asimily.com/product/vulnerability-prioritization/\n[8]: https://asimily.com/product/threat-response/\n[9]: https://asimily.com/product/governance-risk-compliance/\n[10]: https://asimily.com/product/configuration-control/\n[11]: https://asimily.com/product/iot-patching/\n[12]: https://asimily.com/product/operational-efficiency/\n[13]: https://asimily.com/product/risk-modeling/\n[14]: https://asimily.com/product/integrations/\n[15]: #\n[16]: https://asimily.com/industries/energy-utilities/\n[17]: https://asimily.com/industries/financial-services/\n[18]: https://asimily.com/industries/government/\n[19]: https://asimily.com/industries/healthcare/\n[20]: https://asimily.com/industries/higher-education/\n[21]: https://asimily.com/industries/hospitality-iot-security/\n[22]: https://asimily.com/industries/life-sciences/\n[23]: https://asimily.com/industries/manufacturing/\n[24]: https://asimily.com/industries/retail/\n[25]: https://asimily.com/industries/transportation/\n[26]: #\n[27]: https://asimily.com/solutions/automated-iot-visibility-deep-categorization/\n[28]: https://asimily.com/solutions/iot-device-detail-enrichment/\n[29]: https://asimily.com/solutions/continuous-iot-vulnerability-detection/\n[30]: https://asimily.com/solutions/risk-based-iot-vulnerability-prioritization/\n[31]: https://asimily.com/solutions/iot-device-prioritization-by-risk/\n[32]: https://asimily.com/solutions/efficient-security-risk-mitigation-workflows/\n[33]: https://asimily.com/solutions/network-segmentation-and-microsegmentation/\n[34]: https://asimily.com/solutions/fda-recalls-and-security-advisories/\n[35]: https://asimily.com/solutions/medical-device-utilization/\n[36]: https://asimily.com/solutions/pre-purchase-security-risk-avoidance/\n[37]: https://asimily.com/solutions/risk-reduction-services/\n[38]: https://asimily.com/solutions/ot-security/\n[39]: https://asimily.com/solutions/iot-risk-simulator/\n[40]: https://asimily.com/solutions/incident-response-readiness-with-packet-capture/\n[41]: https://asimily.com/solutions/it-capabilities/\n[42]: https://asimily.com/compliance-cmmc/\n[43]: https://asimily.com/compliance-cyberscope/\n[44]: https://asimily.com/compliance-dora/\n[45]: https://asimily.com/compliance-fda/\n[46]: https://asimily.com/compliance-hipaa/\n[47]: https://asimily.com/compliance-mitre-attack-framework/\n[48]: https://asimily.com/compliance-nerc-cip/\n[49]: https://asimily.com/compliance-nis2-directive/\n[50]: https://asimily.com/compliance-nist-csf/\n[51]: https://asimily.com/compliance-pci-dss/\n[52]: https://asimily.com/compliance-zero-trust-security-framework/\n[53]: #\n[54]: https://asimily.com/resources/\n[55]: https://asimily.com/blog/\n[56]: https://asimily.com/resources/faq/\n[57]: https://asimily.com/press/\n[58]: https://asimily.com/resources/glossary/\n[59]: #\n[60]: https://asimily.com/about-us/\n[61]: https://asimily.com/about-us/careers/\n[62]: https://asimily.com/about-us/partners/\n[63]: https://asimily.com/about-us/leadership/\n[64]: https://asimily.com/contact-us/\n[65]: https://asimily.com/request-a-demo/\n[66]: #weglot_switcher\n[67]: https://asimily.com/de/solutions/iot-device-prioritization-by-risk/\n[68]: https://asimily.com/request-a-demo/?utm_source=header&utm_medium=requestdemoCTA\n[69]: https://asimily.com/how-to-choose-the-right-iomt-security-solution-2026/\n[70]: https://asimily.com/blog/track-and-prioritize-real-world-vulnerabilities\n[71]: https://asimily.com/blog/iot-security-mitigate-the-risk-of-device-sprawl/\n[72]: https://gtnr.io/zbH4YrPMB\n[73]: https://gtnr.io/Q5IfCllF6\n[74]: https://gtnr.io/MwH8p7Hjf\n[75]: https://gtnr.io/HUFAfi6ha\n[76]: https://gtnr.io/B2BrW6Zto\n[77]: https://asimily.com/product/overview/\n[78]: https://asimily.com/product/risk-mitigation/\n[79]: https://asimily.com/product/inventory-visibility/\n[80]: https://asimily.com/product/vulnerability-prioritization/\n[81]: https://asimily.com/product/threat-response/\n[82]: https://asimily.com/product/segmentation-orchestration/\n[83]: https://asimily.com/product/iot-patching/\n[84]: https://asimily.com/product/configuration-control/\n[85]: https://asimily.com/product/risk-modeling/\n[86]: https://asimily.com/product/governance-risk-compliance/\n[87]: https://asimily.com/product/operational-efficiency/\n[88]: https://asimily.com/product/integrations/\n[89]: https://asimily.com/industries/energy-utilities/\n[90]: https://asimily.com/industries/financial-services/"
