            "text": "][1]\n* [Platform][2]\n* * * [Overview][3]\n* [Risk Mitigation][4]\n* [Segmentation Orchestration][5]\n* [Inventory and Visibility][6]\n* [Vulnerability Prioritization][7]\n* [Threat and Response][8]\n* [Governance, Risk, and Compliance][9]\n* * * [Configuration Control][10]\n* [IoT Patching][11]\n* [Operational Efficiency][12]\n* [Risk Modeling][13]\n* [Integrations][14]\n* [Industries][15]\n* * * [Energy and Utilities][16]\n* [Financial Services][17]\n* [Government][18]\n* [Healthcare][19]\n* [Higher Education][20]\n* [Hospitality][21]\n* [Life Sciences][22]\n* [Manufacturing][23]\n* [Retail][24]\n* [Transportation and Logistics][25]\n* [Solutions][26]\n* * * #### Connected Device Visibility\n* [Automated IoT Visibility And Deep Categorization][27]\n* [IoT Device Detail Enrichment][28]\n* * #### Vulnerability Detection And Mitigation\n* [Continuous IoT Vulnerability Detection][29]\n* [Risk-based IoT Vulnerability Prioritization][30]\n* [Device Prioritization by Risk][31]\n* [Efficient Mitigation Workflows][32]\n* [Network Segmentation and Microsegmentation][33]\n* * #### IoMT\n* [FDA Recalls and Security Advisories][34]\n* [Medical Device Utilization][35]\n* [IoMT Pre-Purchase Risk Avoidance][36]\n* [Risk Reduction Services][37]\n* * #### IT, IoT and OT\n* [OT Security][38]\n* [IoT Risk Simulator][39]\n* [Incident Response Readiness with Packet Capture][40]\n* [Asimily for IT][41]\n* * #### Compliance and Regulation\n* [CMMC][42]\n* [Cyberscope][43]\n* [DORA][44]\n* [FDA][45]\n* [HIPAA][46]\n* [MITRE ATT&CK][47]\n* [NERC CIP][48]\n* [NIS2][49]\n* [NIST CSF 2.0][50]\n* [PCI-DSS][51]\n* [Zero Trust][52]\n* [Resources][53]\n* * * [All Resources][54]\n* [Blog][55]\n* [FAQ][56]\n* [Press][57]\n* [Glossary][58]\n* [About Us][59]\n* * * [About Asimily][60]\n* [Careers][61]\n* [Partners][62]\n* [Leadership][63]\n* [Contact Us][64]\n* [Request Demo][65]\n* [EN][66]\n* [DE][67]\n[ Request Demo ][68]\n\n# How to Choose the Right\n# IoT Security Solution in 2026\n\nProtecting the growing IoT architecture\nin a complicated security environment\n\n[ Get The Whitepaper ][69]\n\nSimple. Centralized. Fast\n\n## How Asimily Approaches Advisories and Recalls\n\nRecalls and security advisories can target devices, technologies, software versions, or more. Any\ndevice can be hit by a recall at any time. Prioritized remediation and monitoring can help your\nclinical readiness stay high. All of this happens quickly and efficiently, keeping the time burden\nsmall while still keeping you ahead of attackers.\n\n### Simple\n\nRecalls should be easy to learn about, understand, and execute. Asimily parses each recall into\nuseful, searchable, sortable, and assignable information to help execute the required change quickly\nand easily.\n\n### Centralized\n\nTypically, hospitals rely on centralized health care technology-skilled resources to handle recalls,\nmaintenance, and other upgrade needs. Those same scarce resources \u2013 employees or contractors \u2013 need\na single point of truth for which recalls exist, are still relevant, and can be done today.\n\n### Fast\n\nRecall notices from the FDA (and Emtec, for subscribers) quickly appear in the Asimily portal,\nassociated with the relevant devices for your next action.\n\n### Accurate Utilization Data Improves Captial Planning\n\nDiscover how Asimily provides granular insight into device location and utilization metrics,\nempowering hospitals to strategically plan operations.\n\n[ See How ][70]\n\n### Collaboration Between HTM and Security Teams\n\nHTM and cybersecurity teams need to collaborate better and utilize each other\u2019s strengths and\nexpertise to secure hospitals. They can do this best by thoroughly planning and managing the\ninventory, the vulnerabilities, and incident response. Tight collaboration in these three areas can\nbuild a strong foundation when done right.\n\n[ Dive Deeper ][71]\n[How HTM Can Work with Security Teams to Defend HDOs]\n\n#### Our Gartner Peer Insights Reviews\n\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Peer Insights Review 4976678] ][72]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Peer Insights Review 511214] ][73]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Review 4925308] ][74]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Review 4959932] ][75]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Review 4959378] ][76]\n[Previous slide]\n[Next slide]\n* Platform\n* [Overview][77]\n* [Risk Mitigation][78]\n* [Inventory and Visibility][79]\n* [Vulnerability Prioritization][80]\n* [Threat and Response][81]\n* [Segmentation Orchestration][82]\n* [IoT Patching][83]\n* [Configuration Control][84]\n* [Risk Modeling][85]\n* [Governance, Risk, and Compliance][86]\n* [Operational Efficiency][87]\n* [Integrations][88]\n* Industries\n* [Energy and Utilities][89]\n* [Financial Services][90]\n* [Government][91]\n* [Healthcare][92]\n* [Higher Education][93]\n* [Hospitality][94]\n* [Life Sciences][95]\n* [Manufacturing][96]\n* [Retail][97]\n* [Transportation and Logistics][98]\n* Solutions\n* column1\n* [Automated IoT Visibility And Deep Categorization][99]\n* [IoT Device Detail Enrichment][100]\n* [Continuous IoT Vulnerability Detection][101]\n* [Risk-based IoT Vulnerability Prioritization][102]\n* [Device Prioritization by Risk][103]\n* [Efficient Mitigation Workflows][104]\n* [Network Segmentation and Microsegmentation][105]\n* column2\n* [FDA Recalls and Security Advisories][106]\n* [Medical Device Utilization][107]\n* [IoMT Pre-Purchase Risk Avoidance][108]\n* [Risk Reduction Services][109]\n* [IoT Risk Simulator][110]\n* [Incident Response Readiness with Packet Capture][111]\n* [Asimily for IT][112]\n* [IoT Security][113]\n* [OT Security][114]\n* [Medical Devices][115]\n* column3\n* [CMMC][116]\n* [Cyberscope][117]\n* [DORA][118]\n* [FDA][119]\n* [HIPAA][120]\n* [MITRE ATT&CK][121]\n* [NERC CIP][122]\n* [NIS2][123]\n* [PCI-DSS][124]\n* [Zero Trust][125]\n* two columns\n* Resources\n* [All Resources][126]\n* [Blog][127]\n* [FAQ][128]\n* [Glossary][129]\n* About Us\n* [About Asimily][130]\n* [Careers][131]