            "text": "][1]\n* [Platform][2]\n* * * [Overview][3]\n* [Risk Mitigation][4]\n* [Segmentation Orchestration][5]\n* [Inventory and Visibility][6]\n* [Vulnerability Prioritization][7]\n* [Threat and Response][8]\n* [Governance, Risk, and Compliance][9]\n* * * [Configuration Control][10]\n* [IoT Patching][11]\n* [Operational Efficiency][12]\n* [Risk Modeling][13]\n* [Integrations][14]\n* [Industries][15]\n* * * [Energy and Utilities][16]\n* [Financial Services][17]\n* [Government][18]\n* [Healthcare][19]\n* [Higher Education][20]\n* [Hospitality][21]\n* [Life Sciences][22]\n* [Manufacturing][23]\n* [Retail][24]\n* [Transportation and Logistics][25]\n* [Solutions][26]\n* * * #### Connected Device Visibility\n* [Automated IoT Visibility And Deep Categorization][27]\n* [IoT Device Detail Enrichment][28]\n* * #### Vulnerability Detection And Mitigation\n* [Continuous IoT Vulnerability Detection][29]\n* [Risk-based IoT Vulnerability Prioritization][30]\n* [Device Prioritization by Risk][31]\n* [Efficient Mitigation Workflows][32]\n* [Network Segmentation and Microsegmentation][33]\n* * #### IoMT\n* [FDA Recalls and Security Advisories][34]\n* [Medical Device Utilization][35]\n* [IoMT Pre-Purchase Risk Avoidance][36]\n* [Risk Reduction Services][37]\n* * #### IT, IoT and OT\n* [OT Security][38]\n* [IoT Risk Simulator][39]\n* [Incident Response Readiness with Packet Capture][40]\n* [Asimily for IT][41]\n* * #### Compliance and Regulation\n* [CMMC][42]\n* [Cyberscope][43]\n* [DORA][44]\n* [FDA][45]\n* [HIPAA][46]\n* [MITRE ATT&CK][47]\n* [NERC CIP][48]\n* [NIS2][49]\n* [NIST CSF 2.0][50]\n* [PCI-DSS][51]\n* [Zero Trust][52]\n* [Resources][53]\n* * * [All Resources][54]\n* [Blog][55]\n* [FAQ][56]\n* [Press][57]\n* [Glossary][58]\n* [About Us][59]\n* * * [About Asimily][60]\n* [Careers][61]\n* [Partners][62]\n* [Leadership][63]\n* [Contact Us][64]\n* [Request Demo][65]\n* [EN][66]\n* [DE][67]\n[ Request Demo ][68]\n\nEfficient Device Utilization Keeps Attack Surfaces Small\n\n# Security Teams\n# Help Deliver Uptime\n\n###### Downtime is Costly\n\nWhen a multimillion-dollar device isn\u2019t being used as much as it could be, that\u2019s costly. For many\ndevices like MRI machines and Gamma Knives, getting the most safe use out of each one is imperative\nfor financial success.\n\n###### Planning is Difficult without Usage Data\n\nFor many IoMT, especially in medical imaging, it is difficult to tell what each device is being used\nfor and when. Without that information, it\u2019s difficult to say what quantity of devices are needed in\nthe future and how they can be best secured.\n\n###### Buying More IoMT is Expensive\n\nOften, the answer to resource shortages is simply buying more. However, without good inventory\ninformation, utilization information, and a history of device usage in a very granular fashion, that\nmight be an expensive way to solve a problem compared to much more affordable ways. In a simple\nexample, do you need more infusion pumps or are they forgotten in a closet? Know for sure.\n\n### How to Choose the Right\n### IoT Security Solution in 2026\n\nProtecting the growing IoT architecture\nin a complicated security environment\n\n[ Get The Whitepaper ][69]\n\nInsightful. Comprehensive. Adaptable.\n\n## How Asimily Drives Optimal Medical Device Utilization\n\nAsimily provides device utilization data for any device, on a realistic day/date/time schedule. With\nthat, device utilization makes sense for each device, modality, or department.\n\n### Insightful\n\nRich data, presented well, can make patterns appear that data tables cannot. With actual device use\ndata compared to what it could be, patterns emerge that drive smart spending.\n\n### Comprehensive\n\nEach device needs detailed usage information, which can be detected from network traffic. Where\npossible, such as for imaging, more detailed information such as body part images can also be\nobtained, to more closely link usage to clinical needs and even revenue.\n\n### Adaptable\n\nNot every IoMT device is equal. Running an MRI 24/7 is not feasible, but operating a respirator\ncould be. Each device has to be compared to a logical usage target, which Asimily allows by hour and\nday of the week.\n\n### Accurate Utilization Data Improves Revenue and Resource Allocation\n\nHospitals need to centrally track and manage their connected medical device inventory to limit the\nwaste of underutilization. Part of creating and maintaining this inventory requires using a solution\ndedicated to device discovery and continuous tracking. Discover how Asimily provides granular\ninsight into device location and utilization metrics, empowering hospitals to strategically plan\noperations.\n\n[ See How ][70]\n\n### Benefits of Monitoring Asset Utilization\n\nManaging assets can be a challenge for any healthcare organization. Discover how Asimily can improve\ncapital planning through utilization monitoring.\n\n[ Dive Deeper ][71]\n[Better-Capital-Planning-Through-Utilization-Monitoring-asimily2]\n\n#### Our Gartner Peer Insights Reviews\n\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Peer Insights Review 4976678] ][72]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Peer Insights Review 511214] ][73]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Review 4925308] ][74]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Review 4959932] ][75]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Review 4959378] ][76]\n[Previous slide]\n[Next slide]\n* Platform\n* [Overview][77]\n* [Risk Mitigation][78]\n* [Inventory and Visibility][79]\n* [Vulnerability Prioritization][80]\n* [Threat and Response][81]\n* [Segmentation Orchestration][82]\n* [IoT Patching][83]\n* [Configuration Control][84]\n* [Risk Modeling][85]\n* [Governance, Risk, and Compliance][86]\n* [Operational Efficiency][87]\n* [Integrations][88]\n* Industries\n* [Energy and Utilities][89]\n* [Financial Services][90]\n* [Government][91]\n* [Healthcare][92]\n* [Higher Education][93]\n* [Hospitality][94]\n* [Life Sciences][95]\n* [Manufacturing][96]\n* [Retail][97]\n* [Transportation and Logistics][98]\n* Solutions\n* column1\n* [Automated IoT Visibility And Deep Categorization][99]\n* [IoT Device Detail Enrichment][100]\n* [Continuous IoT Vulnerability Detection][101]\n* [Risk-based IoT Vulnerability Prioritization][102]\n* [Device Prioritization by Risk][103]\n* [Efficient Mitigation Workflows][104]\n* [Network Segmentation and Microsegmentation][105]\n* column2\n* [FDA Recalls and Security Advisories][106]\n* [Medical Device Utilization][107]\n* [IoMT Pre-Purchase Risk Avoidance][108]\n* [Risk Reduction Services][109]\n* [IoT Risk Simulator][110]\n* [Incident Response Readiness with Packet Capture][111]\n* [Asimily for IT][112]\n* [IoT Security][113]\n* [OT Security][114]\n* [Medical Devices][115]\n* column3\n* [CMMC][116]\n* [Cyberscope][117]\n* [DORA][118]\n* [FDA][119]\n* [HIPAA][120]\n* [MITRE ATT&CK][121]\n* [NERC CIP][122]\n* [NIS2][123]\n* [PCI-DSS][124]\n* [Zero Trust][125]\n* two columns\n* Resources\n* [All Resources][126]\n* [Blog][127]\n* [FAQ][128]\n* [Glossary][129]\n* About Us\n* [About Asimily][130]\n* [Careers][131]\n* [Leadership][132]\n* [Partners][133]\n* [Contact Us][134]\n\n\u00a9 2026 Asimily All Rights Reserved.\n\n[ Privacy Policy ][135]\n[ Product Security ][136]\n\n[1]: https://asimily.com\n[2]: #\n[3]: https://asimily.com/product/overview/\n[4]: https://asimily.com/product/risk-mitigation/\n[5]: https://asimily.com/product/segmentation-orchestration/\n[6]: https://asimily.com/product/inventory-visibility/\n[7]: https://asimily.com/product/vulnerability-prioritization/\n[8]: https://asimily.com/product/threat-response/\n[9]: https://asimily.com/product/governance-risk-compliance/\n[10]: https://asimily.com/product/configuration-control/\n[11]: https://asimily.com/product/iot-patching/\n[12]: https://asimily.com/product/operational-efficiency/\n[13]: https://asimily.com/product/risk-modeling/\n[14]: https://asimily.com/product/integrations/\n[15]: #\n[16]: https://asimily.com/industries/energy-utilities/\n[17]: https://asimily.co