            "text": "][1]\n* [Platform][2]\n* * * [Overview][3]\n* [Risk Mitigation][4]\n* [Segmentation Orchestration][5]\n* [Inventory and Visibility][6]\n* [Vulnerability Prioritization][7]\n* [Threat and Response][8]\n* [Governance, Risk, and Compliance][9]\n* * * [Configuration Control][10]\n* [IoT Patching][11]\n* [Operational Efficiency][12]\n* [Risk Modeling][13]\n* [Integrations][14]\n* [Industries][15]\n* * * [Energy and Utilities][16]\n* [Financial Services][17]\n* [Government][18]\n* [Healthcare][19]\n* [Higher Education][20]\n* [Hospitality][21]\n* [Life Sciences][22]\n* [Manufacturing][23]\n* [Retail][24]\n* [Transportation and Logistics][25]\n* [Solutions][26]\n* * * #### Connected Device Visibility\n* [Automated IoT Visibility And Deep Categorization][27]\n* [IoT Device Detail Enrichment][28]\n* * #### Vulnerability Detection And Mitigation\n* [Continuous IoT Vulnerability Detection][29]\n* [Risk-based IoT Vulnerability Prioritization][30]\n* [Device Prioritization by Risk][31]\n* [Efficient Mitigation Workflows][32]\n* [Network Segmentation and Microsegmentation][33]\n* * #### IoMT\n* [FDA Recalls and Security Advisories][34]\n* [Medical Device Utilization][35]\n* [IoMT Pre-Purchase Risk Avoidance][36]\n* [Risk Reduction Services][37]\n* * #### IT, IoT and OT\n* [OT Security][38]\n* [IoT Risk Simulator][39]\n* [Incident Response Readiness with Packet Capture][40]\n* [Asimily for IT][41]\n* * #### Compliance and Regulation\n* [CMMC][42]\n* [Cyberscope][43]\n* [DORA][44]\n* [FDA][45]\n* [HIPAA][46]\n* [MITRE ATT&CK][47]\n* [NERC CIP][48]\n* [NIS2][49]\n* [NIST CSF 2.0][50]\n* [PCI-DSS][51]\n* [Zero Trust][52]\n* [Resources][53]\n* * * [All Resources][54]\n* [Blog][55]\n* [FAQ][56]\n* [Press][57]\n* [Glossary][58]\n* [About Us][59]\n* * * [About Asimily][60]\n* [Careers][61]\n* [Partners][62]\n* [Leadership][63]\n* [Contact Us][64]\n* [Request Demo][65]\n* [EN][66]\n* [DE][67]\n[ Request Demo ][68]\n\nWhat\u2019s Best to Do Next can be Calculated\n\n# Stop Doing the\n# Wrong Thing Next\n\n###### Triaging Mitigation is Hard\n\nMost security teams have too many fixes to execute, all at once. Determining what is best to do next\n\u2013 triage \u2013 is usually left to informal methods. Usually, there\u2019s no single, clear metric that can be\nused to compare potential work.\n\n###### Guesswork is Imprecise\n\nThe risk reduction from any fix requires understanding the role of the device, its current network\nconfiguration, and the real-world exploitability and severity of a vulnerability. That\u2019s more than a\nhuman mind can process, let alone at the scale of IoT device quantities.\n\n###### Poor Triage Choices are Costly\n\nSometimes what seems to be the next best action is not when it comes to risk reduction. Fixing the\nmost recent severe vulnerability might not actually reduce risk due to newly increased\nexploitability of an older vulnerability. Rigorous analyses are necessary. Worse, when IoT devices\nare remote, it gets even more costly to choose the wrong fix first.\n\n### How to Choose the Right\n### IoT Security Solution in 2026\n\nProtecting the growing IoT architecture\nin a complicated security environment\n\n[ Get The Whitepaper ][69]\n\nQuantified. Fast. Integrated\n\n## How Asimily\u2019s IoT Risk Simulator Saves Time\n\nAsimily\u2019s Risk Simulator allows IoT security fixes to be modeled with a click. You\u2019ll easily see the\nbefore and after, to see if that action was worth the time and effort for risk reduction. The simple\n0-10 Risk Score has subcomponents to better understand why risk can be reduced.\n\n### Quantified\n\nRisk scores are precisely calculated based on all available information, even information that might\nnot be known to security team members. That can include real-world exploitability of\nvulnerabilities, the importance of a device to the organization, or the presence of anomalies\nneeding investigation.\n\n### Fast\n\nLike a spreadsheet, the power of scenario analysis relied largely on speed. Being able to take a\nmore secure scenario from imagination to simulation must happen in seconds, so many simulations can\nbe run by an experienced operator. With a click, Risk Simulator does that.\n\n### Integrated\n\nDevice inventory, vulnerabilities, anomalies, threat intelligence, and more are all needed to have a\nholistic view of risk. That information is centralized with Asimily, to make its risk simulation\neasy to operate and use to save time and effort.\n\n### Forecast Risks to Better Avoid Them\n\nWith Asimily, foresight becomes your greatest ally. Envision, predict, and act with unparalleled\nconfidence, and unlock a new era of proactive risk mitigation.\n\n[ How it Works ][70]\n[Asimily IoT Risk Simulator]\n\n### Shadow IoT: How Unmanaged Devices Put Companies at Risk\n\nShadow IT is a major business risk. Every new connected IoT hardware or software increases your\nattack surface. Learn how to secure your shadow IT devices.\n\n[ Learn How ][71]\n[Shadow IoT How Unmanaged Devices Put Companies at Risk]\n\n#### Our Gartner Peer Insights Reviews\n\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Peer Insights Review 4976678] ][72]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Peer Insights Review 511214] ][73]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Review 4925308] ][74]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Review 4959932] ][75]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Review 4959378] ][76]\n[Previous slide]\n[Next slide]\n* Platform\n* [Overview][77]\n* [Risk Mitigation][78]\n* [Inventory and Visibility][79]\n* [Vulnerability Prioritization][80]\n* [Threat and Response][81]\n* [Segmentation Orchestration][82]\n* [IoT Patching][83]\n* [Configuration Control][84]\n* [Risk Modeling][85]\n* [Governance, Risk, and Compliance][86]\n* [Operational Efficiency][87]\n* [Integrations][88]\n* Industries\n* [Energy and Utilities][89]\n* [Financial Services][90]\n* [Government][91]\n* [Healthcare][92]\n* [Higher Education][93]\n* [Hospitality][94]\n* [Life Sciences][95]\n* [Manufacturing][96]\n* [Retail][97]\n* [Transportation and Logistics][98]\n* Solutions\n* column1\n* [Automated IoT Visibility And Deep Categorization][99]\n* [IoT Device Detail Enrichment][100]\n* [Continuous IoT Vulnerability Detection][101]\n* [Risk-based IoT Vulnerability Prioritization][102]\n* [Device Prioritization by Risk][103]\n* [Efficient Mitigation Workflows][104]\n* [Network Segmentation and Microsegmentation][105]\n* column2\n* [FDA Recalls and Security Advisories][106]\n* [Medical Device Utilization][107]\n* [IoMT Pre-Purchase Risk Avoidance][108]\n* [Risk Reduction Services][109]\n* [IoT Risk Simulator][110]\n* [Incident Response Readiness with Packet Capture][111]\n* [Asimily for IT][112]\n* [IoT Security][113]\n* [OT Security][114]\n* [Medical Devices][115]\n* column3\n* [CMMC][116]\n* [Cyberscope][117]\n* [DORA][118]\n* [FDA][119]\n* [HIPAA][120]\n* [MITRE ATT&CK][121]\n* [NERC CIP][122]\n* [NIS2][123]\n* [PCI-DSS][124]\n* [Zero Trust][125]\n* two columns\n* Resources\n* [All Resources][126]\n* [Blog][127]\n* [FAQ][128]\n* [Glossary][129]\n* About Us\n* [About Asimily][130]\n* [Careers][131]\n* [Leadership][132]\n* [Partners][133]\n* [Contact Us][134]\n\n\u00a9 2026 Asimily All Rights Reserved.\n\n[ Privacy Policy ][135]\n[ Product Security ][136]\n\n[1]: https://asimily.com\n[2]: #\n[3]: https://asimily.com/product/overview/\n[4]: https://asimily.com/product/risk-mitigation/\n[5]: https://asimily.com/product/segmentation-orchestration/\n[6]: https://asimily.com/product/inventory-visibility/\n[7]: https://asimily.com/product/vulnerability-prioritization/\n[8]: https://asimily.com/product/threat-response/\n[9]: https://asimily.com/product/governance-risk-compliance/\n[10]: https://asimily.com/product/configuration-control/\n[11]: https://asimily.com/product/iot-patching/\n[12]: https://asimily.com/product/operational-efficiency/\n[13]: https://asimily.com/product/risk-modeling/\n[14]: https://asimily.com/product/integrations/\n[15]: #\n[16]: https://asimily.com/industries/energy-utilities/\n[17]: