            "url": "https://asimily.com/solutions/incident-response-readiness-with-packet-capture/",
            "text": "][1]\n* [Platform][2]\n* * * [Overview][3]\n* [Risk Mitigation][4]\n* [Segmentation Orchestration][5]\n* [Inventory and Visibility][6]\n* [Vulnerability Prioritization][7]\n* [Threat and Response][8]\n* [Governance, Risk, and Compliance][9]\n* * * [Configuration Control][10]\n* [IoT Patching][11]\n* [Operational Efficiency][12]\n* [Risk Modeling][13]\n* [Integrations][14]\n* [Industries][15]\n* * * [Energy and Utilities][16]\n* [Financial Services][17]\n* [Government][18]\n* [Healthcare][19]\n* [Higher Education][20]\n* [Hospitality][21]\n* [Life Sciences][22]\n* [Manufacturing][23]\n* [Retail][24]\n* [Transportation and Logistics][25]\n* [Solutions][26]\n* * * #### Connected Device Visibility\n* [Automated IoT Visibility And Deep Categorization][27]\n* [IoT Device Detail Enrichment][28]\n* * #### Vulnerability Detection And Mitigation\n* [Continuous IoT Vulnerability Detection][29]\n* [Risk-based IoT Vulnerability Prioritization][30]\n* [Device Prioritization by Risk][31]\n* [Efficient Mitigation Workflows][32]\n* [Network Segmentation and Microsegmentation][33]\n* * #### IoMT\n* [FDA Recalls and Security Advisories][34]\n* [Medical Device Utilization][35]\n* [IoMT Pre-Purchase Risk Avoidance][36]\n* [Risk Reduction Services][37]\n* * #### IT, IoT and OT\n* [OT Security][38]\n* [IoT Risk Simulator][39]\n* [Incident Response Readiness with Packet Capture][40]\n* [Asimily for IT][41]\n* * #### Compliance and Regulation\n* [CMMC][42]\n* [Cyberscope][43]\n* [DORA][44]\n* [FDA][45]\n* [HIPAA][46]\n* [MITRE ATT&CK][47]\n* [NERC CIP][48]\n* [NIS2][49]\n* [NIST CSF 2.0][50]\n* [PCI-DSS][51]\n* [Zero Trust][52]\n* [Resources][53]\n* * * [All Resources][54]\n* [Blog][55]\n* [FAQ][56]\n* [Press][57]\n* [Glossary][58]\n* [About Us][59]\n* * * [About Asimily][60]\n* [Careers][61]\n* [Partners][62]\n* [Leadership][63]\n* [Contact Us][64]\n* [Request Demo][65]\n* [EN][66]\n* [DE][67]\n[ Request Demo ][68]\n\nOT/IoT Traffic Data Enables the Entire Process\n\n# Incident Response\n# Needs Rich Data Fast\n\n###### Too Much Data\n\nRecording every packet from every OT/IoT device is prohibitively expensive and difficult.\nOrganizations have to be selective about what network traffic they record at full packet-level\nfidelity.\n\n###### Difficult to Launch\n\nWhen a device anomaly requires investigation, immediate data capture is essential. Automation can\nfacilitate this process. However, if the packet capture system is separate from the monitoring\nsystem, it may hinder responsiveness and result in data loss.\n\n###### Costly\n\nGetting IoT/OT device data is a necessary early step for the typical incident responder. Without\nreadiness, it can be very expensive (and slow) to set up the software, network access, and secure\ndestination storage.\n\n### How to Choose the Right\n### IoT Security Solution in 2026\n\nProtecting the growing IoT architecture\nin a complicated security environment\n\n[ Get The Whitepaper ][69]\n\nFast, Centralized, Easy\n\n## How to Improve Incident Response Readiness\n\nGrowing OT/IoT inventories bring increased Incident Response readiness requirements. Whether for\ngovernance requirements, security best practices, or both, better Incident Response saves time and\nmoney while reducing the burden on team resources.\n\n### Fast\n\nIncident Response starts with an anomaly that needs investigation. Whether that anomaly is detected\nautomatically by Asimily or manually by your own policies, a first and fast step should be to start\ncapturing data for the questionable OT/ IoT Device for Incident Responders.\n\n### Centralized\n\nWith so many different devices and network segments, having a centralized place with known access to\nOT/IoT traffic is essential. Also, it\u2019s the logical place for packet capture \u2013 a centralized\nlocation that already had access to device traffic. No context hopping between applications is\nneeded.\n\n### Easy\n\nTypically, the Asimily platform will be the first place to diagnose an anomaly due to its\ncomprehensive data, timeline, and reach for OT/IoT devices. As a result, it\u2019s also the right place\nto start preparing for incident responders\u2019 first need \u2013 data about any suspect OT/IoT (or IT for\nthat matter).\n\n### The Necessity of Continuous Vulnerability Detection\n\nAccurately discovering and patching vulnerabilities is one of the biggest issues with securing\nInternet of Things (IoT) devices. Finding these weaknesses in the device firmware or in the\ncommunication protocols and mitigating them quickly can mean the difference between a secure network\nand one that\u2019s open to cyberattackers. This work is unfortunately complicated by the number of IoT\ndevices. With continuous vulnerability detection, organizations gain a more accurate picture of what\npossible weaknesses there are in their IoT devices on a more consistent basis.\n\n[ See Why ][70]\n[The Necessity of Continuous Vulnerability Detection]\n\n### Strong IoT Security Requires Effective Forensic Analysis Capabilities\n\nForensic analysis as a practice also helps security teams evaluate their defenses and discover\npossible weaknesses in their posture management. Any effective forensic investigation into a\ncyberattack, whether successful or not, includes that element of evaluation. So it\u2019s imperative that\nthere is good data collected from every aspect of the network, including the IoT devices that may\nstymie investigations because of the challenge of collecting data.\n\n[ Dive Deeper ][71]\n[Strong IoT Security Requires Effective Forensic Analysis Capabilities]\n\n#### Our Gartner Peer Insights Reviews\n\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Peer Insights Review 4976678] ][72]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Peer Insights Review 511214] ][73]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Review 4925308] ][74]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Review 4959932] ][75]\n[ [Asimily 5 Star Gartner Review 4959378] ][76]\n[Previous slide]\n[Next slide]\n* Platform\n* [Overview][77]\n* [Risk Mitigation][78]\n* [Inventory and Visibility][79]\n* [Vulnerability Prioritization][80]\n* [Threat and Response][81]\n* [Segmentation Orchestration][82]\n* [IoT Patching][83]\n* [Configuration Control][84]\n* [Risk Modeling][85]\n* [Governance, Risk, and Compliance][86]\n* [Operational Efficiency][87]\n* [Integrations][88]\n* Industries\n* [Energy and Utilities][89]\n* [Financial Services][90]\n* [Government][91]\n* [Healthcare][92]\n* [Higher Education][93]\n* [Hospitality][94]\n* [Life Sciences][95]\n* [Manufacturing][96]\n* [Retail][97]\n* [Transportation and Logistics][98]\n* Solutions\n* column1\n* [Automated IoT Visibility And Deep Categorization][99]\n* [IoT Device Detail Enrichment][100]\n* [Continuous IoT Vulnerability Detection][101]\n* [Risk-based IoT Vulnerability Prioritization][102]\n* [Device Prioritization by Risk][103]\n* [Efficient Mitigation Workflows][104]\n* [Network Segmentation and Microsegmentation][105]\n* column2\n* [FDA Recalls and Security Advisories][106]\n* [Medical Device Utilization][107]\n* [IoMT Pre-Purchase Risk Avoidance][108]\n* [Risk Reduction Services][109]\n* [IoT Risk Simulator][110]\n* [Incident Response Readiness with Packet Capture][111]\n* [Asimily for IT][112]\n* [IoT Security][113]\n* [OT Security][114]\n* [Medical Devices][115]\n* column3\n* [CMMC][116]\n* [Cyberscope][117]\n* [DORA][118]\n* [FDA][119]\n* [HIPAA][120]\n* [MITRE ATT&CK][121]\n* [NERC CIP][122]\n* [NIS2][123]\n* [PCI-DSS][124]\n* [Zero Trust][125]\n* two columns\n* Resources\n* [All Resources][126]\n* [Blog][127]\n* [FAQ][128]\n* [Glossary][129]\n* About Us\n* [About Asimily][130]\n* [Careers][131]\n* [Leadership][132]\n* [Partners][133]\n* [Contact Us][134]\n\n\u00a9 2026 Asimily All Rights Reserved.\n\n[ Privacy Policy ][135]\n[ Product Security ][136]\n\n[1]: https://asimily.com\n[2]: #\n[3]: https://asimily.com/product/overview/\n[4]: https://asimily.com/product/risk-mitigation/\n[5]: https://asimily.com/product/segmentation-orchestration/\n[6]: https