            "text": "][1]\n* [Platform][2]\n* * * [Overview][3]\n* [Risk Mitigation][4]\n* [Segmentation Orchestration][5]\n* [Inventory and Visibility][6]\n* [Vulnerability Prioritization][7]\n* [Threat and Response][8]\n* [Governance, Risk, and Compliance][9]\n* * * [Configuration Control][10]\n* [IoT Patching][11]\n* [Operational Efficiency][12]\n* [Risk Modeling][13]\n* [Integrations][14]\n* [Industries][15]\n* * * [Energy and Utilities][16]\n* [Financial Services][17]\n* [Government][18]\n* [Healthcare][19]\n* [Higher Education][20]\n* [Hospitality][21]\n* [Life Sciences][22]\n* [Manufacturing][23]\n* [Retail][24]\n* [Transportation and Logistics][25]\n* [Solutions][26]\n* * * #### Connected Device Visibility\n* [Automated IoT Visibility And Deep Categorization][27]\n* [IoT Device Detail Enrichment][28]\n* * #### Vulnerability Detection And Mitigation\n* [Continuous IoT Vulnerability Detection][29]\n* [Risk-based IoT Vulnerability Prioritization][30]\n* [Device Prioritization by Risk][31]\n* [Efficient Mitigation Workflows][32]\n* [Network Segmentation and Microsegmentation][33]\n* * #### IoMT\n* [FDA Recalls and Security Advisories][34]\n* [Medical Device Utilization][35]\n* [IoMT Pre-Purchase Risk Avoidance][36]\n* [Risk Reduction Services][37]\n* * #### IT, IoT and OT\n* [OT Security][38]\n* [IoT Risk Simulator][39]\n* [Incident Response Readiness with Packet Capture][40]\n* [Asimily for IT][41]\n* * #### Compliance and Regulation\n* [CMMC][42]\n* [Cyberscope][43]\n* [DORA][44]\n* [FDA][45]\n* [HIPAA][46]\n* [MITRE ATT&CK][47]\n* [NERC CIP][48]\n* [NIS2][49]\n* [NIST CSF 2.0][50]\n* [PCI-DSS][51]\n* [Zero Trust][52]\n* [Resources][53]\n* * * [All Resources][54]\n* [Blog][55]\n* [FAQ][56]\n* [Press][57]\n* [Glossary][58]\n* [About Us][59]\n* * * [About Asimily][60]\n* [Careers][61]\n* [Partners][62]\n* [Leadership][63]\n* [Contact Us][64]\n* [Request Demo][65]\n* [EN][66]\n* [DE][67]\n[ Request Demo ][68]\n\nProtecting Technology that Saves Lives\n\n# Securing Vital Medical Devices\n\nInternet-connected medical devices deliver unparalleled patient care, but they are a top target for\ncyber criminals. Safeguard your healthcare operations without disrupting care.\n\n[ Request a Demo ][69]\n[Better Capital Planning Through Utilization Monitoring]\n\nSee, Prevent, Minimize, and Model IoT Risks\n\n## Protect Every Connected Device\n\n### Know Every IoT Device\n\nKeep an accurate inventory of current and new devices, using safe, passive traffic monitoring.\nDevices are classified and you can customize each one.\n\n[IoT]\n\n### Anticipate Threats Proactively\n\nStaying one step ahead of cyber criminals is non-negotiable. Rely on us to discover, inspect, and\nbuttress your connected devices for peak performance and maximum security.\n\n### Acknowledge Risks Without Sacrificing Functionality\n\nPatient care should never rest, and neither should vigilance. We monitor all connected devices in\nyour environment for anomalies and alert you of unusual traffic or communications 24/7.\n\n[IoT Device Security]\n\n## How and Why Medical Devices Get Hacked\n\n### Ransomware\n\nAs more patient data is stored on connected devices and hospitals rely on these devices, it becomes\nmore enticing for cyber criminals to hold the data for ransom.\n\n### Legacy Systems\n\nOutdated medical devices often lack modern security measures, making them prime targets for hackers.\n\n### Target Quantity\n\nWith over 10 billion IoMT targets, some are bound to be attacked successfully.\n\n### Mass Produced\n\nMedical devices are needed in such high quantities that security testing is not always prioritized\nto ship on time, increasing the risk of defects that could lead to vulnerabilities.\n\n### Poorly Guarded\n\nHealthcare professionals wear many hats, and IT expert is not always one of them. Manufacturers\noften prioritize ease of use over security, leading to vulnerabilities.\n\n[ Request a Demo ][70]\n\n### Secure Every IoT Device.\n### Automatically.\n\nCyber threats move fast \u2014 so should you. Asimily gives instant inventory and smart, prioritized risk\nmitigation insights for every IoT, OT, and IoMT device \u2014 so you can take action before threats\nstrike.\n\n[ Schedule a Demo ][71]\n\n### Frequently Asked Questions About OT Security\n\nWhat makes OT security different from IT security?\n\nOT security must prioritize availability and safety over confidentiality. OT environments include\nspecialized protocols (Modbus, DNP3, CIP), legacy systems that can\u2019t be patched, and devices with\n20+ year lifecycles. Asimily\u2019s platform addresses these unique OT security challenges with\nspecialized protocol parsing, compensating controls, and risk-based prioritization designed for\noperational technology.\n\nHow does Asimily handle OT security for legacy equipment?\n\nLegacy OT devices often can\u2019t be updated or replaced. Asimily provides compensating controls through\nnetwork segmentation recommendations, configuration monitoring to detect changes, and behavior\nanalysis to identify anomalies\u2014all without requiring agents or modifications to your OT systems. Our\npassive monitoring ensures zero impact on production systems.\n\nDoes Asimily integrate with our existing security tools?\n\nYes. Asimily\u2019s OT security platform provides robust integrations with SIEM, SOAR, CMDB, and\nvulnerability management platforms. Unlike competitors with limited on-premises integration\ncapabilities, we deliver the unified IT/OT inventory and risk visibility your security operations\ncenter needs to protect against cross-domain attacks.\n\nHow does Asimily help identify and protect our most critical OT assets?\n\nAsimily goes beyond basic asset inventory by identifying your \u201ccrown jewel\u201d OT systems\u2014the devices\nand processes most critical to your operations. Our platform uses contextual analysis to understand\ndevice criticality based on its role in production, safety implications, revenue impact, and\nposition within your Purdue Model architecture. By mapping device relationships and dependencies, we\nhelp you prioritize security investments and implement appropriate compensating controls for your\nmost vital OT infrastructure, whether it\u2019s an aging production line generating significant revenue\nor safety-critical systems in hazardous manufacturing processes.\n\nWhat visibility does Asimily provide into OT security risks across our entire network?\n\nComprehensive OT security requires understanding risks from all network points\u2014not just OT devices\nin isolation. Asimily provides complete visibility into your entire attack surface, including IT/OT\nconvergence points, network neighbors that could serve as pivot points for attackers, and IoT\ndevices that interact with your OT environment. Our platform identifies risks from adjacent systems\nlike HVAC controllers or building management systems that attackers historically exploit to reach\ncritical OT networks. This holistic view ensures you understand and can mitigate risks from any\npotential entry point, not just direct OT vulnerabilities.\n* Platform\n* [Overview][72]\n* [Risk Mitigation][73]\n* [Inventory and Visibility][74]\n* [Vulnerability Prioritization][75]\n* [Threat and Response][76]\n* [Segmentation Orchestration][77]\n* [IoT Patching][78]\n* [Configuration Control][79]\n* [Risk Modeling][80]\n* [Governance, Risk, and Compliance][81]\n* [Operational Efficiency][82]\n* [Integrations][83]\n* Industries\n* [Energy and Utilities][84]\n* [Financial Services][85]\n* [Government][86]\n* [Healthcare][87]\n* [Higher Education][88]\n* [Hospitality][89]\n* [Life Sciences][90]\n* [Manufacturing][91]\n* [Retail][92]\n* [Transportation and Logistics][93]\n* Solutions\n* column1\n* [Automated IoT Visibility And Deep Categorization][94]\n* [IoT Device Detail Enrichment][95]\n* [Continuous IoT Vulnerability Detection][96]\n* [Risk-based IoT Vulnerability Prioritization][97]\n* [Device Prioritization by Risk][98]\n* [Efficient Mitigation Workflows][99]\n* [Network Segmentation and Microsegmentation][100]\n* column2\n* [FDA Recalls and Security Advisories][101]\n* [Medical Device Utilization][102]\n* [IoMT Pre-Purchase Risk Avoidance][103]\n* [Risk Reduction Services][104]\n* [IoT Risk Simulator][105]\n* [Incident Response Readiness with Packet Capture][106]\n* [Asimily for IT][107]\n* [IoT Security][108]\n* [OT Security][109]\n* [Medical Devices][110]\n* column3\n* [CMMC][111]\n* [Cyberscope][112]\n* [DORA][113]\n* [FDA][114]\n* [HIPAA][115]\n* [MITRE ATT&CK][116]\n* [NERC CIP][117]\n* [NIS2][118]\n* [PCI-DSS][119]\n* [Zero Trust][120]\n* two columns\n* Resources\n* [All Resources][121]\n* [Blog][122]\n* [FAQ][123]\n* [Glossary][124]\n* About Us\n* [About Asimily][125]\n* [Careers][126]\n* [Leadership][127]\n* [Partners][128]\n* [Contact Us][129]\n\n\u00a9 2026 Asimily All Rights Reserved.\n\n[ Privacy Policy ][130]\n[ Product Security ][131]\n\n[1]: https://asimily.com\n[2]: #\n[3]: https://asimily.com/product/overview/\n[4]: https://asimily.com/product/risk-mitigation/\n[5]: https://asimily.com/product/segmentation-orchestration/\n[6]: https://asimily.com/product/inventory-visibility/\n[7]: https://asimily.com/product/vulnerability-prioritization/\n[8]: https://asimily.com/product/threat-response/\n[9]: https://asimily.com/product/governance-risk-compliance/\n[10]: https://asimily.com/product/configuration-control/\n[11]: https://asimily.com/product/iot-patching/\n[12]: https://asimily.com/product/operational-efficiency/\n[13]: https://asimily.com/product/risk-modeling/\n[14]: https://asimily.com/product/integrations/\n[15]: #\n[16]: https://asimily.com/industries/energy-utilities/\n[17]: https://asimily.com/industries/financial-services/\n[18]: https://asimily.com/industries/government/\n[19]: https://asimily.com/industries/healthcare/\n[20]: https://asimily.com/industries/higher-education/\n[21]: https://asimily.com/industries/hospitality-iot-security/\n[22]: https://asimily.com/industries/life-sciences/\n[23]: https://asimily.com/industries/manufacturing/\n[24]: https://asimily.com/industries/retail/\n[25]: https://asimily.com/industries/transportation/\n[26]: #\n[27]: https://asimily.com/solutions/automated-iot-visibility-deep-categorization/\n[28]: https://asimily.com/solutions/iot-device-detail-enrichment/\n[29]: https://asimily.com/solutions/continuous-iot-vulnerability-detection/\n[30]: https://asimily.com/solutions/risk-based-iot-vulnerability-prioritization/\n[31]: https://asimily.com/solutions/iot-device-prioritization-by-risk/\n[32]: https://asimily.com/solutions/efficient-security-risk-mitigation-workflows/\n[33]: https://asimily.com/solutions/network-segmentation-and-microsegmentation/\n[34]: https://asimily.com/solutions/fda-recalls-and-security-advisories/\n[35]: https://asimily.com/solutions/medical-device-utilization/\n[36]: https://asimily.com/solutions/pre-purchase-security-risk-avoidance/\n[37]: https://asimily.com/solutions/risk-reduction-services/\n[38]: https://asimily.com/solutions/ot-security/\n[39]: https://asimily.com/solutions/iot-risk-simulator/\n[40]: https://asimily.com/solutions/incident-response-readiness-with-packet-capture/\n[41]: https://asimily.com/solutions/it-capabilities/\n[42]: https://asimily.com/compliance-cmmc/\n[43]: https://asimily.com/compliance-cyberscope/\n[44]: https://asimily.com/compliance-dora/\n[45]: https://asimily.com/compliance-fda/\n[46]: https://asimily.com/compliance-hipaa/\n[47]: https://asimily.com/compliance-mitre-attack-framework/\n[48]: https://asimily.com/compliance-nerc-cip/\n[49]: https://asimily.com/compliance-nis2-directive/\n[50]: https://asimily.com/compliance-nist-csf/\n[51]: https://asimily.com/compliance-pci-dss/\n[52]: https://asimily.com/compliance-zero-trust-security-framework/\n[53]: #\n[54]: https://asimily.com/resources/\n[55]: https://asimily.com/blog/\n[56]: https://asimily.com/resources/faq/\n[57]: https://asimily.com/press/\n[58]: https://as