          {
            "url": "https://cyolo.io/case-studies/global-food-manufacturers-journey-to-scalable-secure-remote-access",
            "text": "[ Product ][1]\n[ Solutions ][2]\n\n### By Challenge\n\nRemote Privileged Access for OT/ICS\n][3] [\nSecure Third-Party Access\n][4] [\nIT/OT Alignment\n][5] [\nRegulatory Compliance\n][6]\n\n### By Industry\n\nManufacturing\n][7] [\nEnergy & Utilities\n][8] [\nAI Data Centers\n][9] [\nAll Industries\n][10]\n[ Partners ][11]\nPartner Program\n][12] [\nPartner Ecosystem\n][13] [\nTechnology Integrations\n][14] [\nBecome a Partner\n][15]\n[ Resources ][16]\n\n### Resources\n\n[ See All Resources ][17]\nNews\n][18] [\nPress Releases\n][19] [\nUpcoming Events\n][20] [\nThird Party Reports\n][21] [\nCase Studies\n][22] [\nAt a Glances\n][23] [\nDatasheet\n][24] [\nWhite Papers\n][25] [\nVideos\n][26]\n\n### Featured content\n\nPress Release\n\n#### Cyolo Releases Powerful New Capabilities to Redefine Secure Remote Access for OT\n\n][27] [\nBlog\n\n#### Why VPNs Are a Poor Fit for Vendor Access in OT Manufacturing Environments\n\n][28] [\nWhite Paper\n\n#### The Paradox of Third-Party OT Access: The Surprising Benefits of Trusting Vendors Less\n\n][29] [\nThird Party Report\n\n#### 2026 Gartner\u00ae Market Guide for CPS Secure Remote Access\n\n][30]\n[ Blog ][31]\n[ Company ][32]\nAbout Us\n][33] [\nCareers\n][34]\n[ Support ][35]\n[ Toggle Search ][36]\n[united-states-flag.svg flag] Eng\n[germany-flag.svg flag] De\n[spain-flag.svg flag] Spa\n[france-flag.svg flag] Fre\n[italy-flag.svg flag] Ita\n[ [united-states-flag.svg flag] Eng ][37] [ [germany-flag.svg flag] De ][38] [ [spain-flag.svg flag]\nSpa ][39] [ [france-flag.svg flag] Fre ][40] [ [italy-flag.svg flag] Ita ][41]\n[ Get a Demo ][42]\nClose Menu\n[ Product ][43]\n[ Solutions ][44]\n[ Remote Privileged Access for OT/ICS ][45] [ Third-Party Secure Access ][46] [ IT/OT Alignment\n][47] [ Regulatory Compliance ][48] [ Manufacturing ][49] [ Energy & Utilities ][50] [ Data Centers\n][51] [ All Industries ][52]\n[ Partners ][53]\n[ Partner Program ][54] [ Partner Ecosystem ][55] [ Technology Integrations ][56] [ Become a Partner\n][57]\n[ Resources ][58]\n[ News ][59] [ Press Releases ][60] [ Third-Party Reports ][61] [ Case Studies ][62] [ At a Glances\n][63] [ Datasheets ][64] [ White Papers ][65] [ Videos ][66]\n[ Blog ][67]\n[ Company ][68]\n[ About Us ][69] [ Careers ][70]\n[ Support ][71] [ Search Toggle Search ][72]\nCase Study\n][73]\n3 min read\n\n# A Global Food Manufacturer\u2019s Journey to Scalable, Secure Remote Access\n\n[ Download as PDF ][74]\n[ Download as PDF ][75]\n[ Background: Scaling with Confidence ][76] [ The Catalyst: Unifying a Disjointed Access Landscape\n][77] [ The Evaluation Process: A Collaborative, Cross-Functional Approach ][78] [ What Mattered\nMost: Usability, Scale, and Trust ][79] [ Success Metrics: Cost, Control, and Continuity ][80] [\nConclusion: Secure Access as an Enabler of Manufacturing Excellence ][81] [ About Cyolo ][82]\n\n*Jonathon Gordon of Takepoint Research interviewed the customer and wrote this case study as part of\nthe \"Can Cybersecurity Drive Growth? The Strategic Role of Secure Remote Access in Manufacturing\"\nresearch report.*\n\n[*Download the complete report here*][83]*. *\n\n## Background: Scaling with Confidence\n\nA global food manufacturing company with dozens of facilities across Europe, the Americas, and Asia\nset out to standardize and secure its remote access capabilities. With nearly half of its plant\ninfrastructure located in Europe alone, the organization was under growing pressure to enable safe,\nseamless collaboration with OEMs, service providers, and engineering partners, without compromising\nits operational integrity.\n\nThe driver? A fragmented approach across plants and regions had created visibility blind spots,\ninconsistent user experiences, and growing security risks.\n\n## The Catalyst: Unifying a Disjointed Access Landscape\n\nPreviously, the organization relied on a legacy solution that was functional but far from optimal.\nThe lack of MFA integration, complex logins, and clunky interfaces led to low user satisfaction and\nreduced adoption.* *\n\n*\u201cThe user experience was poor, logins were complex, the platform wasn\u2019t stable, and third parties\nhated it.\u201d*\n\nEach plant was using its own methods to facilitate third-party access, resulting in significant\ngovernance gaps. The business recognized the need for a globally consistent, centrally managed, and\noperationally efficient platform.\n\n[Manufacturing facility producing chocolate]\n\n## The Evaluation Process: A Collaborative, Cross-Functional Approach\n\nTo address these challenges, the organization launched a structured global RFP. Candidates included\nthe incumbent vendor (offering an updated solution), a leading IT services provider with an\nindustrial offering, and a lesser-known remote access provider with strong usability credentials.\n\nThe evaluation went beyond the security team. Global OT leads, local plant engineers, security\narchitects, and standards bodies were brought together to assess fit and functionality through live\npilots at four to five sites worldwide.\n\n### \"*It wasn\u2019t just about what the security team thought. We had input from the people in the\n### plants, from our standards team, and from those who would actually use the system every day.\n### That collective validation gave us confidence.\"*\n\n**Cyolo \u2013 described as \u201cthe dark horse\u201d \u2013 emerged as the unanimous choice, winning over stakeholders\nwith its usability, compatibility, and flexibility.**\n\n## What Mattered Most: Usability, Scale, and Trust\n\nWhat sealed the decision was simplicity and scale:\n* **No plugins or installations: **users accessed the system via browser\n* **Cross-device support**: compatible with managed and unmanaged PCs and tablets\n* **Contextual access control: **users only saw what they were meant to see\n* **Minimal onboarding time**: enabling quick adoption by internal teams and third parties alike\n\n### *\u201cIt\u2019s the first time we\u2019ve had third parties ask if they could use it for more. Usually, it\u2019s\n### grumbling. But now the reaction is: \u2018Oh, this is quite good. Can we use it for X as well?\u201d*\n\nAdministratively, the team deployed a federated, multi-tenant model, delegating control to 100+ OT\npersonnel across regions, replacing the previous bottlenecked model where only a few admins could\nexecute changes.\n\n### *\u201cWe trusted the team, gave them access, and built in training and documentation. So far, that\n### trust has been rewarded.\u201d*\n\n## Success Metrics: Cost, Control, and Continuity\n\nThe results speak for themselves:\n* **Hundreds of daily users**, including both internal staff and external vendors\n* **Rapid onboarding and operational adoption**, even among non-technical users\n* **Reduction in support tickets**, login issues, and access delays\n* **Compliance alignment** across OT security standards without disruption\n* **Cost-effective transition**, with year-one savings exceeding implementation costs\n\n### *\u201cThe transition costs were more than covered in the first year. We let the team choose what was\n### best for the business, because we knew we could afford all the options.\u201d*\n\nThe rollout was not only secure and scalable, but it was culturally resonant. Built on trust,\ncollaboration, and transparency, the solution embedded itself into daily operations across the\nglobal footprint.\n\n## Conclusion: Secure Access as an Enabler of Manufacturing Excellence\n\nThis case illustrates a key insight from our broader research: **the value of secure remote access\nis magnified when solutions are selected collaboratively, aligned to real-world use cases, and\ndesigned around the user experience.**\n\nWhat began as an effort to close security gaps evolved into a platform for **operational resilience,\ninnovation, and trust **\u2013** **and a textbook example of what it looks like when cybersecurity aligns\nwith business value.\n\n## About Cyolo\n\nCyolo provides secure remote privileged access for cyber-physical systems (CPS). Our solution\nenables industrial enterprises to simply connect employees and third-party vendors to critical\nassets.\n\nCyolo delivers improved security, productivity, and operational agility \u2013 without compromise. To\nlearn more, visit [https://cyolo.io.][84]\n\nMore Case Studies\n[See All Case Studies][85]\nCase Study\n\n#### How Lillehammer Municipality Improved the Security of its Water and Wastewater Operations\n\nRead More\n][86] [\n[Woman working on laptop in an automotive assembly plant]\nCase Study\n\n#### Modernizing Secure Remote Access for a Global Automotive Manufacturer\n\nRead More\n][87] [\nCase Study\n\n#### How Italian Manufacturer Maddalena Modernized Secure Remote Access While Cutting Costs by 70%\n\nRead More\n][88]\n\n##### Product Demo\n\n## See how the Cyolo PRO remote access solution works.\n\nEnsuring secure remote access to on-prem, isolated, and cloud-connected OT environments is easier\nthan you think. See for yourself.\n\n[ Request a Demo ][89]\nCyolo provides secure remote privileged access for cyber-physical systems and OT. Our solution\nenables industrial enterprises to connect employees and third-party vendors to critical assets in a\nway that's secure, safe, and surprisingly simple.\n\nGet in Touch: [**Contact Us**][90]\n\n###### [Product][91]\n\n[Product Overview][92]\n[Industrial Remote Privileged Access][93]\n[Third Party Secure Access][94]\n[Industries][95]\n\n###### [Company][96]\n\n[About Us][97]\n[Careers][98]\n[Partners][99]\n\n###### [Resources][100]\n\n[Blog][101]\n[Press Releases][102]\nCopyright \u00a9 2026 Cyolo LTD. All rights reserved.\n[Cyolo Privacy Policy][103] [Cookie Policy][104] [Vulnerability Disclosure Policy][105]\n\n[1]: /product\n[2]: #\n[3]: /remote-privileged-access-for-ot-ics\n[4]: /safely-manage-3rd-party-access\n[5]: /sra-built-for-ot-backed-by-it\n[6]: /regulatory-compliance\n[7]: /industries/manufacturing\n[8]: /industries/energy-utilities\n[9]: /industries/ai-data-centers\n[10]: /industries\n[11]: #\n[12]: /partners-program\n[13]: /partner-ecosystem\n[14]: /technology-integrations\n[15]: /become-a-partner\n[16]: /resources\n[17]: /resources\n[18]: /news\n[19]: /press-releases\n[20]: /events\n[21]: /third-party-reports\n[22]: /case-studies\n[23]: /at-a-glance\n[24]: /datasheets/enable-privileged-remote-access-with-cyolo-pro\n[25]: /white-papers\n[26]: /videos\n[27]: /press-releases/cyolo-releases-powerful-new-capabilities-to-redefine-secure-remote-access-for-\n[28]: /blog/why-vpns-are-a-poor-fit-for-vendor-access-in-ot-manufacturing-environments\n[29]: /white-papers/how-to-take-control-of-third-party-ot-access\n[30]: /third-party-reports/gartner-market-guide-for-cps-secure-remote-access-2026\n[31]: /blog\n[32]: /company\n[33]: /company\n[34]: /careers\n[35]: https://support.cyolo.io/hc/en-us\n[36]: /search\n[37]: /\n[38]: /de\n[39]: /sp\n[40]: /fr\n[41]: /it\n[42]: /demo\n[43]: /product\n[44]: #\n[45]: /remote-privileged-access-for-ot-ics\n[46]: /safely-manage-3rd-party-access\n[47]: /sra-built-for-ot-backed-by-it\n[48]: /regulatory-compliance\n[49]: /industries/manufacturing\n[50]: /industries/energy-utilities\n[51]: /industries/ai-data-centers\n[52]: /industries\n[53]: #\n[54]: /partners-program\n[55]: /partner-ecosystem\n[56]: /technology-integrations\n[57]: /become-a-partner\n[58]: /resources\n[59]: /news\n[60]: /press-releases\n[61]: /third-party-reports\n[62]: /case-studies\n[63]: /at-a-glance\n[64]: /datasheets/enable-privileged-remote-access-with-cyolo-pro\n[65]: /white-papers\n[66]: /videos\n[67]: /blog\n[68]: /company\n[69]: /company\n[70]: /careers\n[71]: https://support.cyolo.io/hc/en-us\n[72]: /search\n[73]: /case-studies\n[74]: https://info.cyolo.io/hubfs/Case%20Studies/Case%20Study_A%20Global%20Food%20Manufacturer%E2%80\n%99s%20Journey%20to%20Scalable%2c%20Secure%20Remote%20Access.pdf\n[75]: https://info.cyolo.io/hubfs/Case%20Studies/Case%20Study_A%20Global%20Food%20Manufacturer%E2%80\n%99s%20Journey%20to%20Scalable%2c%20Secure%20Remote%20Access.pdf\n[76]: #background-scaling-with-confidence\n[77]: #the-catalyst-unifying-a-disjointed-access-landscape\n[78]: #the-evaluation-process-a-collaborative-cross-functional-approach\n[79]: #what-mattered-most-usability-scale-and-trust\n[80]: #success-metrics-cost-control-and-continuity\n[81]: #conclusion-secure-access-as-an-enabler-of-manufacturing-excellence\n[82]: #about-cyolo\n[83]: https://cy"
