r partners how Huntress has helped them\n\n][112]\nCommunity\n\nGet in touch with the Huntress Community team\n\n][113][\nCommunity\n\nGet in touch with the Huntress Community team\n\n][114]\nCompare Huntress\n][115]\nBitdefender\n][116][\nBitdefender\n][117]\nBlackpoint\n][118][\nBlackpoint\n][119]\nBreach Secure Now!\n][120][\nBreach Secure Now!\n][121]\nCrowdstrike\n][122][\nCrowdstrike\n][123]\nKaseya\n][124][\nKaseya\n][125]\nSentinelOne\n][126][\nSentinelOne\n][127]\nSophos\n][128][\nSophos\n][129]\n[Compare All\n][130][Compare All\n][131]\n* Partners\nPartners\nHUNTRESS HUB\n\nLogin to access top-notch marketing resources, tools, and training.\n\nPartner Portal Login\n[Huntress Cybersecurity]\n][132][\nHUNTRESS HUB\n\nLogin to access top-notch marketing resources, tools, and training.\n\n[Huntress Cybersecurity]\n][133]\nPartners\nMSPs\n\nJoin our partner community to deliver expert-led managed security.\n\n][134][\nMSPs\n\nJoin our partner community to deliver expert-led managed security.\n\n][135]\nResellers\n\nPartner program designed to grow your cybersecurity business.\n\n][136][\nResellers\n\nPartner program designed to grow your cybersecurity business.\n\n][137]\nTech Alliances\n\nDriving innovation through global technology Partnerships\n\n][138][\nTech Alliances\n\nDriving innovation through global technology Partnerships\n\n][139]\nMicrosoft Partnership\n\nA Level-Up for Your Business Security\n\n][140][\nMicrosoft Partnership\n\nA Level-Up for Your Business Security\n\n][141]\n* Company\nCompany\nPress Release\nHuntress Announces Collaboration with Microsoft to Strengthen Cybersecurity for Businesses of All\nSizes\n[Huntress Cybersecurity]\n][142][\nPress Release\nHuntress Announces Collaboration with Microsoft to Strengthen Cybersecurity for Businesses of All\nSizes\n[Huntress Cybersecurity]\n][143]\nOur Story\n\nWe're on a mission to shatter the barriers to enterprise-level security.\n\n][144][\nOur Story\n\nWe're on a mission to shatter the barriers to enterprise-level security.\n\n][145]\nNewsroom\n\nExplore press releases, news articles, media interviews and more.\n\n][146][\nNewsroom\n\nExplore press releases, news articles, media interviews and more.\n\n][147]\nMeet the Team\n\nFounded by former NSA Cyber Operators. Backed by security researchers.\n\n][148][\nMeet the Team\n\nFounded by former NSA Cyber Operators. Backed by security researchers.\n\n][149]\nCareers\n\nReady to shake up the cybersecurity world? Join the hunt.\n\n][150][\nCareers\n\nReady to shake up the cybersecurity world? Join the hunt.\n\n][151]\nAwards\n][152][\nAwards\n][153]\nContact Us\n][154][\nContact Us\n][155]\n* [Portal Login][156]\n* [Support][157]\n* [Blog][158]\n* [Contact][159]\n* [Search][160]\n* [Get a Demo][161]\n* [Start for Free][162]\n[Portal Login][163][Support][164][Blog][165][Contact][166]\nSearchSearch[Close search]\n[Get a Demo][167]\n[Start for Free][168]\n[Glitch effect]\n[Home][169]\nOur Story\n\n# Welcome to the Revolution\n\nWe believe in the power of community, in transparency, and in giving back more than we take. That's\nwhy we're on a mission to shatter the barriers to enterprise-level security.\n\n[Huntress platform]\n\n### 10 Years of Wrecking Hackers\n\nCybersecurity has changed a lot over the last decade, but some things haven\u2019t: We\u2019re still coming up\nwith new ways to wreck hackers, support the community before all else, and protect ALL businesses,\nnot just the 1%.\n\nBut building enterprise-grade cybersecurity for everyone doesn\u2019t happen overnight. Check out how the\nHuntress of today came to be...\n\n[Top Huntress 2025 Announcements ]\n\n** 2025**\n* Celebrated 10 years!\n* Included in the Verizon 2025 DBIR Report\n* [Announced our partnership with Microsoft][170]\n* Launched our partnership with Forte\nRacing\n* Achieved CMMC compliance\n* Named to Forbes America\u2019s Best Startup Employers list\n\n* Made the Built In Best Remote Places to Work list\n* Won the Inc. Best Places to Work award\n* Named to Inc. 5000 Fastest Growing\nPrivate Companies list\n\n** 2024**\n* [Signed CISA Secure By Design pledge][171]\n* Joined CISA JCDC\n* Secured $150M Series D funding\n* Launched Huntress Managed SIEM\n* Reached $100M ARR\n* Won the Inc. Best Places to Work award\n* [Authorized by the Common Vulnerabilities\nand Exposure (CVE) Program as a\nNumbering Authority (CNA)][172]\n\n* Recognized with Microsoft Verified Small\nand Medium Business (SMB) Solution Status\n* [Awarded CRN\u2019s 2024 Product of the Year\nfor Managed ITDR][173]\n\n** 2023**\n* Secured $60M Series C funding\n* Launched MDR for Microsoft 365,\nnow Huntress Managed ITDR\n* Released our first [Threat Report][174]\n* Celebrated 1 year of Huntress SAT\n* Announced SOC2, GDPR, and\nCCPA compliance\n\nSome of our top rapid\n\nresponses of 2023:\n* [CVE-2023-23397][175]\n* [MOVEit][176]\n* [3CX ][177]\n* [PaperCut][178]\n\n** 2022**\n* Launched Huntress Managed EDR\n* Acquired Curricula and Huntress Security\nAwareness Training (SAT) launched\n* Introduced the [Huntress Neighborhood\nWatch program][179]\n* Won the Built In Moxie Award\n\n**2021**\n* Acquired Level Effect to boost EDR\ncapabilities and give partners a holistic\nsecurity view to protect their customers\n* Launched Managed Antivirus\n* Secured $40M Series B funding\n* Launched 24/7 Threat Hunting and\nhost Isolation\n* Learned and shared lessons from the [\nKaseya VSA Supply Chain attack][180]\n\n**2020**\n* Launched the Huntress Security Platform\n* Secured $18M Series A funding\n* Expanded from just footholds to include\n[Ransomware Canaries and External\nRecon][181], adding value and features\nwithout additional cost\n* Grew from 20 to 60 Huntress team members\nto meet partner and customer demand\nand continue our mission\n\n**2019**\n* Aired first episode of Tradecraft\nTuesday, \"Breach Breakdown,\" kicking\noff our popular monthly webinar series\n* Worked with a key partner on an [\nAssisted Remediation][182]\n\n** 2018**\n* Focused on hacker persistence to\nempower our growing community\nas we expanded our partner base\n* Shared our first deep dive into the [\nKaseya VSA vulnerability][183]\n* Reached $100k monthly product\nrevenue\n\n** 2017**\n* Secured a $750k seed round of funding\n* Hosted [Hacking Windows training\nat IT Nation][184]\n* Committed to our \u2018channel-first\u2019 strategy\nto make partners successful in keeping\nmore businesses safe\n\n** 2016**\n* Attended our first MSP tradeshow, IT\nNation\n* Won the [IT Nation Partner Choice Best\nNewcomer award][185]\n\n** 2015**\n* Huntress was born!\n* Accepted into Mach37 with a\n$50k investment\n\n## The Huntress Difference\n\n### Ethical Badasses\n\nFrom accounts payable t"
