            "text": "Webinar - CIP-015 Is Here: Paths to Compliance for Every Organization Register Today\n][1]\n[Support][2]\n\n### SOLUTIONS\n\n][3]\nOT Asset Management\n][4][\nConfiguration & Change Management\n][5][\nPolicy Compliance\n][6][\nVulnerability Management\n][7]\n\n### PLATFORM\n\n][8]\nIndustrial Defender Platform\n][9][\nPhoenix for SMBs\n][10][\nServices\n][11][\nPartners\n][12]\n\n### INDUSTRIES\n\n][13]\nPower\n][14][\nOil & Gas\n][15][\nWater\n][16][\nManufacturing\n][17][\nUS Government\n][18][\nSee all\n][19]\n\n### RESOURCES\n\n][20]\nBlog\n][21][\nPodcast\n][22][\nResource Library\n][23][\nOT Cybersecurity Risk Assessment Calculator\n][24][\nInnovations by Industrial Defender\n][25][\nDeployment\n][26][\nFAQ\n][27]\n\n### COMPANY\n\n][28]\nAbout Us\n][29][\nHow We Compare\n][30][\nDeployment\n][31][\nTeam\n][32][\nEvents\n][33][\nPress\n][34][\nCareers\n][35][\nContact Us\n][36]\n\n### SUPPORT\n\n][37]\n\n### REQUEST DEMO\n\n][38]\nSOLUTIONS\n][39]\nOT Asset Management\n][40]\nConfiguration & Change Management\n][41]\nPolicy Compliance\n][42]\nVulnerability Management\n][43]\nPLATFORM\n][44]\nIndustrial Defender Platform\n][45]\nServices\n][46]\nPartners\n][47]\nINDUSTRIES\n][48]\nPower\n][49]\nOil & Gas\n][50]\nWater\n][51]\nManufacturing\n][52]\nUS Government\n][53]\nSee all\n][54]\nRESOURCES\n][55]\nBlog\n][56]\nPodcast\n][57]\nResource Library\n][58]\nOT Cybersecurity Risk Assessment Calculator\n][59]\nInnovations by Industrial Defender\n][60]\nFAQ\n][61]\nCOMPANY\n][62]\nAbout Us\n][63]\nHow We Compare\n][64]\nTeam\n][65]\nEvents\n][66]\nPress\n][67]\nCareers\n][68]\nContact Us\n][69]\n[Request Demo][70]\nAbout us\n\n# Your Partner in OT Cyber Risk & Compliance\n\nIndustrial Defender has been a leader in OT security and compliance since 2006. U.S. based and\nestablished in 2006, we have built a reputation for being trusted by the largest industrial\norganizations and critical infrastructure operators in the world. Our strength is in providing the\nmost comprehensive OT asset data for managing cyber risk and compliance in operational environments.\n\nHeadquartered outside of Boston, MA, we are a US-based company.\n\n[Get In Touch][71]\nWhy customers choose us\n\n## Industrial Defender has a 99% customer renewal rate.\n\nOur customers continually expand their cybersecurity programs using our scalable platform year after\nyear as they grow and mature. All of our product development and engineering is based in North\nAmerica, with no customers or operations in adversarial nations, and our development team is held to\nthe most stringent cybersecurity standards.\n\n[View Solution Brief][72]\nA single platform for OT asset management and compliance\nHundreds of global deployments at critical infrastructure companies\nA 99% customer renewal rate\nAn industry pioneer\n\n## **Our Story**\n\nIndustrial Defender was founded in 2006, with roots that stretch back even further. The technology\nbehind our platform was first developed in 2002 at Verano and came to market in 2004 as one of the\nfirst purpose-built cybersecurity solutions for industrial control systems. When enterprise SIEMs\nwere too IT-centric to function effectively in industrial control environments, Industrial Defender\nhelped pioneer the field of industrial automation cybersecurity, years ahead of \u201cOT security\u201d\ngaining widespread recognition.\n\n**Purpose-Built for Industrial Operations**\n\nFrom the beginning, we focused on the realities of industrial operations: systems that must stay\nonline, environments that cannot tolerate disruption, and security teams that need deep visibility\nwithout risk to production. Our early industrial SIEM became the foundation for a broader vision,\ndelivering the most comprehensive OT asset data to strengthen cybersecurity and compliance across\ncritical infrastructure. As operators sought greater insight into configurations, firmware, and\nsoftware within their plants and facilities, Industrial Defender evolved to collect that information\nsafely and with unmatched depth.\n\n**U.S.-Owned and Operated, Focused on OT Security**\n\nAfter several years operating as part of larger technology organizations, we re-emerged in 2020 as\nan independent, U.S.-owned company\u2014reaffirming our commitment to solving the unique challenges of OT\ncybersecurity. From our headquarters and development center just outside Boston, Massachusetts, our\nteam continues to innovate for the industrial community we\u2019ve always served.\n\n**From OT Asset Intelligence to Security and Compliance**\n\nToday, Industrial Defender provides an integrated suite of OT cybersecurity and compliance\ncapabilities that begins with deep asset intelligence and extends through configuration and change\nmanagement, vulnerability management, and security monitoring\u2014including IDS, log/event, and firewall\nanalysis. These capabilities have made us a trusted partner for organizations governed by NERC CIP\nand for those aligning with frameworks such as NIS2, IEC 62443, AESCSF, TSA Pipeline Security\nDirectives, and the Saudi OTCC. Our platform\u2019s reporting and evidence-retention features have set\nthe standard for compliance automation across critical infrastructure sectors.\n\n**Our Belief: Protecting Critical Infrastructure Through OT Security**\n\nWe believe that effective OT cybersecurity and compliance begin with truth\u2014a complete, accurate, and\ncontinuously updated understanding of every system in your operational environment. That foundation\nis essential not just for meeting regulatory obligations, but for protecting the infrastructure that\npowers our world. Every capability we build, from asset discovery to monitoring and reporting,\nsupports a single mission: to help operators safeguard the reliability, safety, and resilience of\nthe critical systems that society depends on every day.\n\nIndustrial Defender Platform\n\n# Reduce and Report on Your OT Cyber Risk\n\nOur OT cybersecurity solution enables executives at critical infrastructure companies to make\ninformed cyber risk management decisions.\n\n[Learn More][73]\n\n### What\u2019s happening at Industrial Defender\n\nFeatured\n\n## 3 Key Takeaways from Our 2022 State of OT Cybersecurity Research\n\nHere are the big takeaways from our proprietary research survey of the OT cybersecurity community on\ntoday\u2019s current priorities and barriers for security practitioners.\n[Read Post][74]\nBlog\nEvents\nPress\nWebinars\nCIP-015 Is Not a Fire Drill: Why \"Race to Comply\" Is the Wrong Strategy for INSM\n[Read More][75]\nKuwait\u2019s 2026 Cybersecurity Controls Signal a New Era for Industrial Cybersecurity\n[Read More][76]\nNIST Releases Pre-Draft Call for Updates to SP 800-82\n[Read More][77]\nIn NERC\u2019s New Roadmap, Low Impact is High Attention\n[Read More][78]\nWhat Is the UK Cyber Security and Resilience Bill (CSRB)?\n[Read More][79]\nCounting Down to the New Year with Industrial Defender\n[Read More][80]\nCISA & Partners Release \u201cPrinciples for the Secure Integration of Artificial Intelligence in\nOperational Technology (OT)\u201d\n[Read More][81]\nFERC\u2019s 2025 Lessons Learned: Direct Insights from Commission-Led CIP Audits\n[Read More][82]\nNo items found.\nApril 17, 2026\nIndustrial Defender and KYrON Announce Strategic Partnership to Strengthen Industrial Cybersecurity\nAcross France\n[See More][83]\nPress\nJanuary 8, 2026\nIndustrial Defender Announces Strategic Growth Investment to Accelerate OT and ICS Cybersecurity\nLeadership\n[See More][84]\nPress\nApril 28, 2025\nCyberKnight and Industrial Defender Unite to Enhance OT Security Resilience Across META\n[See More][85]\nPress\nApril 28, 2025\nIndustrial Defender Honored with Two Global InfoSec Awards from Cyber Defense Magazine\n[See More][86]\nIn The News\nMarch 30, 2025\nIndustrial Cybersecurity Market Outlook 2025: Focus on quantifying risk, embracing AI, building\noperational resilience\n[See More][87]\nPress\n