            "url": "https://industrialdefender.com/team",
            "text": "Webinar - CIP-015 Is Here: Paths to Compliance for Every Organization Register Today\n][1]\n[Support][2]\n\n### SOLUTIONS\n\n][3]\nOT Asset Management\n][4][\nConfiguration & Change Management\n][5][\nPolicy Compliance\n][6][\nVulnerability Management\n][7]\n\n### PLATFORM\n\n][8]\nIndustrial Defender Platform\n][9][\nPhoenix for SMBs\n][10][\nServices\n][11][\nPartners\n][12]\n\n### INDUSTRIES\n\n][13]\nPower\n][14][\nOil & Gas\n][15][\nWater\n][16][\nManufacturing\n][17][\nUS Government\n][18][\nSee all\n][19]\n\n### RESOURCES\n\n][20]\nBlog\n][21][\nPodcast\n][22][\nResource Library\n][23][\nOT Cybersecurity Risk Assessment Calculator\n][24][\nInnovations by Industrial Defender\n][25][\nDeployment\n][26][\nFAQ\n][27]\n\n### COMPANY\n\n][28]\nAbout Us\n][29][\nHow We Compare\n][30][\nDeployment\n][31][\nTeam\n][32][\nEvents\n][33][\nPress\n][34][\nCareers\n][35][\nContact Us\n][36]\n\n### SUPPORT\n\n][37]\n\n### REQUEST DEMO\n\n][38]\nSOLUTIONS\n][39]\nOT Asset Management\n][40]\nConfiguration & Change Management\n][41]\nPolicy Compliance\n][42]\nVulnerability Management\n][43]\nPLATFORM\n][44]\nIndustrial Defender Platform\n][45]\nServices\n][46]\nPartners\n][47]\nINDUSTRIES\n][48]\nPower\n][49]\nOil & Gas\n][50]\nWater\n][51]\nManufacturing\n][52]\nUS Government\n][53]\nSee all\n][54]\nRESOURCES\n][55]\nBlog\n][56]\nPodcast\n][57]\nResource Library\n][58]\nOT Cybersecurity Risk Assessment Calculator\n][59]\nInnovations by Industrial Defender\n][60]\nFAQ\n][61]\nCOMPANY\n][62]\nAbout Us\n][63]\nHow We Compare\n][64]\nTeam\n][65]\nEvents\n][66]\nPress\n][67]\nCareers\n][68]\nContact Us\n][69]\n[Request Demo][70]\nOur team\n\n# The team leading the way in critical infrastructure cybersecurity.\n\n### George Kalavantis\n\nActing CEO / COO\n\nAs chief operating officer at Industrial Defender, George is responsible for the operations of the\ncompany. He brings more than 27 years of operational experience to Industrial Defender. His\nexperience and leadership have focused on the development and delivery of technology and compliance\ndriven business services and solutions for critical infrastructure, the delivery of outstanding\nclient service and operational profitability. As a former manager at National Grid US, George has\noperational experience as an asset owner and operations specialist.\n\n### Alex Bagwell\n\nCRO\n\nAlex brings over a decade of expertise selling SaaS and on-prem solutions to cyber and physical\nsecurity teams across OT/ICS, IoT and IT environments. As Industrial Defender\u2019s Chief Revenue\nOfficer, he is responsible for growing and scaling the global sales, channel and sales operations\nfunctions. In his past executive sales roles, Alex was responsible for GTM strategy focused on\nrevenue growth and managing a global security sales team.\n\n### Greg Valentine\n\nSVP Solutions Engineering\n\nGreg has over 30 years of experience in the high software industry. The past 15 of which has been\nfocused on cyber security. Greg currently holds two certifications including an ISC2 \u2013 CISSP, and\nGIAC \u2013 GRID. Greg is responsible for building technical solutions for Industrial Defender so that\nour clients receive the most effective, and most efficient implementations of the Industrial\nDefender software. Prior to working at Industrial Defender, Greg held cybersecurity roles at\nLockheed Martin, Capgemini, and Winternals Software (a sister company to Sysinternals, now owned by\nMicrosoft).\n\n### TC Lau\n\nVP of Customer Services\n\nTC is responsible for customer deployment and customer support operations at Industrial Defender. TC\nbrings extensive experience in leading and growing high tech businesses. Previously, TC held VP and\nDirector level positions at Norkom Technologies, Progress Software, Systinet, Lockheed Martin, and\nLeidos. He was also a founder and served as Chairman, VP of Business Development, and VP of\nOperations at Context Integration, a nationwide business system integrator. TC holds an engineering\ndegree from Massachusetts Institute of Technology.\n\n### Jeff Smigel\n\nVP Engineering\n\nJeff is responsible for software engineering and quality assurance at Industrial Defender. Leading\nour high-caliber engineering teams, he ensures delivery of the innovative, quality products that our\ncustomers have come to expect. Jeff was an early contributor to the Industrial Defender solution and\nhas provided continuity through Industrial Defender\u2019s product history. Previously, Jeff has led\nengineering teams at Lockheed Martin, Leidos, and Capgemini.\n\n### Bryan Mitchell\n\nVP Marketing\n\nBryan leads marketing at Industrial Defender following a decade leading marketing and communications\nat several software companies. He holds bachelor\u2019s degrees in Communications and Spanish from the\nUniversity of Tennessee and a master\u2019s degree in International Relations from Oklahoma University.\nBryan served as a Public Affairs Officer in the U.S. Navy Reserve, including several active-duty\ndeployments overseas.\n\nLet's meet\n\n# Contact Us\n\nFill out a quick form and we\u2019ll be in touch to help answer all your questions.\n\n[Contact Us][71]\nLet\u2019s get to know each other\n\n# Careers\n\nReady to work in one of the fastest growing sectors of the cybersecurity market?\n\n[View Careers][72]\n\n### What\u2019s happening at Industrial Defender\n\nFeatured\n\n## 3 Key Takeaways from Our 2022 State of OT Cybersecurity Research\n\nHere are the big takeaways from our proprietary research survey of the OT cybersecurity community on\ntoday\u2019s current priorities and barriers for security practitioners.\n[Read Post][73]\nBlog\nEvents\nPress\nWebinars\nCIP-015 Is Not a Fire Drill: Why \"Race to Comply\" Is the Wrong Strategy for INSM\n[Read More][74]\nKuwait\u2019s 2026 Cybersecurity Controls Signal a New Era for Industrial Cybersecurity\n[Read More][75]\nNIST Releases Pre-Draft Call for Updates to SP 800-82\n[Read More][76]\nIn NERC\u2019s New Roadmap, Low Impact is High Attention\n[Read More][77]\nWhat Is the UK Cyber Security and Resilience Bill (CSRB)?\n[Read More][78]\nCounting Down to the New Year with Industrial Defender\n[Read More][79]\nCISA & Partners Release \u201cPrinciples for the Secure Integration of Artificial Intelligence in\nOperational Technology (OT)\u201d\n[Read More][80]\nFERC\u2019s 2025 Lessons Learned: Direct Insights from Commission-Led CIP Audits\n[Read More][81]\nNo items found.\nApril 17, 2026\nIndustrial Defender and KYrON Announce Strategic Partnership to Strengthen Industrial Cybersecurity\nAcross France\n[See More][82]\nPress\nJanuary 8, 2026\nIndustrial Defender Announces Strategic Growth Investment to Accelerate OT and ICS Cybersecurity\nLeadership\n[See More][83]\nPress\nApril 28, 2025\nCyberKnight and Industrial Defender Unite to Enhance OT Security Resilience Across META\n[See More][84]\nPress\nApril 28, 2025\nIndustrial Defender Honored with Two Global InfoSec Awards from Cyber Defense Magazine\n[See More][85]\nIn The News\nMarch 30, 2025\nIndustrial Cybersecurity Market Outlook 2025: Focus on quantifying risk, embracing AI, building\noperational resilience\n[See More][86]\nPress\nMarch 26, 2025\nIndustrial Defender Recognized with Three Wins at 2025 Cybersecurity Excellence Awards\n[See More][87]\nPress\nFebruary 11, 2025\nIndustrial Defender Launches Platform 8.0, Elevating Risk Management Capabilities for Operational\nTechnology\n[See More][88]\nPress\nNovember 24, 2024\nFeatured: Delivering a Comprehensive Approach to Fortify ICS Architectures Against Rising Threats,\nPrepare for Recovery\n[See More][89]\nMastering NIS2 Compliance: Best Practices and Regulatory Readiness\n[Watch Webinar][90]\nWebinar: CIP-015 Is Here: Paths to Compliance for Every Organization\n[Watch Webinar][91]\nWebinar: Saudi OTCC: How to Comply with Operational Technology Cybersecurity Controls\n[Watch Webinar][92]\nNERC CIP: Top 5 Areas to Improve\n[Watch Webinar][93]\nIntegrated Data Collection Methods for OT Asset Management\n[Watch Webinar][94]\nImplementing INSM with Industrial Defender\n[Watch Webinar][95]\nWhy Historical Data Matters in OT Security & Compliance\n[Watch Webinar][96]\nWebinar: Defending Against Attackers who use AI as a Weapon\n[Watch Webinar][97]\n\n## Stay up to date.\n\nSign up for our newsletter to receive the latest Industrial Defender news & updates.\n\nPrivacy Policy\n][98]\n\n##### PRODUCTS\n\n[Industrial Defender Platform][99]\n\n##### SERVICES\n\n[Cyber Diligence Service][100][CopilOT\nService^{TM}][101][Commissioning][102][Support][103][Training][104][Sustain][105]\n\n##### SOLUTION BY TYPE\n\n[OT Asset Management][106][Vulnerability Management][107][Security Event Monitoring][108][Compliance\nReporting][109]\n\n##### SOLUTION BY FUNCTION\n\n[Security][110][Compliance][111][Operations][112][Executive][113]\n\n##### SOLUTION BY INDUSTRY\n\n[Building Automation][114][Chemical][115][Electric][116][Federal Government][117][Food &\nAgriculture][118][Maritime][119][Metals & Mining][120][Oil &\nGas][121][Pharmaceuticals][122][Rail][123][Water][124]\n\n##### RESOURCES\n\n[Resource Collection][125][Glossary][126][DefenderSphere][127][IT-OT Integration Lab][128][OT\nCybersecurity Risk Calculator][129][Innovations by ID][130][Glossary][131]\n\n##### COMPANY\n\n[About Us][132][How We Compare][133][Team][134][Events][135][Press][136][Careers][137][Contact\nUs][138]\n\n[1]: /resources/webinar-cip-015-is-here-paths-to-compliance-for-every-organization\n[2]: https://support.industrialdefender.com/wp-login.php?redirect_to=https%3A%2F%2Fsupport.industria\nldefender.com%2F&reauth=1\n[3]: #\n[4]: /solutions/ot-asset-management\n[5]: /solutions/configuration-change-management\n[6]: /solutions/compliance-reporting\n[7]: /solutions/vulnerability-management\n[8]: #\n[9]: /ot-cyber-risk-management\n[10]: #\n[11]: /services\n[12]: /partners-old\n[13]: #\n[14]: /industries/electric-utilities-cybersecurity\n[15]: /industries/oil-gas-