            "url": "https://adventus.com/team",
            "text": "[Skip to content][1]\n* [ Success Stories ][2]\n* [ About Us ][3]\n* [ Contact ][4]\n* [ Careers ][5]\n* [ Customer Portal ][6]\n* [Home][7]\n* [Services][8]\n* [IT Support (Outsourcing) Services][9]\n* [Cybersecurity Solutions & Services][10]\n* [Microsoft 365 Services][11]\n* [Cloud Solutions & Services][12]\n* [IT Infrastructure & System Integration Services][13]\n* [Managed Print Services][14]\n* [Physical Security Solutions and Services][15]\n* [IP Telephony Services][16]\n* [IT Financing Services][17]\n* [ServiceNow Platform Services][18]\n* [Clients][19]\n* [Partners][20]\n* [Awards][21]\n* [Media][22]\n* [News][23]\n* [Events][24]\n* [Blog][25]\n* [Home][26]\n* [Services][27]\n* [IT Support (Outsourcing) Services][28]\n* [Cybersecurity Solutions & Services][29]\n* [Microsoft 365 Services][30]\n* [Cloud Solutions & Services][31]\n* [IT Infrastructure & System Integration Services][32]\n* [Managed Print Services][33]\n* [Physical Security Solutions and Services][34]\n* [IP Telephony Services][35]\n* [IT Financing Services][36]\n* [ServiceNow Platform Services][37]\n* [Clients][38]\n* [Partners][39]\n* [Awards][40]\n* [Media][41]\n* [News][42]\n* [Events][43]\n* [Blog][44]\n* [Home][45]\n* [Services][46]\n* [IT Support (Outsourcing) Services][47]\n* [Cybersecurity Solutions & Services][48]\n* [Microsoft 365 Services][49]\n* [Cloud Solutions & Services][50]\n* [IT Infrastructure & System Integration Services][51]\n* [Managed Print Services][52]\n* [Physical Security Solutions and Services][53]\n* [IP Telephony Services][54]\n* [IT Financing Services][55]\n* [ServiceNow Platform Services][56]\n* [Clients][57]\n* [Partners][58]\n* [Awards][59]\n* [Media][60]\n* [News][61]\n* [Events][62]\n* [Blog][63]\n* [Home][64]\n* [Services][65]\n* [IT Support (Outsourcing) Services][66]\n* [Cybersecurity Solutions & Services][67]\n* [Microsoft 365 Services][68]\n* [Cloud Solutions & Services][69]\n* [IT Infrastructure & System Integration Services][70]\n* [Managed Print Services][71]\n* [Physical Security Solutions and Services][72]\n* [IP Telephony Services][73]\n* [IT Financing Services][74]\n* [ServiceNow Platform Services][75]\n* [Clients][76]\n* [Partners][77]\n* [Awards][78]\n* [Media][79]\n* [News][80]\n* [Events][81]\n* [Blog][82]\n* [ Success Stories ][83]\n* [ About Us ][84]\n* [ Contact ][85]\n* [ Careers ][86]\n\nPublished on\n* 19 Jan 2024\n\n# TeamViewer Exploited to Breach Vulnerable Networks and Deploy Ransomware\n\n**TeamViewer users: beware. Ransomware actors have been abusing the tool to worm their way into\norganization endpoints. Their goal: to deploy encryptors derived from the leaked LockBit ransomware\nbuilder.**\n\nTeamViewer is a widely used remote access tool prized for its ease-of-use and potential as a\nproductivity tool, supplementing remote and hybrid work arrangements around the world. Its\npopularity and ubiquity here was also its downfall, allowing scammers and ransomware actors to abuse\nthe tool, whose goal is to gain access to remote desktops.\n\nThere was a similar scenario of abuse unfolding in March 2016, where attackers exploited users and\ngained unauthorized access through credential stuffing \u2013 obtained from users\u2019 leaked credentials\nonline. This differs from if attackers were able to exploit a zero-day vulnerability in the\nsoftware, which is defined as a vulnerability in a program that was previously unidentified by its\ndevelopers.\n\nTeamViewer continues to be a popular point of attack for ransomware actors. [Huntress\u2019][87] new\nreport justifies this, showing that cybercriminals still prefer these techniques.\n\nOne of the insights gleaned from Huntress\u2019 analysis was a common attacker, where the analysed log\nfiles reflected a connection from the same source. The first compromised endpoint was observed to\nhave multiple accesses by employees in the logs, evincing that staff would use this software for\nactual productive tasks.\n\nThe second endpoint monitored by Huntress that has been running since 2018 shows no activity in the\nlogs for the past three months. This signals to attackers and malicious actors that its less\nfrequently monitored, making it an attractive potential target.\n\nThese cases saw attackers attempting to deploy the ransomware payload via a DLL file executable\npayload with a rundll32.exe command, achieved through a DOS batch file (PP.bat) on the desktop.\n\nThe PP.bat file used to execute ransomware encryptor\nSource: BleepingComputer\n\nThe attack on the first endpoint was successful, although its reach was contained. The second\nattempt saw the effort halted by the antivirus product, forcing repeated payload execution attempts\nwith no success.\n\nWhile Huntress has yet to ascertain if the attacks are traceable to any known ransomware gangs, they\nfound that it resembled LockBit encryptors created using a leaked LockBit Black builder.\n\nIn 2022, the [ransomware builder kit for LockBit 3.0][88] became publicly available, leading to\nswift utilization by the [Bl00dy][89] and [Buhti][90] groups for initiating their respective\ncampaigns.\n\nThis released toolkit enables the generation of diverse encryptor variants, such as an executable, a\nDLL, and an encrypted DLL that demands a password for proper execution.\n\nLeaked LockBit 3.0 build\nSource: BleepingComputer\n\nBased on the IOCs provided by Huntress, the attacks through TeamViewer appear to be using the\npassword protected LockBit 3 DLL.\n\nWhile it is unclear how malicious actors are abusing TeamViewer instances to gain remote access,\nTeamViewer takes these threats extremely seriously. They released a statement about the attacks and\nsecuring installations.\n\n> *At TeamViewer, we take the security and integrity of our platform extremely seriously and\n> unequivocally condemn any form of malicious use of our software.\n> Our analysis shows that most instances of unauthorized access involve a weakening of TeamViewer\u2019s\n> default security settings. This often includes the use of easily guessable passwords which is only\n> possible by using an outdated version of our product. We constantly emphasize the importance of\n> maintaining strong security practices, such as using complex passwords, two-factor-authentication,\n> allow-lists, and regular updates to the latest software versions. These steps are critical in\n> safeguarding against unauthorized access.*\n\nIn order to combat this, TeamViewer has published a list of good practices to clamp down on\nloopholes found via unattended access. Read more about it [here][91].\n\nTo further eliminate potential for errors that might gravely cost your business, secure your\norganization and networks today with Adventus. As a top [Cybersecurity Solutions & Services\nProvider][92], our dedicated Security Operations Centre (SOC) works around the clock to safeguard\nyour employees and assets. We monitor, detect, and respond to any cybersecurity risks or threats\nbefore they threaten your business.\n\nIf your business is using TeamViewer, we recommend a thorough scan of your IT environment to\nidentify any potential malware or further exploits. Rest assured as our SOC team will monitor,\ndetect, and respond to any potential threats. [Get in touch with us][93] today to learn what our\ncybersecurity team can do for your business.\n\n[ View All Blogs ][94]\n\n## Recent Posts\n\n##### [IT Outsourcing in Singapore][95]\n\n##### [Penetration Testing Explained: Think Like a Hacker, Stay Ahead of One][96]\n\n##### [Human Risk Management: Transforming Employees into Your Strongest Firewall][97]\n\n##### [The Hidden Threat in Your Inbox: Why Email Security Matters][98]\n\n##### [Microsoft Teams Phone System: The Ultimate Solution for Modern Business Telephony][99]\n\n##### [Greener Prints, Greater Impact: Steps for Sustainable Printing at Work][100]\n\n##### [From Boardrooms to Classrooms: The Growing Role of Interactive Displays][101]\n\n##### [Microsoft 365 Phishing Threats Are Evolving \u2013 Are Your Defenses?][102]\n\n##### [Skype is Hanging Up \u2014 What\u2019s Your Next Call?][103]\n\n##### [Last Call: Windows 10 End of Support Is Near \u2014 Secure Your Systems Now][104]\n\n[ Linkedin-in ][105]\n* [ About us ][106]\n* [ Contact us ][107]\n* [ Careers ][108]\n* [ Clients ][109]\n* [ Partners ][110]\n* [ Awards ][111]\n* [ IT Support (Outsourcing) Services ][112]\n* [ Cybersecurity Solutions & Services ][113]\n* [ Microsoft 365 Services ][114]\n* [ Cloud Solutions & Services ][115]\n* [ IT Infrastructure Services ][116]\n* [ Managed Print Services ][117]\n* [ Physical Security Solutions & Services ][118]\n* [ IP Telephony Services ][119]\n* [ IT Financing Services ][120]\n* [ ServiceNow Platform Services ][121]\n* Contact Us\n\nSpeak to us about your IT Infrastructure needs\n\n[ Talk to us ][122]\n* SCHEDULE AN APPOINTMENT\n\nConsult with our Enterprise Account Managers and Specialists\n\n[ Let Us Know ][123]\n\nCopyright \u00a9 2026 Adventus Pte Ltd. All rights reserved.\n* [ Privacy Statement ][124]\n* [ Website Usage Terms & Conditions ][125]\n* [ Quality Policy ][126]\n\n[1]: #content\n[2]: /story/\n[3]: /about/\n[4]: /contact-us/\n[5]: /career/\n[6]: https://service.adventus.com/\n[7]: https://adventus.com/\n[8]: #\n[9]: https://adventus.com/it-support-outsourcing-services-singapore-helpdesk/\n[10]: https://adventus.com/cybersecurity/\n[11]: https://adventus.com/microsoft-365-services/\n[12]: https://adventus.com/cloud/\n[13]: https://adventus.com/it-infrastructure/\n[14]: https://adventus.com/managed-print/\n[15]: https://adventus.com/physical-security/\n[16]: https://adventus.com/ip-telephony/\n[17]: https://adventus.com/it-financing/\n[18]: https://adventus.com/servicenow/\n[19]: https://adventus.com/clients/\n[20]: https://adventus.com/partners/\n[21]: https://adventus.com/awards/\n[22]: #\n[23]: https://adventus.com/news/\n[24]: https://adventus.com/events/\n[25]: https://adventus.com/blog/\n[26]: https://adventus.com/\n[27]: #\n[28]: https://adventus.com/it-support-outsourcing-services-singapore-helpdesk/\n[29]: https://adventus.com/cybersecurity/\n[30]: https://adventus.com/microsoft-365-services/\n[31]: https://adventus.com/cloud/\n[32]: https://adventus.com/it-infrastructure/\n[33]: https://adventus.com/managed-print/\n[34]: https://adventus.com/physical-security/\n[35]: https://adventus.com/ip-telephony/\n[36]: https://adventus.com/it-financing/\n[37]: https://adventus.com/servicenow/\n[38]: https://adventus.com/clients/\n[39]: https://adventus.com/partners/\n[40]: https://adventus.com/awards/\n[41]: #\n[42]: https://adventus.com/news/\n[43]: https://adventus.com/events/\n[44]: https://adventus.com/blog/\n[45]: https://adventus.com/\n[46]: #\n[47]: https://adventus.com/it-support-outsourcing-services-singapore-helpdesk/\n[48]: https://adventus.com/cybersecurity/\n[49]: https://adventus.com/microsoft-365-services/\n[50]: https://adventus.com/cloud/\n[51]: https://adventus.com/it-infrastructure/\n[52]: https://adventus.com/managed-print/\n[53]: https://adventus.com/physical-security/\n[54]: https://adventus.com/ip-telephony/\n[55]: https://adventus.com/it-financing/\n[56]: https://adventus.com/servicenow/\n[57]: https://adventus.com/clients/\n[58]: https://adventus.com/partners/\n[59]: https://adventus.com/awards/\n[60]: #\n[61]: https://adventus.com/news/\n[62]: https://adventus.com/events/\n[63]: https://adventus.com/blog/\n[64]: https://adventus.com/\n[65]: #\n[66]: https://adventus.com/it-support-outsourcing-services-singapore-helpdesk/\n[67]: https://adventus.com/cybersecurity/\n[68]: https://adventus.com/microsoft-365-services/\n[69]: https://adventus.com/cloud/\n[70]: https://adventus.com/it-infrastructure/\n[71]: https://adventus.com/managed-print/\n[72]: https://adventus.com/physical-security/\n[73]: https://adventus.com/ip-telephony/\n[74]: https://adventus.com/it-financing/\n[75]: https://adventus.com/servicenow/\n[76]: https://adventus.com/clients/\n[77