ices ][59]\n* [ Managed SmartOps ][60]\n* [ See related resources ][61]\n* Show submenu for Company Company\n* Company\n* [ About Us ][62]\n* [ Leadership Team ][63]\n* [ Careers ][64]\n* [ Locations ][65]\n* Show submenu for Resources Resources\n* Resources\n* [ Blog ][66]\n* [ Customer Stories ][67]\n* [ Resource Library ][68]\n* [ Events ][69]\n* [ ServTrax Portal ][70]\n* [ Partners ][71]\n* [ Government Contracts ][72]\n* Search\n* [Contact Us][73]\n[Contact Us][74]\nSearch\n\nBlog\n\n][75]\nTags\n* [Education][76]\n* [Healthcare][77]\n* [Financial][78]\n* [Government][79]\n* [Hospitality & Gaming][80]\n* [Technology][81]\n* [Utilities][82]\nSearch\n* [Education][83]\n* [Healthcare][84]\n* [Financial][85]\n* [Government][86]\n* [Hospitality & Gaming][87]\n* [Technology][88]\n* [Utilities][89]\n[ Customer Story Building a Future-Ready Data Platform for the City of North Las Vegas From Data\nSilos to Citywide Intelligence ][90]\n\n# Customer Stories\n* [Filter][91]\n* [All][92]\n* [Education][93]\n* [Healthcare][94]\n* [Financial][95]\n* [Government][96]\n* [Hospitality & Gaming][97]\n* [Technology][98]\n* [Utilities][99]\n* [Commercial][100]\n* [Cross-Industry][101]\n* [Defense][102]\n* [Enterprise & Commercial][103]\n* [Insurance][104]\n* [Law Practice][105]\n* [Oil and Gas][106]\n* [Public Sector][107]\n* [Retail][108]\n* [Software][109]\n\nInsurance\n\n### Insurance Claims Provider Migrates from VMware to OpenShift Virtualization, Avoiding 400%\n### License Price Increase\n\nClient Overview: A medium-sized insurance claims processing organization operates with approximately\n20 hosts and over 350 virtual machines in their VMware-based on-premises virtualization environment.\nWith a crucial role in handling insurance claims, their IT infrastructure requires high ...\n\nRead More\n][110]\nFinancial\n\n### Driving Business Intelligence with Executive Insights for a Financial Institution\n\nThe Challenge A financial institution faced challenges gaining clear visibility into transaction\nhealth. Without real-time insight into transaction bottlenecks, identifying issues and optimizing\nperformance was difficult. Additionally, technical telemetry data was not easily translated into ...\n\nRead More\n][111]\nUtilities\n\n### Strengthening Cybersecurity and Threat Response for a Utilities Organization\n\nA utilities organization was approaching a renewal for its Managed Defense and Incident Response\nRetainer services. While these services had been critical in strengthening their cybersecurity\nposture, the organization was concerned about rising costs and was considering exploring alternative\n...\n\nRead More\n][112]\nRetail\n\n### Retail Security Transformation: Shifting to Proactive, Centralized MXDR Services\n\nThe Challenge A retail organization had previously maintained all security responsibilities in-house\nbut encountered challenges scaling and achieving a proactive security posture with their lean\nsecurity operations team. Following the appointment of a new CIO, their primary strategic goal\nbecame ...\n\nRead More\n][113]\nHealthcare\n\n### Transforming Cloud Security for a Large Healthcare Provider With Wiz\n\nA leading healthcare provider operating across AWS, Azure, and Google Cloud needed to strengthen its\ncloud security posture while maintaining compliance with strict healthcare regulations. With\nsensitive patient data at stake, the client required a solution that could provide real-time\nvisibility, ...\n\nRead More\n][114]\nDefense\n\n### From Zero to Audit-Ready: How Arctiq Helped a Defense Contractor Build Their CMMC Foundation\n### Without Breaking the Bank\n\nWhen a growing and strategically positioned defense contractor approached Arctiq, they had just one\nthing: a growing sense of urgency. With CMMC on the horizon, a handful of federal primes were\nleaning harder on flow-down clauses, and had no real sense of how their environment stacked up, but\nthey ...\n\nRead More\n][115]\nTechnology\n\n### Technology Provider Escapes VMware Price Hike with OpenShift Virtualization in 255 Hours\n\nClient Overview: The client is a U.S.-based, mid-sized technology provider operating in tightly\nregulated and government-adjacent sectors. They specialize in managing workforce processes and\ncompliance for public-sector organizations, emphasizing data security and operational reliability.\nThe ...\n\nRead More\n][116]\n[Enabling End-to-End Cyber Resilience]\nHealthcare\n\n### Enabling End-to-End Cyber Resilience for a Global Digital Services Leader\n\nA global healthcare organizationfaced growing complexity in managing data protection across a\ndiverse and hybrid IT environment. As their operations scaled, so did the volume and sensitivity of\nthe data they managed - ranging from internal operational systems to cloud-hosted applications and\n...\n\nRead More\n][117]\n[How a Cyber Supply Chain Attack Triggered a Security Transformation]\nCross-Industry\n\n### From Alert to Action \u2014 How a Cyber Supply Chain Attack Triggered a Security Transformation\n\nAs a large North American organization with operations spanning various sectors, this company had\nalready established a strong foundation for cybersecurity. With dozens of locations and an expanding\ndigital footprint, they were an existing Arctiq customer, leveraging Managed SIEM and Managed ...\n\nRead More\n][118]\n[1][119] [2][120] [3][121] [4][122] [ All ][123] [ Next ][124]\n[ [Logo] ][125]\nStay informed about the latest technology trends and enterprise solutions\n\nBy subscribing, you agree to our privacy policy and consent to receive updates.\n* [ [LinkedIn] ][126]\n* [ [Youtube] ][127]\n* [COMPANY][128]\n* [About Us][129]\n* [Careers][130]\n* [Locations][131]\n* [SOLUTIONS][132]\n* [Hybrid Cloud\nInfrastructure][133]\n* [Network & Connected\nExperiences][134]\n* [Cybersecurity][135]\n* [Autonomous Operations & Intelligence][136]\n* [Data & AI][137]\n* [Enterprise Service\nManagement][138]\n* [SERVICES][139]\n* [Professional Methodology][140]\n* [Managed Services][141]\n* [Resource Management][142]\n* [Arctiq Capital][143]\n* [INDUSTRIES][144]\n* [Enterprise & Commercial][145]\n* [Government][146]\n* [Education][147]\n* [Healthcare][148]\n* [Utilities][149]\n* [Hospitality & Gaming][150]\n* [Tribal][151]\n\n\u00a9 2026 Arctiq, Inc. All rights reserved.\n* [Privacy Policy][152]\n* [Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information][153]\n\n[1]: #main-content\n[2]: https://arctiq.com/\n[3]:\n[4]: https://arctiq.com/solutions/hybrid-cloud-infrastructure\n[5]: https://arctiq.com/solutions/networking-and-connected-experiences\n[6]: https://arctiq.com/solutions/cybersecurity\n[7]: https://arctiq.com/solutions/autonomous-operations-intelligence\n[8]: https://arctiq.com/solutions/data-ai\n[9]: https://arctiq.com/solutions/enterprise-service-management\n[10]: https://arctiq.com/customer-stories/building-a-future-ready-data-platform-for-the-city-of-nort\nh-las-vegas\n[11]: https://arctiq.com/services/service-iq-methodology\n[12]: https://arctiq.com/services/service-iq/insight\n[13]: https://arctiq.com/services/service-iq/design\n[14]: https://arctiq.com/services/service-iq/build\n[15]: https://arctiq.com/services/service-iq/shift\n[16]: https://arctiq.com/services/service-iq/enable\n[17]: https://arctiq.com/services/service-iq/optimize\n[18]: https://arctiq.com/services/security-advisory-services\n[19]: https://arctiq.com/services/resource-management-services\n[20]: https://arctiq.com/services/arctiq-capital-services\n[21]: https://arctiq.com/services/managed-services-overview\n[22]: https://arctiq.com/services/managed-iq/hybrid-cloud-infrastructure-managed-services\n[23]: https://arctiq.com/services/managed-iq/networking-connected-experiences-managed-services-arcti\n[24]: https://arctiq.com/services/managed-iq/cybersecurity-managed-services\n[25]: https://arctiq.com/services/managed-iq/managed-smartops\n[26]: https://arctiq.com/resources/resource-library\n[27]: https://arctiq.com/about-us\n[