            "url": "https://www.cloudsek.com/case-studies",
            "text": "**\ud83d\ude80 **CloudSEK becomes first Indian origin cybersecurity company to receive investment from **US\nstate** fund\nRead more\n][1]\n\ud83d\ude80 CloudSEK Becomes First Indian Cybersecurity Firm to partner with The Private Office\nRead more\n][2]\n**\ud83d\ude80 **CloudSEK has raised **$19M Series B1 Round **\u2013 Powering the Future of Predictive\nCybersecurity\nRead more\n][3]\n[CloudSEK Logo]\n][4]\nProducts\nNexus AI\nAI Command center & Cyber Risk Quantification\n][5][\nXVigil\nDigital Risk protection\n][6][\nBeVigil\nAttack Surface monitoring\n][7][\nSVigil\nThird party Risk Monitoring\n][8][\nThreat Intelligence\nCyber Threat Intel, IAVs & More\n][9][\nBeVigil Community\nApplication Scanner\n][10][\nExposure\nCheck if your organisation's data is in a data breach\n][11][\nAIVigil\nAI Attack Surface Monitoring\n][12]\nSolutions\nCyber Threats Monitoring\nSurface, Deep, and Dark Web Monitoring\n][13][\nDeep and Dark Web Monitoring\nThreat Monitoring Across the Hidden Web\n][14][\nBrand Threats Monitoring\nProactive Brand Protection\n][15][\nInfrastructure Monitoring\nCatch Risks Before Attacks\n][16][\nPartner Secret Scanning\nAPI/secret Exposure Detection\n][17][\nBeVigil Jenkins CI\nBeVigil-CI secures your mobile app builds\n][18][\nBeVigil OSINT CLI\nUnified CLI/Python for BeVigil OSINT\n][19][\nBeVigil Asset Explorer\nThreat Monitoring Across the Hidden Web\n][20]\nResources\n\n#### Resources\n\nBlog\nStay updated with the latest cybersecurity news, insights, and industry trends\n][21][\nThreat Intelligence\nGet up and running on new threat reports and techniques\n][22][\nKnowledge Base\nBasics of Cybersecurity and see more definitions\n][23][\nWhitepapers & Reports\nThe content team broke their backs making these reports\n][24][\nCustomer stories\nLearn how our customers are making big changes. You have got good company!\n][25][\nCloudSEK Academy\nBe CloudSEK certified!\n][26]\n\n#### Company\n\nIntegrations\nWe are more connected than you know. Explore all Integrations\n][27][\nPartners\n100s of partners and one Shared goal; Secure future for all us\n][28][\nAbout us\nLearn about our story and our mission statement\n][29][\nLife at CloudSEK\nA sneak peek at the awesome life at CloudSEK\n][30][\nCareers\nWe're hiring!\nWe are in love with undeniable talent. Join our team!\n][31][\nEvents\nWe're hiring!\nExplore webinars, panels, and meetups powered by CloudSEK\n][32][\nLegal\nAll the boring but necessary legalese that legal made us add.\n][33][\nCompliance\nProven compliance with top security benchmarks.\n][34]\n\n#### Latest Whitepaper\n\n[CloudSEK: Global Threat Landscape Report 2025]\nAdversary Intelligence\n24 Mar 26\nCloudSEK: Global Threat Landscape Report 2025\n][35]\nFree Tools\nURL Analyser\nScan for malicious links and phishing threats\n][36][\nDeepfake Analyser\nSpot manipulated videos and deepfake scams\n][37][\nThreatLens\nA live feed of scams, phishing, and brand abuse\n][38][\nMobile App Analyser\nDetect security flaws in mobile apps\n][39][\nAsset Explorer\nGain insights on digital assets and subdomains\n][40][\nData Exposure Checker\nSee if your organization's data is on the Dark Web\n][41][\nBeVigil Asset Explorer\nThreat Monitoring Across the Hidden Web\n][42]\nLog in\n][43][\nSchedule a Demo\n][44]\nSchedule a Demo\n][45]\nResources\n\n# Blogs and Articles\n\nExplore Blogs and Research Articles from the team on the latest trends and methods in Cybersecurity.\n\nFeatured\n\n## THE 5060 SIEGE - Industrialized Attacks Against the SIP Telephony Ecosystem\n\n][46]\n\nUncover how an 18-day honeypot captured 15 million automated attacks targeting telephony ecosystems\nin the \"Copy of SIP Honeypot Report.pdf\". Download the full report to expose active VoIP fraud\nnetworks and access 277,632 recovered attacker passwords.\n\nJune 23, 2026\n\n### Subscribe to CloudSEK Resources\n\nSubscribe to the latest industry news, threats and resources.\n\n## Download BeVigil App\n\nAccess to Underground Intelligence, Blog and Threat intelligence articles on your mobile as soon as\nit is published.\n\n[[Google Play button to download App ]][47]\n[Download CloudSEK BeVigil App ]\nJune 23, 2026\nTHE 5060 SIEGE - Industrialized Attacks Against the SIP Telephony Ecosystem\n\nUncover how an 18-day honeypot captured 15 million automated attacks targeting telephony ecosystems\nin the \"Copy of SIP Honeypot Report.pdf\". Download the full report to expose active VoIP fraud\nnetworks and access 277,632 recovered attacker passwords.\n\n][48]\nJune 19, 2026\nInside the FortiBleed Open Directory: A Technical Analysis of What the Attacker Left Behind\n\nAn exposed attacker server has revealed FortiBleed\u2019s complete operation\u2014from credential harvesting\nand GPU-powered cracking to network intrusion and access sales. CloudSEK\u2019s analysis separates\nverified compromises from inflated claims, uncovering what the attackers actually achieved.\n\n][49]\nJune 17, 2026\nOperation Escaneo: Infrastructure Exposure, TTP Analysis, and Attribution Assessment of an Advanced\nIntrusion Campaign Against Mexican Federal Agencies and Financial Institutions\n\nAn exposed attacker server revealed the inner workings of Operation Escaneo\u2014a sophisticated campaign\ntargeting Latin American governments and financial institutions. CloudSEK maps its custom tools,\nexploitation chain, persistence tactics and suspected links to MexicanMafia. Read the full\ninvestigation.\n\n][50]\nJune 17, 2026\nBluekit Phishing as a Service (PhaaS)\n\nBlueKit is turning phishing into a subscription business, offering 87 ready-made kits, automated\naccount takeover and stealthy peer-to-peer infrastructure. CloudSEK\u2019s investigation reveals how this\nmature PhaaS platform helps even low-skilled criminals target banks, cloud services and global\nbrands.\n\n][51]\nJune 11, 2026\nChinese Origin Threat Actors Target FIFA World Cup 2026\n\nAs the FIFA World Cup 2026 begins, a highly sophisticated, Chinese-origin threat operation is\ntargeting global football fans. Utilizing pixel-perfect website clones, a multi-tenant reseller\nnetwork, and an active Man-in-the-Middle framework, these actors intercept payment details and\nbypass SMS-based two-factor authentication in real time to completely compromise accounts.\n\n][52]\nJune 10, 2026\nInside a WooCommerce Payment Skimmer: How Carders Moved From Phishing Pages to Checkout Backdoors\n\nCybercriminals are now targeting real e-commerce checkout pages, not just fake websites. This report\nreveals how a WooCommerce skimmer silently steals card details during genuine payments. Read the\nfull report to understand the hidden risk.\n\n][53]\nJune 2, 2026\nHow an Unauthenticated MCP Server Led to SSRF, LFI, and AWS Credential Theft\n\nA real-world AIVigil finding from a customer environment. One unprotected AI integration endpoint\nwith no login required. An attacker chained Server-Side Request Forgery, Local File Inclusion, and\nlive AWS credential exfiltration into a potential full infrastructure takeover. This is how it\nhappened, and how AIVigil found it first.\n\n][54]\nMay 20, 2026\nHit Wicket: Inside The Expansive Web of Scams Targeting Millions of IPL Fans This Season\n\nCloudSEK\u2019s report exposes a highly sophisticated, seasonal IPL online betting scam ecosystem.\nFraudsters deploy clone platforms, celebrity AI deepfakes, and blackhat SEO tactics to exploit\ngovernment domains and trap unsuspecting fans. Sustained by money mule networks, bulk\nadvertisements, and predatory fake loan apps, this industry intentionally blocks user withdrawals,\ncausing severe financial losses and blackmail.\n\n][55]\nMay 14, 2026\nInside a Tor Backed Supply Chain Worm\n\nCloudSEK TRIAD uncovered a sophisticated npm supply chain attack using a typosquatted package,\ncrypto-javascri, to mimic crypto-js. The malware steals npm and GitHub credentials, hijacks\nmaintainer accounts, republishes trojanized packages, and uses Tor-based command-and-control. The\ncampaign targets Linux developer systems and CI/CD environments, creating serious downstream supply\nchain risk.\n\n][56]\nNext\n][57]\nA newsletter that is upto date\n\n## Subscribe to our newsletter\n\nSubscribe to the latest industry news, threats and resources.\n\nThank you! Your submission has been received!\nOops! Something went wrong while submitting the form.\nWe Respect your privacy. Read our friendly [privacy policy][58].\nJoin our newsletter\nWe\u2019ll send you a nice letter once per week. No spam.\n[Untitled UI logotext][Logo]\n][59]\nProduct\nXVigil\n][60][\nBeVigil\n][61][\nSVigil\nNew\n][62][\nTutorials\n][63][\nPricing\n][64][\nReleases\n][65]\nCompany\nAbout us\n][66][\nCareers\n][67][\nPress\n][68][\nNews\n][69][\nMedia kit\n][70][\nContact\n][71]\nResources\nBlog\n][72][\nNewsletter\n][73][\nEvents\n][74][\nHelp centre\n][75][\nTutorials\n][76][\nSupport\n][77]\nUse Cases\nStartups\n][78][\nEnterprise\n][79][\nGovernment\n][80][\nSaaS\n][81][\nMarketplaces\n][82][\nEcommerce\n][83]\nSocial\nTwitter\n][84][\nLinkedIn\n][85][\nFacebook\n][86][\nGitHub\n][87][\nAngelList\n][88][\nDribbble\n][89]\n\u00a9 2077 Untitled UI\n[Privacy][90][GDPR][91][Disclosure of Vulnerability][92]\n][93][\n][94][\n][95][\n][96]\nProducts\nNexus AI\n][97][\nXVigil\n][98][\nBeVigil\n][99][\nSVigil\n][100][\nThreat Intelligence\n][101][\nCloudSEK Exposure\n][102][\nAIVigil\n][103]\nMobile App\n[[Google Play button to download App ]\n][104]\nSolutions\nCyber Threats Monitoring\n][105][\nDark Web Monitoring\n][106][\nBrand Threat Monitoring\n][107][\nInfra Threat Monitoring\n][108][\nPartners Secret Scanning\n][109][\nBeVigil Jenkins CI\n][110][\nBeVigil OSINT CLI\n][111][\nBeVigil Asset Explorer\n][112][\nTakedowns\n][113]\nResources\nBlogs and Articles\n][114][\nThreat Intelligence\n][115][\nWhitepapers and Reports\n][116][\nKnowledge Base\n][117][\nIntegrations\n][118]\nCommunity\nDiscord Community\n][119][\nStudent Challenge\n][120]\nCompany\nAbout us\n][121][\nCustomers\n][122][\nPartners\n][123][\nReferral Program\n][124][\nLife at CloudSEK\n][125][\nSecure Sips\n][126][\nCareers\n][127][\nAnnouncements\n][128][\nPress\n][129][\nContact Us\n][130]\n[[CloudSEK Logo]][131]\n][132][\n][133][[Linkedin Icon ]][134][\n][135]\n\nAt CloudSEK, we combine the power of Cyber Intelligence, Brand Monitoring, Attack Surface\nMonitoring, Infrastructure Monitoring and Supply Chain Intelligence to give context to our\ncustomers\u2019 digital risks.\n\nGDPR Policy\n][136][\nPrivacy\n][137][\nVulnerability Disclosure\n][138][\nDPA\n][139][\nCookies Policy\n][140][\nSitemap\n][141][\nLLM Info\n][142][\nEULA\n][143]\n\n[1]: https://www.cloudsek.com/ancmt/cloudsek-becomes-first-indian-origin-cybersecurity-company-to-re\nceive-investment-from-a-u-s-state-fund\n[2]: https://www.cloudsek.com/ancmt/cloudsek-becomes-first-active-indian-cybersecurity-firm-to-partn\ner-with-seed-group-a-company-of-the-private-office-of-sheikh-saeed-bin-ahmed-al-maktoum\n[3]: https://www.cloudsek.com/blog/cloudsek-raises-19-million-in-series-b1-funding-to-scale-predicti\nve-cybersecurity-platform\n[4]: /?r=0\n[5]: /nexus\n[6]: /xvigil\n[7]: /bevigil-enterprise\n[8]: /svigil\n[9]: /threat-intelligence\n[10]: https://bevigil.com/?Ref=cloudsek.com\n[11]: https://exposure.cloudsek.com/?Ref=cloudsek.com\n[12]: /aivigil\n[13]: /cyber-threats\n[14]: /cyber-threats/dark-web-monitoring\n[15]: /brand-monitor\n[16]: /bevigil-enterprise\n[17]: https://bevigil.com/bevigil-secrets-scanning-partner-program\n[18]: https://plugins.jenkins.io/bevigil-ci/\n[19]: https://github.com/Bevigil/BeVigil-OSINT-CLI\n[20]: https://bevigil.com/osint-api\n[21]: /blog\n[22]: /threatintelligence\n[23]: /knowledgebase\n[24]: /whitepapers-reports\n[25]: /customers\n[26]: /cloudsek-academy\n[27]: /integrations\n[28]: /partners\n[29]: /about-us\n[30]: /work-life\n[31]: /openings\n[32]: /events\n[33]: /privacy-policy\n[34]: /compliance\n[35]: /whitepapers-reports/cloudsek-global-threat-landscape-report-2025\n[36]: /cyber-threats\n[37]: https://community.cloudsek.com/\n[38]: /brand-monitor\n[39]: https://bevigil.com/?Ref=cloudsek.com\n[40]: https://bevigil.com/?Ref=cloudsek.com\n[41]: https://exposure.cloudsek.com/?Ref=cloudsek.com\n[42]: https://bevigil.com/osint-api\n[43]: #\n[44]: /request-a-demo\n[45]: /request-a-demo\n[46]: /blog/the-5060-siege---industrialized-attacks-against-the-sip-telephony-ecosystem\n[47]: https://csek.me/JWWt\n[48]: /blog/the-5060-siege---industrialized-attacks-against-the-sip-telephony-ecosystem\n[49]: /blog/inside-the-fortibleed-open-directory-a-"
