          {
            "url": "https://cloudsek.com/about-us",
            "text": "**\ud83d\ude80 **CloudSEK becomes first Indian origin cybersecurity company to receive investment from **US\nstate** fund\nRead more\n][1]\n\ud83d\ude80 CloudSEK Becomes First Indian Cybersecurity Firm to partner with The Private Office\nRead more\n][2]\n**\ud83d\ude80 **CloudSEK has raised **$19M Series B1 Round **\u2013 Powering the Future of Predictive\nCybersecurity\nRead more\n][3]\n[CloudSEK Logo]\n][4]\nProducts\nNexus AI\nAI Command center & Cyber Risk Quantification\n][5][\nXVigil\nDigital Risk protection\n][6][\nBeVigil\nAttack Surface monitoring\n][7][\nSVigil\nThird party Risk Monitoring\n][8][\nThreat Intelligence\nCyber Threat Intel, IAVs & More\n][9][\nBeVigil Community\nApplication Scanner\n][10][\nExposure\nCheck if your organisation's data is in a data breach\n][11][\nAIVigil\nAI Attack Surface Monitoring\n][12]\nSolutions\nCyber Threats Monitoring\nSurface, Deep, and Dark Web Monitoring\n][13][\nDeep and Dark Web Monitoring\nThreat Monitoring Across the Hidden Web\n][14][\nBrand Threats Monitoring\nProactive Brand Protection\n][15][\nInfrastructure Monitoring\nCatch Risks Before Attacks\n][16][\nPartner Secret Scanning\nAPI/secret Exposure Detection\n][17][\nBeVigil Jenkins CI\nBeVigil-CI secures your mobile app builds\n][18][\nBeVigil OSINT CLI\nUnified CLI/Python for BeVigil OSINT\n][19][\nBeVigil Asset Explorer\nThreat Monitoring Across the Hidden Web\n][20]\nResources\n\n#### Resources\n\nBlog\nStay updated with the latest cybersecurity news, insights, and industry trends\n][21][\nThreat Intelligence\nGet up and running on new threat reports and techniques\n][22][\nKnowledge Base\nBasics of Cybersecurity and see more definitions\n][23][\nWhitepapers & Reports\nThe content team broke their backs making these reports\n][24][\nCustomer stories\nLearn how our customers are making big changes. You have got good company!\n][25][\nCloudSEK Academy\nBe CloudSEK certified!\n][26]\n\n#### Company\n\nIntegrations\nWe are more connected than you know. Explore all Integrations\n][27][\nPartners\n100s of partners and one Shared goal; Secure future for all us\n][28][\nAbout us\nLearn about our story and our mission statement\n][29][\nLife at CloudSEK\nA sneak peek at the awesome life at CloudSEK\n][30][\nCareers\nWe're hiring!\nWe are in love with undeniable talent. Join our team!\n][31][\nEvents\nWe're hiring!\nExplore webinars, panels, and meetups powered by CloudSEK\n][32][\nLegal\nAll the boring but necessary legalese that legal made us add.\n][33][\nCompliance\nProven compliance with top security benchmarks.\n][34]\n\n#### Latest Whitepaper\n\n[CloudSEK: Global Threat Landscape Report 2025]\nAdversary Intelligence\n24 Mar 26\nCloudSEK: Global Threat Landscape Report 2025\n][35]\nFree Tools\nURL Analyser\nScan for malicious links and phishing threats\n][36][\nDeepfake Analyser\nSpot manipulated videos and deepfake scams\n][37][\nThreatLens\nA live feed of scams, phishing, and brand abuse\n][38][\nMobile App Analyser\nDetect security flaws in mobile apps\n][39][\nAsset Explorer\nGain insights on digital assets and subdomains\n][40][\nData Exposure Checker\nSee if your organization's data is on the Dark Web\n][41][\nBeVigil Asset Explorer\nThreat Monitoring Across the Hidden Web\n][42]\nLog in\n][43][\nSchedule a Demo\n][44]\nSchedule a Demo\n][45]\n\n# Our Vision\n\n*To build the world\u2019s fastest and most reliable AI technology, that identifies and resolves digital\nthreats.*\n\nCloudSEK\u2019s central proposition is leverage Artificial Intelligence to build a rapid and reliable\ndetection, analysis, and alert system that offers swift detection across internet sources ,\nprecision analysis of threats and prompt resolution with minimal human intervention.\nJoin our Team now\n][46]\n\n## Our Mission\n\n*To produce machines that enable Digital Security by emulating human capability to learn and\nevolve.*\n\n**The future is**: systems that can emulate human cognition to understand, learn, and adapt.\nCloudSEK has set its sights on building an AI based system that can navigate the internet like an\nintelligent human, albeit faster, more thoroughly, and with fewer errors.\n\nRead our Principles\n][47]\n\n## Story\n\nInnovation is the nexus of an unaddressed problem and determined problem-solver. And that\u2019s what\nhappened in 2015, when Rahul Sasi, the Founder and CTO of CloudSEK, realized that there wasn\u2019t a\ncomprehensive solution to monitor external cyber threats. There were internal threat monitoring\nsolutions such as Anti-virus, IDS, and IPS, but these did not address the threats posed by the\nsurface web, deep web, dark web, and internet-exposed infrastructure.\n\nThe goal was to build an Al-based threat management platform that detects, analyses, and reports\nactionable threats to organizations. In its first iteration, our platform -XVigil, was partly manual\nand partly driven by machine learning. In its current avatar, the platform is wholly automated,\ngathering and analysing 37 GB of data every day.\n\nRahul Sasi\n\nWhen the initial version was launched in 2017, we showcased the product to our friends in the\nindustry, and within a few months, we had clicked our first order, from a US-based tech company.\nOver the years we have built a diverse team of ambitious individuals, whose complementary skills\nand working styles, has enabled us to serve 37 organizations globally.\n\n## Backed by\n\n[Commvault-logo]\n\n**A leading data backup company**\n\n[seed-group-logo]\n\n**The Private Office of Sheikh Saeed bin Ahmed Al Maktoum**\n\n[us-state-fund-logo]\n\n**Connecticut Innovations**\n\nInvestors\nAccelerated by\n\n## Our Battle Against Digital Threats\n\n## 2015\n\nWe are Starting up\n* CloudSEK was founded by Rahul Sasi in September\n* Raised seed funding from Meeran Foundation\n* The founding team started building an XVigil prototype\nFirst Product Launch \ud83d\ude80\n* Mark 1 Version of XVigil was launched\n* Eastern and BlueJeans Signed up as customers\n\n## 2016\n\n## 2017\n\nMore Improvements \ud83c\udf89\n* Addition of Machine Learning Classifiers capable of identifying the severity levels of threats\n* Mark 2 of XVigil was released\nProduct Upgrades \u2699\ufe0f\n* Pre-series A funding led by Exfinity Venture Partners and StartupXseed\n* Mark 3 of XVigil was unveiled with multiple functionalities\n\n## 2018\n\n## 2019\n\nMarket Expansion \ud83c\udf0e\n\nCloudSEK expanded operations in India, South East Asia and Americas\n\nAwards and Recognitions \ud83c\udfc6\n* Bagged NetApp Excellerator\u2019s \u201cBest Growth Strategy Award\u201d as part of its Fifth Demo Day\n* **CloudSEK XVigil becomes a part of NVIDIA Inception Program**\n* CloudSEK bags Cybersecurity Award at NASSCOM Emerge 50 2020A part of Nasscom Emerge 50 awards in\nCybersecurity Category |** **[**Read more**][48]\n* **CloudSEK Wins NASSCOM-DSCI Excellence Award for Security Product Company of the Year 2020 |\n**[**Read More**][49]\n[CloudSEK Awards]\n\n## 2020\n\n## 2021\n\nFunding \ud83d\udcb5\n\nWe raised an $7 million investment (~INR 50 Cr) in Series A funding led by MassMutual Ventures. This\nbrings the total investment in to ~$10 M.**\n\u200d**\u200d[**Read About the Funding**][50]\n\n**Diving Deeper into Security**\n* Launched BeVigil app on Google Play for app security checks.\n* Rolled out BeVigil Enterprise for advanced External Attack Surface Management (EASM).\n* Unveiled SVigil at DSCI Conclave to counter digital vendor supply-chain threats.\n\n## **2023**\n\n## 2024\n\n**Fighting Misinformation with AI**\n\nWe released a free, AI-powered DeepFake Video Analyzer to help people detect and prevent deepfake\nscams and misinformation.\n\n**The Dawn of a New Era\n\nCloudSEK launched Nexus, an AI-powered cybersecurity command center that unifies threat\nintelligence, integrates attack surface insights, and translates complex cyber risks into clear,\nactionable business impact.\n\n**Renewed Backing, Strengthened Trust\n\nIn May 2025, CloudSEK raised $19 million across its Series A2 and B1 rounds, backed by investors\nlike MassMutual Ventures, Inflexor Ventures, Prana Ventures, Tenacity Ventures, and Commvault. Early\nsupporters such as the Meeran Family, StartupXSeed, Neon Fund, and Exfinity Ventures continue to\nback CloudSEK\u2019s vision.\n\n## **2025**\n\n## 2026\n\n**Global Confidence, Strategic Backing**\n\nCloudSEK secured a strategic investment from Connecticut Innovations, the venture capital arm of the\nState of Connecticut, as part of its $10 million Series B2 round.\n\nJoin our newsletter\nWe\u2019ll send you a nice letter once per week. No spam.\n[Untitled UI logotext][Logo]\n][51]\nProduct\nXVigil\n][52][\nBeVigil\n][53][\nSVigil\nNew\n][54][\nTutorials\n][55][\nPricing\n][56][\nReleases\n][57]\nCompany\nAbout us\n][58][\nCareers\n][59][\nPress\n][60][\nNews\n][61][\nMedia kit\n][62][\nContact\n][63]\nResources\nBlog\n][64][\nNewsletter\n][65][\nEvents\n][66][\nHelp centre\n][67][\nTutorials\n][68][\nSupport\n][69]\nUse Cases\nStartups\n][70][\nEnterprise\n][71][\nGovernment\n][72][\nSaaS\n][73][\nMarketplaces\n][74][\nEcommerce\n][75]\nSocial\nTwitter\n][76][\nLinkedIn\n][77][\nFacebook\n][78][\nGitHub\n][79][\nAngelList\n][80][\nDribbble\n][81]\n\u00a9 2077 Untitled UI\n[Privacy][82][GDPR][83][Disclosure of Vulnerability][84]\n][85][\n][86][\n][87][\n][88]\nProducts\nNexus AI\n][89][\nXVigil\n][90][\nBeVigil\n][91][\nSVigil\n][92][\nThreat Intelligence\n][93][\nCloudSEK Exposure\n][94][\nAIVigil\n][95]\nMobile App\n[[Google Play button to download App ]\n][96]\nSolutions\nCyber Threats Monitoring\n][97][\nDark Web Monitoring\n][98][\nBrand Threat Monitoring\n][99][\nInfra Threat Monitoring\n][100][\nPartners Secret Scanning\n][101][\nBeVigil Jenkins CI\n][102][\nBeVigil OSINT CLI\n][103][\nBeVigil Asset Explorer\n][104][\nTakedowns\n][105]\nResources\nBlogs and Articles\n][106][\nThreat Intelligence\n][107][\nWhitepapers and Reports\n][108][\nKnowledge Base\n][109][\nIntegrations\n][110]\nCommunity\nDiscord Community\n][111][\nStudent Challenge\n][112]\nCompany\nAbout us\n][113][\nCustomers\n][114][\nPartners\n][115][\nReferral Program\n][116][\nLife at CloudSEK\n][117][\nSecure Sips\n][118][\nCareers\n][119][\nAnnouncements\n][120][\nPress\n][121][\nContact Us\n][122]\n[[CloudSEK Logo]][123]\n][124][\n][125][[Linkedin Icon ]][126][\n][127]\n\nAt CloudSEK, we combine the power of Cyber Intelligence, Brand Monitoring, Attack Surface\nMonitoring, Infrastructure Monitoring and Supply Chain Intelligence to give context to our\ncustomers\u2019 digital risks.\n\nGDPR Policy\n][128][\nPrivacy\n][129][\nVulnerability Disclosure\n][130][\nDPA\n][131][\nCookies Policy\n][132][\nSitemap\n][133][\nLLM Info\n][134][\nEULA\n][135]\n\n[1]: https://www.cloudsek.com/ancmt/cloudsek-becomes-first-indian-origin-cybersecurity-company-to-re\nceive-investment-from-a-u-s-state-fund\n[2]: https://www.cloudsek.com/ancmt/cloudsek-becomes-first-active-indian-cybersecurity-firm-to-partn\ner-with-seed-group-a-company-of-the-private-office-of-sheikh-saeed-bin-ahmed-al-maktoum\n[3]: https://www.cloudsek.com/blog/cloudsek-raises-19-million-in-series-b1-funding-to-scale-predicti\nve-cybersecurity-platform\n[4]: /?r=0\n[5]: /nexus\n[6]: /xvigil\n[7]: /bevigil-enterprise\n[8]: /svigil\n[9]: /threat-intelligence\n[10]: https://bevigil.com/?Ref=cloudsek.com\n[11]: https://exposure.cloudsek.com/?Ref=cloudsek.com\n[12]: /aivigil\n[13]: /cyber-threats\n[14]: /cyber-threats/dark-web-monitoring\n[15]: /brand-monitor\n[16]: /bevigil-enterprise\n[17]: https://bevigil.com/bevigil-secrets-scanning-partner-program\n[18]: https://plugins.jenkins.io/bevigil-ci/\n[19]: https://github.com/Bevigil/BeVigil-OSINT-CLI\n[20]: https://bevigil.com/osint-api\n[21]: /blog\n[22]: /threatintelligence\n[23]: /knowledgebase\n[24]: /whitepapers-reports\n[25]: /customers\n[26]: /cloudsek-academy\n[27]: /integrations\n[28]: /partners\n[29]: /about-us\n[30]: /work-life\n[31]: /openings\n[32]: /events\n[33]: /privacy-policy\n[34]: /compliance\n[35]: /whitepapers-reports/cloudsek-global-threat-landscape-report-2025\n[36]: /cyber-threats\n[37]: https://community.cloudsek.com/\n[38]: /brand-monitor\n[39]: https://bevigil.com/?Ref=cloudsek.com\n[40]: https://bevigil.com/?Ref=cloudsek.com\n[41]: https://exposure.cloudsek.com/?Ref=cloudsek.com\n[42]: https://bevigil.com/osint-api\n[43]: #\n[44]: /request-a-demo\n[45]: /request-a-demo\n[46]: /work-life\n[47]: #\n[48]: https://cloudsek.com/ancmt/cloudsek-bags-cybersecurity-award-at-nasscom-emerge-50-2020/\n[49]: https://cloudsek.com/ancmt/cloudsek-wins-nasscom-dsci-excellence-award-for-security-product-co\nmpany-of-the-year-2020/\n[50]: https://cloudsek.com/anc"
