            "url": "https://shieldworkz.com/case-studies/securing-data-centers:-ot-and-iot-cybersecurity-for-modern-facilities",
            "text": "[site-logo]\n][1]\n\nOThello\n\nServices\n\nProducts\n\nIndustries\n\nResources\n\nCompany\n\nRequest a demo\n\n][2]\nSelect LanguageEnglish\n[site-logo]\n][3]\n\nOThello\n\nServices\n\nProducts\n\nIndustries\n\nResources\n\nCompany\n\nRequest a demo\n\n][4]\nSelect LanguageEnglish\n[site-logo]\n][5]\n\n### **Case Study**\n\n# **Securing Data Centers****\n# ****OT & IoT Cybersecurity for Modern Facilities**\n\n### **The changing risk, why data centers need OT & IoT security now**\n\nModern data centers are not just racks and virtual machines. They are living, instrumented\nfacilities - cooling plants, PDUs, UPS, fire systems, access control and thousands of sensors - that\nstraddle the line between IT and physical operations. That convergence creates an attack surface\nthat traditional IT security controls were never built for. Shieldworkz helps decision-makers in\nmanufacturing, energy, telecom and enterprise IT close that gap with industrial-grade OT security\ntailored for the data-center environment.\n\nNote: Our approach and recommendations draw on industry incident analysis and a Shieldworkz\ndata-center use case.\n\n### **Why this Securing Data Centers case study matters**\n\nCyber-related failures are a material cause of downtime: independent outage analysis shows cyber\nincidents are now responsible for a meaningful share of data-center outages.\n\nBreach costs remain high: the global average cost of a data breach reached roughly **$4.9M** in\nrecent industry studies - and impacts that involve operational downtime can be considerably more\nexpensive.\n\nOT/ICS exposure is rising: multiple scans and research projects show tens of thousands - and growing\ninto the hundreds of thousands - of ICS/OT and IoT systems exposed or discoverable online,\nincreasing the odds of opportunistic compromise.\n\nPut plainly: if a cooling system fails, devices overheat and workloads are lost. If a UPS or PDU is\ntampered with, customers and SLAs suffer. The technical and commercial risk is both direct\n(equipment and data loss) and cascading (service outages, regulatory scrutiny, reputational\ndamage).\n\n**Why download the case study**\n\nThis page is for leaders responsible for uptime, compliance and risk - Data Center Managers, OT\nEngineers, Head of Infrastructure, and CISOs. Downloading our detailed case study gives you:\n\nA **real-world remediation plan** built from an actual Shieldworkz data-center engagement (not a\ngeneric checklist).\n\nPractical KPIs and measurable outcomes you can present to procurement and execs (visibility targets,\nMTTR goals, segmentation metrics).\n\nA prioritized roadmap you can implement in phases - so you protect the most critical systems first,\nwith minimal disruption.\n\n### **Key takeaways from the case study**\n\n**Visibility-first wins** - Identify every OT, IoT and embedded device in racks, roof spaces and\nplant rooms. Asset-level inventory is the prerequisite for any control.\n\n**Protocol-aware detection matters** - Signature-only IT tools miss Modbus, BACnet, SNMP and other\nOT telemetry. Protocol-aware NDR and behavior analytics detect early deviations before outages.\n\n**Micro-segmentation prevents escalation** - Segment management, control and operational networks so\na single compromised device cannot traverse to critical systems.\n\n**Protect power & cooling as primary targets** - UPS, chillers and BMS are high-impact assets;\nmonitoring, integrity checks and strict control-plane policies significantly lower outage risk.\n\n**Supply-chain and portable media hygiene** - Verify firmware and sanitize portable media to prevent\nvendor-supplied or contractor-supplied compromise.\n\n### **How Shieldworkz supports data center**\n\nShieldworkz helps data centers strengthen OT security without disrupting operations through a\nfocused, outcome-driven approach. We deliver continuous asset visibility using safe discovery\nmethods and risk-based device scoring to prioritize patching and isolation. Our OT-aware threat\ndetection identifies anomalies in industrial protocols and correlates them with physical behaviors.\nNetwork hardening and micro-segmentation prevent lateral movement, while our integrated OT SOC\nensures rapid, safe incident response. We also provide secure patch management for embedded systems,\nportable media safety, and compliance support aligned with IEC 62443 and NIST SP 800-82, building a\nresilient, compliant, and efficient security framework.\n\n### **Ready to act - get a free, tailored data-center security roadmap**\n\nIf you manage uptime, SLAs, or critical infrastructure, a quick conversation will help us tailor\nrecommendations to your environment. Fill the form to request:\n\nA **30-minute site risk brief**\n\nA **custom roadmap** with phase-1, phase-2 deliverables and transparent cost/benefit estimates\n\nAccess to the full data-center case study and an executive one-pager you can use for board or\nprocurement meetings\n\nComplete the short form and choose a preferred time for a 30-minute consultation. Shieldworkz will\nreturn a prioritized, non-intrusive roadmap you can implement with your operations calendar.\n\n#### Schedule a Consultation to\n#### Secure Modern Data Center Operations\n\n[Cybersecurity website footer]\n\n### About Us\n\nWe secure Operational Technology environments and protect businesses with best-in-class professional\nservices and cyber security solutions.\n\n[Shieldworkz logo footer]\n][6]\n\n#### Company\n\nAbout Us\n\n][7][\n\nContact Us\n\n][8][\n\nPartner Program\n\n][9][\n\nCareers\n\n][10][\n\nEvents\n\n][11][\n\nFAQs\n\n][12]\n\n#### Resources\n\nBlog\n\n][13][\n\nRegulatory Playbooks\n\n][14][\n\nRemediation Guides\n\n][15][\n\nReports\n\n][16][\n\nE-Books\n\n][17][\n\nCase Studies\n\n][18][\n\nUse Cases\n\n][19][\n\nNewsroom\n\n][20][\n\nWebinars\n\n][21][\n\nGlossary\n\n][22]\n\n#### Products\n\nOT Security Platform\n\n][23][\n\nMedia Scan Solution\n\n][24][\n\nPatch Management Solution\n\n][25]\n\n#### Services\n\nOT Security Risk Assessment and Gap Analysis\n\n][26][\n\nManaged SOC Service\n\n][27][\n\nOT Incident Response Retainer Service\n\n][28][\n\nOT Vulnerability Assessment / Penetration Testing Service\n\n][29][\n\nAll Services\n\n][30]\n\n#### Useful Links\n\nOT Security\n\n][31][\n\nNIS2 Compliance\n\n][32][\n\nNERC CIP Framework\n\n][33][\n\nNetwork Detection and Response\n\n][34][\n\nCPS Protection\n\n][35][\n\nSOC as a Service\n\n][36][\n\nIEC 62443\n\n][37]\n][38][\n][39][\n][40][\n][41][\n][42]\n\nCopyright \u00a9 2026, Shieldworkz - All Rights Reserved.\n\nTerms & Conditions\n\n][43][\n\nPrivacy Policy\n\n][44]\n[Cybersecurity website footer]\n\n### About Us\n\nWe secure Operational Technology environments and protect businesses with best-in-class professional\nservices and cyber security solutions.\n\n[Shieldworkz logo footer]\n][45]\n\n#### Company\n\nAbout Us\n\n][46][\n\nContact Us\n\n][47][\n\nPartner Program\n\n][48][\n\nCareers\n\n][49][\n\nEvents\n\n][50][\n\nFAQs\n\n][51]\n\n#### Resources\n\nBlog\n\n][52][\n\nRegulatory Playbooks\n\n][53][\n\nRemediation Guides\n\n][54][\n\nReports\n\n][55][\n\nE-Books\n\n][56][\n\nCase Studies\n\n][57][\n\nUse Cases\n\n][58][\n\nNewsroom\n\n][59][\n\nWebinars\n\n][60][\n\nGlossary\n\n][61]\n\n#### Products\n\nOT Security Platform\n\n][62][\n\nMedia Scan Solution\n\n][63][\n\nPatch Management Solution\n\n][64]\n\n#### Services\n\nOT Security Risk Assessment and Gap Analysis\n\n][65][\n\nManaged SOC Service\n\n][66][\n\nOT Incident Response Retainer Service\n\n][67][\n\nOT Vulnerability Assessment / Penetration Testing Service\n\n][68][\n\nAll Services\n\n][69]\n\n#### Useful Links\n\nOT Security\n\n][70][\n\nNIS2 Compliance\n\n][71][\n\nNERC CIP Framework\n\n][72][\n\nNetwork Detection and Response\n\n][73][\n\nCPS Protection\n\n][74][\n\nSOC as a Service\n\n][75][\n\nIEC 62443\n\n][76]\n][77][\n][78][\n][79][\n][80][\n][81]\n\nCopyright \u00a9 2026, Shieldworkz - All Rights R