            "url": "https://shieldworkz.com/case-studies/securing-a-large-airport-risk-gap-analysis-solution-deployment",
            "text": "[site-logo]\n][1]\n\nOThello\n\nServices\n\nProducts\n\nIndustries\n\nResources\n\nCompany\n\nRequest a demo\n\n][2]\nSelect LanguageEnglish\n[site-logo]\n][3]\n\nOThello\n\nServices\n\nProducts\n\nIndustries\n\nResources\n\nCompany\n\nRequest a demo\n\n][4]\nSelect LanguageEnglish\n[site-logo]\n][5]\n\n### **Case Study**\n\n# **Securing a Large Airport****\n# ****Risk & Gap Analysis + Solution Deployment**\n\n### The evolving threat to airport operations\n\nAirports are among the most complex and safety-critical OT environments on earth. They run\nair-traffic systems, baggage handling, fueling, ground services, terminal systems and security\ncontrols, all wired together across airside and landside domains. When a major regional airport\nasked Shieldworkz to assess and harden its operations, the brief was straightforward but urgent:\nfind the blind spots, prioritize the fixes that impact safety and uptime, and deliver evidence the\nboard and regulators can trust.\n\nThis case study summarizes that engagement: the risks we uncovered, the safety-first approach we\nused, and the measurable outcomes the airport achieved. Use it to understand practical next steps\nfor your operations and to request the full case study and remediation playbook.\n\n### **About the Shieldworkz case study: what you\u2019ll learn**\n\nShieldworkz partnered with a large international airport to run a full-spectrum OT/ICS security\nprogram: a production-safe gap analysis, prioritized threat assessment, targeted remediation, and\nvalidation. This landing page summarizes the engagement and invites decision-makers to download the\nfull case study that contains:\n\nThe initial risk profile and discovery methodology we used in a live airport environment.\n\nReal findings: undocumented field devices, insecure remote maintenance channels, asymmetric\nsegmentation and legacy systems with exploitable configurations.\n\nThe remediation plan we executed-phased to avoid service disruption-and the validation evidence\nprovided to the airport\u2019s board and regulator.\n\nPractical playbooks and KPIs you can adopt immediately.\n\nIf your remit covers runway safety, baggage systems, terminal operations or airside control systems,\nthis case study gives you a battle-tested path to measurable improvement.\n\n**Why download the full case study**\n\nThis case study is practical and tactical-not a marketing brochure. Download it to get:\n\nA clear description of the assessment phases used to map OT risk across terminal, airside and\nlandside systems.\n\nA prioritized remediation playbook that ties fixes to safety, regulatory and financial impact (so\nyou can make the business case to execs).\n\nExample KPIs and an evidence pack template that the airport used to prove progress to regulators and\nboard members.\n\n### **Key takeaways from the case study**\n\n**Make inventory your control plane.** A verified asset registry unlocks prioritized remediation and\nfaster advisory mapping.\n\n**Prioritize by consequence.** Fix air-traffic, power and safety systems before chasing low-impact\nCVEs.\n\n**Start passive-then validate actively.** Passive discovery prevents outages; controlled active\ntesting follows in approved windows.\n\n**Tighten vendor and remote access.** Vendor sessions are common escalation paths-enforce MFA,\nlogging and least-privilege.\n\n**Measure what the board cares about.** Use discovery coverage, MTTR/MTTD, Tier-1 remediation\ncompletion and false-positive reduction as primary KPIs.\n\n### **How Shieldworkz supports airports end-to-end**\n\nShieldworkz combines OT domain expertise, an OT-native security platform, and managed detection\nservices tailored to high-availability environments:\n\nProduction-safe discovery and asset intelligence.\n\nThreat management, vulnerability scoring and OT SIEM integration.\n\nMicro-segmentation, deception/honeypots and secure vendor access controls.\n\nManaged OT SOC with incident response, playbooks and ongoing validation.\n\nTraining and handover so your operations team owns the security lifecycle.\n\n### **Ready to secure your airport without grounding operations?**\n\n**Download the full Shieldworkz case study** to get the remediation playbook, validation artifacts,\nand a prioritized roadmap tailored for large airports. **Fill out the form** to request the study\nand book a free scoping call for a production-safe rapid assessment.\n\n#### Schedule a Meeting With Experts for\n#### Airport Security Transformation\n\n### The evolving threat to airport operations\n\nAirports are among the most complex and safety-critical OT environments on earth. They run\nair-traffic systems, baggage handling, fueling, ground services, terminal systems and security\ncontrols, all wired together across airside and landside domains. When a major regional airport\nasked Shieldworkz to assess and harden its operations, the brief was straightforward but urgent:\nfind the blind spots, prioritize the fixes that impact safety and uptime, and deliver evidence the\nboard and regulators can trust.\n\nThis case study summarizes that engagement: the risks we uncovered, the safety-first approach we\nused, and the measurable outcomes the airport achieved. Use it to understand practical next steps\nfor your operations and to request the full case study and remediation playbook.\n\n### **About the Shieldworkz case study: what you\u2019ll learn**\n\nShieldworkz partnered with a large international airport to run a full-spectrum OT/ICS security\nprogram: a production-safe gap analysis, prioritized threat assessment, targeted remediation, and\nvalidation. This landing page summarizes the engagement and invites decision-makers to download the\nfull case study that contains:\n\nThe initial risk profile and discovery methodology we used in a live airport environment.\n\nReal findings: undocumented field devices, insecure remote maintenance channels, asymmetric\nsegmentation and legacy systems with exploitable configurations.\n\nThe remediation plan we executed-phased to avoid service disruption-and the validation evidence\nprovided to the airport\u2019s board and regulator.\n\nPractical playbooks and KPIs you can adopt immediately.\n\nIf your remit covers runway safety, baggage systems, terminal operations or airside control systems,\nthis case study gives you a battle-tested path to measurable improvement.\n\n**Why download the full case study**\n\nThis case study is practical and tactical-not a marketing brochure. Download it to get:\n\nA clear description of the assessment phases used to map OT risk across terminal, airside and\nlandside systems.\n\nA prioritized remediation playbook that ties fixes to safety, regulatory and financial impact (so\nyou can make the business case to execs).\n\nExample KPIs and an evidence pack template that the airport used to prove progress to regulators and\nboard members.\n\n### **Key takeaways from the case study**\n\n**Make inventory your control plane.** A verified asset registry unlocks prioritized remediation and\nfaster advisory mapping.\n\n**Prioritize by consequence.** Fix air-traffic, power and safety systems before chasing low-impact\nCVEs.\n\n**Start passive-then validate actively.** Passive discovery prevents outages; controlled active\ntesting follows in approved windows.\n\n**Tighten vendor and remote access.** Vendor sessions are common escalation paths-enforce MFA,\nlogging and least-privilege.\n\n**Measure what the board cares about.** Use discovery coverage, MTTR/MTTD, Tier-1 remediation\ncompletion and false-positive reduction as primary KPIs.\n\n### **How Shieldworkz supports airports end-to-end**\n\nShieldworkz combines OT domain expertise, an OT-native security platform, and managed detection\nservices tailored to high-availability environments:\n\nProduction-safe discovery and asset intelligence.\n\nThreat management, vulnerability scoring and OT SIEM integration.\n\nMicro-segmentation, deception/honeypots and secure vendor access controls.\n\nManaged OT SOC with incident response, playbooks and ongoing validation.\n\nTraining and handover so your operations team owns the security lifecycle.\n\n### **Ready to secure your airport without grounding operations?**\n\n**Download the full Shieldworkz case study** to get the remediation playbook, validation artifacts,\nand a prioritized roadmap tailored for large airports. **Fill out the form** to request the study\nand book a free scoping call for a production-safe rapid assessment.\n\n#### Schedule a Meeting With Experts for\n#### Airport Security Transformation\n\n[Cybersecurity website footer]\n\n### About Us\n\nWe secure Operational Technology environments and protect businesses with best-in-class professional\nservices and cyber security solutions.\n\n[Shieldworkz logo footer]\n][6]\n\n#### Company\n\nAbout Us\n\n][7][\n\nContact Us\n\n][8][\n\nPartner Program\n\n][9][\n\nCareers\n\n][10][\n\nEvents\n\n][11][\n\nFAQs\n\n][12]\n\n#### Resources\n\nBlog\n\n][13][\n\nRegulatory Playbooks\n\n][14][\n\nRemediation Guides\n\n][15][\n\nReports\n\n][16][\n\nE-Books\n\n][17][\n\nCase Studies\n\n][18][\n\nUse Cases\n\n][19][\n\nNewsroom\n\n][20][\n\nWebinars\n\n][21][\n\nGlossary\n\n][22]\n\n#### Products\n\nOT Security Platform\n\n][23][\n\nMedia Scan Solution\n\n][24][\n\nPatch Management Solution\n\n][25]\n\n#### Services\n\nOT Security Risk Assessment and Gap Analysis\n\n][26][\n\nManaged SOC Service\n\n][27][\n\nOT Incident Response Retainer Service\n\n][28][\n\nOT Vulnerability Assessment / Penetration Testing Service\n\n][29][\n\nAll Services\n\n][30]\n\n#### Useful Links\n\nOT Security\n\n][31][\n\nNIS2 Compliance\n\n][32][\n\nNERC CIP Framework\n\n][33][\n\nNetwork Detection and Response\n\n][34][\n\nCPS Protection\n\n][35][\n\nSOC as a Service\n\n][36][\n\nIEC 62443\n\n][37]\n][38][\n][39][\n][40][\n][41][\n][42]\n\nCopyright \u00a9 2026, Shieldworkz - All Rights Reserved.\n\nTerms & Conditions\n\n][43][\n\nPrivacy Policy\n\n][44]\n[Cybersecurity website footer]\n\n### About Us\n\nWe secure Operational Technology environments and protect businesses with best-in-class professional\nservices and cyber security solutions.\n\n[Shieldworkz logo footer]\n][45]\n\n#### Company\n\nAbout Us\n\n][46][\n\nContact Us\n\n][47][\n\nPartner Program\n\n][48][\n\nCareers\n\n][49][\n\nEvents\n\n][50][\n\nFAQs\n\n][51]\n\n#### Resources\n\nBlog\n\n][52][\n\nRegulatory Playbooks\n\n][53][\n\nRemediation Guides\n\n][54][\n\nReports\n\n][55][\n\nE-Books\n\n][56][\n\nCase Studies\n\n][57][\n\nUse Cases\n\n][58][\n\nNewsroom\n\n][59][\n\nWebinars\n\n][60][\n\nGlossary\n\n][61]\n\n#### Products\n\nOT Security Platform\n\n][62][\n\nMedia Scan Solution\n\n][63][\n\nPatch Management Solution\n\n][64]\n\n#### Services\n\nOT Security Risk Assessment and Gap Analysis\n\n][65][\n\nManaged SOC Service\n\n][66][\n\nOT Incident Response Retainer Service\n\n][67][\n\nOT Vulnerability Assessment / Penetration Testing Service\n\n][68][\n\nAll Services\n\n][69]\n\n#### Useful Links\n\nOT Security\n\n][70][\n\nNIS2 Compliance\n\n][71][\n\nNERC CIP Framework\n\n][72][\n\nNetwork Detection and Response\n\n][73][\n\nCPS Protection\n\n][74][\n\nSOC as a Service\n\n][75][\n\nIEC 62443\n\n][76]\n][77][\n][78][\n][79][\n][80][\n][81]\n\nCopyright \u00a9 2026, Shieldworkz - All Rights Reserved.\n\nTerms & Conditions\n\n][82][\n\nPrivacy Policy\n\n][83]\n[Cybersecurity website footer]\n\n### About Us\n\nWe secure Operational Technology environments and protect businesses with best-in-class professional\nservices and cyber security solutions.\n\n[Shieldworkz logo footer]\n][84]\n\n#### Company\n\nAbout Us\n\n][85][\n\nContact Us\n\n][86][\n\nPartner Program\n\n][87][\n\nCareers\n\n][88][\n\nEvents\n\n][89]\n\n#### Resources\n\nBlog\n\n][90][\n\nRegulatory Playbooks\n\n][91][\n\nRemediation Guides\n\n][92][\n\nReports\n\n][93][\n\nE-Books\n\n][94][\n\nCase Studies\n\n][95][\n\nUse Cases\n\n][96][\n\nNewsroom\n\n][97][\n\nWeb