          {
            "url": "https://trginternational.com/about-us/",
            "text": "[[TRG International Logo]][1]\n[[TRG International Logo]][2]\n\nSolutions\n\n][3]\n[Resources][4]\n[Stories][5]\n[Events][6]\n[About us][7]\n[Careers][8]\n[Watch Demo][9][Get in Touch][10]\nEnglish\n\n# About Us\n\nTRG International is a global leader in professional services, offering seamless IT solutions. We\ndrive innovations and growth, enabling businesses to focus on core operations.\n\n[TRG International team gathering]\n[TRG International event with partners]\n[TRG International office celebration]\n[TRG International colleagues at an internship programme]\n[TRG International award ceremony]\n[TRG International team members smiling]\n[TRG International at a community event]\n[TRG International company group photo]\n\nFrom a Kitchen Table to Global Impact\n\n## Our story didn't start in a boardroom. It started from Rick's kitchen table.\n\nIn 1990, Rick Yvanovich was posted to Vietnam as a Finance Manager for BP Exploration. Four years\nlater, when oil prices dipped, BP offered him a ticket back to London. Enjoying his time in Vietnam,\nRick chose voluntary redundancy and \"retired.\"\n\nThat retirement lasted exactly one week before boredom set in.\n\n> \u201cBack in the day, there was little to do so I used to implement the system for my peers at other\n> oil companies during the weekends. The rest, they say, is history.\u201d\n\nRick YvanovichFounder & CEO, TRG International\n[Rick Yvanovich, Founder & CEO of TRG International]\n\nKey Milestones\n\n## Three decades of building systems that work\n\nScroll through the moments that shaped TRG \u2014 from a one-person consultancy to a global technology\npartner.\n* [Original TRG logo]1994\n\nTRG International is officially founded\n* [Current TRG logo]2012\n\nUnveiled a new brand identity\n* 2016\n\nOpened a new office in District 2 (now Thu Duc City), Vietnam\n* 2020\n\nAchieved 100% \"virtual readiness\"\n* 2024\n\nCelebrated its 30th anniversary\n* 2026\n\nReceived 3 Infor Partner Network Awards\n* Beyond\n\nContinues to shape the future & empower next-gen talent\n\n## Our Building Blocks\n\n### Purpose Statement\n\nHelp you and your business shine.\n\n### Mission Statement\n\nTo be your preferred partner providing systems that work.\n\n### Vision Statement\n\nGuide your business to greatness every day.\n\n## Our 6 Core Values\n\nIn everything we do, we must ask ourselves if it aligns with our \"Why\". This is our \"Why\",\ninfluencing \"How\" we think and act. Yes, we always start with \"Why?\"\n\nPassionIntegrityInnovationCoaching CultureCollaborationKaizen\n[Working with focus and flow at TRG]\n\n### Passion\n\n#### Key Takeaways\n\nPassion is more than just enthusiasm; it's about achieving a state of flow in activities and aiming\nfor Eudaimonia, or human flourishing, in life. It's the driving force behind TRG's pursuit of\nexcellence and contributes to a greater sense of well-being and fulfilment.\n\nCorrect Behaviour\n\nIndividuals push themselves beyond their comfort zone to achieve higher levels of performance.\n\nIncorrect Behaviour\n\nAn employee does only the bare minimum required for their job.\n\n[Doing the right thing, consistently, at TRG]\n\n### Integrity\n\n#### Key Takeaways\n\nThe moral compass that guides every action and decision at TRG. It's about being honest,\ntransparent, and doing the right thing consistently.\n\nCorrect Behaviour\n\nAn employee admits when they don't know something instead of pretending to understand.\n\nIncorrect Behaviour\n\nA team member takes credit for a colleague's work.\n\n[Ideas and creativity at TRG]\n\n### Innovation\n\n#### Key Takeaways\n\nNot just the generation of new ideas but the willingness to embrace failure as an integral part of\nthe process. It's about learning from mistakes, fostering creativity, and building resilience to\nachieve meaningful breakthroughs.\n\nCorrect Behaviour\n\nAn employee suggests a new approach to a recurring problem, even if it's risky.\n\nIncorrect Behaviour\n\nAn employee sticks to outdated methods and resists new technologies.\n\n[Mentoring and mutual learning at TRG]\n\n### Coaching Culture\n\n#### Key Takeaways\n\nAn ongoing effort to unlock individual potential for collective success. It involves creating a\nvirtuous cycle of growth and achievement through mutual learning.\n\nCorrect Behaviour\n\nAn employee sets up regular coaching / mentoring sessions with newer team members.\n\nIncorrect Behaviour\n\nAn employee declines to help a struggling colleague, saying they're too busy.\n\n[Teams working in sync at TRG]\n\n### Collaboration\n\n#### Key Takeaways\n\nAn intentional act that transcends departmental silos; it's about working as a team toward a common\norganizational goal. Everyone is both accountable and responsible, and the focus is on the bigger\npicture, not just individual team effort.\n\nCorrect Behaviour\n\nAn engineer/consultant consults the sales and marketing teams before finalizing a product feature.\n\nIncorrect Behaviour\n\nAn employee hoards information that could help other departments.\n\n[Continuous improvement and learning at TRG]\n\n### Kaizen\n\n#### Key Takeaways\n\nA commitment to lifelong learning and continuous, incremental improvement. It's about seizing every\nopportunity to grow, personally and professionally, and staying ahead of the curve. The philosophy\nis deeply ingrained in the operational heartbeat of TRG International.\n\nCorrect Behaviour\n\nAn employee regularly updates their skill set to adapt to new industry standards.\n\nIncorrect Behaviour\n\nAn employee dismisses new training opportunities, saying they already know enough.\n\n## Our People\n\nAt TRG International, our people are our greatest asset. Their dedication, expertise, and diverse\ntalents drive our success. Meet the team that makes TRG exceptional.\n\n[Grover Kiranjit Dhari, Head of Human Resources]\n\n### Grover Kiranjit Dhari\n\nHead of Human Resources\n\n][11]\n[Nguyen Duc Hien, Head of Professional Services]\n\n### Nguyen Duc Hien\n\nHead of Professional Services\n\n][12]\n[Nguyen Thuy Duong, Head of Customer Support]\n\n### Nguyen Thuy Duong\n\nHead of Customer Support\n\n][13]\n[Viktor Nagradic, Head of Marketing]\n\n### Viktor Nagradic\n\nHead of Marketing\n\n][14]\n[Andrew Turton, Head of Sales]\n\n### Andrew Turton\n\nHead of Sales\n\n][15]\n[More About Our Superstars][16]\n\n## Trusted by Success-Driven Organizations\n\nThe ultimate measure of our success is the growth of the businesses we support. Here are a few of\nthe clients and partners who trust TRG to optimize their operations.\n\n[Millennium Hotels and Resorts]\n[Dusit Thani]\n[Aman]\n[VinaCapital]\n[Vietcombank]\n[Prudential]\n[Dell]\n[Lenovo]\n[Accor]\n[Acronis]\n[Microsoft]\n[Cisco]\n[Intel]\n[Toyota]\n[Sun Life]\n[Millennium Hotels and Resorts]\n[Dusit Thani]\n[Aman]\n[VinaCapital]\n[Vietcombank]\n[Prudential]\n[Dell]\n[Lenovo]\n[Accor]\n[Acronis]\n[Microsoft]\n[Cisco]\n[Intel]\n[Toyota]\n[Sun Life]\n[Sun Life]\n[Toyota]\n[Intel]\n[Cisco]\n[Microsoft]\n[Acronis]\n[Accor]\n[Lenovo]\n[Dell]\n[Prudential]\n[Vietcombank]\n[VinaCapital]\n[Aman]\n[Dusit Thani]\n[Millennium Hotels and Resorts]\n[Sun Life]\n[Toyota]\n[Intel]\n[Cisco]\n[Microsoft]\n[Acronis]\n[Accor]\n[Lenovo]\n[Dell]\n[Prudential]\n[Vietcombank]\n[VinaCapital]\n[Aman]\n[Dusit Thani]\n[Millennium Hotels and Resorts]\n[View Our Success Stories][17]\n\n## The Scale of Our Trust\n\nSince 1994, TRG International has received numerous awards for our business services and societal\ncontributions. We thank our partners, customers, and stakeholders for recognizing our achievements\nand CSR efforts.\n\n[Infor Channel Partner Conference 2026 awards]\n\nFY25 APAC Net New Partner of the Year\n\nRead the story \u2192][18][\n[Infor Channel Partner Conference 2026 awards]\n\nFY25 APAC Cloud Upgrade Partner of the Year\n\nRead the story \u2192][19][\n[Infor Channel Partner Conference 2026 awards]\n\nFY25 APAC Partner of the Year\n\nRead the story \u2192][20]\n[Most Inspiring Entrepreneur from Vietnam 2024 trophy]\n\nMost Inspiring Entrepreneur from Vietnam in 2024\n\n[Exhibitor of Biztech Vietnam 2024 certificate]\n\nExhibitor of Biztech Vietnam 2024\n\n[Great People Inside]\n\nGreat People Inside Top Sales Award 2019\n\n[WWF Vietnam Green Office Diploma]\n\nGreen Office Diploma Award \u2014 WWF Vietnam\n\n[Microsoft Certified Partner]\n\nMicrosoft Silver Certified Partner\n\n[Microsoft Certified Partner]\n\nMicrosoft Gold Certified Partner\n\n[Microsoft Certified Partner]\n\nMicrosoft Certified Solution Provider\n\n[ACNielsen \u2014 Vietnam Top 50 Best Employers]\n\nVietnam's Top 50 Best Employers\n\n[See All Awards][21]\n\n## We are always saving seats for new talent!\n\nWhether you're seeking a permanent or internship position, you'll be amazed to see that as the\nbusiness grows, you grow too.\n\n[Join Our Team][22]\n[The TRG International team]\n[logo]\n\nWe've thrived since 1994 resulting in lots of experience to share, we are beyond a companion, to\nmore than 1,000 clients in 80+ countries.\n\nFollow us on Social Media\n[[linkedn]][23][[facebook]][24][[youtube]][25]\n[Solutions][26]\n[TRG Solutions][27][Business Challenges][28][Industries][29]\n[Resources][30]\n[Podcasts][31][Blog][32][FAQ][33][Research Portal][34][TRG End-User Training][35]\n[Stories][36]\n[Case Studies][37][CEO Letters][38]\n[About us][39]\n[Our People][40][Awards][41][TRG Cares][42][Testimonials][43]\n[Events][44]\n[Become our Speaker][45][Events Gallery][46][Hire our venue][47]\n[Careers][48]\n[Internships][49][Internships Partners][50]\nFollow us on Social Media\n[[linkedn]][51][[facebook]][52][[Youtube Play Button]][53]\n\u00a9 2026 TRG International[Terms and Conditions][54][Privacy Policy][55]Cookie Preferences\n\u00a9 2026 TRG International\n\n[1]: /\n[2]: /\n[3]: /solutions/\n[4]: /resources/\n[5]: /stories/\n[6]: /events/\n[7]: /about-us/\n[8]: /careers/\n[9]: /watch-demo/\n[10]: /contacts-and-locations/\n[11]: /our-people/grover-kiranjit-dhari/\n[12]: /our-people/nguyen-duc-hien/\n[13]: /our-people/nguyen-thuy-duong/\n[14]: /our-people/viktor-nagradic/\n[15]: /our-people/andrew-turton/\n[16]: /about-us/our-people/\n[17]: /about-us/client-testimonials/\n[18]: /blog/sunsystems-cloud-channel-partner-conference-2026-awards/\n[19]: /blog/sunsystems-cloud-channel-partner-conference-2026-awards/\n[20]: /blog/sunsystems-cloud-channel-partner-conference-2026-awards/\n[21]: /about-us/our-awards/\n[22]: /careers/\n[23]: https://www.linkedin.com/company/trg-international/?originalSubdomain=sg\n[24]: https://www.facebook.com/TRGInternational/?locale=vi_VN\n[25]: https://www.youtube.com/@trginternational_official\n[26]: /solutions/\n[27]: /solutions/\n[28]: /business-challenges/\n[29]: /industries/\n[30]: /resources/\n[31]: /podcasts/\n[32]: /blog/\n[33]: /faq/\n[34]: /research/\n[35]: /trg-end-user-training/\n[36]: /stories/\n[37]: /stories/case-studies/\n[38]: /stories/business-as-unusual/\n[39]: /about-us/\n[40]: /about-us/our-people/\n[41]: /about-us/our-awards/\n[42]: /about-us/csr/\n[43]: /about-us/client-testimonials/\n[44]: /events/\n[45]: /events/become-our-speaker/\n[46]: /events/events-gallery/\n[47]: https://pjscoffeevietnam.com/catering\n[48]: /careers/\n[49]: /careers/internships/\n[50]: /careers/internship-partners/\n[51]: https://www.linkedin.com/company/trg-international/?originalSubdomain=sg\n[52]: https://www.facebook.com/TRGInternational/?locale=vi_VN\n[53]: https://www.youtube.com/@trginternational3812\n[54]: /terms-and-conditions/\n[55]: /privacy-policy/"
