          {
            "url": "https://trginternational.com/solutions/infor-birst/",
            "text": "[[TRG International Logo]][1]\n[[TRG International Logo]][2]\n\nSolutions\n\n][3]\n[Resources][4]\n[Stories][5]\n[Events][6]\n[About us][7]\n[Careers][8]\n[Watch Demo][9][Get in Touch][10]\nEnglish\n\n#### TRG SOLUTION\n\n# Infor Birst\n\nBirst is a cloud business intelligence (BI) tool and business analytics software platform that helps\norganizations understand and optimize complex processes in less time than traditional solutions.\n\n[Infor Birst hero image]\n[Hero section featured image]\n\n## Core Features\n\nInfor HMS is more than just a software solution; it\u2019s a strategic tool for transforming hospitality\nmanagement. Whether you\u2019re looking to enhance guest experiences, optimize operations, or improve\nyour bottom line, our expertise in implementing Infor HMS can help you achieve your business goals.\n\n#### Reservation Management\n\nStreamlines booking processes with real-time availability and centralized control.\n\n[icon]\n\n#### Mobile Access\n\nEmpowers staff to manage operations remotely, enhancing responsiveness and service quality.\n\n[icon]\n\n#### Integrated PMS\n\nUnifies property management with other systems, ensuring seamless operational efficiency.\n\n[icon]\n\n#### Advanced Analytics\n\nDelivers actionable insights through powerful reporting and forecasting tools.\n\n[icon]\n\n#### Cloud Platform\n\nScales with your business, offering flexibility and cost-effective management.\n\n[icon]\n\n#### Guest Preferences\n\nTracks and utilizes guest data to personalize services, enhancing overall guest satisfaction.\n\n[icon]\n\n### TRG\u2019s Expertise\n\nBy partnering with TRG for the implementation of Infor HMS, you can ensure a tailored, seamless, and\nefficient deployment that aligns perfectly with your business goals, driving both operational\nexcellence and enhanced guest experiences.\n\n[circle chape][circle chape]\n\n## Seamless System Integration\n\nWe specialize in integrating Infor HMS with your existing technology stack, ensuring that all\nsystems work together seamlessly. This minimizes disruptions and helps you leverage the full power\nof Infor HMS across your entire operation.\n\n[thumbnail]\n\n#### Minimal Disruption\n\n#### Technology Compatibility\n\n#### Data Consistency\n\n#### Enhanced Performance\n\n#### Future-Proofing\n\n#### Minimal Disruption\n\n#### Technology Compatibility\n\n#### Data Consistency\n\n#### Enhanced Performance\n\n#### Future-Proofing\n\n[circle chape][circle chape]\n\n## Tailored Configuration and Customization\n\nWe configure and customize Infor HMS to match your operational workflows, from reservation\nmanagement to guest services. This personalization ensures that the system not only meets but\nexceeds your business requirements.\n\n[thumbnail]\n\n#### User-Friendly Interface\n\n#### Workflow Optimisation\n\n#### Increased Productivity\n\n#### Personalised Experience\n\n#### Cost Efficiency\n\n#### User-Friendly Interface\n\n#### Workflow Optimisation\n\n#### Increased Productivity\n\n#### Personalised Experience\n\n#### Cost Efficiency\n\n[circle chape][circle chape]\n\n## Comprehensive Training and Support\n\nTRG provides extensive training for your staff, ensuring they are fully equipped to utilize all the\nfeatures of Infor HMS. Our ongoing support guarantees that you continue to get the most out of your\ninvestment, with our team available to assist whenever needed.\n\n[thumbnail]\n\n#### Expert Guidance\n\n#### Staff Empowerment\n\n#### Continuous Support\n\n#### Quick Issue Resolution\n\n#### Knowledge Transfer\n\n#### Expert Guidance\n\n#### Staff Empowerment\n\n#### Continuous Support\n\n#### Quick Issue Resolution\n\n#### Knowledge Transfer\n\n### RESOURCES\n\nLatest resources for **Infor Birst**\n\n[View All Resources[icon]][11]\nSun, Feb 11, 2024\nDownload[icon]\n\n#### Compare On-premises vs. Multi-tenant Cloud for CFO\n\nDiscover how cloud-based financial applications compare to on-premises solutions\n][12][\nSun, Feb 11, 2024\nDownload[icon]\n\n#### Compare On-premises vs. Multi-tenant Cloud for CFO\n\nDiscover how cloud-based financial applications compare to on-premises solutions\n][13][\nMon, Mar 11, 2024\nDownload[icon]\n\n#### Compare On-premises vs. Multi-tenant Cloud for CFO\n\nDiscover how cloud-based financial applications compare to on-premises solutions\n][14]\n\n### INDUSTRIES WE SERVE\n\nTRG has implemented hotel management solutions for hospitality industry. This adaptability is one of\nthe key reasons why large scale hospitality groups choose us for their solution requirements.\n\n[icon][image]\n[Financial Services][15][Manufacturing][16][Retail][17][Insurance][18][Energy][19][Real\nEstate][20][Healthcare and F&B][21][Education][22]\n\n### OUR CLIENT\n\nSome of our satisfied customers utilising our Financial Management Solutions\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n\nbuild at: 2026-06-28T08:03:56.851Z\n[logo]\n\nWe've thrived since 1994 resulting in lots of experience to share, we are beyond a companion, to\nmore than 1,000 clients in 80+ countries.\n\nFollow us on Social Media\n[[linkedn]][23][[facebook]][24][[youtube]][25]\n[Solutions][26]\n[TRG Solutions][27][Business Challenges][28][Industries][29]\n[Resources][30]\n[Podcasts][31][Blog][32][FAQ][33][Research Portal][34][TRG End-User Training][35]\n[Stories][36]\n[Case Studies][37][CEO Letters][38]\n[About us][39]\n[Our People][40][Awards][41][TRG Cares][42][Testimonials][43]\n[Events][44]\n[Become our Speaker][45][Events Gallery][46][Hire our venue][47]\n[Careers][48]\n[Internships][49][Internships Partners][50]\nFollow us on Social Media\n[[linkedn]][51][[facebook]][52][[Youtube Play Button]][53]\n\u00a9 2026 TRG International[Terms and Conditions][54][Privacy Policy][55]Cookie Preferences\n\u00a9 2026 TRG International\n\n[1]: /\n[2]: /\n[3]: /solutions/\n[4]: /resources/\n[5]: /stories/\n[6]: /events/\n[7]: /about-us/\n[8]: /careers/\n[9]: /watch-demo/\n[10]: /contacts-and-locations/\n[11]: /resources/\n[12]: /\n[13]: /\n[14]: /\n[15]: /industries/financial-services/\n[16]: /industries/manufacturing/\n[17]: /business-challenges/retail-management/\n[18]: /industries/insurance/\n[19]: /industries/energy/\n[20]: /industries/real-estate/\n[21]: /industries/healthcare/\n[22]: /solutions/education/\n[23]: https://www.linkedin.com/company/trg-international/?originalSubdomain=sg\n[24]: https://www.facebook.com/TRGInternational/?locale=vi_VN\n[25]: https://www.youtube.com/@trginternational_official\n[26]: /solutions/\n[27]: /solutions/\n[28]: /business-challenges/\n[29]: /industries/\n[30]: /resources/\n[31]: /podcasts/\n[32]: /blog/\n[33]: /faq/\n[34]: /research/\n[35]: /trg-end-user-training/\n[36]: /stories/\n[37]: /stories/case-studies/\n[38]: /stories/business-as-unusual/\n[39]: /about-us/\n[40]: /about-us/our-people/\n[41]: /about-us/our-awards/\n[42]: /about-us/csr/\n[43]: /about-us/client-testimonials/\n[44]: /events/\n[45]: /events/become-our-speaker/\n[46]: /events/events-gallery/\n[47]: https://pjscoffeevietnam.com/catering\n[48]: /careers/\n[49]: /careers/internships/\n[50]: /careers/internship-partners/\n[51]: https://www.linkedin.com/company/trg-international/?originalSubdomain=sg\n[52]: https://www.facebook.com/TRGInternational/?locale=vi_VN\n[53]: https://www.youtube.com/@trginternational3812\n[54]: /terms-and-conditions/\n[55]: /privacy-policy/"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://trginternational.com/about-us/csr/tree-planting/",
            "text": "[[TRG International Logo]][1]\n[[TRG International Logo]][2]\n\nSolutions\n\n][3]\n[Resources][4]\n[Stories][5]\n[Events][6]\n[About us][7]\n[Careers][8]\n[Watch Demo][9][Get in Touch][10]\nEnglish\n\n# Tree Planting\n\n\u201cHe who plants a tree plants a hope\u201d \u2013 Lucy Larcom As we experience the erosion of coastal areas,\nthe intrusion of saltwater and the decline in air quality its not surprising that our annual \u201cTree\nplanting\u201d activity sees active participation!\n\n[Tree Planting hero image]\n[Hero section featured image]\n[icon]\n\n### Passion\n\nTRG International is a company who loves to give back to the communities in which we operate.\n[icon]\n\n### Engagement\n\nOur culture is to provide multiple opportunities for our employees to \u201cgive back\u201d and engage in\nsocietal development and environmental protection through real life hands-on experiences.\n[icon]\n\n### Service\n\nEmployees and their family members annually join a one-day tree planting trip full of exciting and\nfun outdoor activities.\n[circle chape][circle chape]\n01/\n\n#### A fun and healthy exercise\n\n[thumbnail]\n\nAs we experience the erosion of coastal areas, the intrusion of saltwater and the decline in air\nquality its not surprising that our annual \u201cTree planting\u201d activity sees active participation!\nIt\u2019s fun, educational and healthy exercise and we usually morph it into a one-day trip for the whole\nfamily, the kids especially love planting in the mangroves, as what kid doesn\u2019t enjoy squishy mud.\n\nOver the years we have planted thousands of trees of different varieties including: mangrove in\ncoastal areas, coconut in forest regeneration zones, and other varietals in temple grounds and new\nforests.\n\nWe\u2019d really like to plant a million trees, it\u2019ll take us many years to achieve, provide a lot of fun\nand make a very meaningful impact.\n\n[circle chape][circle chape]\n02/\n\n#### How we do it\n\n[thumbnail]\n\nTypically, at a tree planting event, we\u2019ll set a goal of how many trees the company should plant. To\nmake it more competitive, participants split up into teams and compete against each other to see who\nplants the most trees or plants the fastest. In that way, everyone has a chance to show off their\ncompetitive spirit while improving their team working and uncovering more efficient ways to plant\ntrees for a good purpose.\n\nThe outcome of these tree planting events always brings a smile to everyone\u2019s face as they enjoy a\nwonderful time in company with one another while they feel proud of their social achievements.\n\n[circle chape][circle chape]\n03/\n\n#### Why Tree Planting?\n\n[thumbnail]\n\nOver time, tree planting has become one of TRG\u2019s annual CSR activities as it is such a simple act,\nwhich makes a huge contribution to the future of the planet. Every year, we organise a one-day tree\nplanting trip and we invite employees and their family members to join. Not only does the tree\nplanting event have a CSR purpose, it also serves as a social event where teambuilding unfolds.\n\nUsually, we hold the event on our own with the help of a local authority or else we\u2019ll join a\nproject organised by an organisation e.g. WWF or Vietnam\u2019s Chamber of Commerce.\n\nbuild at: 2026-06-28T02:06:34.615Z\n[logo]\n\nWe've thrived since 1994 resulting in lots of experience to share, we are beyond a companion, to\nmore than 1,000 clients in 80+ countries.\n\nFollow us on Social Media\n[[linkedn]][11][[facebook]][12][[youtube]][13]\n[Solutions][14]\n[TRG Solutions][15][Business Challenges][16][Industries][17]\n[Resources][18]\n[Podcasts][19][Blog][20][FAQ][21][Research Portal][22][TRG End-User Training][23]\n[Stories][24]\n[Case Studies][25][CEO Letters][26]\n[About us][27]\n[Our People][28][Awards][29][TRG Cares][30][Testimonials][31]\n[Events][32]\n[Become our Speaker][33][Events Gallery][34][Hire our venue][35]\n[Careers][36]\n[Internships][37][Internships Partners][38]\nFollow us on Social Media\n[[linkedn]][39][[facebook]][40][[Youtube Play Button]][41]\n\u00a9 2026 TRG International[Terms and Conditions][42][Privacy Policy][43]Cookie Preferences\n\u00a9 2026 TRG International\n\n[1]: /\n[2]: /\n[3]: /solutions/\n[4]: /resources/\n[5]: /stories/\n[6]: /events/\n[7]: /about-us/\n[8]: /careers/\n[9]: /watch-demo/\n[10]: /contacts-and-locations/\n[11]: https://www.linkedin.com/company/trg-international/?originalSubdomain=sg\n[12]: https://www.facebook.com/TRGInternational/?locale=vi_VN\n[13]: https://www.youtube.com/@trginternational_official\n[14]: /solutions/\n[15]: /solutions/\n[16]: /business-challenges/\n[17]: /industries/\n[18]: /resources/\n[19]: /podcasts/\n[20]: /blog/\n[21]: /faq/\n[22]: /research/\n[23]: /trg-end-user-training/\n[24]: /stories/\n[25]: /stories/case-studies/\n[26]: /stories/business-as-unusual/\n[27]: /about-us/\n[28]: /about-us/our-people/\n[29]: /about-us/our-awards/\n[30]: /about-us/csr/\n[31]: /about-us/client-testimonials/\n[32]: /events/\n[33]: /events/become-our-speaker/\n[34]: /events/events-gallery/\n[35]: https://pjscoffeevietnam.com/catering\n[36]: /careers/\n[37]: /careers/internships/\n[38]: /careers/internship-partners/\n[39]: https://www.linkedin.com/company/trg-international/?originalSubdomain=sg\n[40]: https://www.facebook.com/TRGInternational/?locale=vi_VN\n[41]: https://www.youtube.com/@trginternational3812\n[42]: /terms-and-conditions/\n[43]: /privacy-policy/"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://trginternational.com/about-us/csr/blood-donations/",
            "text": "[[TRG International Logo]][1]\n[[TRG International Logo]][2]\n\nSolutions\n\n][3]\n[Resources][4]\n[Stories][5]\n[Events][6]\n[About us][7]\n[Careers][8]\n[Watch Demo][9][Get in Touch][10]\nEnglish\n\n# Blood Donations\n\nGive a pint and help save a life! TRG arranges four blood donations a year as part of our ongoing\ncommunity support initiatives. These quarterly blood drives are organized independently by our team,\ndemonstrating our commitment to public health and wellbeing.\n\n[Blood Donations hero image]\n[Hero section featured image]\n\n#### Save a Life!\n\nIn Vietnam, facts and accurate information about blood donation are rather limited. This has\nprevented many potential blood donors volunteering for such a good cause.\n\nFortunately, the interest in blood donation has shown a steady increase over the years as more\norganisations and Chambers of Commerce help to educate people.\nIt results in not only a positive change of understanding of the topic, but also the effort made by\nmore and more people willing to make a difference to others via the blood supply.\n\n#### Consistency\n\nRick, the founder and CEO of TRG International, sets an excellent example. He\u2019s a regular blood\ndonor, and has been active in doing so for almost 30 years now.\n\n[decor]\n[circle chape][circle chape]\n01/\n\n#### Blood Donations at TRG\n\n[thumbnail]\n\nRick tries his best to motivate his staff at TRG International to get involved. As he says, \u201cblood\ndonation is such a simple thing with a huge impact that most people can do\u201d.\n\nWith his commitment and enthusiasm, more and more staff at TRG have slowly stepped forward and taken\npart in the meaningful blood donation events.\n\nTRG arranges four blood donations a year as part of our ongoing community support initiatives. These\nquarterly blood drives are organized independently by our team, demonstrating our commitment to\npublic health and wellbeing.\n\n[circle chape][circle chape]\n02/\n\n#### Why donate blood?\n\n[thumbnail]\n\nAt TRG International, we believe that donating blood is the most precious gift anyone can give, as\nit\u2019s a small but real part of you, freely donated to help save others lives.\n\n5 simple reasons for blood donation:\n* The Joy of Saving Human\n* Lives Free Health Check-up\n* Reduces Risk of Heart Disease\n* Burns Calories\n* Reduces the Risk of Cancer\n\nbuild at: 2026-06-28T07:25:16.970Z\n[logo]\n\nWe've thrived since 1994 resulting in lots of experience to share, we are beyond a companion, to\nmore than 1,000 clients in 80+ countries.\n\nFollow us on Social Media\n[[linkedn]][11][[facebook]][12][[youtube]][13]\n[Solutions][14]\n[TRG Solutions][15][Business Challenges][16][Industries][17]\n[Resources][18]\n[Podcasts][19][Blog][20][FAQ][21][Research Portal][22][TRG End-User Training][23]\n[Stories][24]\n[Case Studies][25][CEO Letters][26]\n[About us][27]\n[Our People][28][Awards][29][TRG Cares][30][Testimonials][31]\n[Events][32]\n[Become our Speaker][33][Events Gallery][34][Hire our venue][35]\n[Careers][36]\n[Internships][37][Internships Partners][38]\nFollow us on Social Media\n[[linkedn]][39][[facebook]][40][[Youtube Play Button]][41]\n\u00a9 2026 TRG International[Terms and Conditions][42][Privacy Policy][43]Cookie Preferences\n\u00a9 2026 TRG International\n\n[1]: /\n[2]: /\n[3]: /solutions/\n[4]: /resources/\n[5]: /stories/\n[6]: /events/\n[7]: /about-us/\n[8]: /careers/\n[9]: /watch-demo/\n[10]: /contacts-and-locations/\n[11]: https://www.linkedin.com/company/trg-international/?originalSubdomain=sg\n[12]: https://www.facebook.com/TRGInternational/?locale=vi_VN\n[13]: https://www.youtube.com/@trginternational_official\n[14]: /solutions/\n[15]: /solutions/\n[16]: /business-challenges/\n[17]: /industries/\n[18]: /resources/\n[19]: /podcasts/\n[20]: /blog/\n[21]: /faq/\n[22]: /research/\n[23]: /trg-end-user-training/\n[24]: /stories/\n[25]: /stories/case-studies/\n[26]: /stories/business-as-unusual/\n[27]: /about-us/\n[28]: /about-us/our-people/\n[29]: /about-us/our-awards/\n[30]: /about-us/csr/\n[31]: /about-us/client-testimonials/\n[32]: /events/\n[33]: /events/become-our-speaker/\n[34]: /events/events-gallery/\n[35]: https://pjscoffeevietnam.com/catering\n[36]: /careers/\n[37]: /careers/internships/\n[38]: /careers/internship-partners/\n[39]: https://www.linkedin.com/company/trg-international/?originalSubdomain=sg\n[40]: https://www.facebook.com/TRGInternational/?locale=vi_VN\n[41]: https://www.youtube.com/@trginternational3812\n[42]: /terms-and-conditions/\n[43]: /privacy-policy/"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://trginternational.com/about-us/csr/charity/",
            "text": "[[TRG International Logo]][1]\n[[TRG International Logo]][2]\n\nSolutions\n\n][3]\n[Resources][4]\n[Stories][5]\n[Events][6]\n[About us][7]\n[Careers][8]\n[Watch Demo][9][Get in Touch][10]\nEnglish\n\n# Charity\n\n\u201cNo one has ever become poor by giving.\u201d \u2013 Anne Frank TRG International is a company who takes\ncharity close to its heart. TRG\u2019s mindset is, \u201cwe help where we can\u201d.\n\n[Charity hero image]\n[Hero section featured image]\n\n\u201cThrough all our charity activities, we aim to share our luck and good fortune to those less\nfortunate and give them hope.\u201d\n\n\u2013 Rick Yvanovich, Founder & CEO\n\nEvery year, TRG International reserves funds for charity programs to help vulnerable communities\nacross Vietnam.\n\nOur commitment to social responsibility has evolved over the years \u2013 from annual orphanage visits\nand fun runs to launching new initiatives to integrate sustainability into our charitable\nactivities.\n\nThrough these initiatives, we\u2019ve been able to make meaningful impacts in communities that need\nsupport the most.\n\n[decor]\n[circle chape][circle chape]\n01/\n\n#### Charity Activities\n\n[Charity Trips]\n\nAt TRG, we believe in the power of giving back. Our aim is to respond timely to urgent appeals and\npartner with established charitable organizations, who have established presence of communities\nneeding assistance, to maximize our impact.\n\nOur company-wide donation matching program continues to be the cornerstone of our charitable\ninitiatives. Through this program, TRG matches every donation made by employees, effectively\ndoubling the impact.\n\nA recent example of our collective action was our response to Typhoon Yagi \u2013 a modest donation of 60\nmillion VND was raised for relief efforts. These funds were donated to the Ho Chi Minh City Vietnam\nFatherland Front Committee to support recovery and rebuilding efforts in the hardest-hit areas of\nnorthern Vietnam.\n\nThis collaborative approach creates a meaningful difference in the lives of those facing challenging\ncircumstances.\n\n[circle chape][circle chape]\n02/\n\n#### Joi Foundation\n\n[Joi Foundation Activity 2025]\n\nThe Joi Foundation represents one of our most consistent charitable partnerships. Founded during the\nCOVID-19 pandemic lockdown in Saigon, this initiative began as a way to provide food for homeless\npeople when resources were scarce.\n\nTRG regularly supports this program by assembling a dedicated team of enthusiastic volunteers, who\nare then accompanied by the foundation\u2019s leaders to prepare 150 portions of banh mi. Once prepared,\nthese sandwiches are delivered to homeless individuals throughout Ho Chi Minh City, providing not\nonly nourishment but also a sense of community and support to those in need.\n\n[circle chape][circle chape]\n03/\n\n#### Fun Runs\n\n[Terry Fox Run]\n\nTRG actively participates in available charity runs throughout the year, which serve dual purposes:\nraising funds for worthy causes while providing excellent team-building opportunities for TRGers.\n\nThe BritCham Fun Run (formerly BBGV Fun Run) has become a tradition that our team eagerly\nanticipates. The event often attracts over 10,000 participants annually and raises billions of VND\nfor charities across Vietnam. Our PJ\u2019s Coffee booth was also present, offering refreshing beverages\nto participants throughout the day.\n\nChildren\u2019s Cancer Run is another event that we are proud to participate in. Our TRGers took steps to\nspread hope and stand with young cancer patients on their journey.\n\nThese events not only support important causes but also provide our team with opportunities to\nconnect outside the office while contributing to the community.\n\nTRG remains committed to participating in these meaningful community runs whenever they are\norganized, as they align perfectly with our values of teamwork, community engagement, and social\nresponsibility.\n\nbuild at: 2026-06-28T07:01:53.821Z\n[logo]\n\nWe've thrived since 1994 resulting in lots of experience to share, we are beyond a companion, to\nmore than 1,000 clients in 80+ countries.\n\nFollow us on Social Media\n[[linkedn]][11][[facebook]][12][[youtube]][13]\n[Solutions][14]\n[TRG Solutions][15][Business Challenges][16][Industries][17]\n[Resources][18]\n[Podcasts][19][Blog][20][FAQ][21][Research Portal][22][TRG End-User Training][23]\n[Stories][24]\n[Case Studies][25][CEO Letters][26]\n[About us][27]\n[Our People][28][Awards][29][TRG Cares][30][Testimonials][31]\n[Events][32]\n[Become our Speaker][33][Events Gallery][34][Hire our venue][35]\n[Careers][36]\n[Internships][37][Internships Partners][38]\nFollow us on Social Media\n[[linkedn]][39][[facebook]][40][[Youtube Play Button]][41]\n\u00a9 2026 TRG International[Terms and Conditions][42][Privacy Policy][43]Cookie Preferences\n\u00a9 2026 TRG International\n\n[1]: /\n[2]: /\n[3]: /solutions/\n[4]: /resources/\n[5]: /stories/\n[6]: /events/\n[7]: /about-us/\n[8]: /careers/\n[9]: /watch-demo/\n[10]: /contacts-and-locations/\n[11]: https://www.linkedin.com/company/trg-international/?originalSubdomain=sg\n[12]: https://www.facebook.com/TRGInternational/?locale=vi_VN\n[13]: https://www.youtube.com/@trginternational_official\n[14]: /solutions/\n[15]: /solutions/\n[16]: /business-challenges/\n[17]: /industries/\n[18]: /resources/\n[19]: /podcasts/\n[20]: /blog/\n[21]: /faq/\n[22]: /research/\n[23]: /trg-end-user-training/\n[24]: /stories/\n[25]: /stories/case-studies/\n[26]: /stories/business-as-unusual/\n[27]: /about-us/\n[28]: /about-us/our-people/\n[29]: /about-us/our-awards/\n[30]: /about-us/csr/\n[31]: /about-us/client-testimonials/\n[32]: /events/\n[33]: /events/become-our-speaker/\n[34]: /events/events-gallery/\n[35]: https://pjscoffeevietnam.com/catering\n[36]: /careers/\n[37]: /careers/internships/\n[38]: /careers/internship-partners/\n[39]: https://www.linkedin.com/company/trg-international/?originalSubdomain=sg\n[40]: https://www.facebook.com/TRGInternational/?locale=vi_VN\n[41]: https://www.youtube.com/@trginternational3812\n[42]: /terms-and-conditions/\n[43]: /privacy-policy/"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://trginternational.com/solutions/great-people-inside/gr8-wellbeing/",
            "text": "[[TRG International Logo]][1]\n[[TRG International Logo]][2]\n\nSolutions\n\n][3]\n[Resources][4]\n[Stories][5]\n[Events][6]\n[About us][7]\n[Careers][8]\n[Watch Demo][9][Get in Touch][10]\nEnglish\n[bg-decor]\nGreat People Inside Assessments\n\n# GR8 Wellbeing\n\nGR8 Wellbeing - the ultimate assessment tool you would ever need for employee engagement,\norganisational health & retention.\n[icon]\n\nSelf-assessment: A person will rate himself/herself.\n\n[icon]\n\nAverage 15 minutes to complete the assessment\n\n[hero image]\n[Hero section featured image]\n\n#### Assessment Dimensions\n\nSolutions for:\n\n#### Assessment Dimensions\n\nGR8 Wellbeing looks at bringing you insightful and relevant information about wellbeing at your\ncurrent workplace. The main focus is to identify specific behavioural tendencies such as optimistic\nthinking, stress managing, perseverance, attention seeking, self awareness and so on. These factors\nare amongst those proven to best predict a person\u2019s tendency to achieve wellness and resilience.\nFrom this, you will be able to identify what solutions and support you can make available for your\nemployees to raise their wellbeing levels. As well as, for recruiting employees and employee\nretention.\n\nIn addition, TRG provides an extensive assessment library with hundreds of dimensions that can be\nleveraged in creating a custom skills-based assessment that supports your organisation\u2019s specific\ncompetencies and unique vision. Whatever the challenge you are facing, we aim to provide a great\nexperience to help you in the best way we can.\n\nSolutions for:\nTraining & Development\n][11][\nRecruitment\n][12][\nRetention & Engagement\n][13]\n\n#### Behaviours\n\nPositive Thinking | Stress and Resilience | Energy and Vitality | Curiosity and Self-awareness |\nNetworking and Connection\n\n[icon]\n[icon]\n[icon]\n\n### RESOURCES\n\nLatest resources for **GR8 Wellbeing**\n\n[View All Resources[icon]][14]\nThu, Jan 11, 2024\nDownload[icon]\n\n#### Compare On-premises vs. Multi-tenant Cloud for CFO\n\nDiscover how cloud-based financial applications compare to on-premises solutions\n][15][\nThu, Jul 11, 2024\nDownload[icon]\n\n#### Compare On-premises vs. Multi-tenant Cloud for CFO\n\nDiscover how cloud-based financial applications compare to on-premises solutions\n][16][\nTue, Jun 11, 2024\nDownload[icon]\n\n#### Compare On-premises vs. Multi-tenant Cloud for CFO\n\nDiscover how cloud-based financial applications compare to on-premises solutions\n][17]\n\n#### Try The Assessment\n\nThe idea that a person should enjoy a healthy work-life balance is not a new concept. Today, it is a\nvery common practice that companies are now striving to promote their employees\u2019 wellbeing, which\ndirectly and positively influences their work performance and consequently productivity and business\nperformance. Research has shown that employees perform better when they feel appreciated and\nsupported by the company. This in turn improves their wellbeing and helps with employee retention,\nas they feel more committed to the company\u2019s goals and objectives.\n\nDue to our current situation, this is more important than ever as many of us are required to work\nfrom home. This brings a new set of challenges, for both the individual and the company to help\ntheir employees to try to stay motivated and focused.\n\nFor the individual, it is about realising the issue and asking for the appropriate solutions.\n\nFor managers, it is vital that you fully understand what mental health is so that they can raise\nawareness and create an environment where employees feel comfortable speaking about it. It is\nessential to timely determine, predict or gauge their employee\u2019s emotional wellbeing and ability to\nmaintain balance, manage stress and relationship. As well as providing the resources and support to\ntheir employees when necessary. There are many latent factors undermining a person\u2019s mental\nwellbeing and often they are not tangible until something bad happens.\n\nBased on the newest theories in the field of industrial and organisational psychology, GR8 Wellbeing\nassessment can be used to identify your employees\u2019 overall state of mind and emotion, thereby\nincreasing job satisfaction and employee retention. As well as keeping workplace depression at bay.\nThis will provide an insight into the steps to take in order to arrange for the best solutions for\nyour employees to create an overall satisfactory state around the workplace.\n\n#### GR8 Wellbeing is recommended for:\n* Generating job satisfaction\n* Improving motivation and engagement\n* Organisational health and happiness\n* Boosting employee retention\n* Creating and promoting a powerful employer brand\n* Driving high-performance\n\n## GR8 Customised\n\n### Provides a unique assessment for your company; You can create one through a simple\n### choose-and-pick exercise in our library of 100+ dimensions. The GR8PI platform is so extensive\n### that you will be impressed by the number of aspects we can measure.\n\n### INDUSTRIES WE SERVE\n\nTRG has implemented technology solutions for industries like financial services, not-for-profit, and\nenergy, oil, and gas, our custom configuration makes it well-suited for many other vertical markets\nas well. This adaptability is one of the key reasons why various industries choose us for their\nsolution requirements.\n\n[icon][image]\n[Financial Services][18][Manufacturing][19][Retail][20][Insurance][21][Energy][22][Real\nEstate][23][Healthcare][24][Education][25]\n\n### OUR CLIENT\n\nSome of our satisfied customers we helped with their Talent Management assessments needs.\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n* [logo]\n\nbuild at: 2026-06-28T02:07:16.619Z\n[logo]\n\nWe've thrived since 1994 resulting in lots of experience to share, we are beyond a companion, to\nmore than 1,000 clients in 80+ countries.\n\nFollow us on Social Media\n[[linkedn]][26][[facebook]][27][[youtube]][28]\n[Solutions][29]\n[TRG Solutions][30][Business Challenges][31][Industries][32]\n[Resources][33]\n[Podcasts][34][Blog][35][FAQ][36][Research Portal][37][TRG End-User Training][38]\n[Stories][39]\n[Case Studies][40][CEO Letters][41]\n[About us][42]\n[Our People][43][Awards][44][TRG Cares][45][Testimonials][46]\n[Events][47]\n[Become our Speaker][48][Events Gallery][49][Hire our venue][50]\n[Careers][51]\n[Internships][52][Internships Partners][53]\nFollow us on Social Media\n[[linkedn]][54][[facebook]][55][[Youtube Play Button]][56]\n\u00a9 2026 TRG International[Terms and Conditions][57][Privacy Policy][58]Cookie Preferences\n\u00a9 2026 TRG International\n\n[1]: /\n[2]: /\n[3]: /solutions/\n[4]: /resources/\n[5]: /stories/\n[6]: /events/\n[7]: /about-us/\n[8]: /careers/\n[9]: /watch-demo/\n[10]: /contacts-and-locations/\n[11]: /business-challenges/talent-management/training-development/\n[12]: /business-challenges/talent-management/recruitment/\n[13]: /business-challenges/talent-management/retention-engagement/\n[14]: /\n[15]: /\n[16]: /\n[17]: /\n[18]: /industries/financial-services/\n[19]: /industries/manufacturing/\n[20]: /business-challenges/retail-management/\n[21]: /industries/insurance/\n[22]: /industries/energy/\n[23]: /industries/real-estate/\n[24]: /industries/healthcare/\n[25]: /solutions/education/\n[26]: https://www.linkedin.com/company/trg-international/?originalSubdomain=sg\n[27]: https://www.facebook.com/TRGInternational/?locale=vi_VN\n[28]: https://www.youtube.com/@trginternational_official\n[29]: /solutions/\n[30]: /solutions/\n[31]: /business-challenges/\n[32]: /industries/\n[33]: /resources/\n[34]: /podcasts/\n[35]: /blog/\n[36]: /faq/\n[37]: /research/\n[38]: /trg-end-user-training/\n[39]: /stories/\n[40]: /stories/case-studies/\n[41]: /stories/business-as-unusual/\n[42]: /about-us/\n[43]: /about-us/our-people/\n[44]: /about-us/our-awards/\n[45]: /about-us/csr/\n[46]: /about-us/client-testimonials/\n[47]: /events/\n[48]: /events/become-our-speaker/\n[49]: /events/events-gallery/\n[50]: https://pjscoffeevietnam.com/catering\n[51]: /careers/\n[52]: /careers/internships/\n[53]: /careers/internship-partners/\n[54]: https://www.linkedin.com/company/trg-international/?originalSubdomain=sg\n[55]: https://www.facebook.com/TRGInternational/?locale=vi_VN\n[56]: https://www.youtube.com/@trginternational3812\n[57]: /terms-and-conditions/\n[58]: /privacy-policy/"
