            "text": "[[ZipDo.co Logo]][1]\n* Services\n[All Services][2][Custom Market Research][3][Industry Reports][4][Software Advisory][5]\n* Market Data\n[All Market Data][6][All Categories][7][AI In Industry(740)][8][Technology Digital\nMedia(605)][9][Safety Accidents(479)][10][Entertainment Events(476)][11][Medical Conditions\nDisorders(476)][12][Mental Health Psychology(402)][13][Social Issues Societal\nTrends(358)][14][Manufacturing Engineering(353)][15][Marketing Advertising(347)][16][Education\nLearning(345)][17]\n* [Software Advice][18]\n[All Software Advice][19][Aerospace Aviation Space(204)][20][Aerospace\nDefense(43)][21][Agriculture Farming(288)][22][AI In Industry(573)][23][Art Design(2119)][24][Arts\nCreative Expression(518)][25][Automotive Services(822)][26][Beverages Alcohol(29)][27]\n* [Editorial Process][28]\n* Company\n[About Us][29][Blog][30][Careers][31][As Seen In][32][Partners][33]\n* [Contact Us][34]\n[[ZipDo Mobile Logo]][35]\u2630\n* [Home][36]\n* Services\n* [All Services][37]\n* [Custom Market Research][38]\n* [Industry Reports][39]\n* [Software Advisory][40]\n* Market Data\n* [All Market Data][41]\n* [All Categories][42]\n* [AI In Industry(740)][43]\n* [Technology Digital Media(605)][44]\n* [Safety Accidents(479)][45]\n* [Entertainment Events(476)][46]\n* [Medical Conditions Disorders(476)][47]\n* [Mental Health Psychology(402)][48]\n* [Social Issues Societal Trends(358)][49]\n* [Manufacturing Engineering(353)][50]\n* [Marketing Advertising(347)][51]\n* [Education Learning(345)][52]\n* [Software Advice][53]\n* [Aerospace Aviation Space(204)][54]\n* [Aerospace Defense(43)][55]\n* [Agriculture Farming(288)][56]\n* [AI In Industry(573)][57]\n* [Art Design(2119)][58]\n* [Arts Creative Expression(518)][59]\n* [Automotive Services(822)][60]\n* [Beverages Alcohol(29)][61]\n* [Biotechnology Pharmaceuticals(192)][62]\n* [Business Finance(5273)][63]\n* [Editorial Process][64]\n* Company\n* [About Us][65]\n* [Careers][66]\n* [As Seen In][67]\n* [Partners][68]\n* [Contact Us][69]\n\n# Market Research You Can Trust \u2014 *AI-Verified*\n\nSince 2021 we've been helping teams worldwide make better decisions with data. Our analysts span\nthree continents; every number we publish is checked against primary sources before it goes live.\n\nOur Story\n\n## How ZipDo Grew Into an AI-Verified Research Platform\n\nZipDo launched in 2021 with one goal: put reliable market data in the hands of everyone who needs it\n\u2014 whether you're at a large enterprise or running a startup.\n\nWe began as a curated stats hub and soon hit a wall: too many numbers online lead back to other\nnumbers, with nobody validating the original study. So we built an AI verification layer that\nreproduces, cross-checks, and validates primary research before we publish.\n\nToday we support thousands of organizations with verified industry reports, bespoke research, and\non-demand analysis. Our work has been cited in 3,000+ articles and by 500+ outlets \u2014 from Microsoft\nand Adobe to Harvard Business Review and The Guardian.\n\n2021\nFounded\n3,000+\nArticles Citing ZipDo\n50+\nIndustry Sectors\n100+\nCountries Reached\n\nWhat Makes Us Different\n\n## We Verify, We Don't Just Aggregate\n\n### AI-Verified Research\n\nWe go beyond collecting stats: our AI reproduces results, cross-checks claims, and stress-tests\nnumbers against primary sources so only verified data gets published.\n\n### Named Analysts & Credentials\n\nReports are authored by real researchers with transparent academic and professional backgrounds. No\nfaceless bylines \u2014 you can see who stands behind each finding.\n\n### Full Source Traceability\n\nEach statistic points back to its primary source. We avoid secondary aggregators; if we can&apos;t\ntrace it to the original research, we don&apos;t run it.\n\n### Humans Have the Final Say\n\nAI does the verification legwork; editors make the call. No stat or product ranking goes live\nwithout explicit human sign-off.\n\nOur Process\n\n## From Source to Publish: Our Five-Step Pipeline\n\nAll content runs through the same workflow. Editors own the decisions; AI scales the verification.\n\n#### Research Collection\n\nWe pull from primary sources, led by our research team\n\n#### Editorial Curation\n\nEditors choose what enters the pipeline\n\n#### AI Verification\n\nAutomated reproduction, cross-reference, and checks\n\n#### Human Review\n\nAn editor validates AI output and gives the go-ahead\n\n#### Human Writing\n\nAnalysts write; AI supports on SEO and formatting\n\n[See the full editorial process \u2192][70]\n\nOur Team\n\n## Who Works on the Data\n\nEach analyst has a profile with credentials, past work, and recent publications.\n\n[Adrian Szabo]\n[\u2192 Full Author Page][71]\n\n### Adrian Szabo\n\nData Analyst\n\nAdrian holds a Master's in Computer Science from Budapest University of Technology and a Bachelor's\nin Digital Media from E\u00f6tv\u00f6s Lor\u00e1nd University. He spent four years at a digital entertainment\nresearch firm in Berlin before freelancing as a gaming market analyst. At ZipDo, he specializes in\ngaming industry analytics, game engine technology, and interactive entertainment.\n\n[Amara Williams]\n[\u2192 Full Author Page][72]\n\n### Amara Williams\n\nResearch Analyst\n\nAmara holds a Master's in Law from Howard University School of Law and a Bachelor's in Business\nAdministration from Spelman College. She spent five years as a legal technology researcher at an\nindependent legal industry advisory firm in Washington, D.C.. She later worked as a freelance legal\noperations analyst. At ZipDo, she covers legal operations technology, contract intelligence\nplatforms, and legal spend management market trends.\n\n[Andr\u00e9 Laurent]\n[\u2192 Full Author Page][73]\n\n### Andr\u00e9 Laurent\n\nMarket Intelligence\n\nAndr\u00e9 holds a Master's in Building Engineering from \u00c9cole des Ponts ParisTech and a Bachelor's in\nComputer Science from T\u00e9l\u00e9com Paris. He spent five years as a smart buildings researcher at an\nindependent property technology advisory firm in Paris. He later worked as a freelance proptech\nanalyst. At ZipDo, he covers smart building technology, building management systems, and commercial\nreal estate IoT market trends.\n\n[Andrew Morrison]\n[\u2192 Full Author Page][74]\n\n### Andrew Morrison\n\nResearch Analyst\n\nAndrew holds a Master's in Finance from University of Edinburgh and a Bachelor's in Engineering from\nHeriot-Watt University. He spent six years as a clean energy finance researcher at an independent\ninfrastructure investment advisory firm in Edinburgh. He later worked as a freelance clean energy\nanalyst. At ZipDo, he covers renewable energy project finance, green infrastructure bonds, and clean\nenergy investment data.\n\n[Anja Petersen]\n[\u2192 Full Author Page][75]\n\n### Anja Petersen\n\nMarket Intelligence\n\nAnja holds a Master's in Organizational Psychology from University of Copenhagen and a Bachelor's in\nHealth Science from University of Southern Denmark. She spent four years as a workplace health\nresearcher at an independent corporate wellness advisory firm in Copenhagen. She later worked as a\nfreelance workplace wellness analyst. At ZipDo, she covers employee wellness platforms, corporate\nfitness technology, and workplace health market trends.\n\n[Annika Holm]\n[\u2192 Full Author Page][76]\n\n### Annika Holm\n\nData Analyst\n\nAnnika holds a Master's in Environmental Economics from the University of Gothenburg and a\nBachelor's in Natural Sciences from the University of Helsinki. She spent four years at a Nordic\nclimate finance advisory firm before freelancing as a climate technology analyst. At ZipDo, she\nfocuses on renewable energy markets, carbon credit trading, and climate technology investment.\n\n[Astrid Johansson]\n[\u2192 Full Author Page][77]\n\n### Astrid Johansson\n\nSenior Data Analyst\n\nAstrid holds a Master's in Information Security from KTH Royal Institute of Technology and a\nBachelor's in Computer Science from Link\u00f6ping University. She spent four years as a digital identity\nresearcher at an independent cybersecurity advisory firm in Stockholm. She later worked as a\nfreelance identity technology analyst. At ZipDo, she covers digital identity platforms,\nauthentication technology, and privacy management market trends.\n\n[Catherine Hale]\n[\u2192 Full Author Page][78]\n\n### Catherine Hale\n\nSenior Market Analyst\n\nCatherine holds a Master's in Sustainability Management from the University of Cambridge and a\nBachelor's in Environmental Studies from Middlebury College. She spent six years at an ESG advisory\nfirm in London producing corporate climate disclosure benchmarks. She later advised asset managers\non ESG reporting standards. At ZipDo, she focuses on sustainability, ESG reporting, and corporate\nresponsibility.\n\n[Chloe Duval]\n[\u2192 Full Author Page][79]\n\n### Chloe Duval\n\nMarket Intelligence\n\nChloe holds a Master's in Hospitality Management from \u00c9cole h\u00f4teli\u00e8re de Lausanne and a Bachelor's\nin Business Administration from HEC Paris. She spent four years as a luxury hospitality researcher\nat an independent hotel industry advisory firm in Paris. She later worked as a freelance hospitality\ntechnology analyst. At ZipDo, she covers luxury hospitality technology, hotel revenue management\nplatforms, and premium travel market trends.\n\n[Clara Weidemann]\n[\u2192 Full Author Page][80]\n\n### Clara Weidemann\n\nSenior Market Analyst\n\nClara holds a Master's in Information Systems from the University of M\u00fcnster and a Bachelor's in\nBusiness Informatics from KIT. She spent six years at an IT advisory firm in Frankfurt leading ERP\nand BI benchmark studies before freelancing as an enterprise software analyst. At ZipDo, she\nspecializes in ERP, business intelligence, and data warehousing markets.\n\n[\u2192 Full Author Page][81]\n\n### Daniel Foster\n\nIndustry Analyst\n\nDaniel holds a Master's in Financial Economics from the University of Exeter. He spent five years as\nan independent financial research analyst, contributing sector reports and regulatory impact\nassessments to boutique advisory firms in the UK. He later worked as a freelance data journalist\ncovering fintech and banking regulation. At ZipDo, he specializes in financial services, insurance,\nand regulatory compliance research.\n\n[\u2192 Full Author Page][82]\n\n### David Chen\n\nMarket Intelligence\n\nDavid holds a Master's in Public Health (Epidemiology) from the University of Toronto. He spent five\nyears as a research associate at a Canadian public health research institute, contributing to\nepidemiological studies published by provincial health authorities. He later worked as a freelance\nhealth data analyst for international health organizations. At ZipDo, he produces health sector\nmarket reports with emphasis on statistical rigor and transparent methodology.\n\n[Elise Bergstr\u00f6m]\n[\u2192 Full Author Page][83]\n\n### Elise Bergstr\u00f6m\n\nData Analyst\n\nElise holds a Master's in Education and Technology from the University of Helsinki and a Bachelor's\nin Information Science from Lund University. She spent four years at a Nordic digital learning\nresearch center contributing to cross-national LMS adoption studies. She later freelanced as an\nedtech analyst. At ZipDo, she focuses on edtech platforms, learning management systems, and academic\npublishing.\n\n[Emma Sutcliffe]\n[\u2192 Full Author Page][84]\n\n### Emma Sutcliffe\n\nSenior Market Analyst\n\nEmma holds a Master's in Business Strategy from University of Oxford Sa\u00efd Business School and a\nBachelor's in Economics from University of Bristol. She spent five years as a subscription economy\nresearcher at an independent digital commerce advisory firm in London. She later worked as a\nfreelance subscription commerce analyst. At ZipDo, she covers subscription commerce platforms,\nmembership economy data, and recurring revenue business model analytics.\n\n[Erik Hansen]\n[\u2192 Full Author Page][85]\n\n### Erik Hansen\n\nData Analyst\n\nErik holds a Master's in Operations Management from Copenhagen Business School and a Bachelor's in\nComputer Science from Technical University of Denmark. He spent four years as a foodservice\ntechnology researcher at an independent restaurant industry advisory firm in Copenhagen. He later\nworked as a freelance foodservice technology analyst. At ZipDo, he covers food delivery logistics,\nda"
