nGovernments\nMemberships\n[MS-ISAC\u00ae][31]Cybersecurity resource for SLTT Governments\n[EI-ISAC\u00ae][32]Critical cybersecurity resource for the nation's SLTT election offices\nState Resources\n[Whole-of-State Security][33]Enabling collaboration and shared responsibility across all levels of\ngovernment\nServices for Members\n[Albert Network Monitoring\u00ae][34]Cost-effective Intrusion Detection System\n[CIS Managed Detection and Response\u2122 (CIS MDR)][35]Device-level protection and response\n[Malicious Code Analysis Platform (MCAP)][36]Web-based sandbox for analyzing suspicious files and\nURLs\n[CIS CyberMarket\u00ae][37]Savings on training and software\n[Malicious Domain Blocking and Reporting Plus][38]Prevent connection to harmful web domains\n[View All CIS Services][39]\n[View All Products & Services][40]\n[Insights][41]\nBack\nInsights\nInsightsExplore trending articles, expert perspectives, real-world applications, and more from the\nbest minds in cybersecurity and IT.\n[Advisories][42]\n[Blog][43]\n[Case Studies][44]\n[Spotlights][45]\n[Newsletters][46]\n[Podcasts][47]\n[Webinars][48]\n[White papers][49]\n[View All Insights][50]\n[Join CIS][51]\nBack\nJoin CIS\nGet InvolvedJoin us on our mission to secure online experiences for all. Become a CIS member,\npartner, or volunteer\u2014and explore our career opportunities.\n[CIS SecureSuite\u00ae Membership][52]\n[Multi-State ISAC (MS-ISAC\u00ae)][53]\n[CIS CyberMarket\u00ae Vendors][54]\n[CIS Communities][55]\n[Our Partners][56]\n[Careers][57]\n[Home][58][About us][59][Media][60][CIS Press Releases][61]CIS Hardened Image Usage on GCP\nQuadruples in 2019\n\n# CIS Hardened Image Usage on GCP Quadruples in 2019\n\n**CIS Hardened Images See 82% increase from 2018 to 2019**\n\nEAST GREENBUSH, N.Y., Mar. 25, 2020 \u2013 As more businesses are moving to the cloud as a way to reduce\ncosts, offer more flexibility and scalability to their operations, and improve data security, CIS\nHardened Images make the transition easier. In 2019, CIS Hardened Images^{\u00ae }consumers clocked more\nthan seven million computed usage hours on Google Cloud Platform (GCP), up from a little over one\nmillion in 2018; that\u2019s an increase of 82 percent.\n\nGCP announced general availability of its Shielded VMs (virtual machines) last year during Google\nCloud Next \u201919 in San Francisco. Using Shielded VMs helps you protect your system from attack\nvectors and ensures your organization is only using supported images. There are currently more than\n20 CIS Hardened Images available on Shielded VMs for operating systems (OS) like CentOS Linux,\nUbuntu Linux, and Microsoft Windows.\n\nAdditionally, CIS and GCP recently released CIS PostgreSQL 11 on CentOS Linux 7 Benchmark \u2013 Level 1.\nThe image of PostgreSQL 11 on CentOS Linux 7 is built on Google\u2019s Shielded VM and preconfigured by\nCIS to the recommendations in the associated CIS Benchmarks.\n\n\u201cWe are extremely proud to offer our Hardened Images on platforms such as GCP and the other major\ncloud service providers,\u201d said Curtis Dukes, CIS Executive Vice President of Security Best Practices\n& Automation Group. \u201cThe continued growth makes it clear that users see a value in a consensus\nbased, secure configuration.\u201d\n\nCIS Hardened Images available on GCP are currently being used in 68 different countries and 38 U.S.\nstates, providing users with a secure, on-demand, and scalable computing environment.\n\n\u201cWe expect usage of our hardened images to continue to rise in 2020 as more users see the security\nbenefit of shielded VMs,\u201d said Dukes.\n\nThe most popular Hardened Images available on GCP in 2019 were:\n* CIS CentOS Linux 7 Benchmark \u2013 Level 1\n* CIS Ubuntu Linux 16.04 Benchmark \u2013 Level 1\n* CIS Microsoft Windows Server 2016 Benchmark- Level 1\n* CIS CentOS Linux 7 Benchmark \u2013 Level 1 on g1-small\n* CIS Red Hat Enterprise Linux 7 Benchmark \u2013 Level 1\n* CIS Ubuntu Linux 18.04 Benchmark \u2013 Level 1\n* CIS Microsoft Windows Server 2016 \u2013 Level 2\n* CIS Microsoft Windows Server 2008 R2 \u2013 Level 1\n\nCIS Hardened Images are virtual machine images pre-configured to applicable CIS Benchmark\nrecommendations. CIS Benchmarks and their corresponding Hardened Images are used by thousands of\norganizations for compliance support with DoD Cloud Computing SRG, FedRAMP, PCI DSS, NIST, and HIPAA\nstandards. They help mitigate common threats such as malware, insufficient authorization, and remote\nintrusion, and are updated every month to address patching and vulnerabilities.\n\nFor a complete list of CIS Hardened Images available on GCP\nvisit: [https://www.cisecurity.org/cis-hardened-image-list/][62]\n\nAbout CIS:\n\nThe Center for Internet Security, Inc. (CIS^{\u00ae}) makes the connected world a safer place for people,\nbusinesses, and governments. We are a community-driven nonprofit, responsible for the CIS\nControls^{\u00ae} and CIS Benchmarks^{\u2122}, globally recognized best practices for securing IT systems and\ndata. We lead a global community of IT professionals to continuously refine these standards to\nproactively safeguard against emerging threats. Our CIS Hardened Images^{\u00ae} provide secure,\non-demand, scalable computing environments in the cloud. CIS is home to the Multi-State Information\nSharing and Analysis Center^{\u00ae} (MS-ISAC^{\u00ae}), the trusted resource for cyber threat prevention,\nprotection, response, and recovery for U.S. State, Local, Tribal, and Territorial (SLTT) government\nentities, and the Elections Infrastructure Information Sharing and Analysis Center^{\u00ae}\n(EI-ISAC^{\u00ae}), which supports the cybersecurity needs of U.S. elections offices. To learn more,\nvisit CISecurity.org or follow us on Twitter: @CISecurity.\n\nContact: Autum Pylant, CIS Senior Communications Specialist\n\n[[email protected]][63]\n\n[About][64]\n[Leadership][65]\n[Board][66]\n[Communities][67]\n[Careers][68]\n[Media][69]\n[Testimonials][70]\n[Events][71]\n[US Cyber Challenge][72]\n[Support][73]\n[Contact][74]\n[Products And Tools][75]\n[CIS Critical Security Controls^{\u00ae}][76]\n[CIS Benchmarks^{\u00ae}][77]\n[CIS Hardened Images^{\u00ae}][78]\n[CIS SecureSuite^{\u00ae}][79]\n[CIS SecureSuite^{\u00ae} Platform][80]\n[CIS-CAT^{\u00ae} Lite][81]\n[CIS-CAT^{\u00ae} Pro Assessor][82]\n[CIS RAM][83]\n[CIS-hosted CSAT][84]\n[CIS WorkBench][85]\n[ThreatWA\u2122][86]\n[For SLTT Governments][87]\n[MS-ISAC^{\u00ae}][88]\n[EI-ISAC^{\u00ae}][89]\n[CIS Services^{\u00ae}][90]\n[Albert Network Monitoring][91]\n[Managed Security Services][92]\n[Managed Detection and Response][93]\n[Malicious Domain Blocking and Reporting Plus][94]\n[CIS CyberMarket^{\u00ae}][95]\n[Explore][96]\n[Blog][97]\n[Whitepapers][98]\n[Newsletters][99]\n[Webinars][100]\n[Case Studies][101]\n[Spotlights][102]\n[Videos][103]\n\nCopyright^{\u00a9} 2026 Center for Internet Security^{\u00ae}\n\n[Privacy Notice][104]\n[Twitter][105][Facebook][106][YouTube][107][LinkedIn][108]\n\n[1]: /\n[2]: https://portal.cisecurity.org/\n[3]: /cis-hardened-image-list\n[4]: /support\n[5]: https://workbench.cisecurity.org/\n[6]: /#/\n[7]: /about-us\n[8]: /about-us/cis-leadership-principles\n[9]: /about-us/leadership\n[10]: /testimonials\n[11]: /about-us/media\n[12]: /event-calendar\n[13]: https://learn.cisecurity.org/contact-us\n[14]: /\n[15]: /controls\n[16]: /communities/controls\n[17]: https://learn.cisecurity.org/cis-ram-v2-2\n[18]: /cis-securesuite/benefits/cis-securesuite-platform\n[19]: /threatwa\n[20]: /cis-securesuite/benefits/cis-securesuite-platform\n[21]: /cis-benchmarks\n[22]: /communities/benchmarks\n[23]: /cybersecurity-tools/cis-cat-pro\n[24]: /cis-hardened-images\n[25]: /industry\n[26]: /topics\n[27]: /secure-cyber-city-initiative\n[28]: /cis-securesuite\n[29]: /cis-securesuite\n[30]: https://enroll.cisecurity.org/memberships/#/\n[31]: /ms-isac\n[32]: /ei-isac\n[33]: /whole-of-state-security\n[34]: /services/albert-network-monitoring\n[35]: /services/managed-detection-and-response\n[36]: /services/malicious-code-analysis-platform\n[37]: /services/cis-cybermarket\n[38]: /services/mdbrplus\n[39]: /services\n[40]: /cybersecurity-tools\n[41]: /insights\n[42]: /advisory\n[43]: /insights/blog\n[44]: /insights/case-study\n[45]: /insights/spotlight\n[46]: /insights/newsletter\n[47]: /insights/podcast\n[48]: /insights/webinar\n[49]: /insights/white-papers\n[50]: /insights/all\n[51]: /\n[52]: /cis-securesuite\n[53]: /ms-isac\n[54]: /services/cis-cybermarket/vendor-information\n[55]: /communities\n[56]: /about-us/partners\n[57]: https://cisecurity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/CIS_External_Career_Site\n[58]: /\n[59]: /about-us\n[60]: /about-us/media\n[61]: /about-us/media/press-release\n[62]: /cis-hardened-image-list\n[63]: /cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#d1bcb4b5b8b091b2b8a2b4b2a4a3b8a5a8ffbea3b6\n[64]: /about-us\n[65]: /about-us/leadership\n[66]: /about-us/board\n[67]: /communities\n[68]: https://cisecurity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/CIS_External_Career_Site\n[69]: /about-us/media\n[70]: /testimonials\n[71]: /event-calendar\n[72]: http://www.uscyberchallenge.org/\n[73]: /support\n[74]: https://learn.cisecurity.org/contact-us\n[75]: /cybersecurity-tools\n[76]: /controls\n[77]: /cis-benchmarks\n[78]: /cis-hardened-images\n[79]: /cis-securesuite\n[80]: /cis-securesuite/benefits/cis-securesuite-platform\n[81]: https://learn.cisecurity.org/cis-cat-lite\n[82]: /cybersecurity-tools/cis-cat-pro\n[83]: https://learn.cisecurity.org/cis-ram-v2-2\n[84]: /cis-securesuite/benefits/cis-securesuite-platform\n[85]: https://workbench.cisecurity.org/\n[86]: /threatwa\n[87]: /isac\n[88]: /ms-isac\n[89]: /ei-isac\n[90]: /services\n[91]: /services/albert-network-monitoring\n[92]: /services/managed-security-services-mss\n[93]: /services/managed-detection-and-response\n[94]: /services/mdbrplus\n[95]: /services/cis-cybermarket\n[96]: /insights\n[97]: /insights/blog\n[98]: /insights/white-papers\n[99]: /insights/newsletter\n[100]: /insights/webinar\n[101]: /insights/case-study\n[102]: /insights/spotlight\n[103]: https://www.youtube.com/user/TheCISecurity\n[104]: /privacy-notice\n[105]: https://twitter.com/CISecurity/\n[106]: https://www.facebook.com/CenterforIntSec/\n[107]: https://www.youtube.com/user/TheCISecurity/\n[108]: https://www.linkedin.com/company/the-center-for-internet-security/"
