          {
            "url": "https://www.cisecurity.org/about-us/media/press-release/cis-releases-cis-cat-pro-assessor-v4",
            "text": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app.\n[[CIS - Center for Internet Security\u00ae]][1]\n[CIS Portal Login][2][CIS Hardened Images^{\u00ae}][3][Support][4][CIS WorkBench Sign In][5]\nAlert Level: guarded\n[Company][6]\nBack\nCompany\nWho We AreCIS is an independent, nonprofit organization with a mission to create confidence in the\nconnected world.\n[About Us][7]\n[Leadership Principles][8]\n[Leadership Team][9]\n[Testimonials][10]\n[Media][11]\n[Events][12]\n[Contact Us][13]\n[Solutions][14]\nBack\nSolutions\n[Icon]Secure Your Organization\n[CIS Critical Security Controls\u00ae][15]Prioritized & simplified best practices\n[CIS Controls Community][16]Help develop and maintain the Controls\n[CIS RAM][17]Information security risk assessment method\n[CIS CSAT][18]Assess & measure Controls implementation\n[ThreatWA\u2122][19]Insights into emerging cyber & physical threats\n[CIS SecureSuite\u00ae Platform][20]Assess and measure CIS Controls implementation and conformance to the\nCIS Benchmarks\n[Icon]Secure Specific Platforms\n[CIS Benchmarks\u2122][21]100+ vendor-neutral configuration guides\n[CIS Benchmarks Community][22]Develop & update secure configuration guides\n[CIS-CAT\u00aePro Assessor][23]Assess system conformance to CIS Benchmarks\n[CIS Hardened Images\u00ae][24]Virtual images hardened to CIS Benchmarks on cloud service provider\nmarketplaces\n[Situation]Track Specific Threats\n[Industries][25]Your industry's specific threats & needs\n[Topics][26]Dive deeper into specific cybersecurity topics\n[Secure Cyber City\u2122][27]Expertise for cybersecurity resilience and community empowerment\n[SecureSuite\u00ae]\n[CIS SecureSuite\u00ae (Multi-Year Discounts Available)][28]Start secure and stay secure with integrated\ncybersecurity tools and resources designed to help you implement CIS Benchmarks and CIS Controls\n[Learn More][29][Apply Now][30]\n[U.S. State, Local, Tribal & Territorial Governments]U.S. State, Local, Tribal & Territorial\nGovernments\nMemberships\n[MS-ISAC\u00ae][31]Cybersecurity resource for SLTT Governments\n[EI-ISAC\u00ae][32]Critical cybersecurity resource for the nation's SLTT election offices\nState Resources\n[Whole-of-State Security][33]Enabling collaboration and shared responsibility across all levels of\ngovernment\nServices for Members\n[Albert Network Monitoring\u00ae][34]Cost-effective Intrusion Detection System\n[CIS Managed Detection and Response\u2122 (CIS MDR)][35]Device-level protection and response\n[Malicious Code Analysis Platform (MCAP)][36]Web-based sandbox for analyzing suspicious files and\nURLs\n[CIS CyberMarket\u00ae][37]Savings on training and software\n[Malicious Domain Blocking and Reporting Plus][38]Prevent connection to harmful web domains\n[View All CIS Services][39]\n[View All Products & Services][40]\n[Insights][41]\nBack\nInsights\nInsightsExplore trending articles, expert perspectives, real-world applications, and more from the\nbest minds in cybersecurity and IT.\n[Advisories][42]\n[Blog][43]\n[Case Studies][44]\n[Spotlights][45]\n[Newsletters][46]\n[Podcasts][47]\n[Webinars][48]\n[White papers][49]\n[View All Insights][50]\n[Join CIS][51]\nBack\nJoin CIS\nGet InvolvedJoin us on our mission to secure online experiences for all. Become a CIS member,\npartner, or volunteer\u2014and explore our career opportunities.\n[CIS SecureSuite\u00ae Membership][52]\n[Multi-State ISAC (MS-ISAC\u00ae)][53]\n[CIS CyberMarket\u00ae Vendors][54]\n[CIS Communities][55]\n[Our Partners][56]\n[Careers][57]\n[Home][58][About us][59][Media][60][CIS Press Releases][61]CIS Releases CIS-CAT Pro Assessor v4\n\n# CIS Releases CIS-CAT Pro Assessor v4\n\n### Updated Assessment Tool Available to CIS SecureSuite\u00ae Members Now Includes Remote Assessment\n\nNovember 6, 2018\n\nEast Greenbush, NY\n\nCIS^{\u00ae}, (Center for Internet Security, Inc.) announced the introduction of CIS-CAT Pro Assessor v4\ntoday, which now includes remote assessment capabilities.\u201cBased on user demand, we are excited to\nadd a remote assessment capability to our premier CIS Benchmark assessment tool,\u201d said Curtis Dukes,\nCIS Executive Vice President of Security Automation & Best Practices Group.\n\n#### The CIS-CAT Pro Assessor v4 features include:\n* **Remote assessment** through the Command Line Interface (CLI). CIS-CAT Pro Assessor v4 allows\nusers to assess remote endpoints via the command line. Remotely assess Windows endpoints using\nWinRM and an \u201cephemeral\u201d agent, and Unix^{\u00ae}/Linux^{\u00ae }systems primarily using SSH and an\n\u201cephemeral\u201d agent.\n* **Single server installation**: Using CIS-CAT Pro Assessor v4\u2019s remote features requires users to\nplace the assessor tool only on one server. The added benefit to this method is that organizations\nneed Java\u00ae 1.8 installed and updated on the server where CIS-CAT Pro Assessor v4 resides\n* **Report integration** **with CIS-CAT Pro Dashboard**: CIS-CAT Pro Assessor v4 continues to pair\nwith the newly updated CIS-CAT Pro Dashboard to show system compliance over time. Users can sort\nand view assessment results by compliance type, department, or any other category using the custom\ntagging feature. Alerts occur within the dashboard when assessment scores drop.\n* **Secure content support:** CIS-CAT Pro Assessor v4 supports Security Content Automation Protocol\n(SCAP) 1.2 data-stream collections, XCCDF 1.2-based content, and OVAL^{\u00ae }Definitions files, such\nas inventory and vulnerability definitions.\n\nThis robust update to CIS-CAT Pro is available to download via the CIS WorkBench. CIS\nSecureSuite^{ }Members can download it now at [https://workbench.cisecurity.org/files][62].\n\n### Tips for Success with CIS-CAT Pro\n\nCIS will continue to support CIS-CAT Pro Assessor v3 and encourages SecureSuite members to use the\nversion that works best for their environment. Both v3 and v4 require an accessible Java Runtime\nEnvironment (JRE). CIS-CAT Pro Assessor v3 requires 1.6 or later, while CIS-CAT Pro Assessor v4\nrequires 1.8 or later.\n\nCIS-CAT Pro Assessor v4 is only available through the CLI. Users requiring a graphical interface can\ncontinue to use CIS-CAT Pro v3. CIS-CAT Pro\u2019s future roadmap includes assessment orchestration using\nCIS-CAT Pro Dashboard\u2019s graphical interface.\n\nCIS Benchmark coverage: At release, CIS-CAT Pro Assessor v4 can be used with a selection of more\nthan 65+ CIS Benchmarks\u2122. See the *CIS-CAT Pro Assessor Coverage Guide *for the most up-to-date\ninformation regarding platform coverage.\n\nFor more information, visit: [https://www.cisecurity.org/cis-securesuite/][63]\n\n[About][64]\n[Leadership][65]\n[Board][66]\n[Communities][67]\n[Careers][68]\n[Media][69]\n[Testimonials][70]\n[Events][71]\n[US Cyber Challenge][72]\n[Support][73]\n[Contact][74]\n[Products And Tools][75]\n[CIS Critical Security Controls^{\u00ae}][76]\n[CIS Benchmarks^{\u00ae}][77]\n[CIS Hardened Images^{\u00ae}][78]\n[CIS SecureSuite^{\u00ae}][79]\n[CIS SecureSuite^{\u00ae} Platform][80]\n[CIS-CAT^{\u00ae} Lite][81]\n[CIS-CAT^{\u00ae} Pro Assessor][82]\n[CIS RAM][83]\n[CIS-hosted CSAT][84]\n[CIS WorkBench][85]\n[ThreatWA\u2122][86]\n[For SLTT Governments][87]\n[MS-ISAC^{\u00ae}][88]\n[EI-ISAC^{\u00ae}][89]\n[CIS Services^{\u00ae}][90]\n[Albert Network Monitoring][91]\n[Managed Security Services][92]\n[Managed Detection and Response][93]\n[Malicious Domain Blocking and Reporting Plus][94]\n[CIS CyberMarket^{\u00ae}][95]\n[Explore][96]\n[Blog][97]\n[Whitepapers][98]\n[Newsletters][99]\n[Webinars][100]\n[Case Studies][101]\n[Spotlights][102]\n[Videos][103]\n\nCopyright^{\u00a9} 2026 Center for Internet Security^{\u00ae}\n\n[Privacy Notice][104]\n[Twitter][105][Facebook][106][YouTube][107][LinkedIn][108]\n\n[1]: /\n[2]: https://portal.cisecurity.org/\n[3]: /cis-hardened-image-list\n[4]: /support\n[5]: https://workbench.cisecurity.org/\n[6]: /#/\n[7]: /about-us\n[8]: /about-us/cis-leadership-principles\n[9]: /about-us/leadership\n[10]: /testimonials\n[11]: /about-us/media\n[12]: /event-calendar\n[13]: https://learn.cisecurity.org/contact-us\n[14]: /\n[15]: /controls\n[16]: /communities/controls\n[17]: https://learn.cisecurity.org/cis-ram-v2-2\n[18]: /cis-securesuite/benefits/cis-securesuite-platform\n[19]: /threatwa\n[20]: /cis-securesuite/benefits/cis-securesuite-platform\n[21]: /cis-benchmarks\n[22]: /communities/benchmarks\n[23]: /cybersecurity-tools/cis-cat-pro\n[24]: /cis-hardened-images\n[25]: /industry\n[26]: /topics\n[27]: /secure-cyber-city-initiative\n[28]: /cis-securesuite\n[29]: /cis-securesuite\n[30]: https://enroll.cisecurity.org/memberships/#/\n[31]: /ms-isac\n[32]: /ei-isac\n[33]: /whole-of-state-security\n[34]: /services/albert-network-monitoring\n[35]: /services/managed-detection-and-response\n[36]: /services/malicious-code-analysis-platform\n[37]: /services/cis-cybermarket\n[38]: /services/mdbrplus\n[39]: /services\n[40]: /cybersecurity-tools\n[41]: /insights\n[42]: /advisory\n[43]: /insights/blog\n[44]: /insights/case-study\n[45]: /insights/spotlight\n[46]: /insights/newsletter\n[47]: /insights/podcast\n[48]: /insights/webinar\n[49]: /insights/white-papers\n[50]: /insights/all\n[51]: /\n[52]: /cis-securesuite\n[53]: /ms-isac\n[54]: /services/cis-cybermarket/vendor-information\n[55]: /communities\n[56]: /about-us/partners\n[57]: https://cisecurity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/CIS_External_Career_Site\n[58]: /\n[59]: /about-us\n[60]: /about-us/media\n[61]: /about-us/media/press-release\n[62]: https://workbench.cisecurity.org/files\n[63]: /cis-securesuite\n[64]: /about-us\n[65]: /about-us/leadership\n[66]: /about-us/board\n[67]: /communities\n[68]: https://cisecurity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/CIS_External_Career_Site\n[69]: /about-us/media\n[70]: /testimonials\n[71]: /event-calendar\n[72]: http://www.uscyberchallenge.org/\n[73]: /support\n[74]: https://learn.cisecurity.org/contact-us\n[75]: /cybersecurity-tools\n[76]: /controls\n[77]: /cis-benchmarks\n[78]: /cis-hardened-images\n[79]: /cis-securesuite\n[80]: /cis-securesuite/benefits/cis-securesuite-platform\n[81]: https://learn.cisecurity.org/cis-cat-lite\n[82]: /cybersecurity-tools/cis-cat-pro\n[83]: https://learn.cisecurity.org/cis-ram-v2-2\n[84]: /cis-securesuite/benefits/cis-securesuite-platform\n[85]: https://workbench.cisecurity.org/\n[86]: /threatwa\n[87]: /isac\n[88]: /ms-isac\n[89]: /ei-isac\n[90]: /services\n[91]: /services/albert-network-monitoring\n[92]: /services/managed-security-services-mss\n[93]: /services/managed-detection-and-response\n[94]: /services/mdbrplus\n[95]: /services/cis-cybermarket\n[96]: /insights\n[97]: /insights/blog\n[98]: /insights/white-papers\n[99]: /insights/newsletter\n[100]: /insights/webinar\n[101]: /insights/case-study\n[102]: /insights/spotlight\n[103]: https://www.youtube.com/user/TheCISecurity\n[104]: /privacy-notice\n[105]: https://twitter.com/CISecurity/\n[106]: https://www.facebook.com/CenterforIntSec/\n[107]: https://www.youtube.com/user/TheCISecurity/\n[108]: https://www.linkedin.com/company/the-center-for-internet-security/"
