            "url": "https://www.cisecurity.org/about-us/media/press-release/etsi-cis-controls-technical-reports",
            "text": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app.\n[[CIS - Center for Internet Security\u00ae]][1]\n[CIS Portal Login][2][CIS Hardened Images^{\u00ae}][3][Support][4][CIS WorkBench Sign In][5]\nAlert Level: guarded\n[Company][6]\nBack\nCompany\nWho We AreCIS is an independent, nonprofit organization with a mission to create confidence in the\nconnected world.\n[About Us][7]\n[Leadership Principles][8]\n[Leadership Team][9]\n[Testimonials][10]\n[Media][11]\n[Events][12]\n[Contact Us][13]\n[Solutions][14]\nBack\nSolutions\n[Icon]Secure Your Organization\n[CIS Critical Security Controls\u00ae][15]Prioritized & simplified best practices\n[CIS Controls Community][16]Help develop and maintain the Controls\n[CIS RAM][17]Information security risk assessment method\n[CIS CSAT][18]Assess & measure Controls implementation\n[ThreatWA\u2122][19]Insights into emerging cyber & physical threats\n[CIS SecureSuite\u00ae Platform][20]Assess and measure CIS Controls implementation and conformance to the\nCIS Benchmarks\n[Icon]Secure Specific Platforms\n[CIS Benchmarks\u2122][21]100+ vendor-neutral configuration guides\n[CIS Benchmarks Community][22]Develop & update secure configuration guides\n[CIS-CAT\u00aePro Assessor][23]Assess system conformance to CIS Benchmarks\n[CIS Hardened Images\u00ae][24]Virtual images hardened to CIS Benchmarks on cloud service provider\nmarketplaces\n[Situation]Track Specific Threats\n[Industries][25]Your industry's specific threats & needs\n[Topics][26]Dive deeper into specific cybersecurity topics\n[Secure Cyber City\u2122][27]Expertise for cybersecurity resilience and community empowerment\n[SecureSuite\u00ae]\n[CIS SecureSuite\u00ae (Multi-Year Discounts Available)][28]Start secure and stay secure with integrated\ncybersecurity tools and resources designed to help you implement CIS Benchmarks and CIS Controls\n[Learn More][29][Apply Now][30]\n[U.S. State, Local, Tribal & Territorial Governments]U.S. State, Local, Tribal & Territorial\nGovernments\nMemberships\n[MS-ISAC\u00ae][31]Cybersecurity resource for SLTT Governments\n[EI-ISAC\u00ae][32]Critical cybersecurity resource for the nation's SLTT election offices\nState Resources\n[Whole-of-State Security][33]Enabling collaboration and shared responsibility across all levels of\ngovernment\nServices for Members\n[Albert Network Monitoring\u00ae][34]Cost-effective Intrusion Detection System\n[CIS Managed Detection and Response\u2122 (CIS MDR)][35]Device-level protection and response\n[Malicious Code Analysis Platform (MCAP)][36]Web-based sandbox for analyzing suspicious files and\nURLs\n[CIS CyberMarket\u00ae][37]Savings on training and software\n[Malicious Domain Blocking and Reporting Plus][38]Prevent connection to harmful web domains\n[View All CIS Services][39]\n[View All Products & Services][40]\n[Insights][41]\nBack\nInsights\nInsightsExplore trending articles, expert perspectives, real-world applications, and more from the\nbest minds in cybersecurity and IT.\n[Advisories][42]\n[Blog][43]\n[Case Studies][44]\n[Spotlights][45]\n[Newsletters][46]\n[Podcasts][47]\n[Webinars][48]\n[White papers][49]\n[View All Insights][50]\n[Join CIS][51]\nBack\nJoin CIS\nGet InvolvedJoin us on our mission to secure online experiences for all. Become a CIS member,\npartner, or volunteer\u2014and explore our career opportunities.\n[CIS SecureSuite\u00ae Membership][52]\n[Multi-State ISAC (MS-ISAC\u00ae)][53]\n[CIS CyberMarket\u00ae Vendors][54]\n[CIS Communities][55]\n[Our Partners][56]\n[Careers][57]\n[Home][58][About us][59][Media][60][CIS Press Releases][61]ETSI Publishes the CIS Controls\u2122 as\nTechnical Reports\n\n# ETSI Publishes the CIS Controls\u2122 as Technical Reports\n\nOctober 5, 2018\n\nSophia Antipolis, France\n\nThe European Standards Institute\u2019s (ETSI) technical committee CYBER has updated its five-part\ninternational compendium of Technical Reports to protect networks from cyber-attacks: the \u201c*Critical\nSecurity Controls for Effective Cyber Defence*\u201d are based on the CIS\u00ae (Center for Internet Security,\nInc.) CIS Controls\u2122 and related materials. The Reports use the CIS Controls v7 recommendations to\ndescribe the prioritized set of actions that collectively form a defence-in-depth set of best\npractices that mitigate the most common attacks against systems and networks.\n\n\u201c*Building a strong cyber defence for an enterprise is increasingly challenging. Access exists to an\nextraordinary array of security tools and technology, security standards, and countless other\nguidance and recommendations. But all of this technology, information, and oversight has become a\nveritable \u201cFog of More\u201d: competing options, priorities, opinions, and claims that can paralyze or\ndistract an enterprise from vital action. Therefore, we are honored that ETSI recognized the\nimportance of the CIS Controls\u2019 prioritized \u201cdo first\u201d advice to improve global cyber defence by\ntaking this action,*\u201d said Tony Sager, CIS Senior Vice President and Chief Evangelist.\n\n\u201c*ETSI\u2019s expertise on security is a well-known asset among cybersecurity stakeholders and TC CYBER\nrecognizes the benefits brought by the CIS Controls to enhance the cybersecurity posture of\nindustry, administrations and end users,*\u201d says Alex Leadbeater, chairman of the ETSI Technical\nCommittee CYBER, \u201c*The ETSI Technical Reports reflect the combined knowledge of actual attacks and\neffective defences of experts from every part of the cyber security ecosystem.*\u201d This ensures that\nthe CIS Controls are an effective and specific set of technical measures available to detect,\nprevent, respond, and mitigate damage from the most common to the most advanced of those attacks.\nThese ETSI Reports were updated with the recent releases of both the CIS Controls v7 and related\nmaterials to enable network providers to respond to the latest cyber security threats and meet new\nrequirements such as GDPR compliance and cloud data centre hardening.\n\n[TR 103305-1][62] addresses \u201cThe CIS Controls.\u201d It captures and describes the prioritized set of\nactions that collectively form a defence-in-depth set of best practices that mitigate the most\ncommon attacks against systems and networks.\n\n[TR 103305-2][63], on measurement and auditing, is an evolving repository for measurement and\neffectiveness tests of CIS Control implementations.\n\nBecause of their rapidly scaling importance and need for defensive measures, the mobile device and\nInternet of Things (IoT) sectors are treated in TR 103305-3 on Service Sector Implementations.\n\n[TR 103305-4][64], deals with Facilitation Mechanisms and provides a placeholder for reference\ninformation for several especially useful mechanisms: Hardened Images, Mappings and Compliance,\nGuide for Small- and Medium-Sized Enterprises, and Risk Assessment Method.\n\n[TR 103305-5][65], on privacy enhancement, includes a privacy impact assessment and use of the\nControls to help meet provisions of the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).\n\n#### About CIS\n\nCIS\u00ae (Center for Internet Security, Inc.) is a forward-thinking, non-profit entity that harnesses\nthe power of a global IT community to safeguard private and public organizations against cyber\nthreats. The CIS Controls and CIS Benchmarks\u2122 are the global standard and recognized best practices\nfor securing IT systems and data against the most pervasive attacks. These proven guidelines are\ncontinuously refined and verified by a volunteer, global community of experienced IT professionals.\nOur CIS Hardened Images\u2122 are virtual machine emulations preconfigured to provide secure, on-demand,\nand scalable computing environments in the cloud. CIS is home to both the Multi-State Information\nSharing and Analysis Center\u00ae (MS-ISAC\u00ae), the go-to resource for cyber threat prevention, protection,\nresponse, and recovery for U.S. State, Local, Tribal, and Territorial government entities, and the\nElections Infrastructure Information Sharing and Analysis Center\u2122 (EI-ISAC\u2122), which supports the\ncybersecurity needs of U.S. State, Local and Territorial elections offices. To learn more, visit\n[CISecurity.org][66] or follow us on Twitter: [@CISecurity][67].\n\n#### About ETSI\n\nETSI provides members with an open and inclusive environment to support the timely development,\nratification and testing of globally applicable standards for ICT-enabled systems, applications and\nservices across all sectors of industry and society. We are a not-for-profit body with more than 800\nmember organizations worldwide, drawn from 66 countries and five continents. Members comprise a\ndiversified pool of large and small private companies, research entities, academia, government and\npublic organizations. ETSI is one of only three bodies officially recognized by the EU as a European\nStandards Organization (ESO). For more information please visit: [www.etsi.org][68].\n\n[About][69]\n[Leadership][70]\n[Board][71]\n[Communities][72]\n[Careers][73]\n[Media][74]\n[Testimonials][75]\n[Events][76]\n[US Cyber Challenge][77]\n[Support][78]\n[Contact][79]\n[Products And Tools][80]\n[CIS Critical Security Controls^{\u00ae}][81]\n[CIS Benchmarks^{\u00ae}][82]\n[CIS Hardened Images^{\u00ae}][83]\n[CIS SecureSuite^{\u00ae}][84]\n[CIS SecureSuite^{\u00ae} Platform][85]\n[CIS-CAT^{\u00ae} Lite][86]\n[CIS-CAT^{\u00ae} Pro Assessor][87]\n[CIS RAM][88]\n[CIS-hosted CSAT][89]\n[CIS WorkBench][90]\n[ThreatWA\u2122][91]\n[For SLTT Governments][92]\n[MS-ISAC^{\u00ae}][93]\n[EI-ISAC^{\u00ae}][94]\n[CIS Services^{\u00ae}][95]\n[Albert Network Monitoring][96]\n[Managed Security Services][97]\n[Managed Detection and Response][98]\n[Malicious Domain Blocking and Reporting Plus][99]\n[CIS CyberMarket^{\u00ae}][100]\n[Explore][101]\n[Blog][102]\n[Whitepapers][103]\n[Newsletters][104]\n[Webinars][105]\n[Case Studies][106]\n[Spotlights][107]\n[Videos][108]\n\nCopyright^{\u00a9} 2026 Center for Internet Security^{\u00ae}\n\n[Privacy Notice][109]\n[Twitter][110][Facebook][111][YouTube][112][LinkedIn][113]\n\n[1]: /\n[2]: https://portal.cisecurity.org/\n[3]: /cis-hardened-image-list\n[4]: /support\n[5]: https://workbench.cisecurity.org/\n[6]: /#/\n[7]: /about-us\n[8]: /about-us/cis-leadership-principles\n[9]: /about-us/leadership\n[10]: /testimonials\n[11]: /about-us/media\n[12]: /event-calendar\n[13]: https://learn.cisecurity.org/contact-us\n[14]: /\n[15]: /controls\n[16]: /communities/controls\n[17]: https://learn.cisecurity.org/cis-ram-v2-2\n[18]: /cis-securesuite/benefits/cis-securesuite-platform\n[19]: /threatwa\n[20]: /cis-securesuite/benefits/cis-securesuite-platform\n[21]: /cis-benchmarks\n[22]: /communities/benchmarks\n[23]: /cybersecurity-tools/cis-cat-pro\n[24]: /cis-hardened-images\n[25]: /industry\n[26]: /topics\n[27]: /secure-cyber-city-initiative\n[28]: /cis-securesuite\n[29]: /cis-securesuite\n[30]: https://enroll.cisecurity.org/memberships/#/\n[31]: /ms-isac\n[32]: /ei-isac\n[33]: /whole-of-state-security\n[34]: /services/albert-network-monitoring\n[35]: /services/managed-detection-and-response\n[36]: /services/malicious-code-analysis-platform\n[37]: /services/cis-cybermarket\n[38]: /services/mdbrplus\n[39]: /services\n[40]: /cybersecurity-tools\n[41]: /insights\n[42]: /advisory\n[43]: /insights/blog\n[44]: /insights/case-study\n[45]: /insights/spotlight\n[46]: /insights/newsletter\n[47]: /insights/podcast\n[48]: /insights/webinar\n[49]: /insights/white-papers\n[50]: /insights/all\n[51]: /\n[52]: /cis-securesuite\n[53]: /ms-isac\n[54]: /services/cis-cybermarket/vendor-information\n[55]: /communities\n[56]: /about-us/partners\n[57]: https://cisecurity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/CIS_External_Career_Site\n[58]: /\n[59]: /about-us\n[60]: /about-us/media\n[61]: /about-us/media/press-release\n[62]: https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_tr/103300_103399/10330501/03.01.01_60/tr_10330501v030101p.pd\n[63]: https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_tr/103300_103399/10330502/02.01.01_60/tr_10330502v020101p.pd\n[64]: https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_tr/103300_103399/10330504/02.01.01_60/tr_10330504v020101p.pd\n[65]: https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_tr/103300_103399/10330505/02.01.01_60/tr_10330505v020101p.pd\n[66]: https://www.CISecurity.org\n[67]: https://twitter.com/CISecurity\n[68]: http://www.etsi.org\n[69]: /about-us\n[70]: /about-us/leadership\n[71]: /about-us/board\n[72]: /communities\n[73]: https://cisecurity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/CIS_External_Career_Site\n[74]: /about-us/media\n[75]: /testimonials\n[76]: /event-cale"
