            "url": "https://www.cisecurity.org/about-us/media/press-release/internet-of-things-needs-to-be-more-secure",
            "text": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app.\n[[CIS - Center for Internet Security\u00ae]][1]\n[CIS Portal Login][2][CIS Hardened Images^{\u00ae}][3][Support][4][CIS WorkBench Sign In][5]\nAlert Level: guarded\n[Company][6]\nBack\nCompany\nWho We AreCIS is an independent, nonprofit organization with a mission to create confidence in the\nconnected world.\n[About Us][7]\n[Leadership Principles][8]\n[Leadership Team][9]\n[Testimonials][10]\n[Media][11]\n[Events][12]\n[Contact Us][13]\n[Solutions][14]\nBack\nSolutions\n[Icon]Secure Your Organization\n[CIS Critical Security Controls\u00ae][15]Prioritized & simplified best practices\n[CIS Controls Community][16]Help develop and maintain the Controls\n[CIS RAM][17]Information security risk assessment method\n[CIS CSAT][18]Assess & measure Controls implementation\n[ThreatWA\u2122][19]Insights into emerging cyber & physical threats\n[CIS SecureSuite\u00ae Platform][20]Assess and measure CIS Controls implementation and conformance to the\nCIS Benchmarks\n[Icon]Secure Specific Platforms\n[CIS Benchmarks\u2122][21]100+ vendor-neutral configuration guides\n[CIS Benchmarks Community][22]Develop & update secure configuration guides\n[CIS-CAT\u00aePro Assessor][23]Assess system conformance to CIS Benchmarks\n[CIS Hardened Images\u00ae][24]Virtual images hardened to CIS Benchmarks on cloud service provider\nmarketplaces\n[Situation]Track Specific Threats\n[Industries][25]Your industry's specific threats & needs\n[Topics][26]Dive deeper into specific cybersecurity topics\n[Secure Cyber City\u2122][27]Expertise for cybersecurity resilience and community empowerment\n[SecureSuite\u00ae]\n[CIS SecureSuite\u00ae (Multi-Year Discounts Available)][28]Start secure and stay secure with integrated\ncybersecurity tools and resources designed to help you implement CIS Benchmarks and CIS Controls\n[Learn More][29][Apply Now][30]\n[U.S. State, Local, Tribal & Territorial Governments]U.S. State, Local, Tribal & Territorial\nGovernments\nMemberships\n[MS-ISAC\u00ae][31]Cybersecurity resource for SLTT Governments\n[EI-ISAC\u00ae][32]Critical cybersecurity resource for the nation's SLTT election offices\nState Resources\n[Whole-of-State Security][33]Enabling collaboration and shared responsibility across all levels of\ngovernment\nServices for Members\n[Albert Network Monitoring\u00ae][34]Cost-effective Intrusion Detection System\n[CIS Managed Detection and Response\u2122 (CIS MDR)][35]Device-level protection and response\n[Malicious Code Analysis Platform (MCAP)][36]Web-based sandbox for analyzing suspicious files and\nURLs\n[CIS CyberMarket\u00ae][37]Savings on training and software\n[Malicious Domain Blocking and Reporting Plus][38]Prevent connection to harmful web domains\n[View All CIS Services][39]\n[View All Products & Services][40]\n[Insights][41]\nBack\nInsights\nInsightsExplore trending articles, expert perspectives, real-world applications, and more from the\nbest minds in cybersecurity and IT.\n[Advisories][42]\n[Blog][43]\n[Case Studies][44]\n[Spotlights][45]\n[Newsletters][46]\n[Podcasts][47]\n[Webinars][48]\n[White papers][49]\n[View All Insights][50]\n[Join CIS][51]\nBack\nJoin CIS\nGet InvolvedJoin us on our mission to secure online experiences for all. Become a CIS member,\npartner, or volunteer\u2014and explore our career opportunities.\n[CIS SecureSuite\u00ae Membership][52]\n[Multi-State ISAC (MS-ISAC\u00ae)][53]\n[CIS CyberMarket\u00ae Vendors][54]\n[CIS Communities][55]\n[Our Partners][56]\n[Careers][57]\n[Home][58][About us][59][Media][60][CIS Press Releases][61]\u201cInternet of Things\u201d Needs to be More\nSecure\n\n# \u201cInternet of Things\u201d Needs to be More Secure\n\n## Center for Internet Security Joins Call for IoT Security Standards\n\nEAST GREENBUSH, N.Y. and WASHINGTON, D.C., February 15, 2021- Network-connected devices are found in\nmost households around the world and the Internet of Things (IoT) has become part of daily life.\nWhile items like smart TVs, watches and home surveillance systems offer convenience to consumers,\nthey can also pose security threats when they are not manufactured and maintained with standard\nsecurity practices.\n\nThe Center for Internet Security, Inc. (CIS\u00ae) is joining more than 100 other entities in calling for\nmanufacturers and vendors to adhere to a set of security standards when placing these devices on the\nmarket. Establishing a global baseline of security for internet connected devices is a step toward a\nmore secure digital future.\n\nAccording to CIS CEO John Gilligan, \u201cThe speed of evolution of modern information technologies can\nresult in new products that lack adequate cyber protections. The World Economic Forum recognized\nthis gap in the Internet of Things (IoT) space and coordinated the development of an international,\nmulti-stakeholder consensus of five effective, common-sense best practices to serve as a global\nbaseline for IoT security. The result is intended help manufacturers and vendors identify and\nimplement the most important device security that can help ensure that IoT devices can be relied\nupon by consumers around the world.\u201d\n\nYou can read the World Economic Forum statement in its entirety at:\n[https://cybertechaccord.org/industry-hackers-and-consumers-for-a-global-baseline-for-consumer-iot-s\necurity/][62]\n\nTo speak with WEF\u2019s Jeff Merritt, head of the Council on the Connected World, please contact Lisa\nChamberlain at [[email protected]][63].\n\nTo speak with CIS\u2019s John Gilligan, please contact Kelly Wyland at [[email protected]][64].\n\n**About us:**\n\nThe Center for Internet Security, Inc. (CIS\u00ae) makes the connected world a safer place for people,\nbusinesses, and governments through our core competencies of collaboration and innovation. We are a\ncommunity-driven nonprofit, responsible for the CIS Critical Security Controls\u00ae and CIS Benchmarks\u2122,\nglobally recognized best practices for securing IT systems and data. We lead a global community of\nIT professionals to continuously evolve these standards and provide products and services to\nproactively safeguard against emerging threats. Our CIS Hardened Images\u00ae provide secure, on-demand,\nscalable computing environments in the cloud. CIS is home to the Multi-State Information Sharing and\nAnalysis Center\u00ae (MS-ISAC\u00ae), the trusted resource for cyber threat prevention, protection, response,\nand recovery for U.S. State, Local, Tribal, and Territorial government entities, and the Elections\nInfrastructure Information Sharing and Analysis Center\u00ae (EI-ISAC\u00ae), which supports the rapidly\nchanging cybersecurity needs of U.S. election offices. To learn more, visit cisecurity.org or follow\nus on Twitter: @CISecurity.\n\n[About][65]\n[Leadership][66]\n[Board][67]\n[Communities][68]\n[Careers][69]\n[Media][70]\n[Testimonials][71]\n[Events][72]\n[US Cyber Challenge][73]\n[Support][74]\n[Contact][75]\n[Products And Tools][76]\n[CIS Critical Security Controls^{\u00ae}][77]\n[CIS Benchmarks^{\u00ae}][78]\n[CIS Hardened Images^{\u00ae}][79]\n[CIS SecureSuite^{\u00ae}][80]\n[CIS SecureSuite^{\u00ae} Platform][81]\n[CIS-CAT^{\u00ae} Lite][82]\n[CIS-CAT^{\u00ae} Pro Assessor][83]\n[CIS RAM][84]\n[CIS-hosted CSAT][85]\n[CIS WorkBench][86]\n[ThreatWA\u2122][87]\n[For SLTT Governments][88]\n[MS-ISAC^{\u00ae}][89]\n[EI-ISAC^{\u00ae}][90]\n[CIS Services^{\u00ae}][91]\n[Albert Network Monitoring][92]\n[Managed Security Services][93]\n[Managed Detection and Response][94]\n[Malicious Domain Blocking and Reporting Plus][95]\n[CIS CyberMarket^{\u00ae}][96]\n[Explore][97]\n[Blog][98]\n[Whitepapers][99]\n[Newsletters][100]\n[Webinars][101]\n[Case Studies][102]\n[Spotlights][103]\n[Videos][104]\n\nCopyright^{\u00a9} 2026 Center for Internet Security^{\u00ae}\n\n[Privacy Notice][105]\n[Twitter][106][Facebook][107][YouTube][108][LinkedIn][109]\n\n[1]: /\n[2]: https://portal.cisecurity.org/\n[3]: /cis-hardened-image-list\n[4]: /support\n[5]: https://workbench.cisecurity.org/\n[6]: /#/\n[7]: /about-us\n[8]: /about-us/cis-leadership-principles\n[9]: /about-us/leadership\n[10]: /testimonials\n[11]: /about-us/media\n[12]: /event-calendar\n[13]: https://learn.cisecurity.org/contact-us\n[14]: /\n[15]: /controls\n[16]: /communities/controls\n[17]: https://learn.cisecurity.org/cis-ram-v2-2\n[18]: /cis-securesuite/benefits/cis-securesuite-platform\n[19]: /threatwa\n[20]: /cis-securesuite/benefits/cis-securesuite-platform\n[21]: /cis-benchmarks\n[22]: /communities/benchmarks\n[23]: /cybersecurity-tools/cis-cat-pro\n[24]: /cis-hardened-images\n[25]: /industry\n[26]: /topics\n[27]: /secure-cyber-city-initiative\n[28]: /cis-securesuite\n[29]: /cis-securesuite\n[30]: https://enroll.cisecurity.org/memberships/#/\n[31]: /ms-isac\n[32]: /ei-isac\n[33]: /whole-of-state-security\n[34]: /services/albert-network-monitoring\n[35]: /services/managed-detection-and-response\n[36]: /services/malicious-code-analysis-platform\n[37]: /services/cis-cybermarket\n[38]: /services/mdbrplus\n[39]: /services\n[40]: /cybersecurity-tools\n[41]: /insights\n[42]: /advisory\n[43]: /insights/blog\n[44]: /insights/case-study\n[45]: /insights/spotlight\n[46]: /insights/newsletter\n[47]: /insights/podcast\n[48]: /insights/webinar\n[49]: /insights/white-papers\n[50]: /insights/all\n[51]: /\n[52]: /cis-securesuite\n[53]: /ms-isac\n[54]: /services/cis-cybermarket/vendor-information\n[55]: /communities\n[56]: /about-us/partners\n[57]: https://cisecurity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/CIS_External_Career_Site\n[58]: /\n[59]: /about-us\n[60]: /about-us/media\n[61]: /about-us/media/press-release\n[62]: https://cybertechaccord.org/industry-hackers-and-consumers-for-a-global-baseline-for-consumer-\niot-security/\n[63]: /cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#88c4e1fbe9a6cbe0e9e5eaedfae4e9e1e6c8ffedeee7fafde5a6e7faef\n[64]: /cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#2249474e4e5b0c555b4e434c4662414b51474157504b565b0c4d5045\n[65]: /about-us\n[66]: /about-us/leadership\n[67]: /about-us/board\n[68]: /communities\n[69]: https://cisecurity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/CIS_External_Career_Site\n[70]: /about-us/media\n[71]: /testimonials\n[72]: /event-calendar\n[73]: http://www.uscyberchallenge.org/\n[74]: /support\n[75]: https://learn.cisecurity.org/contact-us\n[76]: /cybersecurity-tools\n[77]: /controls\n[78]: /cis-benchmarks\n[79]: /cis-hardened-images\n[80]: /cis-securesuite\n[81]: /cis-securesuite/benefits/cis-securesuite-platform\n[82]: https://learn.cisecurity.org/cis-cat-lite\n[83]: /cybersecurity-tools/cis-cat-pro\n[84]: https://learn.cisecurity.org/cis-ram-v2-2\n[85]: /cis-securesuite/benefits/cis-securesuite-platform\n[86]: https://workbench.cisecurity.org/\n[87]: /threatwa\n[88]: /isac\n[89]: /ms-isac\n[90]: /ei-isac\n[91]: /services\n[92]: /services/albert-network-monitoring\n[93]: /services/managed-security-services-mss\n[94]: /services/managed-detection-and-response\n[95]: /services/mdbrplus\n[96]: /services/cis-cybermarket\n[97]: /insights\n[98]: /insights/blog\n[99]: /insights/white-papers\n[100]: /insights/newsletter\n[101]: /insights/webinar\n[102]: /insights/case-study\n[103]: /insights/spotlight\n[104]: https://www.youtube.com/user/TheCISecurity\n[105]: /privacy-notice\n[106]: https://twitter.com/CISecurity/\n[107]: https://www.facebook.com/CenterforIntSec/\n[108]: https://www.youtube.com/user/TheCISecurity/\n[109]: https://www.linkedin.com/company/the-center-for-internet-security/"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://cisecurity.org/about-us",
            "text": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app.\n[[CIS - Center for Internet Security\u00ae]][1]\n[CIS Portal Login][2][CIS Hardened Images^{\u00ae}][3][Support][4][CIS WorkBench Sign In][5]\nAlert Level: guarded\n[Company][6]\nBack\nCompany\nWho We AreCIS is an independent, nonprofit organization with a mission to create confidence in the\nconnected world.\n[About Us][7]\n[Leadership Principles][8]\n[Leadership Team][9]\n[Testimonials][10]\n[Media][11]\n[Events][12]\n[Contact Us][13]\n[Solutions][14]\nBack\nSolutions\n[Icon]Secure Your Organization\n[CIS Critical Security Controls\u00ae][15]Prioritized & simplified best practices\n[CIS Controls Community][16]Help develop and maintain the Controls\n[CIS RAM][17]Information security risk assessment method\n[CIS CSAT][18]Assess & measure Controls implementation\n[ThreatWA\u2122][19]Insights into emerging cyber & physical threats\n[CIS SecureSuite\u00ae Platform][20]Assess and measure CIS Controls implementation and conformance to the\nCIS Benchmarks\n[Icon]Secure Specific Platforms\n[CIS Benchmarks\u2122][21]100+ vendor-neutral configuration guides\n[CIS Benchmarks Community][22]Develop & update secure configuration guides\n[CIS-CAT\u00aePro Assessor][23]Assess system conformance to CIS Benchmarks\n[CIS Hardened Images\u00ae][24]Virtual images hardened to CIS Benchmarks on cloud service provider\nmarketplaces\n[Situation]Track Specific Threats\n[Industries][25]Your industry's specific threats & needs\n[Topics][26]Dive deeper into specific cybersecurity topics\n[Secure Cyber City\u2122][27]Expertise for cybersecurity resilience and community empowerment\n[SecureSuite\u00ae]\n[CIS SecureSuite\u00ae (Multi-Year Discounts Available)][28]Start secure and stay secure with integrated\ncybersecurity tools and resources designed to help you implement CIS Benchmarks and CIS Controls\n[Learn More][29][Apply Now][30]\n[U.S. State, Local, Tribal & Territorial Governments]U.S. State, Local, Tribal & Territorial\nGovernments\nMemberships\n[MS-ISAC\u00ae][31]Cybersecurity resource for SLTT Governments\n[EI-ISAC\u00ae][32]Critical cybersecurity resource for the nation's SLTT election offices\nState Resources\n[Whole-of-State Security][33]Enabling collaboration and shared responsibility across all levels of\ngovernment\nServices for Members\n[Albert Network Monitoring\u00ae][34]Cost-effective Intrusion Detection System\n[CIS Managed Detection and Response\u2122 (CIS MDR)][35]Device-level protection and response\n[Malicious Code Analysis Platform (MCAP)][36]Web-based sandbox for analyzing suspicious files and\nURLs\n[CIS CyberMarket\u00ae][37]Savings on training and software\n[Malicious Domain Blocking and Reporting Plus][38]Prevent connection to harmful web domains\n[View All CIS Services][39]\n[View All Products & Services][40]\n[Insights][41]\nBack\nInsights\nInsightsExplore trending articles, expert perspectives, real-world applications, and more from the\nbest minds in cybersecurity and IT.\n[Advisories][42]\n[Blog][43]\n[Case Studies][44]\n[Spotlights][45]\n[Newsletters][46]\n[Podcasts][47]\n[Webinars][48]\n[White papers][49]\n[View All Insights][50]\n[Join CIS][51]\nBack\nJoin CIS\nGet InvolvedJoin us on our mission to secure online experiences for all. Become a CIS member,\npartner, or volunteer\u2014and explore our career opportunities.\n[CIS SecureSuite\u00ae Membership][52]\n[Multi-State ISAC (MS-ISAC\u00ae)][53]\n[CIS CyberMarket\u00ae Vendors][54]\n[CIS Communities][55]\n[Our Partners][56]\n[Careers][57]\n[Home][58]About us\n\n# About us\n\nThe Center for Internet Security, Inc. (CIS^{\u00ae}) makes the connected world a safer place for people,\nbusinesses, and governments through our core competencies of collaboration and innovation.\n\nWe are a community-driven nonprofit, responsible for the CIS Controls^{\u00ae} and CIS Benchmarks\u00ae,\nglobally recognized best practices for securing IT systems and data. We lead a global community of\nIT professionals to continuously evolve these standards and provide products and services to\nproactively safeguard against emerging threats. Our CIS Hardened Images\u00ae provide secure, on-demand,\nscalable computing environments in the cloud.\n\nCIS is home to the Multi-State Information Sharing and Analysis Center^{\u00ae} (MS-ISAC^{\u00ae}), the\ntrusted resource for cyber threat prevention, protection, response, and recovery for U.S. State,\nLocal, Tribal, and Territorial government entities.\n\n### Our Commitment\n\nCIS operates as a mission driven, nonprofit organization dedicated to making the connected world a\nsafer place. Our employees adhere to our [Code of Ethics][59], [Leadership Principles][60], and\n[Code of Conduct][61], consistent with our collaborative, nonpartisan, vendor-agnostic operating\nmodel. These values guide our decisions and actions and build trust in our capabilities, enabling us\nto achieve our mission.\n\n### The CIS Vision\n\nLeading the global community to secure our ever-changing connected world.\n\n### The CIS Mission\n\nOur mission is to make the connected world a safer place by developing, validating, and promoting\ntimely best practice solutions that help people, businesses, and governments protect themselves\nagainst pervasive cyber threats.\n\n### CIS Funding\n\nCIS receives funding through various means, including direct sales of various cybersecurity best\npractices tools and resources, like [CIS SecureSuite Membership][62] and [CIS Hardened Images][63],\nand cybersecurity services like [CIS Endpoint Security Services][64]. Previously funded by the\nfederal government, the Multi-State Information Sharing and Analysis Center (MS-ISAC) is now\noperated by CIS through a member-funded model to continue it's mission of improving the overall\ncybersecurity posture of U.S. State, Local, Tribal, and Territorial government organizations.\n\n### 25 Years of Creating Confidence in the Connected World\n\nTwenty-five years ago, business and social use of the internet surged \u2013 and so did cybersecurity\nthreats. Many organizations were exposed, lacking sufficient resources or expertise to defend\nthemselves. Experts from government agencies, private sector innovation labs, and top security\ninstitutions came together as a community to shares ideas and labor to directly address these\nthreats. Their efforts resulted in the creation of the Center for Internet Security (CIS).\n\n[Learn more about CIS\u2019s 25 years of history][65]\n\n### Media\n\n[CIS Media Page][66]\n[Rumor Control][67]\n\n### About CIS\n\n[CIS 2024 Year in Review][68]\n[CIS Culture][69]\n[CIS Cares][70]\n[IDEA Alliance][71]\n[Alan Paller Laureate Program][72]\n\n### Leadership\n\n[CIS Code of Ethics][73]\n[CIS Leadership Principles][74]\n[Code of Conduct][75]\n[Leadership Team][76]\n[Board of Directors][77]\n\nIf you would like to inquire about having a CIS cybersecurity expert attend or speak at your event,\nplease send your request to [[email protected]][78]\n\n## Information Hub\n\nBlog Post06.25.2026\n[CIS Controls Accreditation Drives Global Cybersecurity Standards][79]\n[Read More Blog Post][80]\nPress Release06.22.2026\n[Center for Internet Security Report Warns of Illicit Sports Betting, Fraud and Athlete Safety Risks\nDuring FIFA World Cup 2026][81]\n[Read More Press Release][82]\nWhite Paper06.18.2026\n[Illicit Sports Betting and Match Integrity Risks to Large-Scale Events][83]\n[Read More White Paper][84]\nBlog Post06.18.2026\n[CIS Benchmarks June 2026 Update][85]\n[Read More Blog Post][86]\n[About][87]\n[Leadership][88]\n[Board][89]\n[Communities][90]\n[Careers][91]\n[Media][92]\n[Testimonials][93]\n[Events][94]\n[US Cyber Challenge][95]\n[Support][96]\n[Contact][97]\n[Products And Tools][98]\n[CIS Critical Security Controls^{\u00ae}][99]\n[CIS Benchmarks^{\u00ae}][100]\n[CIS Hardened Images^{\u00ae}][101]\n[CIS SecureSuite^{\u00ae}][102]\n[CIS SecureSuite^{\u00ae} Platform][103]\n[CIS-CAT^{\u00ae} Lite][104]\n[CIS-CAT^{\u00ae} Pro Assessor][105]\n[CIS RAM][106]\n[CIS-hosted CSAT][107]\n[CIS WorkBench][108]\n[ThreatWA\u2122][109]\n[For SLTT Governments][110]\n[MS-ISAC^{\u00ae}][111]\n[EI-ISAC^{\u00ae}][112]\n[CIS Services^{\u00ae}][113]\n[Albert Network Monitoring][114]\n[Managed Security Services][115]\n[Managed Detection and Response][116]\n[Malicious Domain Blocking and Reporting Plus][117]\n[CIS CyberMarket^{\u00ae}][118]\n[Explore][119]\n[Blog][120]\n[Whitepapers][121]\n[Newsletters][122]\n[Webinars][123]\n[Case Studies][124]\n[Spotlights][125]\n[Videos][126]\n\nCopyright^{\u00a9} 2026 Center for Internet Security^{\u00ae}\n\n[Privacy Notice][127]\n[Twitter][128][Facebook][129][YouTube][130][LinkedIn][131]\n\n[1]: /\n[2]: https://portal.cisecurity.org/\n[3]: /cis-hardened-image-list\n[4]: /support\n[5]: https://workbench.cisecurity.org/\n[6]: /#/\n[7]: /about-us\n[8]: /about-us/cis-leadership-principles\n[9]: /about-us/leadership\n[10]: /testimonials\n[11]: /about-us/media\n[12]: /event-calendar\n[13]: https://learn.cisecurity.org/contact-us\n[14]: /\n[15]: /controls\n[16]: /communities/controls\n[17]: https://learn.cisecurity.org/cis-ram-v2-2\n[18]: /cis-securesuite/benefits/cis-securesuite-platform\n[19]: /threatwa\n[20]: /cis-securesuite/benefits/cis-securesuite-platform\n[21]: /cis-benchmarks\n[22]: /communities/benchmarks\n[23]: /cybersecurity-tools/cis-cat-pro\n[24]: /cis-hardened-images\n[25]: /industry\n[26]: /topics\n[27]: /secure-cyber-city-initiative\n[28]: /cis-securesuite\n[29]: /cis-securesuite\n[30]: https://enroll.cisecurity.org/memberships/#/\n[31]: /ms-isac\n[32]: /ei-isac\n[33]: /whole-of-state-security\n[34]: /services/albert-network-monitoring\n[35]: /services/managed-detection-and-response\n[36]: /services/malicious-code-analysis-platform\n[37]: /services/cis-cybermarket\n[38]: /services/mdbrplus\n[39]: /services\n[40]: /cybersecurity-tools\n[41]: /insights\n[42]: /advisory\n[43]: /insights/blog\n[44]: /insights/case-study\n[45]: /insights/spotlight\n[46]: /insights/newsletter\n[47]: /insights/podcast\n[48]: /insights/webinar\n[49]: /insights/white-papers\n[50]: /insights/all\n[51]: /\n[52]: /cis-securesuite\n[53]: /ms-isac\n[54]: /services/cis-cybermarket/vendor-information\n[55]: /communities\n[56]: /about-us/partners\n[57]: https://cisecurity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/CIS_External_Career_Site\n[58]: /\n[59]: https://learn.cisecurity.org/code-of-ethics\n[60]: /about-us/cis-leadership-principles\n[61]: https://learn.cisecurity.org/code-of-conduct\n[62]: /cis-securesuite\n[63]: /cis-hardened-images\n[64]: /services/managed-detection-and-response\n[65]: /about-us/history\n[66]: /about-us/media\n[67]: /about-us/rumor-control\n[68]: /insights/white-papers/cis-year-in-review-2024\n[69]: /about-us/cis-culture\n[70]: /about-us/cis-cares\n[71]: /about-us/idea-alliance\n[72]: /about-us/alan-paller-laureate-program\n[73]: https://learn.cisecurity.org/code-of-ethics\n[74]: /about-us/cis-leadership-principles\n[75]: https://learn.cisecurity.org/code-of-conduct\n[76]: /about-us/leadership\n[77]: /about-us/board\n[78]: /cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#cfaab9aaa1bbbc8faca6bcaaacbabda6bbb6e1a0bda8\n[79]: /insights/blog/cis-controls-accreditation-drives-global-cybersecurity-standards\n[80]: /insights/blog/cis-controls-accreditation-drives-global-cybersecurity-standards\n[81]: /about-us/media/press-release/center-for-internet-security-report-warns-of-illicit-sports-bett\ning-fraud-and-athlete-safety-risks-during-fifa-world-cup-2026\n[82]: /about-us/media/press-release/center-for-internet-security-report-warns-of-illicit-sports-bett\ning-fraud-and-athlete-safety-risks-during-fifa-world-cup-2026\n[83]: /insights/white-papers/illicit-sports-betting-match-integrity-risks-large-scale-events\n[84]: /insights/white-papers/illicit-sports-betting-match-integrity-risks-large-scale-events\n[85]: /insights/blog/cis-benchmarks-june-2026-update\n[86]: /insights/blog/cis-benchmarks-june-2026-update\n[87]: /about-us\n[88]: /about-us/leadership\n[89]: /about-us/board\n[90]: /communities\n[91]: https://cisecurity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/CIS_External_Career_Site\n[92]: /about-us/media\n[93]: /testimonials\n[94]: /event-calendar\n[95]: http://www.uscyberchallenge.org/\n[96]: /support\n[97]: https://learn.cisecurity.org/contact-us\n[98]: /cybersecurity-tools\n[99]: /controls\n[100]: /cis-benchmarks\n[101]: /cis-hardened-images\n[102]: /cis-securesuite\n[103]: /cis-securesuite/benefits/cis-securesuite-platform\n[104]: https://learn.cisecurity.org/cis-cat-lite\n[105]: /cybersecurity-tools/cis-cat-pro\n[106]: https://learn.cisecurity"
