        "crawl_text": "Robert Bosch Centre for Cyber-Physical Systems, IISc Research and Academic Centre Part of Indian Institute of Science (IISc) India Interdisciplinary research collaborations State-of-the-art CPS laboratory (Makery) Strong partnerships with technology companies and startups IDR Building, near CeNSE, Indian Institute of Science, Bangalore, 560012 India PhD Student awarded TCS Research Scholar Program Scholarship Qualcomm Innovation Fellowship Super Winner 2023 Advancing research in Cyber-Physical Systems Fostering interdisciplinary collaborations Developing innovative solutions for societal and industrial needs A leading research center in Cyber-Physical Systems in India IISc RBCCPS &#8211; Robert Bosch Centre for Cyber-Physical Systems\n\nResearch\n\nResearch Clusters\n\nControl and Optimization\n\nRobotics\n\nAI and ML\n\nSocio Technical Systems\n\nLabs and Centers\n\nCenter for Networked Intelligence\n\nCiSTUP\n\nFOCAS Lab\n\nHiRO Lab\n\nIISc-Nokia CoE for Networked Robotics\n\nStochastic Robotics Lab\n\nVISTA Lab\n\nResearch Facilities\n\nProjects\n\nPublications\n\nPeople\n\nFaculty\n\nStaff\n\nResearch Students\n\nMTech Students\n\nPostdocs\n\nAlumni\n\nAcademics\n\nCourses\n\nAdmissions\n\nMtech RAS\n\nMTech AI\n\nResearch Programmes\n\nResults\n\nCurriculum\n\nMtech RAS\n\nResearch Programmes\n\nFellowships\n\nOpportunities\n\nCurrent Openings\n\nUpdates\n\nEvents\n\nNews\n\nPlacements\n\nTenders\n\nCyPhySS\n\nCyPhySS 2023\n\nCyPhySS 2024\n\nAbout\n\nAbout Us\n\nCollaborations\n\nIISc\n\nARTPARK\n\nGallery\n\nContact Us\n\nMenu\n\nResearch\n\nResearch Clusters\n\nControl and Optimization\n\nRobotics\n\nAI and ML\n\nSocio Technical Systems\n\nLabs and Centers\n\nCenter for Networked Intelligence\n\nCiSTUP\n\nFOCAS Lab\n\nHiRO Lab\n\nIISc-Nokia CoE for Networked Robotics\n\nStochastic Robotics Lab\n\nVISTA Lab\n\nResearch Facilities\n\nProjects\n\nPublications\n\nPeople\n\nFaculty\n\nStaff\n\nResearch Students\n\nMTech Students\n\nPostdocs\n\nAlumni\n\nAcademics\n\nCourses\n\nAdmissions\n\nMtech RAS\n\nMTech AI\n\nResearch Programmes\n\nResults\n\nCurriculum\n\nMtech RAS\n\nResearch Programmes\n\nFellowships\n\nOpportunities\n\nCurrent Openings\n\nUpdates\n\nEvents\n\nNews\n\nPlacements\n\nTenders\n\nCyPhySS\n\nCyPhySS 2023\n\nCyPhySS 2024\n\nAbout\n\nAbout Us\n\nCollaborations\n\nIISc\n\nARTPARK\n\nGallery\n\nContact Us\n\ncps_group_photo_2024Jul\n\nSlide 2\n\nRBCCPS\n\nLegged Robots\n\nSlide 3\n\nRBCCPS\n\nMobile Robots\n\nAbout RBCCPS\n\nMission is to advance the field of cyber-physical systems\n\nThrough research, innovation, and collaboration we strive to advance the field of cyber-physical systems. We aim to\n\nDevelop cutting-edge technologies\n\nPromote interdisciplinary research\n\nContribute to societal and industrial needs in the domain of cyber-physical systems\n\nAbout RBCCPS\n\nVision is to establish itself as a globally recognized center of excellence in CPS\n\nThe RBCCPS envisions becoming a global leader in the research and development of CPS. RBCCPS envisions achieving this vision by\n\nFostering interdisciplinary research collaborations\n\nConducting cutting-edge research\n\nDeveloping innovative solutions that integrate physical and computational systems\n\nAbout RBCCPS\n\nInnovation-driven excellence in CPS research to create positive impact.\n\nExcellence, Interdisciplinary Approach, Impact, Ethical Conduct, Knowledge sharing.\n\nStriving for excellence in research, innovation, education, and collaboration.\n\nBridging disciplines through research and innovation.\n\nAddressing real-world challenges with ethical CPS technology, promoting open collaboration.\n\nOur Mission\n\nOur Vision\n\nCore Values\n\nLatest events, news and updates at RBCCPS\n\nLatest News News\n\n14 Jan\n\nBest demo in COMSNETS 2024\n\nCongratulations to Navin Kumar and Sudarshan Bandopadhyay MTech students from RBCCPS for securing runner up under the demos and exhibit section of COMSNETS 2024\n\nRead More +\n\nLatest News\n\n28 Jul\n\nPhD Student of RBCCPS Awarded TCS Research Scholar Program (RSP) Scholarship\n\nCongratulations to Ajay Kumar Sandula, a PhD student at RBCCPS, for his remarkable achievement! Under the guidance of Dr. Pradipta Biswas as his main guide and Dr. Debasish Ghose as ...\n\nRead More +\n\nLatest News\n\n03 Jul\n\nCongratulations!- Qualcomm Innovation Fellowship Super Winner 2023\n\nCongratulations!!! Siddarth Asokan, RBCCPS PhD student has bagged the Qualcomm Innovation Fellowship Super Winner for 2023. He has secured this fellowship for the 4th time! and if that was not ...\n\nRead More +\n\nIn Press\n\nMedia\n\n22 Aug\n\nFaculty at RBCCPS&#8217;s contribution in success of CHANDRAYAAN-3\n\nProf. Radhakant Padhi worked closely with ISRO to develop an algorithm for soft landing of chandrayaan-3. To know more about prof.Padhi&#8217;s contribution watch the following interviews: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zRIWHnIJYwI https://www.ndtv.com/video/news/news/no-doubt-chandrayaan-3-will-safely-land-on-moon-scientist-to-ndtv-718751\n\nRead More +\n\nMedia\n\n07 Aug\n\nIISc introduces indegenous autopilot system for drones\n\nThe Artificial Intelligence and Robotics Laboratory (AIRL) at the Indian Institute of Science (IISc) Bangalore has announced a significant achievement in the field of unmanned aerial systems. In a remarkable ...\n\nRead More +\n\nCollaboration\n\nAbout\n\nIISc\n\nARTPARK\n\nFacilities\n\nPeople\n\nCourses\n\nFacebook-f\n\nTwitter\n\nInstagram * Research\n* Research Clusters\n* [Control and Optimization][1]\n* [Robotics][2]\n* [AI and ML][3]\n* [Socio Technical Systems][4]\n* Labs and Centers\n* [Center for Networked Intelligence][5]\n* [CiSTUP][6]\n* [FOCAS Lab][7]\n* [HiRO Lab][8]\n* [IISc-Nokia CoE for Networked Robotics][9]\n* [Stochastic Robotics Lab][10]\n* [VISTA Lab][11]\n* [Research Facilities][12]\n* [Projects][13]\n* [Publications][14]\n* People\n* [Faculty][15]\n* [Staff][16]\n* [Research Students][17]\n* [MTech Stude