            "url": "https://www.roboticstomorrow.com/products/software-sensors--circuits/3",
            "text": "* [White Papers][1]\n* [Events Calendar][2]\n* [Featured Products][3]\n* [Company Directory][4]\n[[RoboticsTomorrow logo]][5]\n\nOnline Robotics Trade Magazine\nIndustrial Automation, Robots and Unmanned Vehicles\n\n**Search**\n\n## Site Search\n\nEnter Keywords\n(separate each word with a space)\n\n**Limit search to:**\n\nEntire Site\nArticles\nNews\nCompanies\n\n**[Advanced Search][6]**\n* [Home][7]\n* [News][8]\n* [Industrial Robotics][9]\n* [Mobile Robots][10]\n* [Factory Automation][11]\n* [Other Topics][12]\n* [Site Services][13]\n\n# Industrial Automation, Robots and Unmanned Vehicles Products - Software, Sensors & Circuits\n\n**[List Your Product Here][14]**\n\n[[US Digital's New L2 Low Profile Motor Encoder]][15]\n\n### [US Digital's New L2 Low Profile Motor Encoder][16]\n\nThe L2 incremental encoder uses US Digital's proven EM1 optical encoder module and disk, which has\nbillions of device-hours of dependable service in customer applications. This product continues US\nDigital's strong reputation for reliable, field-tested encoders. The L2 is US Digital's lowest\nheight encoder that uses the EM1 module. It has a 0.75 in. bolt-spacing mount. The maximum\nresolution is 1250 CPR (5000 PPR with quadrature). The L2 comes with a single-ended output. Another\nbenefit of the L2 incremental encoder is its fast installation. The cover snaps onto the base to\nsecure the module. It is designed for use with a high-retention connector or cable (sold\nseparately). Like all US Digital products, the L2 is designed and manufactured in Vancouver,\nWashington, USA. It is backed by prompt access to our technical and customer service teams with\nsame-day shipping on most orders.\n\n[Learn More About US Digital][17]\n\n[[Palladyne IQ - Unlocking new frontiers for robotic performance.]][18]\n\n### [Palladyne IQ - Unlocking new frontiers for robotic performance.][19]\n\nPalladyne IQ is a closed-loop autonomy software that uses artificial intelligence (AI) and machine\nlearning (ML) technologies to provide human-like reasoning capabilities for industrial robots and\ncollaborative robots (cobots). By enabling robots to perceive variations or changes in the\nreal-world environment and adapt to them dynamically, Palladyne IQ helps make robots smarter today\nand ready to handle jobs that have historically been too complex to automate.\n\n[Learn More About Palladyne AI Corp.][20]\n\n[[Nion: Next-level time-of-flight ]][21]\n\n### [Nion: Next-level time-of-flight ][22]\n\nThe new Nion 3D camera advances Time-of-Flight (ToF) technology with exceptional resolution, speed,\nand industrial robustness. Designed for demanding applications such as logistics, warehousing,\nindustrial automation, and robotics, Nion delivers high-resolution depth data with real-time\nperformance for faster, safer, and more flexible operations. At its core is the 1.2-megapixel\nTime-of-Flight sensor AF0130 from onsemi's Hyperlux ID family, offering up to four times the\nresolution of conventional VGA-based ToF cameras and significantly higher data density. Active\n940-nm laser illumination ensures accurate and stable measurements in low-light conditions,\nartificial lighting, and even direct sunlight. With an IP67-rated housing, Nion is built for\nreliable operation in dusty, wet, and thermally challenging industrial environments. A user-friendly\nAPI with IDS peak support and compliance with the GigE Vision standard enable fast integration and\nflexible deployment in high-resolution 3D applications. The Nion 3D camera is now available from IDS\nImaging Development Systems.\n\n[Learn More About IDS Imaging Development Systems Inc.][23]\n\n[[Model TR1 Tru-Trac]][24]\n\n### [Model TR1 Tru-Trac][25]\n\nThe Model TR1 Tru-Trac\u00ae linear measurement solution is a versatile option for tracking velocity,\nposition, or distance over a wide variety of surfaces. An integrated encoder, measuring wheel, and\nspring-loaded torsion arm in one, compact unit, the Model TR1 is easy to install. The spring-loaded\ntorsion arm offers adjustable torsion load, allowing the Model TR1 to be mounted in almost any\norientation - even upside-down. The threaded shaft on the pivot axis is field reversible, providing\nmounting access from either side. With operating speeds up to 3000 feet per minute, a wide variety\nof configuration options - including multiple wheel material options - and a housing made from a\ndurable, conductive composite material that minimizes static buildup, the Model TR1 Tru-Trac\u00ae is the\nideal solution for countless applications.\n\n[Learn More About Encoder Products Company][26]\n\n#### Industrial Automation, Robots and Unmanned Vehicles Products\n* [**Last 10 Products Added**][27]\n* [Automate 2026][28]\n* [Hardware & Components][29]\n* [Software, Sensors & Circuits][30]\n* [Motion Control][31]\n* [Design and Development][32]\n* [Operation and Maintenance][33]\n* [Industrial Robots][34]\n* [Collaborative and Service Robots][35]\n\n**[List Your Product Here][36]**\n\n[List Your Product][37]\n\n#### Sponsors\n\n[[Newsletters]][38][[White Papers]][39]\n[[Events]][40][[News]][41]\n\nSocials\n\n#### Most Popular Articles\n\n[Automate 2026 Q&A with Mouser][42]\n\n05/27/26 | [Other Topics][43]\n\n[Automate 2026 Q&A with DESTACO][44]\n\n06/02/26 | [Industrial Robotics][45]\n\n[Tactile Sensor Technology][46]\n\n05/15/26 | [Other Topics][47]\n\n[The Steam Controller and an Industrial Robot: An Unexpected Intersection][48]\n\n05/19/26 | [Industrial Robotics][49]\n\n[Imitation learning is reshaping the training of physical AI for industrial environments][50]\n\n05/19/26 | [Industrial Robotics][51]\n[Articles & Stories][52] | [News][53]\n\n#### Events and Conferences\n\n[MACHINA 2026][54]\n\nJul 07 | 07 2026, Station F, Paris, France\n\n[Commercial UAV Expo][55]\n\nSep 01 | 03 2026, Las Vegas, NV\n\n[5th Annual Unmanned Systems West][56]\n\nSep 08 | 09 2026, San Diego, CA\n\n[International Manufacturing Technology Show - IMTS 2026][57]\n\nSep 14 | 19 2026, McCormick Place, Chicago, IL\n\n[5th Annual Unmanned Maritime Systems Technology (UMST) ][58]\n\nSep 14 | 16 2026, Arlington, VA\n[More Events][59]\n\n#### Site Services\n* [Feature Your Company][60]\n* [Publish Your News][61]\n* [Promote Your Products / Services][62]\n* [List Your Event][63]\n* [Advertise Your Brand][64]\n* [Contribute Articles and Stories ][65]\n* [Subscribe to Newsletters][66]\n* [Search - Articles, Companies, News][67]\n\nSocials\n\n[Full List of Site Services][68]\n\n#### Off Topic\n\n**Manufacturing & Automation**\n* [Workholding Device Manufacturer Eliminates Stockouts After 2-Month ERP Rollout][69]\n* [How Manufacturers and System Integrators Can Build Pricing Power in a Commodity Market][70]\n* [ISP Tuning: Machine Vision vs Human Vision Explained][71]\n* [How Recognition Champions Influence Consistency, Safety Culture, and Day-to-Day Performance][72]\n* [The State of Agentic Cybersecurity][73]\n\n[ManufacturingTomorrow][74]\n\n# More Industrial Automation, Robots and Unmanned Vehicles Resources\n\n* [Contact Info][75]\n* [Bloggers and Associate Authors][76]\n* [Privacy Policy][77]\n* [Advertise][78]\n\n[Subscribe][79] | [Search][80] | [Promote Products][81] | [Feature Your Company][82] | [Publish\nNews][83] | [List Event][84]\n\n[Articles][85] | [News][86] | [Stories][87] | [Products][88] | [Companies][89] |[ Events][90]\n\n[BTH Tech Publications]\n\n\u00a9 2010 - 2026 RoboticsTomorrow - All Rights Reserved\nPowered by BTH Management\n\n[1]: /whitepapers.php\n[2]: /events.php\n[3]: /products.php\n[4]: /company_directory_search.php\n[5]: https://www.roboticstomorrow.com\n[6]: /search.php\n[7]: /\n[8]: /stream/news/\n[9]: /main/robotics\n[10]: /main/personal-service\n[11]: /main/factory-automation\n[12]: /main/unmanned-other-topics\n[13]: /site_services.php\n[14]: /site_services.php\n[15]: /products.php?track=689\n[16]: /products.php?track=689\n[17]: /company_directory/us-digital/10399\n[18]: /products.php?track=1343\n[19]: /products.php?track=1343\n[20]: /company_directory/palladyne-ai-corp/14078\n[21]: /products.php?track=894\n[22]: /products.php?track=894\n[23]: /company_directory/ids-imaging-development-systems-inc/10072\n[24]: /products.php?track=849\n[25]: /products.php?track=849\n[26]: /company_directory/encoder-products-company/11091\n[27]: /products/robotics-products/new\n[28]: /products/show/automate2026/Automate26\n[29]: /products/hardware--components/1\n[30]: /products/software-sensors--circuits/3\n[31]: /products/motion-control/7\n[32]: /products/design-and-development/6\n[33]: /products/operation-and-maintenance/8\n[34]: /products/industrial-robots/11\n[35]: /products/collaborative-and-service-robots/13\n[36]: /site_services.php\n[37]: /site_services.php\n[38]: https://visitor.r20.constantcontact.com/d.jsp?llr=s9wzelzab&p=oi&m=1126729309010&sit=br6cuoelb\n&f=22dae9f3-8365-40d9-8f70-a6370e95d152\n[39]: /whitepapers.php\n[40]: /events.php\n[41]: /stream/news/\n[42]: /article/2026/05/automate-2026-qa-with-mouser/26631\n[43]: /category/unmanned-other-topics\n[44]: /article/2026/06/automate-2026-qa-with-destaco/26663\n[45]: /category/robotics\n[46]: /article/2026/05/tactile-sensor-technology/26573\n[47]: /category/unmanned-other-topics\n[48]: /article/2026/05/the-steam-controller-and-an-industrial-robot-an-unexpected-intersection/26593\n[49]: /category/robotics\n[50]: /article/2026/05/imitation-learning-is-reshaping-the-training-of-physical-ai-for-industrial-en\nvironments/26594\n[51]: /category/robotics\n[52]: /stream/articles/\n[53]: /stream/news/\n[54]: https://www.raisesummit.com/machina\n[55]: https://bit.ly/UAVExpoCB\n[56]: https://bit.ly/4ujN5us\n[57]: https://www.imts.com/?utm_source=roboticstomorrow&utm_medium=cwdigital&utm_campaign=imts2026me\ndia\n[58]: https://www.smgconferences.com/defence/northamerica/conference/umst-usa/booknow?utm_source=Med\nia-Partner&utm_medium=Robotics-Tomorrow&utm_campaign=Social-Post&utm_id=D-450\n[59]: /events.php\n[60]: /company_directory_search.php\n[61]: /streaming.php?type=n\n[62]: /products.php\n[63]: /events.php\n[64]: /advertise.php\n[65]: /associates.php#Article\n[66]: /subscribe.php\n[67]: /search.php\n[68]: /site_services.php\n[69]: http://www.manufacturingtomorrow.com/article/2026/06/workholding-device-manufacturer-eliminate\ns-stockouts-after-2-month-erp-rollout/27635\n[70]: http://www.manufacturingtomorrow.com/article/2026/06/how-manufacturers-and-system-integrators-\ncan-build-pricing-power-in-a-commodity-market/27634\n[71]: http://www.manufacturingtomorrow.com/article/2026/06/isp-tuning-machine-vision-vs-human-vision\n-explained/27633\n[72]: http://www.manufacturingtomorrow.com/article/2026/06/how-recognition-champions-influence-consi\nstency-safety-culture-and-day-to-day-performance/27618\n[73]: http://www.manufacturingtomorrow.com/article/2026/06/the-state-of-agentic-cybersecurity/27614\n[74]: http://www.manufacturingtomorrow.com\n[75]: /contact.php\n[76]: /associates.php\n[77]: /privacy.php\n[78]: /advertise.php\n[79]: /subscribe.php\n[80]: /search.php\n[81]: /site_services.php#Partner\n[82]: /site_services.php#Directory\n[83]: /site_services.php#News\n[84]: /site_services.php#Events\n[85]: /streaming.php?type=a\n[86]: /streaming.php?type=n\n[87]: /streaming.php?type=s\n[88]: /products.php\n[89]: /company_directory_search.php\n[90]: /events.php"
