            "text": "* [White Papers][1]\n* [Events Calendar][2]\n* [Featured Products][3]\n* [Company Directory][4]\n[[RoboticsTomorrow logo]][5]\n\nOnline Robotics Trade Magazine\nIndustrial Automation, Robots and Unmanned Vehicles\n\n**Search**\n\n## Site Search\n\nEnter Keywords\n(separate each word with a space)\n\n**Limit search to:**\n\nEntire Site\nArticles\nNews\nCompanies\n\n**[Advanced Search][6]**\n* [Home][7]\n* [News][8]\n* [Industrial Robotics][9]\n* [Mobile Robots][10]\n* [Factory Automation][11]\n* [Other Topics][12]\n* [Site Services][13]\n\n# Industrial Automation, Robots and Unmanned Vehicles Products - Motion Control\n\n**[List Your Product Here][14]**\n\n[[Elmo Motion Control - The Platinum Line, a new era in servo control]][15]\n\n### [Elmo Motion Control - The Platinum Line, a new era in servo control][16]\n\nSignificantly enhanced servo performance, higher EtherCAT networking precision, richer servo\noperation capabilities, more feedback options, and certified smart Functional Safety. Elmo's\nindustry-leading Platinum line of servo drives provides faster and more enhanced servo performance\nwith wider bandwidth, higher resolutions, and advanced control for better results. Platinum drives\noffer precise EtherCAT networking, faster cycling, high synchronization, negligible jitters, and\nnear-zero latency. They are fully synchronized to the servo loops and feature-rich feedback support,\nup to three feedbacks simultaneously (with two absolute encoders working simultaneously). The\nPlatinum Line includes one of the world's smallest Functional Safety, and FSoE-certified servo\ndrives with unique SIL capabilities.\n\n[Learn More About Elmo Motion Control Inc.][17]\n\n[[Powerful robot drives: Perfect solutions for modern robotics]][18]\n\n### [Powerful robot drives: Perfect solutions for modern robotics][19]\n\nWith a focus on high power density and system integration, maxon supports application optimized\nrobot designs and provides engineering services including design, simulation, and system\noptimization even for highly complex robotic architectures. maxon provides high precision drive\nsolutions for multi axis robotic systems requiring absolute repeatability, high efficiency, and\ndynamic performance. Complemented by design, simulation, and system optimization support, maxon\nenables application optimized robotic architectures with high power density and seamless system\nintegration.\n\n[Learn More About maxon group][20]\n\n[[High Performance Servo Drives for localized and distributed control applications from\nServo2Go.com]][21]\n\n### [High Performance Servo Drives for localized and distributed control applications from\n### Servo2Go.com][22]\n\nEngineered to drive brushless and brush servomotors in torque, velocity or position mode,\nServo2Go.com offers a broad selection of servo drives in a wide range of input voltages and output\npower levels.\n\n[Learn More About Electromate][23]\n\n#### Industrial Automation, Robots and Unmanned Vehicles Products\n* [**Last 10 Products Added**][24]\n* [Automate 2026][25]\n* [Hardware & Components][26]\n* [Software, Sensors & Circuits][27]\n* [Motion Control][28]\n* [Design and Development][29]\n* [Operation and Maintenance][30]\n* [Industrial Robots][31]\n* [Collaborative and Service Robots][32]\n\n**[List Your Product Here][33]**\n\n[List Your Product][34]\n\n#### Sponsors\n\n[[Newsletters]][35][[White Papers]][36]\n[[Events]][37][[News]][38]\n\nSocials\n\n#### Most Popular Articles\n\n[Automate 2026 Q&A with Mouser][39]\n\n05/27/26 | [Other Topics][40]\n\n[Automate 2026 Q&A with DESTACO][41]\n\n06/02/26 | [Industrial Robotics][42]\n\n[Tactile Sensor Technology][43]\n\n05/15/26 | [Other Topics][44]\n\n[The Steam Controller and an Industrial Robot: An Unexpected Intersection][45]\n\n05/19/26 | [Industrial Robotics][46]\n\n[Imitation learning is reshaping the training of physical AI for industrial environments][47]\n\n05/19/26 | [Industrial Robotics][48]\n[Articles & Stories][49] | [News][50]\n\n#### Events and Conferences\n\n[MACHINA 2026][51]\n\nJul 07 | 07 2026, Station F, Paris, France\n\n[Commercial UAV Expo][52]\n\nSep 01 | 03 2026, Las Vegas, NV\n\n[5th Annual Unmanned Systems West][53]\n\nSep 08 | 09 2026, San Diego, CA\n\n[International Manufacturing Technology Show - IMTS 2026][54]\n\nSep 14 | 19 2026, McCormick Place, Chicago, IL\n\n[5th Annual Unmanned Maritime Systems Technology (UMST) ][55]\n\nSep 14 | 16 2026, Arlington, VA\n[More Events][56]\n\n#### Site Services\n* [Feature Your Company][57]\n* [Publish Your News][58]\n* [Promote Your Products / Services][59]\n* [List Your Event][60]\n* [Advertise Your Brand][61]\n* [Contribute Articles and Stories ][62]\n* [Subscribe to Newsletters][63]\n* [Search - Articles, Companies, News][64]\n\nSocials\n\n[Full List of Site Services][65]\n\n#### Off Topic\n\n**Manufacturing & Automation**\n* [Workholding Device Manufacturer Eliminates Stockouts After 2-Month ERP Rollout][66]\n* [How Manufacturers and System Integrators Can Build Pricing Power in a Commodity Market][67]\n* [ISP Tuning: Machine Vision vs Human Vision Explained][68]\n* [How Recognition Champions Influence Consistency, Safety Culture, and Day-to-Day Performance][69]\n* [The State of Agentic Cybersecurity][70]\n\n[ManufacturingTomorrow][71]\n\n# More Industrial Automation, Robots and Unmanned Vehicles Resources\n\n* [Contact Info][72]\n* [Bloggers and Associate Authors][73]\n* [Privacy Policy][74]\n* [Advertise][75]\n\n[Subscribe][76] | [Search][77] | [Promote Products][78] | [Feature Your Company][79] | [Publish\nNews][80] | [List Event][81]\n\n[Articles][82] | [News][83] | [Stories][84] | [Products][85] | [Companies][86] |[ Events][87]\n\n[BTH Tech Publications]\n\n\u00a9 2010 - 2026 RoboticsTomorrow - All Rights Reserved\nPowered by BTH Management\n\n[1]: /whitepapers.php\n[2]: /events.php\n[3]: /products.php\n[4]: /company_directory_search.php\n[5]: https://www.roboticstomorrow.com\n[6]: /search.php\n[7]: