        "crawl_text": "[Skip to main content][1]\n1. [Home][2]\n[RZ Copilot Key Visual Male two Screens 2026]\n\n# What if AI could do an engineer\u2019s most tedious work?\n\nWe\u2019ve launched the Eigen Engineering Agent, purpose-built AI for industrial automation engineering.\nIt moves AI beyond generating suggestions to executing engineering tasks end-to-end. Now available\nfor more than 600,000 TIA Portal users.\n\n[Start free trial][3][How AI transforms Engineering][4]\n[CES 2026: Roland Busch & Jensen Huang, Siemens & NVIDIA]\n\n## Building the operating system for Industrial AI\n\nTogether with NVIDIA, we are building the Industrial AI operating system for the physical world.\nRead the latest news from our ever-expanding partnership here.\n\n[Learn more][5]\n[Vectron X Primary - Tec Keyvisual 16to9]\n\n## Vectron X \u2013 the next dimension of rail technology\n\nThe next generation of locomotives for freight and passenger transport combines the proven platform\ntechnology with app-based functionalities, open interfaces for third-party providers, in an open\necosystem \u2013 connecting people, places and portfolios more closely than ever before.\n\n[Read more][6]\n[bx-overview-panoramic-city-skyline-is485896260-xcelerator-shape-hero-2560x1440]\n\n## One digital twin, clear operational insight\n\nAt the University of Wollongong, a digital twin brings together data from 1,000 assets, 500 BMS\npoints, energy meters and documents, to create a single source of truth and enable efficient,\ndata-driven operations acrossthe campus.\n\n[Explore Building X][7]\n[Amazonia rainforest]\n\n## A digital twin in the Amazon rainforest\n\nDeep in the Amazon, a cooperative partnered with Natura to extract essential oils from native\nplants. We brought a digital twin to their extraction process, cutting energy and water use while\nboosting income for the local community by 60%.\n\n[Read the story][8]\n[A person wearing a headset interacts with a holographic display of 3D models and data\nvisualizations.]\n\n### Realize LIVE 2026 | Holland\n\nJoin us June 29 \u2013 July 1 in Amsterdam to explore the future of engineering, simulation, and\nindustrial AI.\n\n[Register now][9]\n**Technology**\n\n## Upgrade reality\n\nThe challenges of tomorrow demand an upgrade today. We power your ideas with artificial\nintelligence, simulation and smart technologies, moving you from digital blueprint to real-world\nimpact.\n\nArtificial intelligence\nDigital twin\nDigital transformation\nInfrastructure\nSoftware-defined automation\nSustainability\nSelect...\nArtificial intelligenceDigital twinDigital transformationInfrastructureSoftware-defined\nautomationSustainability\n[\n[Farma R\u00e1je\u010dek Jahody.]\n][10]\n[**Customer story**\nall\n\n### AI on the family farm helps a robot pick strawberries\n\nMeet Fravebot. It monitors plant health, spots pests early and predicts harvests two weeks out. It\nlearned how in a digital twin first.\n\n][11]\n[Read customer story][12]\n[\n[A person wearing a VR headset is looking at a water efficiency solution illustration.]\n][13]\n[**E-book**\nall\n\n### E-book: Industrial AI across the value chain\n\nHow industrial AI is transforming every step, from product design and engineering to production and\noperations.\n\n][14]\n[Download the e-book][15]\n[\n[A person stands in front of a large screen displaying a graph with a rising line, likely\nrepresenting data or statistics.]\n][16]\n[**Product spotlight **\nall\n\n### Eigen Engineering Agent for TIA Portal\n\nPurpose-built AI that autonomously plans, codes, configures and validates automation engineering\ntasks. Now generally available.\n\n][17]\n[Start free trial][18]\n[\n[Farma R\u00e1je\u010dek Jahody.]\n][19]\n[**Customer story**\nall\n\n### AI on the family farm helps a robot pick strawberries\n\nMeet Fravebot. It monitors plant health, spots pests early and predicts harvests two weeks out. It\nlearned how in a digital twin first.\n\n][20]\n[Read customer story][2