te][85]\n\n[Request For Quote][86]\n\nDel-Tron Precision is your one-stop shop for ball & crossed roller slides, multi-axis positioning\nand motor-ready lead screw stages, air actuators, recirculating slide guides and crossed roller rail\nsets. Custom linear slides are available.\n\n[ [Del-Tron Precision, Inc.] ][87] $$$\n\n### [Attica Automation][88]\n\nOxford, MI \u00a0|\u00a0 [248-236-2454][89]\n[Request For Quote][90]\n\n[Request For Quote][91]\n\nAt Attica Automation, we design and build assembly machinery that helps manufacturers improve\nproduction efficiency, accuracy, and process consistency. Our company develops automated and\nsemi-automated assembly solutions that support a wide range of production environments, from\nstandalone workstations to fully integrated assembly systems.\n\n[ [Attica Automation] ][92] $$$\n[Get Your Company Listed][93]\n[placeholder image]\n\n## [More Assembly Machinery Manufacturers][94]\n\n\n### Automation Equipment Supplier Directory Overview\n\nFind automation equipment manufacturers, compare automation equipment suppliers, and browse factory\nautomation equipment built for modern production demands. This directory helps buyers source\nassembly machinery manufacturers, custom automation machinery providers, and industrial automation\nequipment partners serving automotive, electronics, medical device, food processing, packaging, and\ngeneral manufacturing markets. Use it to connect with suppliers of automation machinery, assembly\nequipment, and automated assembly equipment designed for throughput, accuracy, repeatability, and\nline integration. Whether you are replacing manual stations or planning a larger upgrade, this page\nsupports faster research, cleaner comparisons, and more informed supplier selection.\n\n### Assembly Equipment in Modern Manufacturing\n\nAssembly equipment supports repeatable production by moving parts through fastening, joining,\npressing, sorting, and transfer steps with greater consistency than manual processes. Buyers often\nuse this category to compare systems for electronics, medical products, consumer goods, and other\noperations where speed and uniformity matter across high-volume runs.\n\n### Automated Assembly Equipment Systems\n\nAutomated assembly equipment builds on that foundation by coordinating motion, handling, feeding,\nand verification into a more complete production solution. These systems are widely used in\nautomotive component manufacturing, appl"
