ogies\n* Promote interdisciplinary research\n* Contribute to societal and industrial needs in the domain of cyber-physical systems\n\nAbout RBCCPS\n\n## Vision is to establish itself as a globally recognized center of excellence in CPS\n\nThe RBCCPS envisions becoming a global leader in the research and development of CPS. RBCCPS\nenvisions achieving this vision by\n* Fostering interdisciplinary research collaborations\n* Conducting cutting-edge research\n* Developing innovative solutions that integrate physical and computational systems\n\nAbout RBCCPS\n\n## Innovation-driven excellence in CPS research to create positive impact.\n\nExcellence, Interdisciplinary Approach, Impact, Ethical Conduct, Knowledge sharing.\n* Striving for excellence in research, innovation, education, and collaboration.\n* Bridging disciplines through research and innovation.\n* Addressing real-world challenges with ethical CPS technology, promoting open collaboration.\n* #### Our Mission\n* #### Our Vision\n* #### Core Values\n\n# Latest events, news and updates at RBCCPS\n\n[Latest News][85] [News][86]\n\n14\n\nJan\n\n#### [Best demo in COMSNETS 2024][87]\n\nCongratulations to Navin Kumar and Sudarshan Bandopadhyay MTech students from RBCCPS for securing\nrunner up under the demos and exhibit section of COMSNETS 2024\n\n[Read More+][88]\n\n[Latest News][89]\n\n28\n\nJul\n\n#### [PhD Student of RBCCPS Awarded TCS Research Scholar Program (RSP) Scholarship][90]\n\nCongratulations to Ajay Kumar Sandula, a PhD student at RBCCPS, for his remarkable achievement!\nUnder the guidance of Dr. Pradipta Biswas as his main guide and Dr. Debasish Ghose as ...\n\n[Read More+][91]\n\n[Latest News][92]\n\n03\n\nJul\n\n#### [Congratulations!- Qualcomm Innovation Fellowship Super Winner 2023][93]\n\nCongratulations!!! Siddarth Asokan, RBCCPS PhD student has bagged the Qualcomm Innovation Fellowship\nSuper Winner for 2023. He has secured this fellowship for the 4th time! and if that was not ...\n\n[Read More+][94]\n\n# In Press\n\n[Media][95]\n\n22\n\nAug\n\n#### [Faculty at RBCCPS\u2019s contribution in success of CHANDRAYAAN-3][96]\n\nProf. Radhakant Padhi worked closely with ISRO to develop an algorithm for soft landing of\nchandrayaan-3. To know more about prof.Padhi\u2019s contribution watch the following interviews:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zRIWHnIJYwI\nhttps://www.ndtv.com/video/news/news/no-doubt-chandrayaan-3-will-safely-land-on-moon-scientist-to-nd\ntv-718751\n\n[Read More+][97]\n\n[Media][98]\n\n07\n\nAug\n\n#### [IISc introduces indegenous autopilot system for drones][99]\n\nThe Artificial Intelligence and Robotics Laboratory (AIRL) at the Indian Institute of Science (IISc)\nBangalore has announced a significant achievement in the field of unmanned aerial systems. In a\nremarkable ...\n\n[Read More+][100]\n\n## Collaboration\n\n[artpark-logo-e]\n[wipro-e]\n[google-e]\n[siemens-e]\n[nokia-e]\n[serb-logo-e]\n[tcs-e]\n[gok-logo-e]\n[isro-logo-e]\n[drdo-logo-e]\n[dst-logo-e]\n[indian-army-logo-e]\n* [ About ][101]\n* [ IISc ][102]\n* [ ARTPARK ][103]\n* [ Facilities ][104]\n* [ People ][105]\n* [ Courses ][106]\nFacebook-f Twitter Instagram\n\n[1]: https://cps.iisc.ac.in/control-and-optimization/\n[2]: https://cps.iisc.ac.in/robotics/\n[3]: https://cps.iisc.ac.in/ai-machine-learning/\n[4]: https://cps.iisc.ac.in/socio-technical-systems/\n[5]: https://cni.iisc.ac.in/\n[6]: https://cistup.iisc.ac.in/\n[7]: https://www.focaslab.com/\n[8]: https://iisc-hiro.github.io/\n[9]: https://cps.iisc.ac.in/researchlab/iisc-nokia-coe/\n[10]: https://www.stochlab.com/\n[11]: https://www.vistalabiisc.com/\n[12]: https://cps.iisc.ac.in/facilities/\n[13]: https://cps.iisc.ac.in/research/projects/\n[14]: https://cps.iisc.ac.in/research/publications/\n[15]: https://cps.iisc.ac.in/faculty/\n[16]: https://cps.iisc.ac.in/staff/\n[17]: https://cps.iisc.ac.in/research-students\n[18]: https://cps.iisc.ac.in/mtech-students\n[19]: https://cps.iisc.ac.in/postdocs\n[20]: https://cps.