        "crawl_text": "* [White Papers][1]\n* [Events Calendar][2]\n* [Featured Products][3]\n* [Company Directory][4]\n[[RoboticsTomorrow logo]][5]\n\nOnline Robotics Trade Magazine\nIndustrial Automation, Robots and Unmanned Vehicles\n\n**Search**\n\n## Site Search\n\nEnter Keywords\n(separate each word with a space)\n\n**Limit search to:**\n\nEntire Site\nArticles\nNews\nCompanies\n\n**[Advanced Search][6]**\n* [Home][7]\n* [News][8]\n* [Industrial Robotics][9]\n* [Mobile Robots][10]\n* [Factory Automation][11]\n* [Other Topics][12]\n* [Site Services][13]\n\n[The Steam Controller and an Industrial Robot: An...][14]\n\n[KNF - Automation Technology Requires Reliable and Durable...][15]\n\n[Roboverse Reply Impresses at ELROB 2026 With Intelligent...][16]\n\n#### Robotics and Automation - Articles, Stories & Interviews\n\n### [Omnidirectional Mobile Robotics: Foundations, Advantages, and Industrial Applications][17]\n\n**Article from Robotnik**\nWhen the industrial application demands agile workflows, maximally optimized aisles, and millimeter\nrepeatability in coupling operations, omnidirectional mobile robotics positions itself as an\nindispensable strategic investment.\n\n### [Embodied AI: Industrial Manufacturing\u2019s Answer to the Great Margin Squeeze][18]\n\n**Kristi Martindale, Chief Commercial Officer | [Palladyne AI][19]**\nEmbodied AI-enabled robotics helps companies address the \u201cgreat margin squeeze\u201d head-on and shift to\na high-mix manufacturing approach with faster changeovers and fewer exceptions that stop the line \u2014\nwithout adding engineering bandwidth.\n\n### [Imitation learning is reshaping the training of physical AI for industrial environments][20]\n\n**Anders Billes\u00f8 Beck, Vice President of Technology | [Universal Robots][21]**\nImitation learning is changing how industrial robots are trained, shifting from rigid programming to\nlearning through real-world interaction. Anders Billes\u00f8 Beck explains why data quality, force and\nproduction-grade hardware matter.\n\n### [Time-of-Flight as a key technology for cost-sensitive 3D applications][22]\n\n**Patrick Schick, Product Manager for 3D Vision | [IDS Imaging][23]**\nIn this article, Patrick Schick, Product Manager for 3D Vision at IDS, explains the background and\ntechnical decisions behind Nion, puts iToF technology into context, and highlights typical areas of\napplication.\n\n### [The Steam Controller and an Industrial Robot: An Unexpected Intersection][24]\n\n**Case Study from | [ENCY Software][25]**\nA standard wireless controller may seem far removed from the factory floor. ENCY Software\u2019s work on\nENCY Hyper shows why tactile, analog input can still matter when programming industrial robots and\ncobots.\n\n### [Automate 2026 Q&A with DESTACO][26]\n\n**Q&A with | [DESTACO][27]**\nAt Booth 2218 visitors will see a wide range of DESTACO technologies in action, including robotic\ngripping, tool changing, workholding, and automation solutions designed to improve flexibility,\nsimplify integration, and increase productivity.\n\n### [Tactile Sensor Technology][28]\n\n**Q&A with Dr. Alexander Schmitz, CEO and co-founder of | [Xela Robotics][29]**\nHumanoid robots are expected to enter our homes soon, and a sense of touch is crucial for safe and\ncapable humanoids. Homes are challenging, unstructured and highly dynamic environments.\n\n[Interested in contributing an article or review?][30]\n\n[More Articles and Stories][31] \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0[Featured Articles][32]\n\n#### Robotics and Automation - Featured Stories\n\n### [6 Key Considerations When Integrating Robotics With HF Welding Machines][33]\n\n**Article from Emily Newton, Revolutionized**\nSuccessfully integrating robotics with HF welding machines requires more than installing equipment.\nRobots can only accelerate manufacturing cycles, protect workers from hazards and eliminate errors\nlike burn-through when implemented properly.\n\n### [How AI Is Powering Smarter, More Connected Logistics Operations][34]\n\n**Article from Andreas Podwojewski, Managing Director, North America at Arvato**\nToday, in an increasingly unpredictable environment, it\u2019s no longer about deploying more robots;\nit\u2019s about deploying them in smarter, more adaptable ways. AI is supporting this shift, working as\nthe intelligence layer behind modern logistics operations.\n\n### [A3's Automate 2026 Opens Next Week in Chicago][35]\n\n**News from Automate Show**\nNorth America\u2019s largest robotics and automation event brings humanoids, AI, industrial robots and\nthe future of automation to McCormick Place June 22-25\n[All Robotics and Automation Stories][36]\n\n#### Robotics and Automation - News Headlines\n\n### [Roboverse Reply Impresses at ELROB 2026 With Intelligent Robotic Systems for Critical\n### Missions][37]\n\n06/26/26, 09:07 AM | [Mobile Robots][38] | [Other Topics][39]\nTeaming up with ELP, a specialist for technical equipment for defusing service, the company\ndemonstrated outstanding performance alongside a field of international participants from June 15 to\n19, proving that its autonomous solutions operate reliably under real-world conditions.\n\n### * [White Papers][1]\n* [Events Calendar][2]\n* [Featured Products][3]\n* [Company Directory][4]\n[[RoboticsTomorrow logo]][5]\n\nOnline Robotics Trade Magazine\nIndustrial Automation, Robots and Unmanned Vehicles\n\n**Search**\n\n## Site Search\n\nEnter Keywords\n(separate each word with a space)\n\n**Limit search to:**\n\nEntire Site\nArticles\nNews\nCompanies\n\n**[Advanced Search][6]**\n* [Home][7]\n* [News][8]\n* [Industrial Robotics][9]\n* [Mobile Robots][10]\n* [Factory Automation][11]\n* [Other Topics][12]\n* [Site Services][13]\n\n[The Steam Controller and an Industrial Robot: An...][14]\n\n[KNF - Automation Technology Requires Reliable and Durable...][15]\n\n[Roboverse Reply Impresses at ELROB 2026 With Intelligent...][16]\n\n#### Robotics and Automation - Articles, Stories & Interviews\n\n### [Omnidirectional Mobile Robotics: Foundations, Advantages, and Industrial Applications][17]\n\n**Article from Robotnik**\nWhen the industrial application demands agile workflows, maximally optimized aisles, and millimeter\nrepeatability in coupling operations, omnidirectional mobile robotics positions itself as an\nindispensable strategic investment.\n\n### [Embodied AI: Industrial Manufacturing\u2019s Answer to the Great Margin Squeeze][18]\n\n**Kristi Martindale, Chief Commercial Officer | [Palladyne AI][19]**\nEmbodied AI-enabled robotics helps companies address the \u201cgreat margin squeeze\u201d head-on and shift to\na high-mix manufacturing approach with faster changeovers and fewer exceptions that stop the line \u2014\nwithout adding engineering bandwidth.\n\n### [Imitation learning is reshaping the training of physical AI for industrial environments][20]\n\n**Anders Billes\u00f8 Beck, Vice President of Technology | [Universal Robots][21]**\nImitation learning is changing how industrial robots are trained, shifting from rigid programming to\nlearning through real-world interaction. Anders Billes\u00f8 Beck explains why data quality, force and\nproduction-grade hardware matter.\n\n### [Time-of-Flight as a key technology for cost-sensitive 3D applications][22]\n\n**Patrick Schick, Product Manager for 3D Vision | [IDS Imaging][23]**\nIn this article, Patrick Schick, Product Manager for 3D Vision at IDS, explains the background and\ntechnical decisions behind Nion, puts iToF technology into context, and highlights typical areas of\napplication.\n\n### [The Steam Controller and an Industrial Robot: An Unexpected Intersection][24]\n\n**Case Study from | [ENCY Software][25]**\nA standard wireless controller may seem far removed from the factory floor. ENCY Software\u2019s work on\nENCY Hyper shows why tactile, analog input can still matter when programming industrial robots and\ncobots.\n\n### [Automate 2026 Q&A with DESTACO][26]\n\n**Q&A with | [DESTACO][27]**\nAt Booth 2218 visitors will see a wide range of DESTACO technologies in action, including robotic\ngripping, tool changing, workholding, and automation solutions designed to improve flexibility,\nsimplify integration, and increase productivity.\n\n### [Tactile Sensor Technology][28]\n\n**Q&A with Dr. Alexander Schmitz, CEO and co-founder of | [Xela Robotics][29]**\nHumanoid robots are expected to enter our homes soon, and a sense of touch is crucial for safe and\ncapable humanoids. Homes are challenging, unstructured and highly dynamic environments.\n\n[Interested in contributing an article or review?][30]\n\n[More Articles and Stories][31] \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0[Featured Articles][32]\n\n#### Robotics and Automation - Featured Stories\n\n### [6 Key Considerations When Integrating Robotics With HF Welding Machines][33]\n\n**Article from Emily Newton, Revolutionized**\nSuccessfully integrating robotics with HF welding machines requires more than installing equipment.\nRobots can only accelerate manufacturing cycles, protect workers from hazards and eliminate errors\nlike burn-through when implemented properly.\n\n### [How AI Is Powering Smarter, More Connected Logistics Operations][34]\n\n**Article from Andreas Podwojewski, Managing Director, North America at Arvato**\nToday, in an increasingly unpredictable environment, it\u2019s no longer about deploying more robots;\nit\u2019s about deploying them in smarter, more adaptable ways. AI is supporting this shift, working as\nthe intelligence layer behind modern logistics operations.\n\n### [A3's Automate 2026 Opens Next Week in Chicago][35]\n\n**News from Automate Show**\nNorth America\u2019s largest robotics and automation event brings humanoids, AI, industrial robots and\nthe future of automation to McCormick Place June 22-25\n[All Robotics and Automation Stories][36]\n\n#### Robotics and Automation - News Headlines\n\n### [Roboverse Reply Impresses at ELROB 2026 With Intelligent Robotic Systems for Critical\n### Missions][37]\n\n06/26/26, 09:07 AM | [Mobile Robots][38] | [Other Topics][39]\nTeaming up with ELP, a specialist for technical equipment for defusing service, the company\ndemonstrated outstanding performance alongside a field of international participants from June 15 to\n19, proving that its autonomous solutions operate reliably under real-world conditions.\n\n### [German Economy Calls for Faster Humanoid Robotics Adoption][40]\n\n06/26/26, 09:06 AM | [Industrial Robotics][41] | [Factory Automation][42]\n82 % consider humanoid robots drivers of future innovation\n\n### [DEEPX and Sixfab Launch 'DEEPX AI HAT' to Drive Edge Physical AI on Raspberry Pi][43]\n\n06/26/26, 09:00 AM | [Industrial Robotics][44] | [Mobile Robots][45]\n-Partnership delivers high-performance, low-power AI acceleration directly to the global Raspberry\nPi ecosystem -Eliminates cloud dependency for real-time inference in robotics and smart automation\n-Rolls out production-ready Starter Kit and SDKs to lower entry barriers for global developers\n\n### [Mouser Expands Industrial Automation Portfolio with New Manufacturer Additions to Support\n### Next-Gen Systems][46]\n\n06/25/26, 06:58 PM | [Industrial Robotics][47] | [Factory Automation][48] | [Mouser Electronics][49]\nThis expansion broadens access to critical technologies across AI, connectivity, power, control, and\nsensing, which are key building blocks for today's increasingly integrated industrial environments.\n\n### [Hirebotics Launches Industry's First No-Code, Explosion-Proof Cobot Solution for Painting][50]\n\n06/25/26, 06:56 PM | [Industrial Robotics][51] | [Mobile Robots][52]\nBuilt on FANUC's CRX-10iA/L Paint hardware and Hirebotics' Beacon Platform, the Cobot Painter\neliminates the need for dedicated paint cells and complex programming\n[All News Headlines][53] | [Publish Your News][54]\n\n#### Robotics and Automation - Fe